,{"author":{"account":{"login":"wakir-labs","providerType":"User"},"email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"authoredDate":"2026-05-19T16:18:34Z","committedDate":"2026-05-19T16:18:34Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:54:51.416Z","repositoryId":1230764008,"sha":"155861868e0be7de9695b7dcd43c268b31fcbb9f"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"wakir-labs","providerType":"User"},"email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"authoredDate":"2026-05-19T16:13:47Z","committedDate":"2026-05-19T16:13:47Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:54:51.416Z","repositoryId":1230764008,"sha":"3a6927cb21efee250ace73ebb05d49291599fefd"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"wakir-labs","providerType":"User"},"email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"authoredDate":"2026-05-19T16:12:47Z","committedDate":"2026-05-19T16:12:47Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:54:51.416Z","repositoryId":1230764008,"sha":"db1c77ca7e9688ec0eea13ca6dc2c94a10de01a7"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"wakir-labs","providerType":"User"},"email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"authoredDate":"2026-05-19T16:10:13Z","committedDate":"2026-05-19T16:10:13Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:54:51.416Z","repositoryId":1230764008,"sha":"24666b719603f7857dec332c96edddb62927a9f3"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"wakir-labs","providerType":"User"},"email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"authoredDate":"2026-05-19T16:09:59Z","committedDate":"2026-05-19T16:09:59Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:54:51.416Z","repositoryId":1230764008,"sha":"f3091bdd3d4074aeece91dc270e81265dbb47193"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:54:51.416Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/281068747?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs","id":281068747,"login":"wakir-labs","node_id":"U_kgDOEMDEyw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/55545ae4dd897d67639f357c07e7cdde04b34039/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T09:28:19Z","email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T09:28:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"A corrupted share that is not corrupted is not a counterexample; make the vector bite by construction (#564)\n\n* A corrupted share that is not corrupted is not a counterexample; make the vector bite by construction\n\n`test_combine_corrupted_share_raises_value_error` was red once on\n2026-09-23 (DID NOT RAISE ValueError) and green on a re-run of the same\ntree. It was not weather.\n\nThe test generated a fresh 2-of-3 split and overwrote word 5 of share 0\nwith the literal \"academic\". Words 0..3 of a SLIP-39 mnemonic are header\nfields and the last three are the RS1024 checksum, so index 5 sits in\nthe share-value field, whose content is uniform over the 1024-word\nlexicon. \"academic\" is lexicon index 0. When the draw already put\n\"academic\" there, the assignment changed nothing, the share stayed\nvalid, combine returned the master, and pytest reported DID NOT RAISE.\n\nMeasured, not argued:\n\n- Exhaustive sweep over all 1024 lexicon words at the corruption site:\n  1023 raise, exactly one does not -- the word already there. One\n  mechanism, no second.\n- Sampled rate over 20000 fresh splits: 11 degenerate draws\n  (5.5e-4; structural expectation 1/1024 = 9.8e-4).\n- Reproduced deterministically: under a seeded RNG, seed\n  b\"degenerate-draw/1030\" yields a share whose word 5 is \"academic\";\n  the old test body then returns the correct master and does not raise.\n\nThe repair adds no retry and no flaky marker:\n\n1. `corrupt_mnemonic_word` refuses a replacement equal to the word\n   already at the position and raises `IneffectiveCorruption`. An\n   ineffective corruption now fails by name instead of silently\n   satisfying the assertion under test.\n2. The generated-share vector runs under a pinned RNG\n   (`shamir_mnemonic.shamir.RANDOM_BYTES`, the seam the reference\n   implementation reassigns in its own `generate_vectors.py`), so the\n   mnemonic under corruption is the same string on every run.\n3. A second vector corrupts the canonical SLIP-39 mnemonic, which\n   carries no randomness at all.\n\nNegative controls, both of which go red when the guard is removed:\n\n- `test_corruption_helper_rejects_a_no_op_replacement` feeds the helper\n  the word already in place.\n- `test_header_words_are_constant_for_the_phase_1a_layout` records that\n  word 2 is \"academic\" for every share the single-group layout ever\n  issues, so the same defect at that position would be degenerate 100%\n  of the time rather than 0.1%.\n\nAlso withdraws an untrue claim in the canonical-vector docstring: we\ncan pin the issuance RNG; upstream does it itself.\n\nNet +5 tests, collected identically in the production and sandbox\nlanes, so the tests.yml drift envelope (EXPECTED_DELTA 563) is\nunchanged: 3349 -> 3354 collected, 0 failures.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Replace the sampled flake rate with the run that finished\n\nThe 20 000-split sample quoted in the previous commit was a low draw\n(11 observed against 19.5 expected). The 100 000-split run has since\nfinished and says something stronger than a rate:\n\n  did_not_raise = 95, no-op corruptions = 95\n\nThe two counts are equal. Every run of the old test body that failed\nto raise was a run whose draw already carried \"academic\" at index 5,\nand every such draw failed to raise. That is the sampled form of the\nexhaustive sweep result, over a different population: the no-op is not\nthe main mechanism, it is the only one.\n\nRate 9.50e-4 against the structural expectation 1/1024 = 9.77e-4.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Reza Tehrani <fabian@callandor.gmbh>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ebb62df336d3e03fbda663c0faccb8c4a01c099b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/trees/ebb62df336d3e03fbda663c0faccb8c4a01c099b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/commits/55545ae4dd897d67639f357c07e7cdde04b34039","verification":{"payload":"tree ebb62df336d3e03fbda663c0faccb8c4a01c099b\nparent 98563d80e1c8b6b1348fed5320e9ce26c5cc5b44\nauthor wakir-labs <xypu4r8e@addy.io> 1790155699 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790155699 +0200\n\nA corrupted share that is not corrupted is not a counterexample; make the vector bite by construction (#564)\n\n* A corrupted share that is not corrupted is not a counterexample; make the vector bite by construction\n\n`test_combine_corrupted_share_raises_value_error` was red once on\n2026-09-23 (DID NOT RAISE ValueError) and green on a re-run of the same\ntree. It was not weather.\n\nThe test generated a fresh 2-of-3 split and overwrote word 5 of share 0\nwith the literal \"academic\". Words 0..3 of a SLIP-39 mnemonic are header\nfields and the last three are the RS1024 checksum, so index 5 sits in\nthe share-value field, whose content is uniform over the 1024-word\nlexicon. \"academic\" is lexicon index 0. When the draw already put\n\"academic\" there, the assignment changed nothing, the share stayed\nvalid, combine returned the master, and pytest reported DID NOT RAISE.\n\nMeasured, not argued:\n\n- Exhaustive sweep over all 1024 lexicon words at the corruption site:\n  1023 raise, exactly one does not -- the word already there. One\n  mechanism, no second.\n- Sampled rate over 20000 fresh splits: 11 degenerate draws\n  (5.5e-4; structural expectation 1/1024 = 9.8e-4).\n- Reproduced deterministically: under a seeded RNG, seed\n  b\"degenerate-draw/1030\" yields a share whose word 5 is \"academic\";\n  the old test body then returns the correct master and does not raise.\n\nThe repair adds no retry and no flaky marker:\n\n1. `corrupt_mnemonic_word` refuses a replacement equal to the word\n   already at the position and raises `IneffectiveCorruption`. An\n   ineffective corruption now fails by name instead of silently\n   satisfying the assertion under test.\n2. The generated-share vector runs under a pinned RNG\n   (`shamir_mnemonic.shamir.RANDOM_BYTES`, the seam the reference\n   implementation reassigns in its own `generate_vectors.py`), so the\n   mnemonic under corruption is the same string on every run.\n3. A second vector corrupts the canonical SLIP-39 mnemonic, which\n   carries no randomness at all.\n\nNegative controls, both of which go red when the guard is removed:\n\n- `test_corruption_helper_rejects_a_no_op_replacement` feeds the helper\n  the word already in place.\n- `test_header_words_are_constant_for_the_phase_1a_layout` records that\n  word 2 is \"academic\" for every share the single-group layout ever\n  issues, so the same defect at that position would be degenerate 100%\n  of the time rather than 0.1%.\n\nAlso withdraws an untrue claim in the canonical-vector docstring: we\ncan pin the issuance RNG; upstream does it itself.\n\nNet +5 tests, collected identically in the production and sandbox\nlanes, so the tests.yml drift envelope (EXPECTED_DELTA 563) is\nunchanged: 3349 -> 3354 collected, 0 failures.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Replace the sampled flake rate with the run that finished\n\nThe 20 000-split sample quoted in the previous commit was a low draw\n(11 observed against 19.5 expected). The 100 000-split run has since\nfinished and says something stronger than a rate:\n\n  did_not_raise = 95, no-op corruptions = 95\n\nThe two counts are equal. Every run of the old test body that failed\nto raise was a run whose draw already carried \"academic\" at index 5,\nand every such draw failed to raise. That is the sampled form of the\nexhaustive sweep result, over a different population: the no-op is not\nthe main mechanism, it is the only one.\n\nRate 9.50e-4 against the structural expectation 1/1024 = 9.77e-4.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Reza Tehrani <fabian@callandor.gmbh>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs5uzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmOUQAGqCSy0OdChBx/GEHIshRHPh\nSvYA559YwDerJAnVT6g0qN/NBIylPmAAcWHR3PakaxY9haenByyoxhaGLA7DTUVl\nJTSDrreSJFJdi90Ftgh/TMO/urd+FFcJTqMcsTFYmnpqCpFg51haHosve5VGe3Fq\nn1x/uyZWTxvvCkiaOuoNqSgo9ms04HB2oYgdytoMkPPsmLLJtOVd/r3M76Y/TTu3\nFwAoZ4TuHL8Zf2U606ajqDQc98RvXioksbq+no5KYuzA+I1mbib5S9IuF/Dstq/C\npc8HnFCo3uSJKOVq591w0ALzmUCPIscIkmdgCLb7SjDgKzJsyJ7anVGtBpsmNcRg\nvdsqxu5N1c59NLes8WHa7ebbsEl86Pv9xprrKhxC4Sk7og5oIzn72EWyTLmOhpEM\nCnU4QKMnwiSDEQfP2HcSLe755nzoFeY/+gcyejVPon8uvDYrOpZRKvfQeewaSufe\nUnXA+Kmpu6OAx3EKf4ir087E3UvaYnFHscgc/zBeDBntuGTUe+SMM3DXp5uGHXut\n23K6sxE1aZMmsgTyDqeE2NwY/OswbW70BRFGHFeWcbJM2lltd9MET0qJTfylh1a4\nIbxNFt3NrvBmfCDRbXQLJkOYwK2sXm8kmDsJH0bdHwpSAC7aYM6e9fAwqDWOnazD\nH2s01B03iHrEuRxCD92Z\n=NNkd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T09:28:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/55545ae4dd897d67639f357c07e7cdde04b34039","node_id":"C_kwDOSVv36NoAKDU1NTQ1YWU0ZGQ4OTdkNjc2MzlmMzU3YzA3ZTdjZGRlMDRiMzQwMzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/98563d80e1c8b6b1348fed5320e9ce26c5cc5b44","sha":"98563d80e1c8b6b1348fed5320e9ce26c5cc5b44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/98563d80e1c8b6b1348fed5320e9ce26c5cc5b44"}],"sha":"55545ae4dd897d67639f357c07e7cdde04b34039","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/55545ae4dd897d67639f357c07e7cdde04b34039"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githu