:"311d43258e4cc64e68da467b19c40d4e9beeb452","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/trees/311d43258e4cc64e68da467b19c40d4e9beeb452"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/commits/98563d80e1c8b6b1348fed5320e9ce26c5cc5b44","verification":{"payload":"tree 311d43258e4cc64e68da467b19c40d4e9beeb452\nparent 223e4095ca6b432f36c0ca39682c755297df0f5d\nauthor wakir-labs <xypu4r8e@addy.io> 1790153852 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790153852 +0200\n\nSay that the gap at the writing end is closed, because it is (#563)\n\nThe test plan still read \"is being closed there in parallel\" for the stager''s\nown validity check. It was closed in #561: the stager refuses a document with\nno entry carrying use == \"x509-svid\" and a non-empty x5c, and compares it\nagainst the root it holds.\n\nA test plan for a window that is about to go live, describing a closed state as\nwork in progress, is the same class this whole pass is about - documentation\nthat asserts a property the code no longer has, in the friendlier direction.\n\nText by Amara Osei; carried over by Mira after the merge deleted her branch.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs5R8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWrAQADcqUb+K7bNJRcaXLuUV/Kc5\nAEB2/ELAGjHPPdq4Oi88fIPkXNHj7d6l/gUCK2DgudrVWj0k0JdN0choEi0r4KKJ\nvbwA1jW+oqbP04bFBckoeBoJCYfvpKJFQRYbGRrZInGF90msTOj1IdJQL3djQArl\nuRx9BHm69+e+7/Lg+1GB+YmIw+Dh3IAFlAnmyT1dtAswtFdyvTf+ZAh5pc0Sdnva\neXJuTBxvQSDweLT0KrgPqgMoYn52bR3rinuwW7uO0T/DwMb+ym8tLyeUQSoar/yv\nt3hl8WWroQwW0/OZFGxp1PErcHQCqZD1Ia30WH98ew2AANTb51G7VbTJmigv7bsc\nZKy1GKO97h7Kv01mRNPYBJxyIRSDnBKQ5RU1Ov8Rd8q2eKHMLHQ9iq7F0clqqsjF\n8TalUcG3033AfnHzeGLV1MiDzvx9Ro/x8pSrxWyK6245tYnScx3KbZ8Fah+o1zYc\n/cSRc4/Pa9r2QG/PvqbqdydSghlaithlXAkcmuokwxjnGPRFfQpjIDuD5sou7C4A\nBPXbJH1nBsdq11qQ1lAo6y7O1d7mTRhsVyMhxoKQlob8c1WWyhyNGsk9leX5J14H\neDNnyfSNiZ6+hloo0olRjEhRsEBcNWtP42E3YGuLI+VhaCX/Hoq9lCxzkc4udmsR\nHL6t26BA/fMdsBKpK+8w\n=LyHP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T08:57:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/98563d80e1c8b6b1348fed5320e9ce26c5cc5b44","node_id":"C_kwDOSVv36NoAKDk4NTYzZDgwZTFjOGI2YjEzNDhmZWQ1MzIwZTljZTI2YzVjYzViNDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/223e4095ca6b432f36c0ca39682c755297df0f5d","sha":"223e4095ca6b432f36c0ca39682c755297df0f5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/223e4095ca6b432f36c0ca39682c755297df0f5d"}],"sha":"98563d80e1c8b6b1348fed5320e9ce26c5cc5b44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/98563d80e1c8b6b1348fed5320e9ce26c5cc5b44"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/281068747?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs","id":281068747,"login":"wakir-labs","node_id":"U_kgDOEMDEyw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/223e4095ca6b432f36c0ca39682c755297df0f5d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T08:50:25Z","email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T08:50:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Measure the seven days, and make the control that proves the measurement work (#562)\n\n* Measure the seven days, and make the control that proves the measurement work\n\nADR-0076 gives the substrate seven days to show that it attests rather\nthan that it is up. Smoke 6/6 on 2026-05-15 was correct and worthless:\nat the moment of a single measurement a working substrate and a freshly\nfilled cache are identical. The difference is only in movement, and\nmovement is only visible in a series.\n\nThis is the harness for that window: an hourly sampler on the node and a\njudge off it.\n\nThe split is forced. Both live VMs run Fedora CoreOS with no python3, so\nanything on the node is bash over openssl. And a per-run verdict would\nhave to answer from one sample a question only the series can answer --\nwhich is how the May evidence was produced.\n\nTwo rules run through it.\n\nNot-evidence is not green. Every judgement has three outcomes, never\ntwo. require_measured() is the single line where a missing value becomes\nUNKNOWN; a violations.append is where a present and wrong value becomes\nFAIL. A window with a hole in it exits 2 and may not be quoted.\n\nThe verdict is computed, never read. The sample record carries\nmeasurements and no opinion, and the judge refuses a record that grows a\nverdict-shaped field. That defect was found twice in this repository on\n2026-09-22 in two different shapes; this is the structural answer rather\nthan a third comment about it.\n\nA fourth assurance beyond the decision paper''s three, and the reason is\nthe negative control the decision makes mandatory. Z1, Z2 and Z3 cannot\nsee an emptied bundles volume: a running agent keeps renewing from its\nown cache, so deleting the staged anchor changes nothing it does. That\nis not hypothetical, it is the state both nodes were in from May. Z4\nwatches the staged anchor -- presence, overlap with the authorities the\nserver actually holds, and the freshness of the re-staging timer the ADR\nnames as the next silent obligation. Without it the mandated control\nwould come out green and take the meaning of every green window with it.\nTV-ACC-P-51 runs the whole thing end to end and asserts the asymmetry:\nred on the anchor, green on everything else.\n\nWhat F1 counts needed a reading. Under UpstreamAuthority the root stands\nstill for years by design and the signing intermediate turns over once\nper ca_ttl, so a rotation counter fed from the bundle set would read\nzero for the entire window and the falsification would be unreachable.\nThe counter is the authority that signed the leaf; the bundle-set\ncounter is reported next to it and not gated on. The test plan flags\nthis as a reading of the decision, not a quotation of it.\n\nThe cold-agent probe is excluded from the standing assurances and judged\nseparately. Folding a deliberate outage into Z1..Z4 would mean the\nwindow can only pass if the falsification the board insisted on is\nskipped.\n\nThe staged anchor is a contract with the bootstrap''s staging step, read\nhere and owned there. Nothing under infra/spire/ is touched, and a test\nasserts it. One assumption in that contract can produce a false red and\nis written down rather than worked around: if the re-staging step skips\nthe rename when the bundle has not changed, the anchor''s mtime stands\nstill on a healthy substrate.\n\nBuilt and hermetically proven. Not armed: the window starts after the\nbilateral cutover, which is operator hand.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* The control has to outlast the thing that undoes it, and the window has to be checked before it starts\n\nThree findings from the DevOps and identity-substrate cross-reviews, all\nof them in my hand.\n\n1. The mandatory negative control could not run against the re-staging\ntimer. The timer restores the staged anchor every 30 minutes; the probe\nsamples hourly. An operator following the old procedure removed the\nanchor and got it back before a single sample could see it gone. The\nmarked slice then held no absent anchor, the anchor assurance over it\nread PASS, and the judge failed the entire window on day seven with\n\"the negative control did not go red\".\n\nThat sentence was wrong twice. Nobody had performed the control, and\nthe finding was about the procedure rather than the instrument. The\njudge now separates three cases: never saw the anchor missing, saw it\nmissing fewer times than the procedure asks for, and saw it missing and\nthe assurance still did not fail. The first two are UNKNOWN and name the\ntimer; only the third is a FAIL, and it is the assertion the whole\nmechanism rests on. Keeping \"not measured\" apart from \"measured and bad\"\nis the rule this harness runs on, and it did not hold for the control\nitself.\n\nThe procedure stops the timer first and restarts it with an explicit\nre-stage afterwards, and the control now has an acceptance criterion\nthat is checked minutes later instead of on day seven:\nsamples_with_anchor_absent >= 2, read from the same report.\n\n2. The window had preconditions nobody had written down, two of them\nfalse on a freshly bootstrapped node. WAKIR_PILOT_MODE defaults to\nsingle-org, where the anchor is never staged and Z4 is correctly red for\nall 168 samples for a reason that has nothing to do with trust. And\nspire-agent api fetch x509 returns workload SVIDs, so it needs a\nregistration entry matching the calling context -- the bootstrap creates\nnone, and the only documented recipe names a parent id for an attestor\nthat is not configured. Without it a real agent answers PermissionDenied\nand Z1, Z2 and F1 are red for a week out of \"nobody is registered\".\n\nSection 6 gets a step 0 with an acceptance criterion: the exact entry to\ncreate, the mode to check, the timer to enable, and a dry run that must\nexit 0 with all four sources ok before the window may open. The probe\nnow classifies a refusal as a refusal instead of folding it into \"the\nAPI did not answer\" -- same verdict, a sentence the operator can act on,\nand a matched-then-dropped stderr so no SPIFFE ID reaches the record.\n\n3. Both authority sets are X.509 sets by construction. A bundle holding\none jwt-svid key and no X.509 authority is well-formed, is genuine\nserver-issued key material, and puts a real agent into a retry loop with\n\"no certificates found in trust bundle\" -- while sharing its JWT key with\nthe server''s key set. The overlap was already computed from x5c, so it\nwas right, but by inference rather than by assertion: any x5c was taken,\nwherever it sat. It is now taken only from entries that declare\nuse=x509-svid, the JWT key ids take part in no comparison, and a vector\nholds the line. The same gap at the writing end is being closed in\nparallel; it is worth having at both ends, because \"what to write\" and\n\"is what is there an anchor\" are two questions about one file.\n\nTwo mutations run against the new guards: dropping the absent-sample\nrequirement kills the two control vectors, dropping the use scoping\nkills the smuggled-x5c vector.\n\nNot taken on here, per instruction: the four post-merge obligations,\nincluding the Persistent= comment in my own timer.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Withdraw an assurance my own timer could not keep, and make the withdrawal run\n\nThe acceptance probe timer carried Persistent=true with a comment saying\nit caught up the sample missed over a reboot inside the window. It does\nnot. man systemd.timer, verified against systemd 258 on 2026-09-23:\n\"Note that this setting only has an effect on timers configured with\nOnCalendar=\".\n\nThe behaviour was never wrong -- OnBootSec=3min was doing that work. The\nassurance was, and a false assurance in a comment about an instrument is\nthe miniature of the defect this whole acceptance window exists to\nanswer: a trust-bundle path that sat documented, correct and written by\nnobody for 127 days.\n\nThe setting is removed rather than paired with an OnCalendar=. Even\nworking, a catch-up run would only add a sample stamped now -- which is\nexactly what OnBootSec= already produces -- and it would not fill the\ngap in the series. The gap is not hidden either way: the judge reports a\nstretch without samples as an unexplained coverage gap and the window\ncomes out UNKNOWN, which is the correct answer about an hour nobody\nwatched and better than a setting that looks like it prevented one.\n\nFound in cross-review rather than by anything that runs, which is why it\nis now something that runs: TV-ACC-P-80 rejects Persistent= without\nOnCalendar= in the two unit files this change owns, TV-ACC-P-81 keeps\nthe directive that does the work from being removed with the one that\ndid not, and TV-ACC-P-82 is the guard''s own negative control -- a check\nover unit files is the kind that passes because its parser found\nnothing, so the parser is driven against the shape it must reject, the\ntwo it must accept, and the trap of the same word appearing in a\ncomment. Which it now does, in this very file, explaining why the\nsetting is gone.\n\nScoped to the two units this module owns. The same rule holds for the\nre-staging timer beside them and is being applied there by its owner;\nasserting it across a directory this module does not own would be a lint\nwearing a test''s clothes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Re-derive the lane counts after the rebase instead of adding them up\n\nTwo waves landed in the same three files. The counts here come from\ntooling/ci/lane_inventory.py --sync against the rebased tree (430 modules,\n327 required), not from 428+2: two numbers that happen to add up are not a\nmeasurement.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Fred <fabian@callandor.gmbh>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"67bb1c33c17c43bdde1df09ac5898c7d4009a6e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/trees/67bb1c33c17c43bdde1df09ac5898c7d4009a6e4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/commits/223e4095ca6b432f36c0ca39682c755297df0f5d","verification":{"payload":"tree 67bb1c33c17c43bdde1df09ac5898c7d4009a6e4\nparent 396f4bf76f1bfaa2898485bfd5faf6d9a7b6c8f9\nauthor wakir-labs <xypu4r8e@addy.io> 1790153425 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790153425 +0200\n\nMeasure the seven days, and make the control that proves the measurement work (#562)\n\n* Measure the seven days, and make the control that proves the measurement work\n\nADR-0076 gives the substrate seven days to show that it attests rather\nthan that it is up. Smoke 6/6 on 2026-05-15 was correct and worthless:\nat the moment of a single measurement a working substrate and a freshly\nfilled cache are identical. The difference is only in movement, and\nmovement is only visible in a series.\n\nThis is the harness for that window: an hourly sampler on the node and a\njudge off it.\n\nThe split is forced. Both live VMs run Fedora CoreOS with no python3, so\nanything on the node is bash over openssl. And a per-run verdict would\nhave to answer from one sample a question only the series can answer --\nwhich is how the May evidence was produced.\n\nTwo rules run through it.\n\nNot-evidence is not green. Every judgement has three outcomes, never\ntwo. require_measured() is the single line where a missing value becomes\nUNKNOWN; a violations.append is where a present and wrong value becomes\nFAIL. A window with a hole in it exits 2 and may not be quoted.\n\nThe verdict is computed, never read. The sample record carries\nmeasurements and no opinion, and the judge refuses a record that grows a\nverdict-shaped field. That defect was found twice in this repository on\n2026-09-22 in two different shapes; this is the structural answer rather\nthan a third comment about it.\n\nA fourth assurance beyond the decision paper''s three, and the reason is\nthe negative control the decision makes mandatory. Z1, Z2 and Z3 cannot\nsee an emptied bundles volume: a running agent keeps renewing from its\nown cache, so deleting the staged anchor changes nothing it does. That\nis not hypothetical, it is the state both nodes were in from May. Z4\nwatches the staged anchor -- presence, overlap with the authorities the\nserver actually holds, and the freshness of the re-staging timer the ADR\nnames as the next silent obligation. Without it the mandated control\nwould come out green and take the meaning of every green window with it.\nTV-ACC-P-51 runs the whole thing end to end and asserts the asymmetry:\nred on the anchor, green on everything else.\n\nWhat F1 counts needed a reading. Under UpstreamAuthority the root stands\nstill for years by design and the signing intermediate turns over once\nper ca_ttl, so a rotation counter fed from the bundle set would read\nzero for the entire window and the falsification would be unreachable.\nThe counter is the authority that signed the leaf; the bundle-set\ncounter is reported next to it and not gated on. The test plan flags\nthis as a reading of the decision, not a quotation of it.\n\nThe cold-agent probe is excluded from the standing assurances and judged\nseparately. Folding a deliberate outage into Z1..Z4 would mean the\nwindow can only pass if the falsification the board insisted on is\nskipped.\n\nThe staged anchor is a contract with the bootstrap''s staging step, read\nhere and owned there. Nothing under infra/spire/ is touched, and a test\nasserts it. One assumption in that contract can produce a false red and\nis written down rather than worked around: if the re-staging step skips\nthe rename when the bundle has not changed, the anchor''s mtime stands\nstill on a healthy substrate.\n\nBuilt and hermetically proven. Not armed: the window starts after the\nbilateral cutover, which is operator hand.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* The control has to outlast the thing that undoes it, and the window has to be checked before it starts\n\nThree findings from the DevOps and identity-substrate cross-reviews, all\nof them in my hand.\n\n1. The mandatory negative control could not run against the re-staging\ntimer. The timer restores the staged anchor every 30 minutes; the probe\nsamples hourly. An operator following the old procedure removed the\nanchor and got it back before a single sample could see it gone. The\nmarked slice then held no absent anchor, the anchor assurance over it\nread PASS, and the judge failed the entire window on day seven with\n\"the negative control did not go red\".\n\nThat sentence was wrong twice. Nobody had performed the control, and\nthe finding was about the procedure rather than the instrument. The\njudge now separates three cases: never saw the anchor missing, saw it\nmissing fewer times than the procedure asks for, and saw it missing and\nthe assurance still did not fail. The first two are UNKNOWN and name the\ntimer; only the third is a FAIL, and it is the assertion the whole\nmechanism rests on. Keeping \"not measured\" apart from \"measured and bad\"\nis the rule this harness runs on, and it did not hold for the control\nitself.\n\nThe procedure stops the timer first and restarts it with an explicit\nre-stage afterwards, and the control now has an acceptance criterion\nthat is checked minutes later instead of on day seven:\nsamples_with_anchor_absent >= 2, read from the same report.\n\n2. The window had preconditions nobody had written down, two of them\nfalse on a freshly bootstrapped node. WAKIR_PILOT_MODE defaults to\nsingle-org, where the anchor is never staged and Z4 is correctly red for\nall 168 samples for a reason that has nothing to do with trust. And\nspire-agent api fetch x509 returns workload SVIDs, so it needs a\nregistration entry matching the calling context -- the bootstrap creates\nnone, and the only documented recipe names a parent id for an attestor\nthat is not configured. Without it a real agent answers PermissionDenied\nand Z1, Z2 and F1 are red for a week out of \"nobody is registered\".\n\nSection 6 gets a step 0 with an acceptance criterion: the exact entry to\ncreate, the mode to check, the timer to enable, and a dry run that must\nexit 0 with all four sources ok before the window may open. The probe\nnow classifies a refusal as a refusal instead of folding it into \"the\nAPI did not answer\" -- same verdict, a sentence the operator can act on,\nand a matched-then-dropped stderr so no SPIFFE ID reaches the record.\n\n3. Both authority sets are X.509 sets by construction. A bundle holding\none jwt-svid key and no X.509 authority is well-formed, is genuine\nserver-issued key material, and puts a real agent into a retry loop with\n\"no certificates found in trust bundle\" -- while sharing its JWT key with\nthe server''s key set. The overlap was already computed from x5c, so it\nwas right, but by inference rather than by assertion: any x5c was taken,\nwherever it sat. It is now taken only from entries that declare\nuse=x509-svid, the JWT key ids take part in no comparison, and a vector\nholds the line. The same gap at the writing end is being closed in\nparallel; it is worth having at both ends, because \"what to write\" and\n\"is what is there an anchor\" are two questions about one file.\n\nTwo mutations run against the new guards: dropping the absent-sample\nrequirement kills the two control vectors, dropping the use scoping\nkills the smuggled-x5c vector.\n\nNot taken on here, per instruction: the four post-merge obligations,\nincluding the Persistent= comment in my own timer.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Withdraw an assurance my own timer could not keep, and make the withdrawal run\n\nThe acceptance probe timer carried Persistent=true with a comment saying\nit caught up the sample missed over a reboot inside the window. It does\nnot. man systemd.timer, verified against systemd 258 on 2026-09-23:\n\"Note that this setting only has an effect on timers configured with\nOnCalendar=\".\n\nThe behaviour was never wrong -- OnBootSec=3min was doing that work. The\nassurance was, and a false assurance in a comment about an instrument is\nthe miniature of the defect this whole acceptance window exists to\nanswer: a trust-bundle path that sat documented, correct and written by\nnobody for 127 days.\n\nThe setting is removed rather than paired with an OnCalendar=. Even\nworking, a catch-up run would only add a sample stamped now -- which is\nexactly what OnBootSec= already produces -- and it would not fill the\ngap in the series. The gap is not hidden either way: the judge reports a\nstretch without samples as an unexplained coverage gap and the window\ncomes out UNKNOWN, which is the correct answer about an hour nobody\nwatched and better than a setting that looks like it prevented one.\n\nFound in cross-review rather than by anything that runs, which is why it\nis now something that runs: TV-ACC-P-80 rejects Persistent= without\nOnCalendar= in the two unit files this change owns, TV-ACC-P-81 keeps\nthe directive that does the work from being removed with the one that\ndid not, and TV-ACC-P-82 is the guard''s own negative control -- a check\nover unit files is the kind that passes because its parser found\nnothing, so the parser is driven against the shape it must reject, the\ntwo it must accept, and the trap of the same word appearing in a\ncomment. Which it now does, in this very file, explaining why the\nsetting is gone.\n\nScoped to the two units this module owns. The same rule holds for the\nre-staging timer beside them and is being applied there by its owner;\nasserting it across a directory this module does not own would be a lint\nwearing a test''s clothes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Re-derive the lane counts after the rebase instead of adding them up\n\nTwo waves landed in the same three files. The counts here come from\ntooling/ci/lane_inventory.py --sync against the rebased tree (430 modules,\n327 required), not from 428+2: two numbers that happen to add up are not a\nmeasurement.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Fred <fabian@callandor.gmbh>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs5LRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJ4sQAAcrZB9tWq5TlUBvjI8doA/c\n2Pw9zZe0xfWwk/6VxFjP4N4zeHXHX+G8aJf6Tm0XRJK2wSG7pK2aHiA5dYVLm6x9\n7owL4rqyJ+s/w6op+f3O4+URaxDyyK5wjIw1dtOz2MZk74ZBqjDBb8L7mWIvdohn\niJKU0U0rCc5g5y27aqae6HI3Xw1WtKmzQnNpXf56pBKUCtrJ1mXIXCAX5b921e6j\n6IKQlvZgM3CPnaW5hYQ+z75eAAhg19KIVv7YVvOMgUCVc7IYmtWHdvAKgWypMwQY\nTV/c7BxbOhW1T0y1BgK2WUFJH7Iem/29YLcPqNUHoA/p2Zv+O+mXEKltaaOrtYqf\nUkXwqaKOd2JIl3TkJUhlFK36MeV+/Wj0CxN7v8GF9q0clT0+Qh