`tests/ci/`, which `lane-ci-meta`\nruns wholesale, and that job is in the acceptance-gate aggregator''s\n`needs:` and `GATE_RESULTS` -- so it inherits a required context\ninstead of adding one. A new context would need a branch-protection\nchange and an exact display name, which is the PR #102\nforever-pending class. The CLI also runs as its own step so the first\nthing an engineer reads is the per-site guidance, not an assertion\ndiff.\n\nThe tests are built around negative controls, because a clean tree is\ngreen under a working scanner and under a broken one alike: an\ninjected address must go red, each enforced block is exercised\nseparately, addresses outside the set (including the RFC 5737 ranges\nused as replacements) must not fire, and an allow-listed address is\ngreen with a live date and red with an expired one. Both halves were\nmutation-checked -- disabling the scanner fails five tests, and making\nexpired entries keep applying fails exactly the one that names it.\n\nWhat it does not catch is written down in the module docstring rather\nthan left to be discovered: the history, non-RFC1918 private space\n(CGNAT, link-local, IPv6 ULA), public addresses, hostnames and\nusernames, non-literal forms, and untracked files. Gap 4 is populated\ntoday -- 32 occurrences of an operator home-directory path across 19\nfiles, including functional quadlet mounts -- and is left for a change\nthat owns the behaviour, not bundled in here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mira Kessler <mira@wakir.local>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsmEXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfwUQAEXrIyHbTghJIqaAGq443xc/\nNae3KHjm9lPgvC9kHku8MHtVV+mPiWhAsnL097L1QtkdPUQR27gnttNxBuJrJR/0\n57IDZqpzbMRhbnilPUPj8ncTfSCrful5D1d5FZ1FgGXLPe7sqNA/ZWTSHtKmNh+T\nD5EtZ/Hy3Jk7/JRWPzEkbdpjUTKvAQf6EycgQo8fJtN+9JFzMv9kOiGtWDPl7Zy3\npQ5Ty1xG08m5Jt