l":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/9bb5ab1f58d48850ca67db78ed7f5dc5b20a3daf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T16:26:51Z","email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T16:26:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(archive): prune 29 dead artefacts from the public tree (ADR-0072 4d) (#536)\n\nThe Phase-4 sweep archived dead migration tooling, dashboards, tests and\nfixtures instead of deleting them, because the sweep agents cannot remove\nfiles. This completes that step: 29 artefacts with no remaining reference\nare dropped from the tree and stay reachable from the tag\narchive/pre-phase-4.\n\nFour archived dashboards and one SLI/SLO catalogue are kept because live\nalert rules and docs/observability/aggregator-monitoring.md still name\nthem; removing those needs the references updated first.\n\nEvidence and reports are untouched: they carry the audit trail, including\nthe OpenTimestamps attestation of the Phase-3 completion marker.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"427f97c0e4fde4109f58edfaaf7a0300ec6f2b8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/trees/427f97c0e4fde4109f58edfaaf7a0300ec6f2b8b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/commits/9bb5ab1f58d48850ca67db78ed7f5dc5b20a3daf","verification":{"payload":"tree 427f97c0e4fde4109f58edfaaf7a0300ec6f2b8b\nparent 615f8ef64fb4cc2147f996e1afe60d15572c4f34\nauthor wakir-labs <xypu4r8e@addy.io> 1789403211 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789403211 +0200\n\nchore(archive): prune 29 dead artefacts from the public tree (ADR-0072 4d) (#536)\n\nThe Phase-4 sweep archived dead migration tooling, dashboards, tests and\nfixtures instead of deleting them, because the sweep agents cannot remove\nfiles. This completes that step: 29 artefacts with no remaining reference\nare dropped from the tree and stay reachable from the tag\narchive/pre-phase-4.\n\nFour archived dashboards and one SLI/SLO catalogue are kept because live\nalert rules and docs/observability/aggregator-monitoring.md still name\nthem; removing those needs the references updated first.\n\nEvidence and reports are untouched: they carry the audit trail, including\nthe OpenTimestamps attestation of the Phase-3 completion marker.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqCBLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJCMQADZUwF7Nc/pIsUuCs1pKBp8R\nT6kXO86I3pE276cPV6tBHMRuisTha6A1i1FLqF/bj9uLZwdWlWwqg/CKM1+r5qk0\n950vcrkauX516WGeME0x6RTi/Qa+AKddqyQAFwVW9wBBCH2by7UXi6+niyVf+5kg\nTy64COfwdnGxCLNWv58YSDLYwN08Qt9Y+R5knEx4rfgIBzI5Qy3UD27OLxqn1XS5\nii5xP2XxQFweqe7VtkLWjHT4/oLyjRPRAr5t2bLzC44xfTtyHKVjmR/i91dRRd7v\n2zENP2h9AUubgu9WhhMZqPzM6sKAsQ1hgdo6HxBZQdeQtbWACCGq3P5DJLzl+za8\nJ0dt6fkHXeNfxdQScOshhJ4qMSItTtYkSoanbjnwoZADxAnK87wG7yyC8vumFCZT\nLdf4IIqVZzFZow8K7TFQQrPz1Qlt7Sw4pteVib6Fj1Q6qbiS56R95ruNZ/IUD0KP\nb4ZVvFZ7x5ZthnNgffnVr5uAeK9XGyrd2K6AePSVDy54L2GDLAqbM49/SDp4e9xY\nkRRNivVG8dosuQz/C44CdTny6SAyLgHySOwKFtfHAweV5buH7HbwP61c/lk1K8WA\nw13L8r8i97xeor0J6cZR3gI2TvZxP0nbzwJt3irjRlkIW0ZFO73g62SSMM5xBrCA\nVClCkQThqYV8YqYmdjbS\n=OHdC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T16:26:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/9bb5ab1f58d48850ca67db78ed7f5dc5b20a3daf","node_id":"C_kwDOSVv36NoAKDliYjVhYjFmNThkNDg4NTBjYTY3ZGI3OGVkN2Y1ZGM1YjIwYTNkYWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/615f8ef64fb4cc2147f996e1afe60d15572c4f34","sha":"615f8ef64fb4cc2147f996e1afe60d15572c4f34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/615f8ef64fb4cc2147f996e1afe60d15572c4f34"}],"sha":"9bb5ab1f58d48850ca67db78ed7f5dc5b20a3daf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/9bb5ab1f58d48850ca67db78ed7f5dc5b20a3daf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/281068747?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs","id":281068747,"login":"wakir-labs","node_id":"U_kgDOEMDEyw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/615f8ef64fb4cc2147f996e1afe60d15572c4f34/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T09:26:03Z","email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T09:26:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(phase-4): add QUICKSTART.md with measured external-reviewer path (ADR-0072 W6) (#535)\n\n* docs(phase-4): add QUICKSTART.md with measured external-reviewer path (ADR-0072 W6)\n\nThe external review asks that a non-Wakir engineer understands and runs\nthe core proof path in under ten minutes. QUICKSTART.md is that path:\nwhat the chain proves in one paragraph, exact prerequisites, three\ncommands from clone to a five-step JSON report, how to read the report\n(ok vs skipped vs failed, and why external_verify is skipped without\nthe verifier installed), and the measured timings from a bare\npython:3.13-slim container.\n\nTwo findings from that container run are written into the page rather\nthan smoothed over: python:3.13-slim ships neither git nor make, and the\nproof path needs no `pip install -e .` at all — the driver puts the repo\nroot on sys.path itself, and the Merkle root is byte-identical to a\nfully installed run. The only install the path needs is wakir-verify,\nwhich is also the only step that costs real wall-clock time.\n\nREADME links the page from the top. Forward links to STABILITY.md and\ndocs/architecture/layers.md are intentional; both land separately.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(phase-4): fill in the measured container timings (ADR-0072 W6)\n\nNumbers from the final clean run: 269.7 s from clone to a five-ok\nreport. The pip step for the verifier is the only meaningful cost and\nit varied 124-266 s across runs, so it is named as the one thing that\ncan push a reviewer towards the ten-minute mark.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"327ff664b08a01c6c5c3d12c365b8ee8a71b6468","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/trees/327ff664b08a01c6c5c3d12c365b8ee8a71b6468"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/commits/615f8ef64fb4cc2147f996e1afe60d15572c4f34","verification":{"payload":"tree 327ff664b08a01c6c5c3d12c365b8ee8a71b6468\nparent abeb49d4cb8cf420a2e8a66c734ada1b73388537\nauthor wakir-labs <xypu4r8e@addy.io> 1789377963 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789377963 +0200\n\ndocs(phase-4): add QUICKSTART.md with measured external-reviewer path (ADR-0072 W6) (#535)\n\n* docs(phase-4): add QUICKSTART.md with measured external-reviewer path (ADR-0072 W6)\n\nThe external review asks that a non-Wakir engineer understands and runs\nthe core proof path in under ten minutes. QUICKSTART.md is that path:\nwhat the chain proves in one paragraph, exact prerequisites, three\ncommands from clone to a five-step JSON report, how to read the report\n(ok vs skipped vs failed, and why external_verify is skipped without\nthe verifier installed), and the measured timings from a bare\npython:3.13-slim container.\n\nTwo findings from that container run are written into the page rather\nthan smoothed over: python:3.13-slim ships neither git nor make, and the\nproof path needs no `pip install -e .` at all — the driver puts the repo\nroot on sys.path itself, and the Merkle root is byte-identical to a\nfully installed run. The only install the path needs is wakir-verify,\nwhich is also the only step that costs real wall-clock time.\n\nREADME links the page from the top. Forward links to STABILITY.md and\ndocs/architecture/layers.md are intentional; both land separately.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(phase-4): fill in the measured container timings (ADR-0072 W6)\n\nNumbers from the final clean run: 269.7 s from clone to a five-ok\nreport. The pip step for the verifier is the only meaningful cost and\nit varied 124-266 s across runs, so it is named as the one thing that\ncan push a reviewer towards the ten-minute mark.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqp72rCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFZgQAFcLk7DtcaZWZ153P7s2DMLu\nRoWRO+csDu9a00HcqkUdjYn4LN50WG5eOdYhPmzTgUYSKA+0BU8fbwQmK2pinljZ\n/i1ZW49MkxP7Rsj6BtFyYuET1RQ+MLphxi3VV5RyqvcMQ8Bs7RE+QhFt1EYeqYTI\nLV+9ZbXj0ZrQt+CmFd7RMQT3gS7dPaBtWxxn8JKelZW5Jkyjj6xQdJ5P4d+O8qSR\njXewcSSzYhTSkMsJUBj2+YWoEg+0guCYmSMH5sWISR3f6lxbJ0U/fgn5+dpQSG7x\nESEnD6Enmt20bxpeZMy+eK64m0UYdro0CUhAjqHBlHgyhGAM3Flnca/XplJn4yqC\n8+1iVBphY2spezlBc8z3ctB79To5qskduntIQ5NrJplJgozl3wHrcjz4+wQebRqd\nm6aTv5alWzMQGV8Tl9HMJqaQdAwCaeOK0Ea5HtfkMa6CdAxpYRMQcS57vAS++8BO\naj5+7G9Ubaq0Z8iblHv1rLkcJK0TnUyJwvpGeTzBUOlDivnW6rji6DDgZWEe87r/\n6ZIJBHrac2PtzByCKfA+1s9W/o+e0pz1YjZlrsfLw9sbIxuj6mgt7jiiO8+BJdYU\nzI7D1B+1Rp4jxFjRDJ68qc4W/h8zM5ldeUx6V0AimBDOJIB5ixp6LfEFicA/5NGG\nx1SDjGDxWnUyuAGZReyk\n=S7N6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T09:26:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/615f8ef64fb4cc2147f996e1afe60d15572c4f34","node_id":"C_kwDOSVv36NoAKDYxNWY4ZWY2NGZiNGNjMjE0N2Y5OTZlMWFmZTYwZDE1NTcyYzRmMzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/abeb49d4cb8cf420a2e8a66c734ada1b73388537","sha":"abeb49d4cb8cf420a2e8a66c734ada1b73388537","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/abeb49d4cb8cf420a2e8a66c734ada1b73388537"}],"sha":"615f8ef64fb4cc2147f996e1afe60d15572c4f34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/615f8ef64fb4cc2147f996e1afe60d15572c4f34"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/281068747?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs","id":281068747,"login":"wakir-labs","node_id":"U_kgDOEMDEyw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/abeb49d4cb8cf420a2e8a66c734ada1b73388537/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T09:08:26Z","email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T09:08:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(phase-4): add STABILITY.md and architecture layer map (ADR-0072 W6) (#534)\n\n* docs(phase-4): add STABILITY.md with per-component maturity (ADR-0072 W6)\n\nA reader coming from outside needs to know which parts of this\nrepository they can lean on. This adds that as one table: every\ncomponent gets a status from the vocabulary the external review\nproposed (stable-ish / beta / experimental / internal / deprecated /\nplanned) and a note naming the gate, fixture cohort or artefact that\nbacks it.\n\nTwo rules keep the file from drifting into marketing: a `stable-ish`\nrow must name the gate that would fail on a silent change, and a row\nclaiming live evidence must name the artefact. Where the review''s\nexample values no longer match the tree the file deviates and says\nwhy — the bridge audit writer is now covered by the proof-path gate,\nand the persona engine row hid a real split between its hash-pinned\ndeterministic core and its untested routing layer.\n\nDocumentation only. No behaviour change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(phase-4): add architecture layer map with the proof path drawn through it (ADR-0072 W6)\n\nFive layers, one question each, mapped onto the real modules of this\nrepository with the boundary upward and downward spelled out. Then\nthe part that actually earns its keep: the proof path from protocol\nevent to machine-readable report as a single line, with the file that\nimplements each step and the gate that fails if it breaks.\n\nLayer 5 is marked explicitly as not on the proof path, with the\nmisreading it prevents named. You can verify a Wakir audit trail with\nno SPIRE, no NATS, no containers and no Rust binaries running, and\nthat independence is the point of the construction rather than an\naccident of packaging.\n\nTwo caveats are in the document rather than in a commit message\nnobody reads: a skipped external verification can never pass the\ngate, and Bitcoin time-binding sits one step beyond the gated line\nbecause production anchoring still waits on an operator activation.\n\nDocumentation only. No behaviour change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7e7998bbb9e2caafb838473bba2dbc824a30b77f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/trees/7e7998bbb9e2caafb838473bba2dbc824a30b77f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/commits/abeb49d4cb8cf420a2e8a66c734ada1b73388537","verification":{"payload":"tree 7e7998bbb9e2caafb838473bba2dbc824a30b77f\nparent c26fd2548fe18d859ec8cf7b3d8fa83adce6cbe4\nauthor wakir-labs <xypu4r8e@addy.io> 1789376906 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789376906 +0200\n\ndocs(phase-4): add STABILITY.md and architecture layer map (ADR-0072 W6) (#534)\n\n* docs(phase-4): add STABILITY.md with per-component maturity (ADR-0072 W6)\n\nA reader coming from outside needs to know which parts of this\nrepository they can lean on. This adds that as one table: every\ncomponent gets a status from the vocabulary the external review\nproposed (stable-ish / beta / experimental / internal / deprecated /\nplanned) and a note naming the gate, fixture cohort or artefact that\nbacks it.\n\nTwo rules keep the file from drifting into marketing: a `stable-ish`\nrow must name the gate that would fail on a silent change, and a row\nclaiming live evidence must name the artefact. Where the review''s\nexample values no longer match the tree the file deviates and says\nwhy — the bridge audit writer is now covered by the proof-path gate,\nand the persona engine row hid a real split between its hash-pinned\ndeterministic core and its untested routing layer.\n\nDocumentation only. No behaviour change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(phase-4): add architecture layer map with the proof path drawn through it (ADR-0072 W6)\n\nFive layers, one question each, mapped onto the real modules of this\nrepository with the boundary upward and downward spelled out. Then\nthe part that actually earns its keep: the proof path from protocol\nevent to machine-readable report as a single line, with the file that\nimplements each step and the gate that fails if it breaks.\n\nLayer 5 is marked explicitly as not on the proof path, with the\nmisreading it prevents named. You can verify a Wakir audit trail with\nno SPIRE, no NATS, no containers and no Rust binaries running, and\nthat independence is the point of the construction rather than an\naccident of packaging.\n\nTwo caveats are in the document rather than in a commit message\nnobody reads: a skipped external verification can never pass the\ngate, and Bitcoin time-binding sits one step beyond the gated line\nbecause production anchoring still waits on an operator activation.\n\nDocumentation only. No behaviour change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqp7mKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPGQQACiMr31U80a7Uc5xO01N7p20\nb2BBNwspD5c+cAol88VpKgSLexR+yIgRGL6glI1h2JPPz2osFkz7ZieJQ65cOLD8\nZUlhZ/y+Be1F83JSRWadUwLyh5TSHYjqY6pDGrpuEFq2iwQb5vCDfiO6nNNGAg3C\nidaCr9YQQpsEEpCoLluhromhVxkHZIkgiW9+ka4imw5ID0QuZus7Ks/KiXk3Zp0v\nGqbdowC9lwPcLEiG4M274raOdO4olt7hxQWoGx5seRpgtOgBb33FMIgtReib3mII\nDHnr2oHx886Sl4IhBX4M4eW+kpUHaE9/QbNl/fPr6i+paWWnczR1XxQkAk0D7C0d\nFNNRjTXWBoO7V54PIyZ8yv/LB2JSQP9PvS4TXGTbICS73zP+3lKUl5P+1791Hi+9\nuDBaAna6RTZQKHYaXkQXQ6SiL2nF6K02whh6E3jTjBeVtb0e54eqGScI6D0wg8L6\nkeSggPwmqGi+J5d6FUXElfe9/ns/N2F8Ue96dV4VQTTGaHkumXQP40qdCdpHcfHX\nmbivYaaB06csFj4ARIHHKiLsx7/WS824LUE2P10oNSHLexTAtoBSdudd0Cq4tFvw\nRwNn4Uxp+zfoDe2C0LuV8ahSPq6KyyA9SLx19kT1EVd5T527gvwiOYex36D3lJaE\nLTjd535j05przO8pxLCM\n=uFf1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T09:08:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/abeb49d4cb8cf420a2e8a66c734ada1b73388537","node_id":"C_kwDOSVv36NoAKGFiZWI0OWQ0Y2I4Y2Y0MjBhMmU4YTY2YzczNGFkYTFiNzMzODg1Mzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/c26fd2548fe18d859ec8cf7b3d8fa83adce6cbe4","sha":"c26fd2548fe18d859ec8cf7b3d8fa83adce6cbe4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/c26fd2548fe18d859ec8cf7b3d8fa83adce6cbe4"}],"sha":"abeb49d4cb8cf420a2e8a66c734ada1b73388537","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/abeb49d4cb8cf420a2e8a66c734ada1b73388537"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/281068747?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs","id":281068747,"login":"wakir-labs","node_id":"U_kgDOEMDEyw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/c26fd2548fe18d859ec8cf7b3d8fa83adce6cbe4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T23:26:29Z","email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T23:26:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from test suites + add archaeology-lint gate (ADR-0072 W5/Amara) (#533)\n\n* chore(phase-4): rename test files and fixtures away from sprint archaeology\n\nRenames 67 test modules and one fixture directory whose names encoded\ndevelopment-day, sprint or wave counters (`*_tagNN.py`, `test_welle_N_*`,\n`*-tag64/`) to names that describe the substance under test. All inbound\nreferences are pulled along: 8 CI workflows, 5 persona-engine scripts,\ntooling allowlists and stubs, 12 docs and the cross-referencing tests.\n\nJob display names in every workflow are byte-identical; only `run:` paths\nand one step-name comment changed, so the 13 required contexts are\nunaffected.\n\nADR-0072 Sub-Item 4d-2 (W5/Amara), tranche 1 of 5.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): scrub development archaeology from tests/ prose\n\nRewrites comments and module/class/function docstrings across 228 test\nmodules: day- and sprint-counters dropped, migration waves renamed to\n`wave N`, persona names replaced by the owning zone or role, working-mode\nvocabulary (\"Continuous-Mode-Marathon\", \"AR-Hand\", \"Auftrag-Anker\")\nreplaced by plain English.\n\nThe rewrite is tokenizer-driven and only touches COMMENT tokens and\nstandalone string expressions; assertion literals, identifiers and data\nare untouched by construction, and double-backtick code spans are masked\nso pinned names stay byte-identical. `tests/` drops from 240 files /\n~2800 hit lines to 115 files / 711 hit lines; what remains is literal\ndata pinned against documents outside this zone.\n\nADR-0072 Sub-Item 4d-2 (W5/Amara), tranche 2 of 5.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): scrub development archaeology from wirelang/tests/ prose\n\nSame tokenizer-driven rewrite as tranche 2, applied to 157 modules under\n`wirelang/tests/`, plus doctest protection: lines starting with `>>>` or\n`...` are passed through untouched after the first pass mangled three\ndoctest blocks.\n\n`wirelang/tests/` drops from 155 files to 55; the remainder is literal\ndata pinned against manifests, specs and fixtures outside this zone.\n\nADR-0072 Sub-Item 4d-2 (W5/Amara), tranche 3 of 5.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(tests): unblock tests/audit and drop two transient-state pins\n\nItem A — broken import on main. `tests/audit/test_trajectory_resync_tag61.py`\nloaded `tooling/ci/audit_cross_repo_drift_allowlist.py`, removed with the\ndead Phase-3c tooling in PR #526. The resulting collection error took out\nthe whole `tests/audit/` directory, and no required workflow covers it, so\nit went unnoticed across four sweeps.\n\nDecision: archive, not repair. Two thirds of the suite pinned a one-off\nre-sync *score* (\"92 / ENFORCE-READY\", \"76 / ENFORCE-CAUTION\") for a\nmigration that finished on 2026-05-20 — a transient state, and there is no\ncompat tooling to re-point it at. The invariants underneath it are real and\nsurvive the helper, so they are carried forward helper-free in\n`tests/audit/test_protocol_mirror_seed_integrity.py` (22 tests): seed-file\npresence, JSON validity with a Wirelang `$id`, Apache-2.0 SPDX posture,\nbyte-equality against `wirelang/schemas/`, README inventory, and a new\ncheck that the seed directory holds no un-mirrored extra file.\n\nTwo further tests pinned transient state rather than an invariant and went\nred when the surrounding prose was scrubbed:\n\n  * `test_T15_source_of_truth_mentions_tag_64_coverage` asserted a\n    development-day label in the v0.4.4 draft. It now asserts that §1\n    declares the source-of-truth direction and the sample-block coverage\n    extension — the statements a reader needs to tell a reserve item from\n    a contract.\n  * `test_t11_manifest_carries_v042_cross_reference` asserted a\n    development-day origin in MANIFEST-0.5.1. It now asserts that the\n    cross-reference names the reconciliation suite that keeps the two\n    surfaces consistent.\n\n`pytest` collects and passes `tests/audit` for the first time since PR #526.\n\nADR-0072 Sub-Item 4d-2 (W5/Amara), tranche 4 of 5.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): retire the self-contained half of the migration-marathon bundle\n\nCross-zone recommendation from the observability sweep: the marathon\nbundle observes a migration that completed on 2026-05-20 and survives only\nbecause QA tests hold it. This change acts on the part of that\nrecommendation that can be verified as self-contained, and documents the\nrest rather than guessing at it.\n\nArchived (code + the tests that pinned it, 13 files):\n\n  * per-wave trend heatmap generator and its Prometheus emitter — their\n    dashboard and runbook were already archived, so they emitted metrics\n    nothing rendered;\n  * the cutover-day live-stream aggregator and its dashboard — the watch\n    loop that drove them is already archived;\n  * the watch-day practice run and verdict rules — the watch-day spec and\n    runbook are already archived;\n  * the marathon closeout verifier;\n  * six test modules, the only remaining consumers of the above.\n\nEach was checked for live consumers first: no workflow, Makefile target,\nactive runbook or importing module references any of them; the only\ninbound references were intra-bundle and from their own tests.\n\nNOT archived, with reason (AR-hand candidates in the PR body instead):\n\n  * `dashboards/phase-3-marathon-alerts.yaml` and\n    `phase-3-marathon-slo-burn-rate-alerts.yaml` — byte-mirrored into\n    `wirelang/specs/protocol-mirror-seed/` and pinned by a cross-repo\n    compatibility gate; removing them is an ordered two-repo operation\n    that has to start in wakir-protocol, not a single-zone edit.\n  * the final-bilanz generator, its samples and its output schema — one\n    motion across three zones, flagged as such in the docs sweep.\n  * the pre-cutover probe failure-rate tracker — still referenced from the\n    live cosign keyless drift probe.\n\nADR-0072 Sub-Item 4d-2 (W5/Amara), tranche 5 of 6.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): scrub archaeology from assertion messages and retire dead fixtures\n\nSecond scrub pass over `tests/` and `wirelang/tests/`: 131 modules whose\nassertion *messages* still carried day-counters, sprint anchors or persona\nnames. `assert cond, msg` renders `msg` only when the assertion fails and\nnever compares it, so the rewrite cannot change a test outcome — and the\nguarantee is enforced rather than asserted: each file is re-parsed after\nthe edit and its AST, with every `Assert.msg` blanked, must equal the AST\nof the original, otherwise the file is left untouched.\n\nAlso archives two orphaned fixture sets under\n`tests/observability/fixtures/`. Both were inputs to\n`tooling/ops/_bulk_activate_required_checks.py`, removed in the\ninfrastructure sweep; nothing in the tree referenced either. They are now\n`docs/archive/dead-fixtures/branch-protection-walking-skeleton-{7,8}-pool/`,\nwhich also resolves a directory collision created in tranche 1 (the two\nsets differ only by suffix, so the rename nested one inside the other).\n\nADR-0072 Sub-Item 4d-2 (W5/Amara), tranche 6 of 7.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci(phase-4): add archaeology-lint as a step on the required license gate\n\nClosing gate for ADR-0072 sub-item 4d: `tooling/ci/archaeology_lint.py`\nscans every tracked file and fails on development-day counters, sprint\nanchors, operator-hand vocabulary and internal persona names outside\n`.archaeology-allowlist.yaml`. It runs as Stage 6 of the\n`License-Hygiene Gate (ADR-0061)` job, which already reports a required\nstatus context on every pull request with no path filter — so the gate\ntakes effect without a branch-protection change.\n\nAllowlist schema. Every entry needs `path` and `reason` plus exactly one\njustification: `pinned_by`, naming the test or tool that nails the literal\nbyte-for-byte, or `deferred_to`, naming the zone that owns a surface this\nsweep could not edit. Neither, both, an empty value, an unknown field or a\nwrong version is a hard schema error — an exception that does not say why\nit exists is not an exception. The lint also fails on allowlist entries\nthat match nothing, so the file shrinks as the tree gets cleaner rather\nthan accumulating dead exceptions. 41 entries today: 32 pinned, 9\ndeferred, covering the hand-overs documented in all five W5 briefs.\n\nScope decision, recorded in the lint''s docstring. The enforced regex is\nnarrower than the sweep regex: `Welle`, `Cutover`, `KW-NN` and `Marathon`\nare not enforced. Three zone sweeps independently reported that those four\nwords live on in shipped code as metric names, alert-group names, routing\nclasses, state-file names and identifiers — enforcing them would have\nproduced roughly 180 entries whose content is \"this is a name, not a diary\nentry\", and an allowlist that long stops being read. What is enforced is\nthe vocabulary with no legitimate reason to appear in a published\nartefact.\n\n`tests/ci/test_archaeology_lint.py` (32 tests) pins the schema rules, the\nenforced and deliberately-unenforced vocabulary, the glob matching, the\nexclusions, and that the tree is clean as shipped.\n\nADR-0072 Sub-Item 4d-2 (W5/Amara), tranche 7 of 7.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): rename the last archaeology filename in the QA zone\n\n`test_marathon_closeout_routing_tag78.py` was the only test file left\ncarrying a day counter in its name. The suite stays — it pins the alert\nnames and routing classes in `dashboards/phase-3-marathon-alerts.yaml`,\nwhich is not retired in this PR — so it is renamed to what it tests.\n\nNo file under `tests/` or `wirelang/tests/` now carries a `tag`, `sprint`\nor wave counter in its name.\n\nADR-0072 Sub-Item 4d-2 (W5/Amara).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"05f908ce72c9a6af57e9bef089f2d4dca2385cff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/trees/05f908ce72c9a6af57e9bef089f2d4dca2385cff"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/commits/c26fd2548fe18d859ec8cf7b3d8fa83adce6cbe4","verification":{"payload":"tree 05f908ce72c9a6af57e9bef089f2d4dca2385cff\nparent 57c5d08751ff43053e1ce7b775c117d619eefb31\nauthor wakir-labs <xypu4r8e@addy.io> 1789341989 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789341989 +0200\n\nchore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from test suites + add archaeology-lint gate (ADR-0072 W5/Amara) (#533)\n\n* chore(phase-4): rename test files and fixtures away from sprint archaeology\n\nRenames 67 test modules and one fixture directory whose names encoded\ndevelopment-day, sprint or wave counters (`*_tagNN.py`, `test_welle_N_*`,\n`*-tag64/`) to names that describe the substance under test. All inbound\nreferences are pulled along: 8 CI workflows, 5 persona-engine scripts,\ntooling allowlists and stubs, 12 docs and the cross-referencing tests.\n\nJob display names in every workflow are byte-identical; only `run:` paths\nand one step-name comment changed, so the 13 required contexts are\nunaffected.\n\nADR-0072 Sub-Item 4d-2 (W5/Amara), tranche 1 of 5.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): scrub development archaeology from tests/ prose\n\nRewrites comments and module/class/function docstrings across 228 test\nmodules: day- and sprint-counters dropped, migration waves renamed to\n`wave N`, persona names replaced by the owning zone or role, working-mode\nvocabulary (\"Continuous-Mode-Marathon\", \"AR-Hand\", \"Auftrag-Anker\")\nreplaced by plain English.\n\nThe rewrite is tokenizer-driven and only touches COMMENT tokens and\nstandalone string expressions; assertion literals, identifiers and data\nare untouched by construction, and double-backtick code spans are masked\nso pinned names stay byte-identical. `tests/` drops from 240 files /\n~2800 hit lines to 115 files / 711 hit lines; what remains is literal\ndata pinned against documents outside this zone.\n\nADR-0072 Sub-Item 4d-2 (W5/Amara), tranche 2 of 5.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): scrub development archaeology from wirelang/tests/ prose\n\nSame tokenizer-driven rewrite as tranche 2, applied to 157 modules under\n`wirelang/tests/`, plus doctest protection: lines starting with `>>>` or\n`...` are passed through untouched after the first pass mangled three\ndoctest blocks.\n\n`wirelang/tests/` drops from 155 files to 55; the remainder is literal\ndata pinned against manifests, specs and fixtures outside this zone.\n\nADR-0072 Sub-Item 4d-2 (W5/Amara), tranche 3 of 5.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(tests): unblock tests/audit and drop two transient-state pins\n\nItem A — broken import on main. `tests/audit/test_trajectory_resync_tag61.py`\nloaded `tooling/ci/audit_cross_repo_drift_allowlist.py`, removed with the\ndead Phase-3c tooling in PR #526. The resulting collection error took out\nthe whole `tests/audit/` directory, and no required workflow covers it, so\nit went unnoticed across four sweeps.\n\nDecision: archive, not repair. Two thirds of the suite pinned a one-off\nre-sync *score* (\"92 / ENFORCE-READY\", \"76 / ENFORCE-CAUTION\") for a\nmigration that finished on 2026-05-20 — a transient state, and there is no\ncompat tooling to re-point it at. The invariants underneath it are real and\nsurvive the helper, so they are carried forward helper-free in\n`tests/audit/test_protocol_mirror_seed_integrity.py` (22 tests): seed-file\npresence, JSON validity with a Wirelang `$id`, Apache-2.0 SPDX posture,\nbyte-equality against `wirelang/schemas/`, README inventory, and a new\ncheck that the seed directory holds no un-mirrored extra file.\n\nTwo further tests pinned transient state rather than an invariant and went\nred when the surrounding prose was scrubbed:\n\n  * `test_T15_source_of_truth_mentions_tag_64_coverage` asserted a\n    development-day label in the v0.4.4 draft. It now asserts that §1\n    declares the source-of-truth direction and the sample-block coverage\n    extension — the statements a reader needs to tell a reserve item from\n    a contract.\n  * `test_t11_manifest_carries_v042_cross_reference` asserted a\n    development-day origin in MANIFEST-0.5.1. It now asserts that the\n    cross-reference names the reconciliation suite that keeps the two\n    surfaces consistent.\n\n`pytest` collects and passes `tests/audit` for the first time since PR #526.\n\nADR-0072 Sub-Item 4d-2 (W5/Amara), tranche 4 of 5.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): retire the self-contained half of the migration-marathon bundle\n\nCross-zone recommendation from the observability sweep: the marathon\nbundle observes a migration that completed on 2026-05-20 and survives only\nbecause QA tests hold it. This change acts on the part of that\nrecommendation that can be verified as self-contained, and documents the\nrest rather than guessing at it.\n\nArchived (code + the tests that pinned it, 13 files):\n\n  * per-wave trend heatmap generator and its Prometheus emitter — their\n    dashboard and runbook were already archived, so they emitted metrics\n    nothing rendered;\n  * the cutover-day live-stream aggregator and its dashboard — the watch\n    loop that drove them is already archived;\n  * the watch-day practice run and verdict rules — the watch-day spec and\n    runbook are already archived;\n  * the marathon closeout verifier;\n  * six test modules, the only remaining consumers of the above.\n\nEach was checked for live consumers first: no workflow, Makefile target,\nactive runbook or importing module references any of them; the only\ninbound references were intra-bundle and from their own tests.\n\nNOT archived, with reason (AR-hand candidates in the PR body instead):\n\n  * `dashboards/phase-3-marathon-alerts.yaml` and\n    `phase-3-marathon-slo-burn-rate-alerts.yaml` — byte-mirrored into\n    `wirelang/specs/protocol-mirror-seed/` and pinned by a cross-repo\n    compatibility gate; removing them is an ordered two-repo operation\n    that has to start in wakir-protocol, not a single-zone edit.\n  * the final-bilanz generator, its samples and its output schema — one\n    motion across three zones, flagged as such in the docs sweep.\n  * the pre-cutover probe failure-rate tracker — still referenced from the\n    live cosign keyless drift probe.\n\nADR-0072 Sub-Item 4d-2 (W5/Amara), tranche 5 of 6.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): scrub archaeology from assertion messages and retire dead fixtures\n\nSecond scrub pass over `tests/` and `wirelang/tests/`: 131 modules whose\nassertion *messages* still carried day-counters, sprint anchors or persona\nnames. `assert cond, msg` renders `msg` only when the assertion fails and\nnever compares it, so the rewrite cannot change a test outcome — and the\nguarantee is enforced rather than asserted: each file is re-parsed after\nthe edit and its AST, with every `Assert.msg` blanked, must equal the AST\nof the original, otherwise the file is left untouched.\n\nAlso archives two orphaned fixture sets under\n`tests/observability/fixtures/`. Both were inputs to\n`tooling/ops/_bulk_activate_required_checks.py`, removed in the\ninfrastructure sweep; nothing in the tree referenced either. They are now\n`docs/archive/dead-fixtures/branch-protection-walking-skeleton-{7,8}-pool/`,\nwhich also resolves a directory collision created in tranche 1 (the two\nsets differ only by suffix, so the rename nested one inside the other).\n\nADR-0072 Sub-Item 4d-2 (W5/Amara), tranche 6 of 7.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci(phase-4): add archaeology-lint as a step on the required license gate\n\nClosing gate for ADR-0072 sub-item 4d: `tooling/ci/archaeology_lint.py`\nscans every tracked file and fails on development-day counters, sprint\nanchors, operator-hand vocabulary and internal persona names outside\n`.archaeology-allowlist.yaml`. It runs as Stage 6 of the\n`License-Hygiene Gate (ADR-0061)` job, which already reports a required\nstatus context on every pull request with no path filter — so the gate\ntakes effect without a branch-protection change.\n\nAllowlist schema. Every entry needs `path` and `reason` plus exactly one\njustification: `pinned_by`, naming the test or tool that nails