t) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpzElCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqNAQABBaYMY2Xj5pycuaw+4gTb/B\nIDZApHjszPv8McAK9pcNh+mAKOYnqzDZJnYRBt9p2Fb/0PCgnHkGcLh8FqYtoqN+\n0TsGg5/rSPuMqY9VKJhbxjVT2HoM3Dye5TSDpq88Z35StM8YV4xP+DfmGEmsBzRG\nEXOmS8VTIF5uuzpKmlWI6UCFVB5K+mr1ekFU4QAXGX1XChbV3qIVg+d5fLfh1zG2\n8TAtMKnbcp1SZ/PqdvlwgWj1ak/2ECklyr1gdB5uqbtwOyCx/Km1z931zFLyaZ0J\nnCqxf+m1KGrTaHQ36L4ua0b9RY9P3pvgvW+WZfX+UZWebgLwwxvwkb8MVf6BW5yX\nronV6j6pn+TeHUS85iUqQcou+hmLOs54F9DJEEjZPwQmwk9MZ19SJQzvpbOfzR6o\neNK0dbZjQloBQ0GR+oi3gQjeuMbvA0sa/650X13hdLqOTZdKrpaKFxFEUW+1DYOH\nUwT0ytJEb6f/NmLgyrAThukWLSuReclcr5Yiuc/ojGSpawTqB0ElF/kAI5p7ztld\nAJaRfZiRiJOQff5PnYY+w80O3DMOrCt64HEkCs7cJVhg3pyO+zKyw4DJzFma20zF\ntQBwgSx2SVubaFIY2Eia8VTY19a4mdkSfaViBLFcen/rZQOziKOlDYtTbZncMDFy\nZjCLHlpqIuaNC6hVIilD\n=dL/u\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-13T23:26:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/c26fd2548fe18d859ec8cf7b3d8fa83adce6cbe4","node_id":"C_kwDOSVv36NoAKGMyNmZkMjU0OGZlMThkODU5ZWM4Y2Y3YjNkOGZhODNhZGNlNmNiZTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/57c5d08751ff43053e1ce7b775c117d619eefb31","sha":"57c5d08751ff43053e1ce7b775c117d619eefb31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/57c5d08751ff43053e1ce7b775c117d619eefb31"}],"sha":"c26fd2548fe18d859ec8cf7b3d8fa83adce6cbe4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/c26fd2548fe18d859ec8cf7b3d8fa83adce6cbe4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/281068747?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs","id":281068747,"login":"wakir-labs","node_id":"U_kgDOEMDEyw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/57c5d08751ff43053e1ce7b775c117d619eefb31/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T22:57:39Z","email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T22:57:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from persona engine and engine crates (ADR-0072 W5/Selin) (#532)\n\n* chore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from wirelang/persona (ADR-0072 W5/Selin, T1)\n\nScrub of Sprint-/Tag-/persona-name anchors in comments and docstrings of\nthe persona format package. Edits are restricted to comment tokens and\ndocstring string tokens (tokenize-driven); AST equality modulo docstrings\nis asserted per file, so runtime behaviour is unchanged.\n\nAnchor mapping instead of blind deletion:\n- \"Tag-N-Skizze §3.2\" -> \"the design sketch §3.2\"\n- \"Sprint-6 Tag-2 added X\" -> \"A later revision added X\"\n- \"Reza-Cross-Review Zone-B\" -> \"cross-review Zone-B\"\n- \"Selin-side\" -> \"engine-side\", \"Tomás-Pilot\" -> \"the pilot\"\n\nWorking-regex hits in wirelang/persona: 12 files -> 0.\npytest wirelang/tests: failure set byte-identical to baseline 133d112\n(9 pre-existing failures in test_persona_cli_help_text.py, untouched).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from persona_engine modules (ADR-0072 W5/Selin, T2a)\n\n35 modules of wirelang/persona_engine (all except engine.py,\nengine_async.py, welle_state_producer.py, which follow in T2b).\nComment and docstring tokens only, tokenize-driven, AST equality modulo\ndocstrings asserted per file.\n\nSix string literals were scrubbed by hand because they carried the\ntokens in user-visible text (CLI description, three drift-assert\nmessages, one NotImplemented message, one wrapped docstring anchor).\nNone of them is pinned by a test; pytest wirelang/persona_engine/tests\nand tests/persona_engine stay green.\n\nLiving vocabulary is deliberately kept: Welle / Cutover / KW-NN are\nADR-0065/0066 cadence terms with running code behind them\n(welle_state_producer, PRE_AUDITOR_GUARDED_WELLEN, env-var gates), not\narchaeology. Listed as allowlist candidates in the PR body.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from engine, engine_async and welle_state_producer (ADR-0072 W5/Selin, T2b)\n\nThe three remaining persona_engine modules. Same tokenize-driven method\nas T2a. Additional prose mappings for the phase-closing vocabulary:\n\"Phase-3c-Welle-Marathon\" -> \"Phase-3c wave sequence\",\n\"Phase-3-Marathon-Schluss-Acceptance\" -> \"Phase-3 closing acceptance\",\n\"Henrik-cannot-self-sign-off\" -> \"pre-auditor-cannot-self-sign-off\"\n(also in the two PreAuditorGuardError messages; no test pins them).\n\nDeliberate non-change: the V-907 hashed resolver slice of engine.py\n(29 comment lines between the first and the last resolve_*_backend\nreference) is restored byte-identically. wirelang/persona_engine/\nv907-hash-baseline.json pins that slice and its own note requires a\nZone-K cross-review with the WAT side for a refresh, which this sweep\ndoes not have. Scrubbing it turned\ntest_v907_hash_pin_build_step_tag59 red (HASH-PIN-DRIFT); per the\nsweep rule the scrub yields, not the test. Listed as allowlist\ncandidate plus Zone-K follow-up in the PR body.\n\npytest wirelang/tests/persona_engine + wirelang/persona_engine/tests:\ngreen.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from persona_engine tests, manifests and diff engine (ADR-0072 W5/Selin, T2c)\n\nCloses the Python half of the zone: the package-local test helpers\n(conftest marker text, the A8 JetStream-loss module docstring), the\nbridge-audit diff-engine header, and the two historical release\nmanifests 0.5.0-pre-cutover and 0.5.1-pre-cutover.\n\nMarkdown scrub is line-local and blockquote/table/bullet aware, so the\nmanifest tables and the hermetic manifest-integrity tests (43 of them)\nstay green. The author sign-off lines keep the role and drop the\npersonal name.\n\nMANIFEST-0.5.2-final-pre-cutover.md is deliberately untouched: its §1\nComponent-Inventory slice feeds the V-907 composite hash pinned in\nv907-hash-baseline.json, whose refresh needs a Zone-K cross-review.\n\npytest wirelang/tests/persona_engine + wirelang/persona_engine/tests:\ngreen, 0 failures.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from the bridge engine crates (ADR-0072 W5/Selin, T3)\n\npersona-engine-bridge-{audit-replay,audit-writer,diff,forward}: doc\ncomments (`//!`, `///`, `//`), Cargo.toml comment headers, the\n`description` fields and the `authors` fields (personal name plus mail\naddress -> \"Wakir Labs\", same convention as #529).\n\nRust code is untouched except for two test vectors: the slug-validator\nrejection case \"Tomas\" became \"Uppercase\" (the vector''s purpose is the\nuppercase rejection, not the name) and two assertion messages lost\ntheir Tag prefix. No fixture file under tests/fixtures is touched --\nthose bytes feed V-907 pin packs.\n\ncargo test -p for the four crates: green (CARGO_TARGET_DIR=/var/tmp).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from format, frontmatter-parser, fsm, integration-tests and loop-latency-bench (ADR-0072 W5/Selin, T4)\n\nDoc comments, Cargo.toml headers, descriptions, authors, plus the\nloop-latency-bench README. One assertion message lost its Tag prefix.\n\nTwo deliberate non-changes:\n- tests/fixtures/claude-agents/*.md and tests/fixtures/v907_pin_pack/*.md\n  stay byte-identical. They are persona-definition test vectors whose\n  bytes are hashed by the V-907 pin packs; they are also HR-governed\n  content. Allowlist candidates.\n- SYNTHESIS_DEFAULT_EXCEPTIONS in persona-engine-format keeps its\n  rationale strings. They quote persona definitions verbatim and sit\n  next to the live \"aufsichtsrat\" routing value.\n\ncargo test -p for the five crates: green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from migrate-version, recovery, recovery-replay and smoke (ADR-0072 W5/Selin, T5)\n\nDoc comments, Cargo.toml headers and the smoke README. One wrapped\n\"(Selin Sprint-Pengine-8 PR #65 ...)\" anchor in the recovery crate''s\nmodule header was rejoined by hand to \"(PR #65, ...)\".\n\ncargo test -p for the four crates: green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from state-backing, subscribe-loop and the two V-907 crates (ADR-0072 W5/Selin, T6)\n\nDoc comments, Cargo.toml headers and READMEs. Three assertion messages\nlost their Tag prefix; one slug-validator rejection vector \"Reza\"\nbecame \"Uppercase\" (the vector tests uppercase rejection).\n\ntests/fixtures/v907_pin_pack/*.md stay byte-identical -- the\nrecompute-bench hashes those bytes.\n\ncargo test -p for the four crates: green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a6c7c02240e410b002c6504d8ac7caae3e132eb6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/trees/a6c7c02240e410b002c6504d8ac7caae3e132eb6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/commits/57c5d08751ff43053e1ce7b775c117d619eefb31","verification":{"payload":"tree a6c7c02240e410b002c6504d8ac7caae3e132eb6\nparent 310cd7fda012e86c75a2e1001e49da9b51a44929\nauthor wakir-labs <xypu4r8e@addy.io> 1789340259 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789340259 +0200\n\nchore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from persona engine and engine crates (ADR-0072 W5/Selin) (#532)\n\n* chore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from wirelang/persona (ADR-0072 W5/Selin, T1)\n\nScrub of Sprint-/Tag-/persona-name anchors in comments and docstrings of\nthe persona format package. Edits are restricted to comment tokens and\ndocstring string tokens (tokenize-driven); AST equality modulo docstrings\nis asserted per file, so runtime behaviour is unchang