lopment archaeology from state-backing, subscribe-loop and the two V-907 crates (ADR-0072 W5/Selin, T6)\n\nDoc comments, Cargo.toml headers and READMEs. Three assertion messages\nlost their Tag prefix; one slug-validator rejection vector \"Reza\"\nbecame \"Uppercase\" (the vector tests uppercase rejection).\n\ntests/fixtures/v907_pin_pack/*.md stay byte-identical -- the\nrecompute-bench hashes those bytes.\n\ncargo test -p for the four crates: green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpypjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACC0QAACuNcpUWr59RzLMEva0R4y6\n6fSmpt6bF54zwLrinmNOBUETFAh21ws2HHUBBIvzoMecInpBTy/pzFsC+TIFM4Sv\ni0Td5Lc4p67J+EzOiQ5cgxMGFwESIxEQtpp50sLe2nY0wi6Kyf/Xln0y6QO76BKX\nWpeSwcrrRdm+ekTPogU6qkSniT1nXcHuAkNas0Trf8f4AprDWlZo9dooFapg4AsH\n9210WoLlSvpOzDf+P9xPq3Lgv/0QvuifdkwwcH3iacxNfTQkT+yZgSac9VfJaA7o\n3TurdegmUrdJuIAJTCKsh62jmnQOh0SPmz+cHh676MNIYk/+T9cv9BiUbFeIougf\nLKAt03t6CvCp81+k69qQIXFTDSyAcT7eT6nIyCOIK0IrGKyDF7cNw+bpegmYbo8r\nBgnytuwSpufdi4YNxCrdWAsu2cWXEV5MRTE8o69ITykGSIh+1fVn/jGbsK+IkLBX\nRQV30LNKmCwndyW0KPblhteFIVYkDksoAtq5aqffXPlV2SbdFaL90wFvqzvE0Ols\ntrIjgSqieEowic9v8idLWg99hJfRu5e9H4QV35hOp3nnJE7uK5NhK3V83gV5dp/R\nBHSscjGEQYwCG3JXy2vTxbYZ+mrKFK5cjBVjLxQWwS61+cpYIm+031USeaqCm2+g\n9+3GNoKs65Lxv0a+8dEu\n=lV/S\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-13T22:57:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/57c5d08751ff43053e1ce7b775c117d619eefb31","node_id":"C_kwDOSVv36NoAKDU3YzVkMDg3NTFmZjQzMDUzZTFjZTdiNzc1YzExN2Q2MTllZWZiMzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/310cd7fda012e86c75a2e1001e49da9b51a44929","sha":"310cd7fda012e86c75a2e1001e49da9b51a44929","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/310cd7fda012e86c75a2e1001e49da9b51a44929"}],"sha":"57c5d08751ff43053e1ce7b775c117d619eefb31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/57c5d08751ff43053e1ce7b775c117d619eefb31"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/281068747?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs","id":281068747,"login":"wakir-labs","node_id":"U_kgDOEMDEyw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/310cd7fda012e86c75a2e1001e49da9b51a44929/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T21:41:20Z","email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T21:41:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from observability surface (ADR-0072 W5/Noa) (#531)\n\n* fix(observability): make cosign G1/G2 guide tests state-agnostic\n\nT-G1G2-04 and T-G1G2-06 pinned a transient BLOCKED state rather than a\ndrift invariant, so both went red when the substrate legitimately moved\nforward:\n\n* welle5/6/7 container units received resolved image digests (#499), so\n  the guide''s inventory table looked \"spurious\" to T-04 although the\n  guide correctly documents which files participate in the G1 closeout.\n* the pinned Sigstore trust root was refreshed by operator hand on\n  2026-05-20 (real Fulcio root CA SHA-256 + Rekor shard id), so T-06''s\n  \"must still equal PENDING_OPERATOR_HAND_REFRESH\" assertion could only\n  ever hold before that refresh.\n\nBoth tests now assert the invariant that actually protects the operator:\nT-04 rejects guide entries for files that do not exist on disk (closed\nslots stay listed), T-06 rejects a half-refreshed trust root and checks\nthe documented value shape once refreshed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): retire dead migration dashboards, scrub the live ones\n\nThe Phase-3 migration finished on 2026-05-20. Five dashboards only ever\nqueried metrics that were produced during that migration and are no\nlonger emitted by anything in the tree; they are moved to\ndocs/archive/dead-dashboards/ as deletion candidates (nothing in the\nrepo references them — verified by filename grep across tests, scripts,\ntooling, docs and workflows):\n\n* cutover-day-morgen-verdict-tile.json\n* phase-3c-cross-welle-coordination.json\n* persona-engine-phase-3c-welle-status.json\n* per-welle-trend-heatmap.json\n* phase-3-marathon-slo-final.json\n\nThe four surviving dashboards keep every panel query byte-for-byte;\nonly __comment, tags and description fields were rewritten to state\nwhat the panel measures instead of which day it was built on.\n\npersona-engine-health.json is the one structural change: panels 9-11\nqueried mira_hourly_* gauges whose producer (scripts/mira-hourly-\nwatchdog.py) was deleted in #527, and panel 12 was an explicit\nduplicate of panel 3 that existed only as an at-a-glance companion to\nthat cluster. Four panels that can never render data are removed; the\nremaining eight are untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): scrub development archaeology from observability scripts\n\nComments, docstrings and user-facing strings (CLI --help text, generated\nreport headers) no longer carry sprint-day numbers, wave numbers,\ncalendar-week anchors or persona names. Where a token carried a real\nstatement, the statement stays and the anchor moves to what it actually\ndescribes (\"the default picks up the carrier-image installer\" instead of\n\"Tag-55 default ...\"); where it was pure provenance, it is gone.\n\nBehaviour is unchanged: every file was rewritten under an AST comparison\nwith string constants normalised away, so no code path, argument,\ndefault or identifier moved. pytest tests/observability is green.\n\nscripts/observability/cutover-day-watch.sh is archived rather than\nscrubbed: it drives the migration-day watch loop that ended on\n2026-05-20 and no test, workflow or script references it.\n\nThree files are deliberately untouched and carry over as allowlist\ncandidates, documented in the PR body: alert-rule-to-mira-notify-\nbridge.py (byte-mirrored into wirelang/specs/protocol-mirror-seed, so it\ncan only move together with that mirror), phase-3-final-bilanz-\ngenerator.py and pre-cutover-probe-failure-rate-tracker.py (wave and\nsign-off vocabulary lives in their identifiers and in test-pinned report\noutput).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): retire dead observability docs, scrub the live ones\n\nSix documents describe a migration event that ended on 2026-05-20 — the\ncutover-day watch loop, the pre-cutover watch day, the pre-cutover probe\ndashboard, the per-wave trend heatmap, the marathon SLO catalogue and\nthe watch-day marker catalogue. None of them documents a surviving\nscript interface, so they move to docs/archive/dead-migration-tooling/\nas deletion candidates. No test or tool loads them; the scripts that\nmention them do so in prose only, and those mentions are updated here.\n\nThe documents that still describe running services keep every technical\nstatement and lose the archaeology around it. Personas become the role\nthey played, because that is what a reader outside the company can act\non: \"Kai''s node-exporter Quadlet\" becomes \"container-infra''s\nnode-exporter Quadlet\", \"Tomas'' WAT-Core\" becomes \"the WAT core\",\n\"Strategy-Hand-Mira halts releases\" becomes \"the CEO halts releases\".\nDay and calendar-week anchors are dropped; where one carried meaning\n(\"stable from Tag-46\") the statement is rewritten to say the thing\n(\"stable\").\n\nTwo documents are deliberately untouched: pre-mortem-failure-mode-\nnotify-catalog.md and live-smoke-stability-window-operator-runbook.md\nare byte-mirrored into wirelang/specs/protocol-mirror-seed and pinned\nby tooling/ci, so they can only move together with that mirror. Both\nare listed as allowlist candidates in the PR body.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): drop calendar-week labels from the live-stream dashboard\n\nThe welle template options carried the migration calendar week in their\ndisplay text. The test pins the option values, not the labels, so the\nweek anchors go and the component names stay.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d5516b086b060e28a2ad881d4afc426b08433a5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/trees/d5516b086b060e28a2ad881d4afc426b08433a5d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/commits/310cd7fda012e86c75a2e1001e49da9b51a44929","verification":{"payload":"tree d5516b086b060e28a2ad881d4afc426b08433a5d\nparent 133d112921fe7b27b15b48a86cd55a5081c33eb4\nauthor wakir-labs <xypu4r8e@addy.io> 1789335680 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789335680 +0200\n\nchore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from observability surface (ADR-0072 W5/Noa) (#531)\n\n* fix(observability): make cosign G1/G2 guide tests state-agnostic\n\nT-G1G2-04 and T-G1G2-06 pinned a transient BLOCKED state rather than a\ndrift invariant, so both went red when the substrate legitimately moved\nforward:\n\n* welle5/6/7 container units received resolved image digests (#499), so\n  the guide''s inventory table looked \"spurious\" to T-04 although the\n  guide correctly documents which files participate in the G1 closeout.\n* the pinned Sigstore trust root was refreshed by operator hand on\n  2026-05-20 (real Fulcio root CA SHA-256 + Rekor shard id), so T-06''s\n  \"must still equal PENDING_OPERATOR_HAND_REFRESH\" assertion could only\n  ever hold before that refresh.\n\nBoth tests now assert the invariant that actually protects the operator:\nT-04 rejects guide entries for files that do not exist on disk (closed\nslots stay listed), T-06 rejects a half-refreshed trust root and checks\nthe documented value shape once refreshed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): retire dead migration dashboards, scrub the live ones\n\nThe Phase-3 migration finished on 2026-05-20. Five dashboards only ever\nqueried metrics that were produced during that migration and are no\nlonger emitted by anything in the tree; they are moved to\ndocs/archive/dead-dashboards/ as deletion candidates (nothing in the\nrepo references them — verified by filename grep across tests, scripts,\ntooling, docs and workflows):\n\n* cutover-day-morgen-verdict-tile.json\n* phase-3c-cross-welle-coordination.json\n* persona-engine-phase-3c-welle-status.json\n* per-welle-trend-heatmap.json\n* phase-3-marathon-slo-final.json\n\nThe four surviving dashboards keep every panel query byte-for-byte;\nonly __comment, tags and description fields were rewritten to state\nwhat the panel measures instead of which day it was built on.\n\npersona-engine-health.json is the one structural change: panels 9-11\nqueried mira_hourly_* gauges whose producer (scripts/mira-hourly-\nwatchdog.py) was deleted in #527, and panel 12 was an explicit\nduplicate of panel 3 that existed only as an at-a-glance companion to\nthat cluster. Four panels that can never render data are removed; the\nremaining eight are untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): scrub development archaeology from observability scripts\n\nComments, docstrings and user-facing strings (CLI --help text, generated\nreport headers) no longer carry sprint-day numbers, wave numbers,\ncalendar-week anchors or persona names. Where a token carried a real\nstatement, the statement stays and the anchor moves to what it actually\ndescribes (\"the default picks up the carrier-image installer\" instead of\n\"Tag-55 default ...\"); where it was pure provenance, it is gone.\n\nBehaviour is unchanged: every file was rewritten under an AST comparison\nwith string constants normalised away, so no code path, argument,\ndefault or identifier moved. pytest tests/observability is green.\n\nscripts/observability/cutover-day-watch.sh is archived rather than\nscrubbed: it drives the migration-day watch loop that ended on\n2026-05-20 and no test, workflow or script references it.\n\nThree files are deliberately untouched and carry over as allowlist\ncandidates, documented in the PR body: alert-rule-to-mira-notify-\nbridge.py (byte-mirrored into wirelang/specs/protocol-mirror-seed, so it\ncan only move together with that mirror), phase-3-final-bilanz-\ngenerator.py and pre-cutover-probe-failure-rate-tracker.py (wave and\nsign-off vocabulary lives in their identifiers and in test-pinned report\noutput).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): retire dead observability docs, scrub the live ones\n\nSix documents describe a migration event that ended on 2026-05-20 — the\ncutover-day watch loop, the pre-cutover watch day, the pre-cutover probe\ndashboard, the per-wave trend heatmap, the marathon SLO catalogue and\nthe watch-day marker catalogue. None of them documents a surviving\nscript interface, so they move to docs/archive/dead-migration-tooling/\nas deletion candidates. No test or tool loads them; the scripts that\nmention them do so in prose only, and those mentions are updated here.\n\nThe documents that still describe running services keep every technical\nstatement and lose the archaeology around it. Personas become the role\nthey played, because that is what a reader outside the company can act\non: \"Kai''s node-exporter Quadlet\" becomes \"container-infra''s\nnode-exporter Quadlet\", \"Tomas'' WAT-Core\" becomes \"the WAT core\",\n\"Strategy-Hand-Mira halts releases\" becomes \"the CEO halts releases\".\nDay and calendar-week anchors are dropped; where one carried meaning\n(\"stable from Tag-46\") the statement is rewritten to say the thing\n(\"stable\").\n\nTwo documents are deliberately untouched: pre-mortem-failure-mode-\nnotify-catalog.md and live-smoke-stability-window-operator-runbook.md\nare byte-mirrored into wirelang/specs/protocol-mirror-seed and pinned\nby tooling/ci, so they can only move together with that mirror. Both\nare listed as allowlist candidates in the PR body.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): drop calendar-week labels from the live-stream dashboard\n\nThe welle template options carried the migration calendar week in their\ndisplay text. The test pins the option values, not the labels, so the\nweek anchors go and the component names stay.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpxiACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6eUQAER31V1mgdwKL1jcaWOPtFC3\nh/KVH+XFweM0pUoFEuq4QUScXIZBRykkBwp7qfgurw++DQo0PHHKqD4HbN6D0sT2\ncWHaUmkFJhFVIunQT7Aced4dwDeN6AZdZ2XXDKDtscv8Hdyjllqc2wm/aR1ZFS5n\nYGbq+Z2aPBBY91v+WNcLrxATq3KIolPTWIcmeN6Pc/+HX6RaGdmBIyNFscM4ESy/\nDB3KO3X2hNOYCSR4ivAI5q4LnyWwS4h+F5p7OQhUX+ixaIGWQJbykjT4ptwrHk/B\ni0nxGJzaHCiEgf7FSFCh0+IKbcS6oZ4fjrjK6DuxaiaQwccnalb/NHPVjbNiyIMx\nvWzgQVJ6oBeRRWojIEj7SV6DPVqMNVAyTQUEK4vyETCMxsMNumIeSZP78EFJ0wGY\nSjV/upCMcRWsc4rQZHYgFuD7Jg9A22CfpJWPmHOC4RlrB+xzHq2JC7n8vbpjiFIW\nNxtAesozi3AW342/8OdcWLygYxm7DiWnKjD+wzh3ZnURTGKopZoxZ/bBs1MqvGoX\nE4lZQW3mYwCnPjP09m+jfkvQoxZPfFCvbF+XvkVg6XUOLGrOSvCOLfsO3MoeGN46\nhDT9ZoScArAGDe2Dqxl+y5sTq/3fnQt+jdlCzCPtT/m+g5oX03iIsUsvBCrAuccX\nYiWQqjQS83EZDGdmMNgi\n=N7D7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-13T21:41:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/310cd7fda012e86c75a2e1001e49da9b51a44929","node_id":"C_kwDOSVv36NoAKDMxMGNkN2ZkYTAxMmU4NmM3NWEyZTEwMDFlNDlkYTliNTFhNDQ5Mjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/133d112921fe7b27b15b48a86cd55a5081c33eb4","sha":"133d112921fe7b27b15b48a86cd55a5081c33eb4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/133d112921fe7b27b15b48a86cd55a5081c33eb4"}],"sha":"310cd7fda012e86c75a2e1001e49da9b51a44929","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/310cd7fda012e86c75a2e1001e49da9b51a44929"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/281068747?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs","id":281068747,"login":"wakir-labs","node_id":"U_kgDOEMDEyw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/133d112921fe7b27b15b48a86cd55a5081c33eb4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T21:27:14Z","email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T21:27:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(phase-4): second archaeology pass over the wirelang spec documents (ADR-0072 W5/Reza, follow-up to #529) (#530)\n\n* chore(phase-4): second archaeology pass over the wirelang spec documents (ADR-0072 W5/Reza, follow-up to #529)\n\nPR #529 landed the wirelang Python modules and the 15 Rust protocol\ncrates; both are at zero hits for the W5 working regex. The spec\ndocuments under wirelang/specs/ were left at the first pass. This PR is\nthe second pass over them.\n\nMethod: line-local scrub for tables, code fences, list items and list\ncontinuations (leading indentation preserved byte-exactly), plus a\nparagraph-aware pass that joins, scrubs and re-wraps only the prose\nparagraphs that actually contain a stamp. Line-break hyphenation\nrepaired after the re-wrap.\n\nSubstantive mappings, not blind deletion:\n- \"**Tag-6 (v0.19.0) is additive relative to Tag-5 (v0.18.2):**\" ->\n  \"**v0.19.0 is additive relative to v0.18.2:**\". The schema version is\n  the durable anchor; the tag was the calendar anchor.\n- Version-history rows \"| 0.28.0 | ... | Tag-6 lands the **X**\" ->\n  \"| 0.28.0 | ... | Lands the **X**\".\n- \"All Tag-1 + Tag-3 + Tag-5 surfaces remain unchanged\" ->\n  \"All previously shipped surfaces remain unchanged\".\n- Named sprints (Sprint-Pengine-N, Sprint-Migration-*, Sprint-Bridge-*,\n  Sprint-Rust-*) dropped; stamp-as-subject -> \"This revision\".\n\nMatching lines in wirelang/specs (without protocol-mirror-seed):\n1662 -> 588, across 21 remaining files.\n\nCross-zone one-liner: tests/specs/test_wirelang_spec_v0_4_3_pre_cutover_\nfreeze.py::T-09 asserted the literal \"Tag-50\" in wirelang-spec-v0-4-3.md.\nThe spec now cites \"PR #320 (v0.4.2)\" — PR number and schema version are\nthe durable anchors. The assertion is dropped; the two remaining ones\n(v0.4.2 present, PR #320 present) carry the intent. Caused here,\nrepaired here.\n\nKnown gaps, deliberately out of scope:\n- wirelang/specs/protocol-mirror-seed/ (8 files) is a byte-mirror of the\n  observability dashboards and runbooks; tests/observability asserts the\n  mirror is byte-identical to its primary, so it has to move with the\n  primary in the observability sweep. Allowlist candidate.\n- The residual 588 lines sit in the accumulated version-history tables and\n  per-revision test-count bookkeeping of the larger specs\n  (schema-registry-spec.md alone is ~8.2k lines). Converting those to\n  version-anchored prose is editorial work on normative documents, not\n  pattern work. Marked WIP, not force-fitted by regex.\n\nInvariants: 17/17 canonical schema digests unchanged vs. 3beeea9;\npytest tests/ + wirelang/ green except the failures that already fail on\nmain (tests/audit collection error from the removed\ntooling/ci/audit_cross_repo_drift_allowlist.py, cosign-g1-g2,\nwelle-telemetry, persona-cli help-text colouring under Python 3.14).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(phase-4): exclude the sealed spec wirelang-spec-v0-4-3.md from the sweep (ADR-0072 W5/Reza, self-repair)\n\nwirelang-spec-v0-4-3.md carries `status: pre-cutover-freeze` plus\n`freeze-marker: kw-24-cutover-gate` and is content-sealed: the CI job\n\"wirelang spec v0.4.3 freeze-seal probe\" recomputes the seal and\nrequires verdict SEAL-INTACT. The second archaeology pass changed the\nbody and turned the verdict into SEAL-ALLOWED-DELTA, which is a red\nRequired check.\n\nA frozen document must not be edited by a sweep; it can only change\nthrough its documented errata mechanism. The file and the T-09\nassertion in tests/specs/test_wirelang_spec_v0_4_3_pre_cutover_freeze.py\nare restored byte-identical to main. wirelang-spec-v0-4-3.md is an\nexplicit allowlist candidate for archaeology-lint: the residual stamps\nin it are sealed content and stay until an errata revision lifts them.\n\nAlso noted for the sweep: wirelang-spec-v0-4-4-draft.md carries\n`status: post-cutover-reserve-draft` and is NOT seal-probed, so it\nremains in scope.\n\nVerified after the revert: freeze-seal probe 21/21 green locally,\n17/17 canonical schema digests unchanged, pytest tests/ + wirelang/\ngreen except the pre-existing main-tip failures.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"87facb960180872312fea1aefa939dffc509bb2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/trees/87facb960180872312fea1aefa939dffc509bb2b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/commits/133d112921fe7b27b15b48a86cd55a5081c33eb4","verification":{"payload":"tree 87facb960180872312fea1aefa939dffc509bb2b\nparent 9d3e98c6bba44c386e808e1d0544344ef6167028\nauthor wakir-labs <xypu4r8e@addy.io> 1789334834 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789334834 +0200\n\nchore(phase-4): second archaeology pass over the wirelang spec documents (ADR-0072 W5/Reza, follow-up to #529) (#530)\n\n* chore(phase-4): second archaeology pass over the wirelang spec documents (ADR-0072 W5/Reza, follow-up to #529)\n\nPR #529 landed the wirelang Python modules and the 15 Rust protocol\ncrates; both are at zero hits for the W5 working regex. The spec\ndocuments under wirelang/specs/ were left at the first pass. This PR is\nthe second pass over them.\n\nMethod: line-local scrub for tables, code fences, list items and list\ncontinuations (leading indentation preserved byte-exactly), plus a\nparagraph-aware pass that joins, scrubs and re-wraps only the prose\nparagraphs that actually contain a stamp. Line-break hyphenation\nrepaired after the re-wrap.\n\nSubstantive mappings, not blind deletion:\n- \"**Tag-6 (v0.19.0) is additive relative to Tag-5 (v0.18.2):**\" ->\n  \"**v0.19.0 is additive relative to v0.18.2:**\". The schema version is\n  the durable anchor; the tag was the calendar anchor.\n- Version-history rows \"| 0.28.0 | ... | Tag-6 lands the **X**\" ->\n  \"| 0.28.0 | ... | Lands the **X**\".\n- \"All Tag-1 + Tag-3 + Tag-5 surfaces remain unchanged\" ->\n  \"All previously shipped surfaces remain unchanged\".\n- Named sprints (Sprint-Pengine-N, Sprint-Migration-*, Sprint-Bridge-*,\n  Sprint-Rust-*) dropped; stamp-as-subject -> \"This revision\".\n\nMatching lines in wirelang/specs (without protocol-mirror-seed):\n1662 -> 588, across 21 remaining files.\n\nCross-zone one-liner: tests/specs/test_wirelang_spec_v0_4_3_pre_cutover_\nfreeze.py::T-09 asserted the literal \"Tag-50\" in wirelang-spec-v0-4-3.md.\nThe spec now cites \"PR #320 (v0.4.2)\" — PR number and schema version are\nthe durable anchors. The assertion is dropped; the two remaining ones\n(v0.4.2 present, PR #320 present) carry the intent. Caused here,\nrepaired here.\n\nKnown gaps, deliberately out of scope:\n- wirelang/specs/protocol-mirror-seed/ (8 files) is a byte-mirror of the\n  observability dashboards and runbooks; tests/observability asserts the\n  mirror is byte-identical to its primary, so it has to move with the\n  primary in the observability sweep. Allowlist candidate.\n- The residual 588 lines sit in the accumulated version-history tables and\n  per-revision test-count bookkeeping of the larger specs\n  (schema-registry-spec.md alone is ~8.2k lines). Converting those to\n  version-anchored prose is editorial work on normative documents, not\n  pattern work. Marked WIP, not force-fitted by regex.\n\nInvariants: 17/17 canonical schema digests unchanged vs. 3beeea9;\npytest tests/ + wirelang/ green except the failures that already fail on\nmain (tests/audit collection error from the removed\ntooling/ci/audit_cross_repo_drift_allowlist.py, cosign-g1-g2,\nwelle-telemetry, persona-cli help-text colouring under Python 3.14).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(phase-4): exclude the sealed spec wirelang-spec-v0-4-3.md from the sweep (ADR-0072 W5/Reza, self-repair)\n\nwirelang-spec-v0-4-3.md carries `status: pre-cutover-freeze` plus\n`freeze-marker: kw-24-cutover-gate` and is content-sealed: the CI job\n\"wirelang spec v0.4.3 freeze-seal probe\" recomputes the seal and\nrequires verdict SEAL-INTACT. The second archaeology pass changed the\nbody and turned the verdict into SEAL-ALLOWED-DELTA, which is a red\nRequired check.\n\nA frozen document must not be edited by a sweep; it can only change\nthrough its documented errata mechanism. The file and the T-09\nassertion in tests/specs/test_wirelang_spec_v0_4_3_pre_cutover_freeze.py\nare restored byte-identical to main. wirelang-spec-v0-4-3.md is an\nexplicit allowlist candidate for archaeology-lint: the residual stamps\nin it are sealed content and stay until an errata revision lifts them.\n\nAlso noted for the sweep: wirelang-spec-v0-4-4-draft.md carries\n`status: post-cutover-reserve-draft` and is NOT seal-probed, so it\nremains in scope.\n\nVerified after the revert: freeze-seal probe 21/21 green locally,\n17/17 canonical schema digests unchanged, pytest tests/ + wirelang/\ngreen except the pre-existing main-tip failures.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpxUyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAR80QAHXubnP7jSKwr97D4AhYgkEY\nObt7OGHRymecqxG+PtvRL3gPx7BrPEaiAVEP2XheGNxCXDGho4NmoLF0PirWDe/3\nJbJRi0JNeg2h/YbWvL2FsjHSwItSh32sFPd0v2j6sqbOlTVbZY/IA6Zr0GYurh02\n6OpMD5FO3bXm88L5PPNIevKaBA1Hn3iWU+QCJ5auJIx5fujjFaDbcpkGR5/26xba\n/tieyizCsfQSLkaJ+ZY8cSTvbPNxF15vkcD4fG1o11HTOwxjWjtt9nECyEH62pLB\nXgYVdwoDGKG5brzz1meTXS6lEno44+7+1r/0oQvMrvp4fZVaN2