1fe7b27b15b48a86cd55a5081c33eb4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/281068747?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs","id":281068747,"login":"wakir-labs","node_id":"U_kgDOEMDEyw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/9d3e98c6bba44c386e808e1d0544344ef6167028/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T21:15:06Z","email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T21:15:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from docs, wat, scripts and root (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás) (#527)\n\n* chore(phase-4): archive WAT live-run evidence, drop dead cutover/phase-3c docs, rename sketch docs (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, part 1)\n\nArchaeology sweep of docs/ per ADR-0072 sub-item 4d-2 and the CTO\nimplementation plan §2.6 classification (keep / design-doc / archive):\n\n- archive (evidence): the six WAT TV-1/TV-2/TV-3 live-run and live-stamp\n  memos move to docs/archive/evidence/wat-live-runs/ (indexed in\n  docs/archive/README.md); the two tag-suffixed file names are replaced\n  by run ordinals.\n- archive (delete, history at tag archive/pre-phase-4): 22 runbooks under\n  docs/operations/ and 11 quality-gate specs that belonged to the Phase-3c\n  cutover workflows removed in W1 (welle-N runbooks, cutover runbook,\n  trigger gates, eve-recipe patches, g1/g2 checklist, marathon acceptance,\n  doppel-welle specs, kw-24 acceptance criteria), the sprint-6/7 closeouts,\n  the sprint-9 race-resolution note, the migration-pilot setup, the\n  quadlet rotation stub, the cosign/synadia activation sketch, the ADR-0070\n  runtime copy (authoritative in the corporate ADR tree), and the 2026-05-18\n  cross-repo sync report superseded by the 05-19 refresh.\n- design-doc: docs/quadlet-systemd-migration-skizze.md becomes\n  docs/design-notes/quadlet-systemd-migration.md.\n- rename: docs/spiffe-z-a-jwt-svid-skizze.md -> docs/spiffe-jwt-svid-identity.md,\n  docs/test-plans/sprint-qa-tag-15-e2e-pilot-smoke.md -> docs/test-plans/e2e-pilot-smoke.md;\n  in-zone references updated. Cross-zone references (quadlet/*.container\n  Documentation= lines, test docstrings) are listed in the PR body for the\n  parallel W5 owners.\n\nContent of the retained files is scrubbed in the follow-up commits.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): archive audit reports as evidence, drop dead cutover/phase-3c scripts and docs, scrub runbooks (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, part 2)\n\nZone docs/, scripts/, reports/, root — secured from the run aborted at 09:33.\n\n- reports/audit/ → docs/archive/evidence/audits/ (3 evidence reports, entries\n  in docs/archive/README.md); remaining reports/ deleted (cross-repo sync\n  audit superseded by the tooling/compat gate, W4 #526).\n- Delete dead scripts: phase-3c cutover dry-run / observability tracker /\n  welle status emitter, welle-* day-0 pipelines + telemetry emitters,\n  mira-hourly-watchdog (+ systemd units), cross-repo-sync-audit,\n  *_skizze prototypes, run-tests-acceptance-baseline.sh.\n- Delete dead docs: operations/* cutover recipes, pre-mortems, strict-flip\n  map, handoff plan; quality-gates/* cutover run-order, pre-mortem coverage\n  matrix, welle state-file conventions; persona-engine/* welle plans;\n  audit/* one-off audits; decisions/adr-errata-tag-55; test-counts-convention.\n- Rename scripts/install-persona-tomas-quadlet.sh → install-persona-quadlet.sh.\n- Scrub orchestrator-nats-kv-phase-1-runbook.md (sprint/tag section index,\n  §7 sprint backlog, §8 verification stamps → history pointer; 2819 → 703\n  lines); fix links/pointers to moved or removed files in docs and scripts.\n- Delete .alert-routing-cross-repo-allowlist.yaml (no references left).\n\nCode changes limited to comments/docstrings/strings; behaviour unchanged.\nHistory for all removed files: tag archive/pre-phase-4.\n\nIdempotency counter docs (excl. archive): 162 @3beeea9 → 109 @cab0c00 → 92 now.\nZone counter (docs+wat+scripts+reports+samples+root): 233 → 179 → 142.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(phase-4): drop tests that only pinned removed docs/scripts, follow renamed evidence paths (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, coupled — handover Amara Teil 2)\n\nCoupled test changes under the W5 zone rule (tests/ and wirelang/tests/ are\nAmara''s zone, Teil 2). Nothing here changes tested behaviour.\n\n- Deleted (30 files): tests that exclusively pinned artefacts removed in\n  this PR — docs/operations pre-mortems, promotion sequencing, res-d4 deep\n  dive, strict-flip readiness map, handoff plan; phase-3c / welle-* scripts;\n  mira-hourly-watchdog; cross-repo-sync-audit (+ tag52 refresh report);\n  *_skizze prototypes; adr-errata-tag-55; adr-spec-compliance and 0.5.2\n  production-readiness audit reports; state-file producer wiring plan.\n  Each would have failed on the missing artefact. Full table in PR #527.\n- Path follow-ups (7 files): reports/audit/* → docs/archive/evidence/audits/*,\n  install-persona-tomas-quadlet.sh → install-persona-quadlet.sh, docstring\n  pointers to removed docs → \"git history, tag archive/pre-phase-4\".\n- Partial removals (2 files): test_cosign_drift_coverage_a6.py drops TV-A6-20\n  (+ fixture) which read pre-mortem-failure-mode-coverage.md;\n  test_welle_6_producer_w5_fix_tag74.py drops the reconciliation-doc\n  existence check. Remaining tests in both files untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(ci): follow evidence-report rename in engine-version-drift allowlist (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, path follow-up in Kai zone)\n\ntooling/ci/engine-version-drift-allowlist.json is Kai''s W5 zone; verified\nkai/phase-4-w5-sweep-infra does not touch the file (git diff 3beeea9..kai\nempty). Minimal path follow-up only:\nreports/audit/persona-engine-0-5-3-production-readiness-2026-05-19.md →\ndocs/archive/evidence/audits/persona-engine-0-5-3-production-readiness-2026-05-19.md.\nReason text (Tag-NN wording) left for Kai''s sweep.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): fix pointers to moved/removed files in docs and scripts (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, part 2b)\n\nRemaining unstaged modifications from the 09:33 run, secured:\n- docs/archive/README.md: entries for the three evidence audit reports.\n- Links reports/audit/* → docs/archive/evidence/audits/* (nats audit doc,\n  bug-42 suite, test plan), install-persona-tomas-quadlet.sh →\n  install-persona-quadlet.sh (test plan, migrate helpers, script header).\n- Pointers to removed docs → \"git history, tag archive/pre-phase-4\"\n  (aggregator-workflow, parity runbook, a6 coverage, ots operator setup\n  frontmatter, a2 coverage companion row, spire-agent table row).\n- orchestrator-nats-kv-phase-1-runbook.md: drop sprint/tag section index,\n  §7 sprint backlog and §8 verification stamps (2819 → 703 lines, history\n  pointer kept).\n- scripts: docstring parity references to removed mira-hourly-watchdog.py\n  and cross-repo-sync-audit.py neutralised; --report example path updated.\n\nComments/docstrings only; behaviour unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): scrub development archaeology from wat/ (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 1)\n\n18 files under wat/: docstrings, comments, argparse help texts only.\nSprint/Tag anchors removed or neutralised (\"an earlier revision\", \"this\nmodule\"), persona attributions dropped or replaced by track wording,\n\"Aufsichtsrat-readable\" -> \"reviewer-readable\". Version anchors kept where\nthey exist (schema 0.2.0 signature slot). No behaviour change: AST of all\n17 .py files identical to HEAD modulo string constants; tests/wat green.\n\nZone counter (docs+wat+scripts+samples+root): 142 -> 124 files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(phase-4): restore Amara-zone tests, archive the evidence they pin (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, red-test fix)\n\nFixes the red `wirelang suite` on PR #527: commit 144be82 deleted four\nfiles under wirelang/tests/ (Amara''s zone, Teil 2). One of them,\ntest_tag56_production_readiness_audit.py, is referenced by\ntooling/ci/engine-version-drift-allowlist.json, so\ntest_drift_allowlist_refresh_tag67.py::test_t07_every_entry_path_exists\nfailed with \"allowlist entry references non-existent path\".\n\n- Reverted all four deletions under wirelang/tests/; the zone now shows\n  zero deletions and zero renames against 3beeea9.\n- The two audit reports those tests pin are kept as evidence instead of\n  being dropped: reports/audit/persona-engine-0-5-2-production-readiness\n  and reports/audit/adr-spec-compliance-audit → docs/archive/evidence/\n  audits/, the ADR errata addendum → docs/archive/evidence/decisions/\n  adr-errata-path-typo-fixes.md (tag-NN dropped from the filename).\n  docs/archive/README.md lists all three.\n- Restored docs/persona-engine/state-file-producer-wiring-plan.md and\n  welle-5-kw-anchor-reconciliation-tag74.md in place: both are pinned by\n  Amara tests on content and referenced by tooling/ literals (Kai zone).\n  Listed as archaeology-lint allowlist candidates in the PR body instead.\n- Remaining test changes are path follow-ups only (5 files, pointer\n  updates to the archived evidence).\n\nAllowlist path check: every entry in engine-version-drift-allowlist.json\nresolves again. Affected suites green locally.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): scrub development archaeology from scripts/ (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 2)\n\nComment/docstring/echo-text scrub across 41 files in scripts/ (observability\nsub-tree excluded, Noa''s zone). Time anchors (Tag-NN, Sprint-N, Welle-N, KW-NN)\nreplaced by version/schema anchors or dropped, persona names replaced by the\nowning track (\"Noa''s tracker\" -> \"the SRE track''s tracker\"), German leftovers\ntranslated.\n\nBehaviour unchanged:\n- 28 Python files verified AST-identical after stripping docstrings and\n  blanking string constants; the only remaining string-constant deltas are\n  human-readable report/help text.\n- 13 shell/unit files pass `bash -n`; only comments and echo texts changed.\n- One deliberate exception: the `boot_baseline` literal in\n  scripts/persona-engine/boot-self-test-v2.py keeps its \"Tag-50\" token because\n  wirelang/tests/persona_engine/test_boot_self_test_v2_tag50.py asserts it in\n  the JSON report. Listed as an archaeology-lint allowlist candidate; the\n  literal can be scrubbed together with the test in Amara''s Teil 2.\n\nCoupled test change (Amara zone, handover Teil 2):\n- tests/integration/test_bug_42_regression_suite_tag_48.py — the pinned\n  metric/schema-id floors were derived from a Tag-43 baseline that counted\n  three scripts removed in this PR; floors lowered by three, wording\n  de-anchored. No other assertion touched.\n\npytest: wirelang/ green, tests/ green except two pre-existing failures in\ntests/observability/test_cosign_g1_g2_operator_setup_guide.py and the\npre-existing collection error in tests/audit/test_trajectory_resync_tag61.py\n(all three inherit from main, inputs untouched here — see PR body).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): scrub development archaeology from root manifests (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 3)\n\npyproject.toml and REUSE.toml: comment-only scrub of sprint/tag anchors and\npersona names; pytest marker *descriptions* translated to English wording\n(marker names and all dependency/extras/script entries unchanged). Both files\nre-parse with tomllib.\n\nZone counter after this tranche: 91 files with archaeology hits (baseline 162).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): scrub last archaeology anchors in scripts/ (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 4)\n\nSix files: internal sprint codenames in module docstrings, a persona-named\nnotify feed in a --help string, a \"Cutover-blocker\" alert summary reworded to\n\"Release-blocker\", a German leftover in a shell comment, a PR reference with a\ntag anchor. Strings are operator-facing text only; no test pins any of them\n(verified by grep over tests/ and wirelang/tests/).\n\nRemaining in scripts/: the CutoverPlan dataclass in\nscripts/ci/adr-0068-migration-step-3-cutover.py (code identifier, domain term)\nand the boot_baseline literal pinned by a wirelang test — both listed as\narchaeology-lint allowlist candidates in the PR body.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <duplicate@noreply.invalid>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(phase-4): scrub archaeology from WAT specs, CI notes and trust-mode doc (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 5)\n\n15 low-hit docs: sprint/tag/KW anchors dropped, German terms translated,\npersona names replaced by the owning track or by the role (\"escalate to the\nCEO persona\"), persona sign-off lines at the end of docs removed. Code spans,\nfenced blocks, link targets and YAML front-matter untouched, so file names,\nstate-file keys and command lines keep working.\n\nZone counter: 162 (baseline 3beeea9) -> 76 files with hits after this tranche.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(phase-4): scrub archaeology from image-build, publisher-CLI and audit docs (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 6)\n\n13 docs under docs/, docs/operations/ and docs/audit/: time anchors dropped,\npersona names replaced by the owning engineering function (\"Selin Çelik\" ->\n\"persona-engine engineering\", \"Noa SRE dashboards\" -> \"SRE engineering\ndashboards\"), persona sign-offs removed, German sentences that carried a\n\"Welle\" anchor translated. Wave numbering (`wave-6 subscribe_loop`) keeps the\nsubstrate meaning; only the German spelling goes.\n\nZone counter: 76 -> 63 files with hits.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(phase-4): scrub archaeology from image-build and OTS-wiring runbooks (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 7)\n\n7 operations docs (v907-verify, svid-workload-identity, state-backing,\nbridge-audit-writer image builds, 15-binary SBOM + reproducibility recipes,\nmanifest-hash OTS anchor wiring): time anchors dropped, persona names replaced\nby the engineering function, the authorisation-path ASCII diagram\nde-personalised and its German heading translated.\n\nZone counter: 63 -> 56 files with hits.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(phase-4): scrub archaeology from test plans, conformance and brand-asset docs (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 8)\n\n6 docs (external-verifier conformance, revocation-event filter, brand-asset\nsnapshot spec, E2E pilot-smoke and live-VM test plans, doppelbetrieb\nacceptance): sprint codenames dropped or replaced by the phase, persona names\nreplaced by the engineering function, \"Sprint\" table columns renamed to\n\"Phase\", German header fragments in the brand-asset spec translated.\n\nZone counter: 56 -> 50 files with hits.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(phase-4): follow renamed runbook section in OTS probe test (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, coupled — handover Amara Teil 2)\n\nCoupled text follow-up in Amara''s zone: tranche 7 renamed\n\"## 7. AR-Authorisierungs-Pfad\" to \"## 7. Authorisation path\" in\ndocs/operations/manifest-hash-ots-anchor-wiring.md and de-personalised the\ndiagram, so test_p14_runbook_has_section_6_and_7 pinned a heading that no\nlonger exists. Assertions now pin the new heading, the pinned cutover window\ndate (2026-06-09) and PR #371 instead of the KW anchor. No other assertion\ntouched, no behaviour change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(phase-4): scrub archaeology from SPIRE, NATS-KV and OTS-wiring runbooks (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 9)\n\n6 docs (SPIRE server/agent phase-2 runbooks, orchestrator NATS-KV runbook,\nWirelang-spec OTS anchor wiring, branch-protection required checks, cross-repo\ndrift runbook): tag/sprint/KW anchors dropped, persona-named sandboxes renamed\n(\"Mira-sandbox\" -> \"the agent sandbox\"), cross-review owners named by function,\nthe OTS runbook''s authorisation section reworded to external-audit wording.\n\nCoupled test follow-up (Amara zone, Teil 2):\ntests/audit/test_wirelang_spec_ots_pre_anchor_probe_tag60.py pinned two section\nheadings and the KW anchor of the runbook; assertions now pin the new headings\nand the cutover date. No behaviour change.\n\nZone counter: 50 -> 44 files with hits.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(phase-4): scrub archaeology from quality-gate docs (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 10)\n\n5 quality-gate docs (failure-mode A2/A6 coverage, bug-42 regression suite,\nphase-1b pilot, phase-2 doppelbetrieb, phase-3 production): sprint/tag anchors\ndropped, persona-named containers and spawns renamed to their function\n(\"Pre-Framework-Tomás-spawn\" -> \"pre-framework agent spawn\", \"Noa-domain\" ->\n\"SRE domain\"), gate owners named by engineering function.\n\nZone counter: 44 -> 39 files with hits.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(phase-4): restore code spans damaged by the scrub pass (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás)\n\nSelf-repair of drift this PR introduced: the punctuation-tidy step of the\nscrub pass also ran inside inline-code spans and dropped empty argument lists\n(`jcs_hash()` -> `jcs_hash`, `pytest.fail()` -> `pytest.fail`, 16 spans across\n6 docs) plus three ellipsis spacings. All spans are restored to their baseline\nform and the tidy step now skips any segment containing a backtick.\n\nVerified: every inline-code span present at 3beeea9 either still exists or was\nintentionally re-pointed (moved evidence paths, removed docs).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(phase-4): scrub WAT manifest-v2 spec and NATS-JWT auth doc (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 11)\n\n- `docs/wat-manifest-v2-spec.md`: §11 replaced the 570-line sprint-by-sprint\n  engineering log with a schema-level change table (0.1.0, 0.2.0) plus the\n  additive-compatibility rule; per-release detail stays in git history at tag\n  `archive/pre-phase-4`. §1–§10 scrubbed of tag/sprint anchors.\n- `docs/nats-jwt-auth-phase-2-4.md`: ASCII architecture diagrams and the\n  follow-up/risk tables de-personalised (\"Reza Sprint-6+\" -> \"protocol track\",\n  \"Tag-10 callback\" -> \"JWT callback\"); German fragments translated.\n\nZone counter: 39 -> 37 files with hits.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(phase-4): scrub WAT-manifest-v2 spec and NATS-JWT-auth doc (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 11)\n\n- `docs/wat-manifest-v2-spec.md`: §11 was a 570-line sprint-by-sprint\n  engineering change log (pure development archaeology on a public spec\n  surface). Replaced by a schema-level change table (0.1.0, 0.2.0) plus the\n  additive-compatibility rule; the detail stays recoverable at the\n  `archive/pre-phase-4` tag. §1–§10 scrubbed in place, normative content\n  unchanged.\n- `docs/nats-jwt-auth-phase-2-4.md`: persona names in the ASCII architecture\n  diagrams and follow-up tables replaced by the owning track, internal branch\n  names dropped, German fragments translated.\n\nZone counter: 39 -> 37 files with hits.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): take over Kai''s four W5 handovers into the Tomás zone (ADR-0072 W5)\n\nFollows PR #528 (Kai, merged as f39f7b1), which removed the `paths:` filters\nfrom the required workflows and deleted four dead tooling helpers.\n\n1. `docs/ci/branch-protection-required-checks.md`: new invariant section — a\n   required workflow carries no `paths:` filter, with license-gate.yml,\n   tests.yml and runtime-acceptance-gates.yml named; the five affected table\n   rows now read \"every PR + push to `main` (no path filter)\".\n2. `scripts/ci/ci_aggregator.py`: the five `SUB_WORKFLOWS` rows that mirrored\n   the removed filters become `path_globs=(\"**\",)`.\n   `tests/ci/test_ci_aggregator_workflow.py` tests 5, 7 and 10 rebaselined:\n   there is no \"required context skipped by a path filter\" case left; the\n   skip-ok-only case is now produced with an empty inventory.\n3. `scripts/pre-commit-spdx-header-check.py`: stale \"mirrors the license-gate\n   path-filter\" comment replaced by the no-filter statement.\n4. `docs/persona-engine/state-file-producer-wiring-plan.md`: pointer to the\n   deleted `audit_trail_marker_constants` helper replaced by a git-history\n   reference. No other doc in the zone referenced the four deleted helpers.\n\ntests/ci green (215 passed, 1 skipped).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(phase-4): scrub archaeology from cosign and Quadlet operator docs (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 12)\n\n6 operations docs (cosign strict-mode activation, cosign policy phase-3b, G1/G2\noperator setup, live-VM acceptance phase-3b, 15-binary SBOM baseline refresh,\nQuadlet phase-3b Rust CLI): tag/sprint/Welle anchors dropped, persona reviewers\nnamed by function, operator-name placeholders instead of a real name in the\ncommit-template example, persona sign-off lines removed.\n\nCoupled test follow-up (Amara zone, Teil 2):\ntests/observability/test_cosign_g1_g2_operator_setup_guide.py pinned the persona\nname of the Zone-C reviewer and the \"— Kai\" sign-off line of the guide. The\nZone-C assertion now pins the reviewing function; the sign-off test is inverted\ninto the Phase-4 rule (public runbooks carry no persona sign-off).\n\nZone counter: 37 -> 31 files with hits.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(phase-4): follow renamed §9 header in live-VM phase-3b doc test (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, coupled)\n\nCoupled text follow-up to tranche 12: the scrub dropped the tag anchor from\n\"## 9. Out of scope (Tag-18)\"; the section-header pin in\ntests/infra/test_live_vm_acceptance_phase_3b.py follows. No behaviour change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* revert(phase-4): restore persona-engine release-notes docs to main state (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás)\n\nThe archaeology scrub of docs/persona-engine/0-5-3-rc1-release-notes.md\nand 0-5-3-final-release-notes.md broke four required checks\n(wirelang suite x3 + ci-aggregator): the Tag-58/Tag-62 release-notes\ntests in wirelang/tests/persona_engine/ pin prose literals in those\nfiles (\"## 4. Pre-Cutover Gate-Map\", \"Closed in Tag-57\", section\nnames).\n\nThe pinning tests live in Amara''s zone (part 2), so the coupled\ndoc/test pair is handed over instead of being rewritten broadly here.\nBoth files are listed as allowlist candidates for archaeology-lint.\n\nZone counter unchanged by this revert beyond the two restored files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): archive four historic decision notes out of docs/decisions (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 13)\n\nFour documents in docs/decisions/ are point-in-time development\nrecords, not active design rationale, and carry 105 archaeology hits\nbetween them. None is referenced from code, tests or active docs\n(the only inbound link was between two of them):\n\n- capability-token-layer-snapshot.md (64 hits)\n- doppelbetrieb-bridge-smoke-acceptance.md (19 hits)\n- phase-3-nodeattestor-migration.md (15 hits)\n- anthropic-prompt-caching-phase-2a.md (7 hits)\n\nThey are moved to docs/archive/evidence/decisions/ with rows in\ndocs/archive/README.md. Deletion is the preferred end state per the\nplan §2.6; the four files are listed in the done brief as operator\ndeletion candidates.\n\nZone counter: 24 -> 20 files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(phase-4): scrub archaeology from the Cut-1/Cut-2 and federation-topology decision notes (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 14)\n\nPersona names, hand-off ownership markers and sprint/tag anchors\nremoved from three decision notes that stay in place because code,\npyproject and infra scripts reference them by path. Statements are\nunchanged; follow-up work is described by what it is instead of who\nwas going to do it in which sprint.\n\nZone counter: 20 -> 17 files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(phase-4): scrub archaeology from the Rust-rewrite roadmap and crate-choice notes (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 15)\n\nBoth files are pinned by path from wirelang/specs/wirelang-spec-v0-4.md\nand its integrity test, so they stay where they are. Persona names,\ninternal zone labels and sprint anchors are replaced by the scope they\nstand for (identity-substrate zone, WAT zone, container zone,\npersona-definition zone); crate pins, versions and rationale are\nuntouched.\n\nZone counter: 17 -> 15 files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(phase-4): scrub the Quadlet design note and the OTS-anchor wiring runbook (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 16)\n\nQuadlet design note: sprint/tag authoring stamps become \"first pass\"\nand \"second pass\", the German \"Skizze\" becomes \"sketch\", persona\nsignature dropped. Verified tool versions, directive names and the\nopen-item list are unchanged.\n\nOTS-anchor wiring runbook: \"Cutover gate\" -> \"Activation gate\",\n\"AR-authorisation\" -> \"maintainer authorisation\". Dates and the\noperator procedure are unchanged.\n\nZone counter: 15 -> 13 files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): archive the SPIFFE JWT-SVID design sketch out of docs/ (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 17)\n\ndocs/spiffe-jwt-svid-identity.md is a phase-2 planning sketch with\n~90 archaeology hits (cross-review ack slots, consensus markers,\nsprint/tag stamps). It is not referenced from code or tests, only\nfrom two active docs that cite its JWT-refresh and SPIFFE-ID-shape\nsections. It moves to docs/archive/evidence/decisions/ as\nspiffe-jwt-svid-identity-sketch.md, the two inbound links follow, and\ndocs/archive/README.md records why it is kept.\n\nZone counter: 13 -> 12 files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(phase-4): scrub the cross-substrate parity runbook (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 18)\n\nOwner lines, persona names, sprint/tag anchors and \"Mira-Hand\"\nmarkers are replaced by roles and operator wording. Substrate paths,\nbinary names, the required-status-check string and the operator\nrecipes are byte-identical, so the two pinning test files\n(tests/infra/test_cross_substrate_parity_3way.py,\ntests/observability/test_cross_substrate_parity_gate_tag57.py) stay\ngreen.\n\nOne \"Tag-57\" literal remains in the addendum heading because\ntest_cross_substrate_parity_gate_tag57.py asserts it verbatim; an\nHTML comment marks it as an archaeology-lint allowlist entry and the\ndone brief hands it to QA.\n\nRunbook hits: 61 -> 2 (both the documented allowlist anchor).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(phase-4): keep the pinned \"Decision-points\"/\"AR\" literals in the federation-topology note (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás)\n\ntests/infra/test_pilot_bootstrap_bug_39_bilateral.py::test_decision_note_content\nasserts both literals verbatim. The test is out of zone (part 2), so\nthe heading keeps them and carries an allowlist comment instead of\ndragging the pin along.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <duplicate@noreply.invalid>","tree":{"sha":"716dfd7b551da74b395595b5583ee7788a6ccf54","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/trees/716dfd7b551da74b395595b5583ee7788a6ccf54"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/commits/9d3e98c6bba44c386e808e1d0544344ef6167028","verification":{"payload":"tree 716dfd7b551da74b395595b5583ee7788a6ccf54\nparent f6461527ea829a910b314fa3fba9f37f158b134e\nauthor wakir-labs <xypu4r8e@addy.io> 1789334106 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789334106 +0200\n\nchore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from docs, wat, scripts and root (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás) (#527)\n\n* chore(phase-4): archive WAT live-run evidence, drop dead cutover/phase-3c docs, rename sketch docs (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, part 1)\n\nArchaeology sweep of docs/ per ADR-0072 sub-item 4d-2 and the CTO\nimplementation plan §2.6 classification (keep / design-doc / archive):\n\n- archive (evidence): the six WAT TV-1/TV-2/TV-3 live-run and live-stamp\n  memos move to docs/archive/evidence/wat-live-runs/ (indexed in\n  docs/archive/README.md); the two tag-suffixed file names are replaced\n  by run ordinals.\n- archive (delete, history at tag archive/pre-phase-4): 22 runbooks under\n  docs/operations/ and 11 quality-gate specs that belonged to the Phase-3c\n  cutover workflows removed in W1 (welle-N runbooks, cutover runbook,\n  trigger gates, eve-recipe patches, g1/g2 checklist, marathon acceptance,\n  doppel-welle specs, kw-24 acceptance criteria), the sprint-6/7 closeouts,\n  the sprint-9 race-resolution note, the migration-pilot setup, the\n  quadlet rotation stub, the cosign/synadia activation sketch, the ADR-0070\n  runtime copy (authoritative in the corporate ADR tree), and the 2026-05-18\n  cross-repo sync report superseded by the 05-19 refresh.\n- design-doc: docs/quadlet-systemd-migration-skizze.md becomes\n  docs/design-notes/quadlet-systemd-migration.md.\n- rename: docs/spiffe-z-a-jwt-svid-skizze.md -> docs/spiffe-jwt-svid-identity.md,\n  docs/test-plans/sprint-qa-tag-15-e2e-pilot-smoke.md -> docs/test-plans/e2e-pilot-smoke.md;\n  in-zone references updated. Cross-zone references (quadlet/*.container\n  Documentation= lines, test docstrings) are listed in the PR body for the\n  parallel W5 owners.\n\nContent of the retained files is scrubbed in the follow-up commits.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): archive audit reports as evidence, drop dead cutover/phase-3c scripts and docs, scrub runbooks (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, part 2)\n\nZone docs/, scripts/, reports/, root — secured from the run aborted at 09:33.\n\n- reports/audit/ → docs/archive/evidence/audits/ (3 evidence reports, entries\n  in docs/archive/README.md); remaining reports/ deleted (cross-repo sync\n  audit superseded by the tooling/compat gate, W4 #526).\n- Delete dead scripts: phase-3c cutover dry-run / observability tracker /\n  welle status emitter, welle-* day-0 pipelines + telemetry emitters,\n  mira-hourly-watchdog (+ systemd units), cross-repo-sync-audit,\n  *_skizze prototypes, run-tests-acceptance-baseline.sh.\n- Delete dead docs: operations/* cutover recipes, pre-mortems, strict-flip\n  map, handoff plan; quality-gates/* cutover run-order, pre-mortem coverage\n  matrix, welle state-file conventions; persona-engine/* welle plans;\n  audit/* one-off audits; decisions/adr-errata-tag-55; test-counts-convention.\n- Rename scripts/install-persona-tomas-quadlet.sh → install-persona-quadlet.sh.\n- Scrub orchestrator-nats-kv-phase-1-runbook.md (sprint/tag section index,\n  §7 sprint backlog, §8 verification stamps → history pointer; 2819 → 703\n  lines); fix links/pointers to moved or removed files in docs and scripts.\n- Delete .alert-routing-cross-repo-allowlist.yaml (no references left).\n\nCode changes limited to comments/docstrings/strings; behaviour unchanged.\nHistory for all removed files: tag archive/pre-phase-4.\n\nIdempotency counter docs (excl. archive): 162 @3beeea9 → 109 @cab0c00 → 92 now.\nZone counter (docs+wat+scripts+reports+samples+root): 233 → 179 → 142.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(phase-4): drop tests that only pinned removed docs/scripts, follow renamed evidence paths (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, coupled — handover Amara Teil 2)\n\nCoupled test changes under the W5 zone rule (tests/ and wirelang/tests/ are\nAmara''s zone, Teil 2). Nothing here changes tested behaviour.\n\n- Deleted (30 files): tests that exclusively pinned artefacts removed in\n  this PR — docs/operations pre-mortems, promotion sequencing, res-d4 deep\n  dive, strict-flip readiness map, handoff plan; phase-3c / welle-* scripts;\n  mira-hourly-watchdog; cross-repo-sync-audit (+ tag52 refresh report);\n  *_skizze prototypes; adr-errata-tag-55; adr-spec-compliance and 0.5.2\n  production-readiness audit reports; state-file producer wiring plan.\n  Each would have failed on the missing artefact. Full table in PR #527.\n- Path follow-ups (7 files): reports/audit/* → docs/archive/evidence/audits/*,\n  install-persona-tomas-quadlet.sh → install-persona-quadlet.sh, docstring\n  pointers to removed docs → \"git history, tag archive/pre-phase-4\".\n- Partial removals (2 files): test_cosign_drift_coverage_a6.py drops TV-A6-20\n  (+ fixture) which read pre-mortem-failure-mode-coverage.md;\n  test_welle_6_producer_w5_fix_tag74.py drops the reconciliation-doc\n  existence check. Remaining tests in both files untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(ci): follow evidence-report rename in engine-version-drift allowlist (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, path follow-up in Kai zone)\n\ntooling/ci/engine-version-drift-allowlist.json is Kai''s W5 zone; verified\nkai/phase-4-w5-sweep-infra does not touch the file (git diff 3beeea9..kai\nempty). Minimal path follow-up only:\nreports/audit/persona-engine-0-5-3-production-readiness-2026-05-19.md →\ndocs/archive/evidence/audits/persona-engine-0-5-3-production-readiness-2026-05-19.md.\nReason text (Tag-NN wording) left for Kai''s sweep.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): fix pointers to moved/removed files in docs and scripts (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, part 2b)\n\nRemaining unstaged modifications from the 09:33 run, secured:\n- docs/archive/README.md: entries for the three evidence audit reports.\n- Links reports/audit/* → docs/archive/evidence/audits/* (nats audit doc,\n  bug-42 suite, test plan), install-persona-tomas-quadlet.sh →\n  install-persona-quadlet.sh (test plan, migrate helpers, script header).\n- Pointers to removed docs → \"git history, tag archive/pre-phase-4\"\n  (aggregator-workflow, parity runbook, a6 coverage, ots operator setup\n  frontmatter, a2 coverage companion row, spire-agent table row).\n- orchestrator-nats-kv-phase-1-runbook.md: drop sprint/tag section index,\n  §7 sprint backlog and §8 verification stamps (2819 → 703 lines, history\n  pointer kept).\n- scripts: docstring parity references to removed mira-hourly-watchdog.py\n  and cross-repo-sync-audit.py neutralised; --report example path updated.\n\nComments/docstrings only; behaviour unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): scrub development archaeology from wat/ (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 1)\n\n18 files under wat/: docstrings, comments, argparse help texts only.\nSprint/Tag anchors removed or neutralised (\"an earlier revision\", \"this\nmodule\"), persona attributions dropped or replaced by track wording,\n\"Aufsichtsrat-readable\" -> \"reviewer-readable\". Version anchors kept where\nthey exist (schema 0.2.0 signature slot). No behaviour change: AST of all\n17 .py files identical to HEAD modulo string constants; tests/wat green.\n\nZone counter (docs+wat+scripts+samples+root): 142 -> 124 files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(phase-4): restore Amara-zone tests, archive the evidence they pin (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, red-test fix)\n\nFixes the red `wirelang suite` on PR #527: commit 144be82 deleted four\nfiles under wirelang/tests/ (Amara''s zone, Teil 2). One of them,\ntest_tag56_production_readiness_audit.py, is referenced by\ntooling/ci/engine-version-drift-allowlist.json, so\ntest_drift_allowlist_refresh_tag67.py::test_t07_every_entry_path_exists\nfailed with \"allowlist entry references non-existent path\".\n\n- Reverted all four deletions under wirelang/tests/; the zone now shows\n  zero deletions and zero renames against 3beeea9.\n- The two audit reports those tests pin are kept as evidence instead of\n  being dropped: reports/audit/persona-engine-0-5-2-production-readiness\n  and reports/audit/adr-spec-compliance-audit → docs/archive/evidence/\n  audits/, the ADR errata addendum → docs/archive/evidence/decisions/\n  adr-errata-path-typo-fixes.md (tag-NN dropped from the filename).\n  docs/archive/README.md lists all three.\n- Restored docs/persona-engine/state-file-producer-wiring-plan.md and\n  welle-5-kw-anchor-reconciliation-tag74.md in place: both are pinned by\n  Amara tests on content and referenced by tooling/ literals (Kai zone).\n  Listed as archaeology-lint allowlist candidates in the PR body instead.\n- Remaining test changes are path follow-ups only (5 files, pointer\n  updates to the archived evidence).\n\nAllowlist path check: every entry in engine-version-drift-allowlist.json\nresolves again. Affected suites green locally.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): scrub development archaeology from scripts/ (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 2)\n\nComment/docstring/echo-text scrub across 41 files in scripts/ (observability\nsub-tree excluded, Noa''s zone). Time anchors (Tag-NN, Sprint-N, Welle-N, KW-NN)\nreplaced by version/schema anchors or dropped, persona names replaced by the\nowning track (\"Noa''s tracker\" -> \"the SRE track''s tracker\"), German leftovers\ntranslated.\n\nBehaviour unchanged:\n- 28 Python files verified AST-identical after stripping docstrings and\n  blanking string constants; the only remaining string-constant deltas are\n  human-readable report/help text.\n- 13 shell/unit files pass `bash -n`; only comments and echo texts changed.\n- One deliberate exception: the `boot_baseline` literal in\n  scripts/persona-engine/boot-self-test-v2.py keeps its \"Tag-50\" token because\n  wirelang/tests/persona_engine/test_boot_self_test_v2_tag50.py asserts it in\n  the JSON report. Listed as an archaeology-lint allowlist candidate; the\n  literal can be scrubbed together with the test in Amara''s Teil 2.\n\nCoupled test change (Amara zone, handover Teil 2):\n- tests/integration/test_bug_42_regression_suite_tag_48.py — the pinned\n  metric/schema-id floors were derived from a Tag-43 baseline that counted\n  three scripts removed in this PR; floors lowered by three, wording\n  de-anchored. No other assertion touched.\n\npytest: wirelang/ green, tests/ green except two pre-existing failures in\ntests/observability/test_cosign_g1_g2_operator_setup_guide.py and the\npre-existing collection error in tests/audit/test_trajectory_resync_tag61.py\n(all three inherit from main, inputs untouched here — see PR body).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): scrub development archaeology from root manifests (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 3)\n\npyproject.toml and REUSE.toml: comment-only scrub of sprint/tag anchors and\npersona names; pytest marker *descriptions* translated to English wording\n(marker names and all dependency/extras/script entries unchanged). Both files\nre-parse with tomllib.\n\nZone counter after this tranche: 91 files with archaeology hits (baseline 162).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): scrub last archaeology anchors in scripts/ (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 4)\n\nSix files: internal sprint codenames in module docstrings, a persona-named\nnotify feed in a --help string, a \"Cutover-blocker\" alert summary reworded to\n\"Release-blocker\", a German leftover in a shell comment, a PR reference with a\ntag anchor. Strings are operator-facing text only; no test pins any of them\n(verified by grep over tests/ and wirelang/tests/).\n\nRemaining in scripts/: the CutoverPlan dataclass in\nscripts/ci/adr-0068-migration-step-3-cutover.py (code identifier, domain term)\nand the boot_baseline literal pinned by a wirelang test — both listed as\narchaeology-lint allowlist candidates in the PR body.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <duplicate@noreply.invalid>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(phase-4): scrub archaeology from WAT specs, CI notes and trust-mode doc (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 5)\n\n15 low-hit docs: sprint/tag/KW anchors dropped, German terms translated,\npersona names replaced by the owning track or by the role (\"escalate to the\nCEO persona\"), persona sign-off lines at the end of docs removed. Code spans,\nfenced blocks, link targets and YAML front-matter untouched, so file names,\nstate-file keys and command lines keep working.\n\nZone counter: 162 (baseline 3beeea9) -> 76 files with hits after this tranche.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(phase-4): scrub archaeology from image-build, publisher-CLI and audit docs (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 6)\n\n13 docs under docs/, docs/operations/ and docs/audit/: time anchors dropped,\npersona names replaced by the owning engineering function (\"Selin Çelik\" ->\n\"persona-engine engineering\", \"Noa SRE dashboards\" -> \"SRE engineering\ndashboards\"), persona sign-offs removed, German sentences that carried a\n\"Welle\" anchor translated. Wave numbering (`wave-6 subscribe_loop`) keeps the\nsubstrate meaning; only the German spelling goes.\n\nZone counter: 76 -> 63 files with hits.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(phase-4): scrub archaeology from image-build and OTS-wiring runbooks (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 7)\n\n7 operations docs (v907-verify, svid-workload-identity, state-backing,\nbridge-audit-writer image builds, 15-binary SBOM + reproducibility recipes,\nmanifest-hash OTS anchor wiring): time anchors dropped, persona names replaced\nby the engineering function, the authorisation-path ASCII diagram\nde-personalised and its German heading translated.\n\nZone counter: 63 -> 56 files with hits.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(phase-4): scrub archaeology from test plans, conformance and brand-asset docs (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 8)\n\n6 docs (external-verifier conformance, revocation-event filter, brand-asset\nsnapshot spec, E2E pilot-smoke and live-VM test plans, doppelbetrieb\nacceptance): sprint codenames dropped or replaced by the phase, persona names\nreplaced by the engineering function, \"Sprint\" table columns renamed to\n\"Phase\", German header fragments in the brand-asset spec translated.\n\nZone counter: 56 -> 50 files with hits.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(phase-4): follow renamed runbook section in OTS probe test (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, coupled — handover Amara Teil 2)\n\nCoupled text follow-up in Amara''s zone: tranche 7 renamed\n\"## 7. AR-Authorisierungs-Pfad\" to \"## 7. Authorisation path\" in\ndocs/operations/manifest-hash-ots-anchor-wiring.md and de-personalised the\ndiagram, so test_p14_runbook_has_section_6_and_7 pinned a heading that no\nlonger exists. Assertions now pin the new heading, the pinned cutover window\ndate (2026-06-09) and PR #371 instead of the KW anchor. No other assertion\ntouched, no behaviour change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(phase-4): scrub archaeology from SPIRE, NATS-KV and OTS-wiring runbooks (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 9)\n\n6 docs (SPIRE server/agent phase-2 runbooks, orchestrator NATS-KV runbook,\nWirelang-spec OTS anchor wiring, branch-protection required checks, cross-repo\ndrift runbook): tag/sprint/KW anchors dropped, persona-named sandboxes renamed\n(\"Mira-sandbox\" -> \"the agent sandbox\"), cross-review owners named by function,\nthe OTS runbook''s authorisation section reworded to external-audit wording.\n\nCoupled test follow-up (Amara zone, Teil 2):\ntests/audit/test_wirelang_spec_ots_pre_anchor_probe_tag60.py pinned two section\nheadings and the KW anchor of the runbook; assertions now pin the new headings\nand the cutover date. No behaviour change.\n\nZone counter: 50 -> 44 files with hits.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(phase-4): scrub archaeology from quality-gate docs (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 10)\n\n5 quality-gate docs (failure-mode A2/A6 coverage, bug-42 regression suite,\nphase-1b pilot, phase-2 doppelbetrieb, phase-3 production): sprint/tag anchors\ndropped, persona-named containers and spawns renamed to their function\n(\"Pre-Framework-Tomás-spawn\" -> \"pre-framework agent spawn\", \"Noa-domain\" ->\n\"SRE domain\"), gate owners named by engineering function.\n\nZone counter: 44 -> 39 files with hits.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(phase-4): restore code spans damaged by the scrub pass (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás)\n\nSelf-repair of drift this PR introduced: the punctuation-tidy step of the\nscrub pass also ran inside inline-code spans and dropped empty argument lists\n(`jcs_hash()` -> `jcs_hash`, `pytest.fail()` -> `pytest.fail`, 16 spans across\n6 docs) plus three ellipsis spacings. All spans are restored to their baseline\nform and the tidy step now skips any segment containing a backtick.\n\nVerified: every inline-code span present at 3beeea9 either still exists or was\nintentionally re-pointed (moved evidence paths, removed docs).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(phase-4): scrub WAT manifest-v2 spec and NATS-JWT auth doc (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 11)\n\n- `docs/wat-manifest-v2-spec.md`: §11 replaced the 570-line sprint-by-sprint\n  engineering log with a schema-level change table (0.1.0, 0.2.0) plus the\n  additive-compatibility rule; per-release detail stays in git history at tag\n  `archive/pre-phase-4`. §1–§10 scrubbed of tag/sprint anchors.\n- `docs/nats-jwt-auth-phase-2-4.md`: ASCII architecture diagrams and the\n  follow-up/risk tables de-personalised (\"Reza Sprint-6+\" -> \"protocol track\",\n  \"Tag-10 callback\" -> \"JWT callback\"); German fragments translated.\n\nZone counter: 39 -> 37 files with hits.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(phase-4): scrub WAT-manifest-v2 spec and NATS-JWT-auth doc (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 11)\n\n- `docs/wat-manifest-v2-spec.md`: §11 was a 570-line sprint-by-sprint\n  engineering change log (pure development archaeology on a public spec\n  surface). Replaced by a schema-level change table (0.1.0, 0.2.0) plus the\n  additive-compatibility rule; the detail stays recoverable at the\n  `archive/pre-phase-4` tag. §1–§10 scrubbed in place, normative content\n  unchanged.\n- `docs/nats-jwt-auth-phase-2-4.md`: persona names in the ASCII architecture\n  diagrams and follow-up tables replaced by the owning track, internal branch\n  names dropped, German fragments translated.\n\nZone counter: 39 -> 37 files with hits.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): take over Kai''s four W5 handovers into the Tomás zone (ADR-0072 W5)\n\nFollows PR #528 (Kai, merged as f39f7b1), which removed the `paths:` filters\nfrom the required workflows and deleted four dead tooling helpers.\n\n1. `docs/ci/branch-protection-required-checks.md`: new invariant section — a\n   required workflow carries no `paths:` filter, with license-gate.yml,\n   tests.yml and runtime-acceptance-gates.yml named; the five affected table\n   rows now read \"every PR + push to `main` (no path filter)\".\n2. `scripts/ci/ci_aggregator.py`: the five `SUB_WORKFLOWS` rows that mirrored\n   the removed filters become `path_globs=(\"**\",)`.\n   `tests/ci/test_ci_aggregator_workflow.py` tests 5, 7 and 10 rebaselined:\n   there is no \"required context skipped by a path filter\" case left; the\n   skip-ok-only case is now produced with an empty inventory.\n3. `scripts/pre-commit-spdx-header-check.py`: stale \"mirrors the license-gate\n   path-filter\" comment replaced by the no-filter statement.\n4. `docs/persona-engine/state-file-producer-wiring-plan.md`: pointer to the\n   deleted `audit_trail_marker_constants` helper replaced by a git-history\n   reference. No other doc in the zone referenced the four deleted helpers.\n\ntests/ci green (215 passed, 1 skipped).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(phase-4): scrub archaeology from cosign and Quadlet operator docs (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 12)\n\n6 operations docs (cosign strict-mode activation, cosign policy phase-3b, G1/G2\noperator setup, live-VM acceptance phase-3b, 15-binary SBOM baseline refresh,\nQuadlet phase-3b Rust CLI): tag/sprint/Welle anchors dropped, persona reviewers\nnamed by function, operator-name placeholders instead of a real name in the\ncommit-template example, persona sign-off lines removed.\n\nCoupled test follow-up (Amara zone, Teil 2):\ntests/observability/test_cosign_g1_g2_operator_setup_guide.py pinned the persona\nname of the Zone-C reviewer and the \"— Kai\" sign-off line of the guide. The\nZone-C assertion now pins the reviewing function; the sign-off test is inverted\ninto the Phase-4 rule (public runbooks carry no persona sign-off).\n\nZone counter: 37 -> 31 files with hits.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(phase-4): follow renamed §9 header in live-VM phase-3b doc test (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, coupled)\n\nCoupled text follow-up to tranche 12: the scrub dropped the tag anchor from\n\"## 9. Out of scope (Tag-18)\"; the section-header pin in\ntests/infra/test_live_vm_acceptance_phase_3b.py follows. No behaviour change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* revert(phase-4): restore persona-engine release-notes docs to main state (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás)\n\nThe archaeology scrub of docs/persona-engine/0-5-3-rc1-release-notes.md\nand 0-5-3-final-release-notes.md broke four required checks\n(wirelang suite x3 + ci-aggregator): the Tag-58/Tag-62 release-notes\ntests in wirelang/tests/persona_engine/ pin prose literals in those\nfiles (\"## 4. Pre-Cutover Gate-Map\", \"Closed in Tag-57\", section\nnames).\n\nThe pinning tests live in Amara''s zone (part 2), so the coupled\ndoc/test pair is handed over instead of being rewritten broadly here.\nBoth files are listed as allowlist candidates for archaeology-lint.\n\nZone counter unchanged by this revert beyond the two restored files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): archive four historic decision notes out of docs/decisions (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 13)\n\nFour documents in docs/decisions/ are point-in-time development\nrecords, not active design rationale, and carry 105 archaeology hits\nbetween them. None is referenced from code, tests or active docs\n(the only inbound link was between two of them):\n\n- capability-token-layer-snapshot.md (64 hits)\n- doppelbetrieb-bridge-smoke-acceptance.md (19 hits)\n- phase-3-nodeattestor-migration.md (15 hits)\n- anthropic-prompt-caching-phase-2a.md (7 hits)\n\nThey are moved to docs/archive/evidence/decisions/ with rows in\ndocs/archive/README.md. Deletion is the preferred end state per the\nplan §2.6; the four files are listed in the done brief as operator\ndeletion candidates.\n\nZone counter: 24 -> 20 files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(phase-4): scrub archaeology from the Cut-1/Cut-2 and federation-topology decision notes (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 14)\n\nPersona names, hand-off ownership markers and sprint/tag anchors\nremoved from three decision notes that stay in place because code,\npyproject and infra scripts reference them by path. Statements are\nunchanged; follow-up work is described by what it is instead of who\nwas going to do it in which sprint.\n\nZone counter: 20 -> 17 files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(phase-4): scrub archaeology from the Rust-rewrite roadmap and crate-choice notes (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 15)\n\nBoth files are pinned by path from wirelang/specs/wirelang-spec-v0-4.md\nand its integrity test, so they stay where they are. Persona names,\ninternal zone labels and sprint anchors are replaced by the scope they\nstand for (identity-substrate zone, WAT zone, container zone,\npersona-definition zone); crate pins, versions and rationale are\nuntouched.\n\nZone counter: 17 -> 15 files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(phase-4): scrub the Quadlet design note and the OTS-anchor wiring runbook (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 16)\n\nQuadlet design note: sprint/tag authoring stamps become \"first pass\"\nand \"second pass\", the German \"Skizze\" becomes \"sketch\", persona\nsignature dropped. Verified tool versions, directive names and the\nopen-item list are unchanged.\n\nOTS-anchor wiring runbook: \"Cutover gate\" -> \"Activation gate\",\n\"AR-authorisation\" -> \"maintainer authorisation\". Dates and the\noperator procedure are unchanged.\n\nZone counter: 15 -> 13 files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): archive the SPIFFE JWT-SVID design sketch out of docs/ (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 17)\n\ndocs/spiffe-jwt-svid-identity.md is a phase-2 planning sketch with\n~90 archaeology hits (cross-review ack slots, consensus markers,\nsprint/tag stamps). It is not referenced from code or tests, only\nfrom two active docs that cite its JWT-refresh and SPIFFE-ID-shape\nsections. It moves to docs/archive/evidence/decisions/ as\nspiffe-jwt-svid-identity-sketch.md, the two inbound links follow, and\ndocs/archive/README.md records why it is kept.\n\nZone counter: 13 -> 12 files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(phase-4): scrub the cross-substrate parity runbook (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás, tranche 18)\n\nOwner lines, persona names, sprint/tag anchors and \"Mira-Hand\"\nmarkers are replaced by roles and operator wording. Substrate paths,\nbinary names, the required-status-check string and the operator\nrecipes are byte-identical, so the two pinning test files\n(tests/infra/test_cross_substrate_parity_3way.py,\ntests/observability/test_cross_substrate_parity_gate_tag57.py) stay\ngreen.\n\nOne \"Tag-57\" literal remains in the addendum heading because\ntest_cross_substrate_parity_gate_tag57.py asserts it verbatim; an\nHTML comment marks it as an archaeology-lint allowlist entry and the\ndone brief hands it to QA.\n\nRunbook hits: 61 -> 2 (both the documented allowlist anchor).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(phase-4): keep the pinned \"Decision-points\"/\"AR\" literals in the federation-topology note (ADR-0072 W5/Tomás)\n\ntests/infra/test_pilot_bootstrap_bug_39_bilateral.py::test_decision_note_content\nasserts both literals verbatim. The test is out of zone (part 2), so\nthe heading keeps them and carries an allowlist comment instead of\ndragging the pin along.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <duplicate@noreply.invalid>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpxJaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAa2EQAKsuL2yjKYWnLkOLdnTn4PXq\nzW1Tlobj4Tm04gw0sbfsuYr70AK1vm0nvGVyBOrQA9rDBjhNhhlPVq0Pl4CYJtt6\ncqF2GxyE4UrtEi8UvpWpkNqFUYdBNbOYyQACSL1HWzJdu/8deoWd8hSD9tZ/ZIfv\nGmuGKLpN31OmbmvkofPS14arZz3oh9ieuv/YrPUnKNnhaietdobQ94Ca4pl/s/hy\nUswobC/FizVj1xpEwwHbhXuGOOM4YvV0OqM1eDqJT9VTth1fEbeIVPLgugwTQSeZ\n9OTgkFR2nFau2axkPzvUrvsHfjbq1Ha4ibhI4ceNLpYo4Ket8XJndecIRuX8XXor\nDU/8JSQ45oMvDK6VTTBhvKtbgceMznMZD/uHqeOSAVWRuRWd/pPyQTQQPRhEL5++\nPjXqvyLfA7gDb7kEwhxUbwo6ENUoUi6pOPedHk213YEXWdlynHfGIjL1tph8XvNG\nQKW9g1+c7JKkDuoF1mklR6kkJ7zvTZgLUfiyDHeLbLBT9PjxaefkSI2aT4bRENXM\na9rpY3rYiHVCJcwYyk/SlxhPfmYoDWoNAVEugCUgWCmvfvAj4DqRFZCap35HOj2h\ngLG7eqfFnN9RlnLc8ES45ezOF3WZlhbmUDImzxEP56pOzFoRpg5rav5NhfZav0j2\n98oOAuX4EzExN8/zrHcy\n=0wmm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-13T21:15:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/9d3e98c6bba44c386e808e1d0544344ef6167028","node_id":"C_kwDOSVv36NoAKDlkM2U5OGM2YmJhNDRjMzg2ZTgwOGUxZDA1NDQzNDRlZjYxNjcwMjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/f6461527ea829a910b314fa3fba9f37f158b134e","sha":"f6461527ea829a910b314fa3fba9f37f158b134e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/f6461527ea829a910b314fa3fba9f37f158b134e"}],"sha":"9d3e98c6bba44c386e808e1d0544344ef6167028","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/9d3e98c6bba44c386e808e1d0544344ef6167028"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/281068747?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs","id":281068747,"login":"wakir-labs","node_id":"U_kgDOEMDEyw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/f6461527ea829a910b314fa3fba9f37f158b134e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T21:06:48Z","email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T21:06:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from wirelang protocol modules and rust protocol crates (ADR-0072 W5/Reza) (#529)\n\n* chore(phase-4): scrub description prose in wirelang schemas (ADR-0072 W5/Reza, T1a)\n\nTranche 1a of the archaeology sweep, zone Reza: description-only edits in\n7 mirrored JSON schemas (caveat-override-event-export, persona-claude-native,\npersona-v2, recovery-drill-outcome, wakir-persona-v1, wakir-wat-manifest-v1,\nwat-manifest-v2). Sprint-/Tag- slot anchors replaced by schema or registry\nversion anchors or removed where purely attributive.\n\nCanonical digests (tooling/compat/compat_canonical.py, strip string-valued\ndescription / x-spdx-*) verified identical for all 17 files before/after.\nNo validation keyword touched.\n\nZone counter (Arbeits-Regex, wirelang without tests/persona/persona_engine):\n95 -> 88 files. wirelang/schemas/*.json: 7 -> 0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(fixtures): re-derive caveat-override-event-export hash-derivate pins after description scrub (ADR-0072 W5/Reza, T1a self-repair)\n\nThe T1a description-only edit of wirelang/schemas/caveat-override-event-export.json\nchanges the raw file bytes (6988 -> 6958) and therefore sha256(file bytes),\nwhich is pinned as a hash derivate in\ntests/fixtures/schema-registry/caveat-override-event-export-v1/\n(anchor-manifest.json schema_file_sha256 + schema_file_bytes, schema.sha256.bin).\nCOXSR-03/04 and HDC-01/02/07 require the derivatives to be re-derived in the\nsame PR that modifies the schema; done here, only the two derived fields and\nthe 32-byte digest changed. Canonical digest of the schema itself is unchanged\n(compat gate green on 90428f4).\n\nLocal: wirelang/tests/test_federation_caveat_override_event_export_schema.py +\ntests/infra/test_hash_derivate_consistency.py -> 20 passed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from wirelang schema modules (ADR-0072 W5/Reza, T2)\n\nScrubs Sprint-/Tag-/persona-name archaeology from the seven Python\nmodules under wirelang/schemas/. Every finding was classified keep\n(substance retained, time anchor replaced by a structural anchor),\nthe remainder deleted as narrative.\n\nInvariants verified:\n- AST identical modulo string constants (docstrings/comments only,\n  plus five argparse help strings whose prose carried Sprint/Tag\n  anchors; no test asserts on them).\n- Canonical schema digests (strip description + x-spdx-*) unchanged\n  for all 17 wirelang/schemas/*.json vs. baseline 3beeea9.\n- pytest -k \"schema or publisher or capability or replication or\n  entry_signing\": 172 passed, 0 failed.\n\nZone counter (working regex, wirelang/ without tests/persona/\npersona_engine): 95 files at 3beeea9 -> 81 files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from wirelang identity, nats, bridge and adapter modules (ADR-0072 W5/Reza, T3)\n\n23 modules under wirelang/identity, wirelang/nats, wirelang/bridge and\nwirelang/adapters. Classification per the W5 rules:\n\n- keep-scrub (majority): sprint/tag time anchors replaced by structural\n  anchors (\"this module\", \"the base backend surface\", \"the DevOps\n  track\"), substance untouched.\n- Cross-review consensus markers Z-1-K-Sprint-4-{1..4} renamed to\n  Z-1-K-{1..4}; the descriptive names (kid-Resolver-Shape,\n  JCS-Resolver-Lock, Curve-Choice, STRICT-Mode-Activation-Owner) carry\n  the identity, the sprint token was the archaeology.\n- archive (deleted): agent-ownership narrative (\"Reza primary, Selin\n  co-owner\"), paired-update memo pointers into agents-workspaces/,\n  closeout-stamp references.\n- Persona names replaced by the owning track (\"the DevOps track\", \"the\n  WAT track\"); TODO(reza-tag-7-plus)/TODO(kai-cross-reference) markers\n  renamed to TODO(spire-live)/TODO(devops-cross-reference).\n\nInvariants verified:\n- AST identical modulo string constants for all 30 touched modules.\n- Canonical schema digests unchanged (17/17 vs. baseline 3beeea9).\n- pytest tests/ (without tests/audit): only the 6 failures that already\n  fail on f39f7b1 (tests/observability/test_cosign_g1_g2_*,\n  tests/scripts/test_welle_{1_2,3}_*) plus the pre-existing collection\n  error in tests/audit/test_trajectory_resync_tag61.py, which imports\n  tooling/ci/audit_cross_repo_drift_allowlist.py removed in 3beeea9.\n  All three are outside this zone and reported, not repaired here.\n\nZone counter (working regex): 95 files at 3beeea9 -> 58 files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(phase-4): repair two scrub-tool regressions in T2/T3 (ADR-0072 W5/Reza, self-repair)\n\nSelf-repair of defects my own T2/T3 commits introduced, per the\nself-repair clause; no design decision, no scope change.\n\n1. Intra-line whitespace collapse. The scrub helper normalised runs of\n   two or more spaces inside lines, which destroyed RST table\n   alignment, aligned trailing comments and aligned CLI-output examples\n   in docstrings. 210 lines restored byte-exactly against 3beeea9; the\n   remaining aligned comment blocks re-flowed by hand.\n2. Two Sphinx roles lost their leading colon (\":func:`x`\" -> \"func:`x`\")\n   because a character class included \":\". Repaired repo-wide across\n   wirelang/.\n\nAlso: one cross-zone one-line follow-up in\nwirelang/tests/test_real_nats_adapter_mirror.py. The test asserted on\nthe literal \"Sprint-7-Closeout-Stempel M-2\" inside a\nNatsAdapterAuthenticationError message that T3 scrubbed to\n\"milestone M-2\". Assertion and its docstring line updated to match;\nthe rest of wirelang/tests/ is untouched and stays with the tests\nsweep.\n\nVerified: AST identical modulo string constants vs. 3beeea9 for all\ntouched modules; 17/17 canonical schema digests unchanged;\npytest tests/ + wirelang/ green except the pre-existing main-tip\nfailures (tests/audit collection error, cosign-g1-g2, welle-telemetry).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from wirelang federation modules (ADR-0072 W5/Reza, T4)\n\n21 modules under wirelang/federation/. Classification:\n\n- keep-scrub: sprint/tag time anchors replaced by structural anchors\n  (\"this module\", \"the base backend surface\", \"a later increment\");\n  every sachaussage kept.\n- archive (deleted): the \"ADR-0050 Tool-Surface-Stempel\" and\n  \"ADR-0049 Pre-Box-Worktree\" blocks in eight modules (authoring-tool\n  and worktree provenance, no evidence value in source), the\n  agents-workspaces memo pointers, and the Zone-D/E1 coordination\n  narrative in multi_org_substrate (substance kept, process removed).\n- Persona names replaced by owning track: \"the DevOps track\", \"the\n  WAT track\", \"the persona-engine track\", \"the QA track\",\n  \"operator-hand\" for Mira-Hand.\n- Five error/description string constants reworded; two of them\n  (\"use put_with_revision once the Tag-2 backend lands\",\n  \"use the live bridge once Tag-3+ lands\") were stale anyway since\n  both surfaces have shipped. No test asserts on them.\n\nInvariants: AST identical modulo string constants; 17/17 canonical\nschema digests unchanged vs. 3beeea9; pytest tests/ + wirelang/ exits 0\n(pre-existing main-tip failures excluded as before).\n\nZone counter (working regex): 95 files at 3beeea9 -> 40 files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from wirelang CLI modules and package docstring (ADR-0072 W5/Reza, T5)\n\nwirelang/cli/*.py and wirelang/__init__.py.\n\n- archive (deleted): the four \"trigger note\" paragraphs in the\n  wirelang package docstring. They recorded which no-op touch was made\n  on which date to force a path-filtered Required-check to fire on\n  three specific PRs. Pure CI-mechanics history, no contract content.\n- keep-scrub: sprint anchors in CLI module docstrings and argparse\n  descriptions replaced by the stable item id (OI-PEFR-7, OI-PEFR-9,\n  OI-PILOT-3) or dropped; \"Mira-Hand\" -> \"operator-hand\",\n  \"Mira-side\" -> \"Operator-side\"; \"stable across Tag-3+\" -> \"stable\".\n\nKnown gap, deliberately not closed here: the module file name\nwirelang/cli/mira_dispatch.py and its launcher bin/wakir-mira-dispatch\nstill carry a persona name. Renaming them touches wirelang/tests/,\ntests/infra/, docs/ and wirelang/persona_engine/cli.py — four zones\nthat are being swept in parallel right now. Listed as an allowlist\ncandidate for archaeology-lint with a follow-up issue for the\ncoordinated rename.\n\nInvariants: AST identical modulo string constants; 17/17 canonical\nschema digests unchanged; pytest wirelang/tests + tests/infra rc=0.\n\nZone counter (working regex): 95 files at 3beeea9 -> 31 files\n(all remaining are wirelang/specs/).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from wirelang spec documents (ADR-0072 W5/Reza, T6)\n\n22 spec documents under wirelang/specs/ (protocol-mirror-seed excluded,\nsee below).\n\nMethod: a line-local pass for tables, code fences and list items, and a\nparagraph-aware pass that joins, scrubs and re-wraps only those prose\nparagraphs that actually contain a stamp (untouched paragraphs stay\nbyte-identical). Line-break hyphenation repaired after the re-wrap.\n\nSubstantive mappings instead of blind deletion:\n- \"**Tag-6 (v0.19.0) is additive relative to Tag-5 (v0.18.2):**\" ->\n  \"**v0.19.0 is additive relative to v0.18.2:**\" — the schema version\n  is the durable anchor, the tag was the calendar anchor.\n- Version-history rows \"| 0.28.0 | ... | Tag-6 lands the **X**\" ->\n  \"| 0.28.0 | ... | Lands the **X**\": the version column already\n  carries the identity.\n- \"All Tag-1 + Tag-3 + Tag-5 + ... surfaces remain byte-identical\" ->\n  \"All previously shipped surfaces remain byte-identical\".\n- Cross-review consensus markers Z-1-K-Sprint-4-{1..4} -> Z-1-K-{1..4}.\n- Agent signature lines (\"— Reza\") removed from six spec documents.\n\nCross-zone one-liner: tests/specs/test_wirelang_spec_v0_4_2_drift_s4_\nreconciliation.py used \"— Reza\" as the terminator of its §9 lookahead.\nThe regex now terminates at end-of-document; the assertions are\nunchanged. Caused by this PR, repaired here, flagged for the tests\nsweep.\n\nKnown gap: wirelang/specs/protocol-mirror-seed/ is untouched. It is a\nbyte-mirror of the observability dashboards and runbooks that belong to\nthe observability sweep, and tests/observability asserts the mirror is\nbyte-identical to its primary. Scrubbing it here would break that\ninvariant; it must move together with the primary. 8 files, allowlist\ncandidate.\n\nInvariants: 17/17 canonical schema digests unchanged; pytest tests/ +\nwirelang/ green except the pre-existing main-tip failures.\n\nZone counter (working regex): 95 files at 3beeea9 -> 31 files, of which\n23 outside protocol-mirror-seed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from the canonical-form, hash, CLI and validator crates (ADR-0072 W5/Reza, T7)\n\nFive protocol crates plus the workspace Cargo.toml:\npersona-canonical-form, persona-canonical-form-yaml, persona-hash,\npersona-cli, persona-validator.\n\n- Doc comments (//!, ///) and // comments: sprint/tag anchors dropped or\n  replaced by the durable anchor (pin name, section number, schema\n  version). \"Mira-Decision\" -> \"Ratified decision\", \"ceo-mandate\" ->\n  \"ratified mandate\", \"Selin-recommendation\" -> \"review recommendation\",\n  \"skizze\" -> \"sketch\", \"Mira-Sandbox\" -> \"the build sandbox\".\n- Workspace Cargo.toml crate registry: the \"Sprint-<Name>-MINI\" crate\n  labels replaced by the Phase-3a item number they already carry, e.g.\n  \"persona-engine-frontmatter-parser : Sprint-Rust-Frontmatter-Parser-\n  MINI (Phase-3a Item 8)\" -> \"... : Phase-3a Item 8\".\n\nNo pub signature touched, no pin constant touched, no test renamed in\nthis group. cargo test for the five crates: 162 passed, 0 failed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from the remaining protocol crates (ADR-0072 W5/Reza, T8)\n\n11 crates not covered by T7: persona-converter, persona-migration,\npersona-migration-resolver, persona-pilot-export,\npersona-engine-{anchor-emitter,anchor-submit-worker,\nfederation-frame-parser,federation-resolver,nats-subjects,\nsvid-workload-identity}.\n\n- Cargo.toml `authors` fields carrying a personal name and address\n  replaced by \"Wakir Labs\"; two package `description` strings that\n  opened with a sprint stamp rewritten to describe the crate.\n- Doc comments (`//!`, `///`) and line comments: sprint/tag anchors\n  dropped or replaced by structural anchors (\"the crate brief\", \"the\n  base\", \"a follow-up\"); cross-references \"<persona> PR #NNN (Tag-NN)\"\n  reduced to \"PR #NNN\"; owning personas replaced by the owning track.\n- \"Welle\" and \"Cutover\" deliberately kept: in ADR-0065/ADR-0066 they\n  are the live migration-wave vocabulary (env-var gate table, welle\n  state files, welle-N smoke docs), not archaeology. Listed as an\n  archaeology-lint allowlist entry in the PR body.\n\nNo behaviour change: comments and package metadata only, no `pub`\nsignature touched, no test renamed. `cargo metadata` parses the\nworkspace.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6ac23a191f74a6a97f2ce9f2822975df62d55f42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/trees/6ac23a191f74a6a97f2ce9f2822975df62d55f42"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/commits/f6461527ea829a910b314fa3fba9f37f158b134e","verification":{"payload":"tree 6ac23a191f74a6a97f2ce9f2822975df62d55f42\nparent f39f7b10e335b01ea3f0f9c686c97eada9e50dc0\nauthor wakir-labs <xypu4r8e@addy.io> 1789333608 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789333608 +0200\n\nchore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from wirelang protocol modules and rust protocol crates (ADR-0072 W5/Reza) (#529)\n\n* chore(phase-4): scrub description prose in wirelang schemas (ADR-0072 W5/Reza, T1a)\n\nTranche 1a of the archaeology sweep, zone Reza: description-only edits in\n7 mirrored JSON schemas (caveat-override-event-export, persona-claude-native,\npersona-v2, recovery-drill-outcome, wakir-persona-v1, wakir-wat-manifest-v1,\nwat-manifest-v2). Sprint-/Tag- slot anchors replaced by schema or registry\nversion anchors or removed where purely attributive.\n\nCanonical digests (tooling/compat/compat_canonical.py, strip string-valued\ndescription / x-spdx-*) verified identical for all 17 files before/after.\nNo validation keyword touched.\n\nZone counter (Arbeits-Regex, wirelang without tests/persona/persona_engine):\n95 -> 88 files. wirelang/schemas/*.json: 7 -> 0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(fixtures): re-derive caveat-override-event-export hash-derivate pins after description scrub (ADR-0072 W5/Reza, T1a self-repair)\n\nThe T1a description-only edit of wirelang/schemas/caveat-override-event-export.json\nchanges the raw file bytes (6988 -> 6958) and therefore sha256(file bytes),\nwhich is pinned as a hash derivate in\ntests/fixtures/schema-registry/caveat-override-event-export-v1/\n(anchor-manifest.json schema_file_sha256 + schema_file_bytes, schema.sha256.bin).\nCOXSR-03/04 and HDC-01/02/07 require the derivatives to be re-derived in the\nsame PR that modifies the schema; done here, only the two derived fields and\nthe 32-byte digest changed. Canonical digest of the schema itself is unchanged\n(compat gate green on 90428f4).\n\nLocal: wirelang/tests/test_federation_caveat_override_event_export_schema.py +\ntests/infra/test_hash_derivate_consistency.py -> 20 passed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from wirelang schema modules (ADR-0072 W5/Reza, T2)\n\nScrubs Sprint-/Tag-/persona-name archaeology from the seven Python\nmodules under wirelang/schemas/. Every finding was classified keep\n(substance retained, time anchor replaced by a structural anchor),\nthe remainder deleted as narrative.\n\nInvariants verified:\n- AST identical modulo string constants (docstrings/comments only,\n  plus five argparse help strings whose prose carried Sprint/Tag\n  anchors; no test asserts on them).\n- Canonical schema digests (strip description + x-spdx-*) unchanged\n  for all 17 wirelang/schemas/*.json vs. baseline 3beeea9.\n- pytest -k \"schema or publisher or capability or replication or\n  entry_signing\": 172 passed, 0 failed.\n\nZone counter (working regex, wirelang/ without tests/persona/\npersona_engine): 95 files at 3beeea9 -> 81 files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from wirelang identity, nats, bridge and adapter modules (ADR-0072 W5/Reza, T3)\n\n23 modules under wirelang/identity, wirelang/nats, wirelang/bridge and\nwirelang/adapters. Classification per the W5 rules:\n\n- keep-scrub (majority): sprint/tag time anchors replaced by structural\n  anchors (\"this module\", \"the base backend surface\", \"the DevOps\n  track\"), substance untouched.\n- Cross-review consensus markers Z-1-K-Sprint-4-{1..4} renamed to\n  Z-1-K-{1..4}; the descriptive names (kid-Resolver-Shape,\n  JCS-Resolver-Lock, Curve-Choice, STRICT-Mode-Activation-Owner) carry\n  the identity, the sprint token was the archaeology.\n- archive (deleted): agent-ownership narrative (\"Reza primary, Selin\n  co-owner\"), paired-update memo pointers into agents-workspaces/,\n  closeout-stamp references.\n- Persona names replaced by the owning track (\"the DevOps track\", \"the\n  WAT track\"); TODO(reza-tag-7-plus)/TODO(kai-cross-reference) markers\n  renamed to TODO(spire-live)/TODO(devops-cross-reference).\n\nInvariants verified:\n- AST identical modulo string constants for all 30 touched modules.\n- Canonical schema digests unchanged (17/17 vs. baseline 3beeea9).\n- pytest tests/ (without tests/audit): only the 6 failures that already\n  fail on f39f7b1 (tests/observability/test_cosign_g1_g2_*,\n  tests/scripts/test_welle_{1_2,3}_*) plus the pre-existing collection\n  error in tests/audit/test_trajectory_resync_tag61.py, which imports\n  tooling/ci/audit_cross_repo_drift_allowlist.py removed in 3beeea9.\n  All three are outside this zone and reported, not repaired here.\n\nZone counter (working regex): 95 files at 3beeea9 -> 58 files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(phase-4): repair two scrub-tool regressions in T2/T3 (ADR-0072 W5/Reza, self-repair)\n\nSelf-repair of defects my own T2/T3 commits introduced, per the\nself-repair clause; no design decision, no scope change.\n\n1. Intra-line whitespace collapse. The scrub helper normalised runs of\n   two or more spaces inside lines, which destroyed RST table\n   alignment, aligned trailing comments and aligned CLI-output examples\n   in docstrings. 210 lines restored byte-exactly against 3beeea9; the\n   remaining aligned comment blocks re-flowed by hand.\n2. Two Sphinx roles lost their leading colon (\":func:`x`\" -> \"func:`x`\")\n   because a character class included \":\". Repaired repo-wide across\n   wirelang/.\n\nAlso: one cross-zone one-line follow-up in\nwirelang/tests/test_real_nats_adapter_mirror.py. The test asserted on\nthe literal \"Sprint-7-Closeout-Stempel M-2\" inside a\nNatsAdapterAuthenticationError message that T3 scrubbed to\n\"milestone M-2\". Assertion and its docstring line updated to match;\nthe rest of wirelang/tests/ is untouched and stays with the tests\nsweep.\n\nVerified: AST identical modulo string constants vs. 3beeea9 for all\ntouched modules; 17/17 canonical schema digests unchanged;\npytest tests/ + wirelang/ green except the pre-existing main-tip\nfailures (tests/audit collection error, cosign-g1-g2, welle-telemetry).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from wirelang federation modules (ADR-0072 W5/Reza, T4)\n\n21 modules under wirelang/federation/. Classification:\n\n- keep-scrub: sprint/tag time anchors replaced by structural anchors\n  (\"this module\", \"the base backend surface\", \"a later increment\");\n  every sachaussage kept.\n- archive (deleted): the \"ADR-0050 Tool-Surface-Stempel\" and\n  \"ADR-0049 Pre-Box-Worktree\" blocks in eight modules (authoring-tool\n  and worktree provenance, no evidence value in source), the\n  agents-workspaces memo pointers, and the Zone-D/E1 coordination\n  narrative in multi_org_substrate (substance kept, process removed).\n- Persona names replaced by owning track: \"the DevOps track\", \"the\n  WAT track\", \"the persona-engine track\", \"the QA track\",\n  \"operator-hand\" for Mira-Hand.\n- Five error/description string constants reworded; two of them\n  (\"use put_with_revision once the Tag-2 backend lands\",\n  \"use the live bridge once Tag-3+ lands\") were stale anyway since\n  both surfaces have shipped. No test asserts on them.\n\nInvariants: AST identical modulo string constants; 17/17 canonical\nschema digests unchanged vs. 3beeea9; pytest tests/ + wirelang/ exits 0\n(pre-existing main-tip failures excluded as before).\n\nZone counter (working regex): 95 files at 3beeea9 -> 40 files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from wirelang CLI modules and package docstring (ADR-0072 W5/Reza, T5)\n\nwirelang/cli/*.py and wirelang/__init__.py.\n\n- archive (deleted): the four \"trigger note\" paragraphs in the\n  wirelang package docstring. They recorded which no-op touch was made\n  on which date to force a path-filtered Required-check to fire on\n  three specific PRs. Pure CI-mechanics history, no contract content.\n- keep-scrub: sprint anchors in CLI module docstrings and argparse\n  descriptions replaced by the stable item id (OI-PEFR-7, OI-PEFR-9,\n  OI-PILOT-3) or dropped; \"Mira-Hand\" -> \"operator-hand\",\n  \"Mira-side\" -> \"Operator-side\"; \"stable across Tag-3+\" -> \"stable\".\n\nKnown gap, deliberately not closed here: the module file name\nwirelang/cli/mira_dispatch.py and its launcher bin/wakir-mira-dispatch\nstill carry a persona name. Renaming them touches wirelang/tests/,\ntests/infra/, docs/ and wirelang/persona_engine/cli.py — four zones\nthat are being swept in parallel right now. Listed as an allowlist\ncandidate for archaeology-lint with a follow-up issue for the\ncoordinated rename.\n\nInvariants: AST identical modulo string constants; 17/17 canonical\nschema digests unchanged; pytest wirelang/tests + tests/infra rc=0.\n\nZone counter (working regex): 95 files at 3beeea9 -> 31 files\n(all remaining are wirelang/specs/).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from wirelang spec documents (ADR-0072 W5/Reza, T6)\n\n22 spec documents under wirelang/specs/ (protocol-mirror-seed excluded,\nsee below).\n\nMethod: a line-local pass for tables, code fences and list items, and a\nparagraph-aware pass that joins, scrubs and re-wraps only those prose\nparagraphs that actually contain a stamp (untouched paragraphs stay\nbyte-identical). Line-break hyphenation repaired after the re-wrap.\n\nSubstantive mappings instead of blind deletion:\n- \"**Tag-6 (v0.19.0) is additive relative to Tag-5 (v0.18.2):**\" ->\n  \"**v0.19.0 is additive relative to v0.18.2:**\" — the schema version\n  is the durable anchor, the tag was the calendar anchor.\n- Version-history rows \"| 0.28.0 | ... | Tag-6 lands the **X**\" ->\n  \"| 0.28.0 | ... | Lands the **X**\": the version column already\n  carries the identity.\n- \"All Tag-1 + Tag-3 + Tag-5 + ... surfaces remain byte-identical\" ->\n  \"All previously shipped surfaces remain byte-identical\".\n- Cross-review consensus markers Z-1-K-Sprint-4-{1..4} -> Z-1-K-{1..4}.\n- Agent signature lines (\"— Reza\") removed from six spec documents.\n\nCross-zone one-liner: tests/specs/test_wirelang_spec_v0_4_2_drift_s4_\nreconciliation.py used \"— Reza\" as the terminator of its §9 lookahead.\nThe regex now terminates at end-of-document; the assertions are\nunchanged. Caused by this PR, repaired here, flagged for the tests\nsweep.\n\nKnown gap: wirelang/specs/protocol-mirror-seed/ is untouched. It is a\nbyte-mirror of the observability dashboards and runbooks that belong to\nthe observability sweep, and tests/observability asserts the mirror is\nbyte-identical to its primary. Scrubbing it here would break that\ninvariant; it must move together with the primary. 8 files, allowlist\ncandidate.\n\nInvariants: 17/17 canonical schema digests unchanged; pytest tests/ +\nwirelang/ green except the pre-existing main-tip failures.\n\nZone counter (working regex): 95 files at 3beeea9 -> 31 files, of which\n23 outside protocol-mirror-seed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from the canonical-form, hash, CLI and validator crates (ADR-0072 W5/Reza, T7)\n\nFive protocol crates plus the workspace Cargo.toml:\npersona-canonical-form, persona-canonical-form-yaml, persona-hash,\npersona-cli, persona-validator.\n\n- Doc comments (//!, ///) and // comments: sprint/tag anchors dropped or\n  replaced by the durable anchor (pin name, section number, schema\n  version). \"Mira-Decision\" -> \"Ratified decision\", \"ceo-mandate\" ->\n  \"ratified mandate\", \"Selin-recommendation\" -> \"review recommendation\",\n  \"skizze\" -> \"sketch\", \"Mira-Sandbox\" -> \"the build sandbox\".\n- Workspace Cargo.toml crate registry: the \"Sprint-<Name>-MINI\" crate\n  labels replaced by the Phase-3a item number they already carry, e.g.\n  \"persona-engine-frontmatter-parser : Sprint-Rust-Frontmatter-Parser-\n  MINI (Phase-3a Item 8)\" -> \"... : Phase-3a Item 8\".\n\nNo pub signature touched, no pin constant touched, no test renamed in\nthis group. cargo test for the five crates: 162 passed, 0 failed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from the remaining protocol crates (ADR-0072 W5/Reza, T8)\n\n11 crates not covered by T7: persona-converter, persona-migration,\npersona-migration-resolver, persona-pilot-export,\npersona-engine-{anchor-emitter,anchor-submit-worker,\nfederation-frame-parser,federation-resolver,nats-subjects,\nsvid-workload-identity}.\n\n- Cargo.toml `authors` fields carrying a personal name and address\n  replaced by \"Wakir Labs\"; two package `description` strings that\n  opened with a sprint stamp rewritten to describe the crate.\n- Doc comments (`//!`, `///`) and line comments: sprint/tag anchors\n  dropped or replaced by structural anchors (\"the crate brief\", \"the\n  base\", \"a follow-up\"); cross-references \"<persona> PR #NNN (Tag-NN)\"\n  reduced to \"PR #NNN\"; owning personas replaced by the owning track.\n- \"Welle\" and \"Cutover\" deliberately kept: in ADR-0065/ADR-0066 they\n  are the live migration-wave vocabulary (env-var gate table, welle\n  state files, welle-N smoke docs), not archaeology. Listed as an\n  archaeology-lint allowlist entry in the PR body.\n\nNo behaviour change: comments and package metadata only, no `pub`\nsignature touched, no test renamed. `cargo metadata` parses the\nworkspace.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpxBoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAv30QAEeWFS3mmU2qwyrNZI5h3P8Y\nliua3DXJXTUqvmkXRbbHc028w0nnaNaSrNp2cME/4+lzyNINEMSs2fQLC+iV9+GO\nj1S4irAJOHARZL8BY3/hhE747RhJBB9IBNudcUIHx6jvRJPhBW6YBpI9z54Wx2bC\nQgL7LnkrqBeQh+ZahDlQZspyONF27nvQ8r6EBTmxSh6fAopZ0UGhj7SoHp1lwcR0\nFm4aILBe