9a910b314fa3fba9f37f158b134e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/f6461527ea829a910b314fa3fba9f37f158b134e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/281068747?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs","id":281068747,"login":"wakir-labs","node_id":"U_kgDOEMDEyw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/f39f7b10e335b01ea3f0f9c686c97eada9e50dc0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T20:05:01Z","email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T20:05:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from infra, quadlet, tooling and workflows (ADR-0072 W5/Kai) (#528)\n\n* chore(phase-4): scrub development archaeology from infra, quadlet, compose, config, bin, policies (W5/Kai, pass 1)\n\nMechanical first pass over the Kai zone of the ADR-0072 W5 sweep:\nremoves Tag-N / Sprint-N / Welle / persona-name / AR-Hand tokens from\ncomments, docstrings, README tables, Containerfile LABEL descriptions\nand Quadlet Description= lines. No FROM/digest, unit-name, path,\nExec=, Image=, Volume= or permission change. cosign policy: notes\ntext only.\n\nPass 1 leaves grammatical stubs behind (dangling parentheses,\n\"in  per\", \"Tag-N\"); pass 2 cleans them file by file. Idempotency\ncounter (working regex, files with hits): infra 80 -> 29,\nquadlet 21 -> 3, compose 2 -> 1, config 2 -> 0, bin 11 -> 3,\npolicies 1 -> 1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): scrub development archaeology from tooling (W5/Kai, pass 1)\n\nMechanical first pass over tooling/audit, tooling/ci, tooling/ots,\ntooling/baselines, tooling/ops and the external-verifier helpers:\nTag-N / Sprint-N / Welle / persona-name tokens removed from module\ndocstrings, comments and README text. No code path, constant, CLI\nflag or exit-code change; verify_branch_protection_required_checks_doc.py\nstays functional. Stub cleanup follows in pass 2.\nIdempotency counter tooling: 44 -> 36 files with hits.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): scrub development archaeology from workflow comments (W5/Kai, pass 1)\n\nWorkflow header comments, step names and echo/summary strings lose\nTag-N / Sprint-N / Welle / persona-name tokens. One non-required job\ndisplay name changed: selinux-hermetic-lane\n\"Mutation-equivalence — Amara Zone-X automation\" ->\n\"Mutation-equivalence — QA mutation-test automation\". The 13 required\njob display names are byte-identical to 3beeea9 (verified against the\nlive protection snapshot). No trigger, permissions, action pin or\nfile-name change. All 41 workflows parse. Idempotency counter\n.github: 37 -> 11 files with hits.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): pass 2 — clean scrub stubs in bin, compose, quadlet, policies and workflows (W5/Kai)\n\nRepairs the grammatical stubs pass 1 left behind (dangling\nparentheses, \"the adds the\", \"#).\", leading-space echo strings,\n\"iteration-N\" fragments) and removes the remaining persona-name and\nTag-N references in these paths. Persona names in cross-review notes\nbecome roles (image-pipeline review, Wirelang side, operator).\n\npolicies/cosign-policy-phase-3b.yaml: the required keys landed_pr /\nlanded_tag stay; values become PR numbers verified from git history\n(#203 bridge-audit-writer, #226 for the four ADR-0066 single-binary\nimages) and non-temporal anchors (phase-3b-carrier-image,\nADR-0066-single-binary-image, phase-3a-foundation-closeout). The\n#246 / #250 anchors pinned by tests are unchanged.\n\nWorkflows: comments, step names and echo strings only; the 13\nrequired job display names are byte-identical to 3beeea9; the\nAR-HAND-GATE token format string is unchanged (validated input).\n\nWorking regex now hits 0 files in bin, compose, config, quadlet,\npolicies and .github.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): pass 2 — clean scrub stubs in infra (W5/Kai)\n\nRepairs the pass-1 stubs in infra (dangling parentheses, leading-space\nsentence fragments, \"iteration-N\", \"the operator''s\" substitutions that\nbroke grammar) and removes the remaining persona-name references:\ncross-review tables now name roles (Wirelang, NATS-Schema, OTS /\nImage-Pipeline, V-904 Identity-Bridge, QA), operator recipes address\n\"Operator\" / \"Infra-Owner\" instead of people, the SPIRE-Agent README\nlayer table loses its Sprint/Tag column.\n\nBehaviour unchanged: no FROM/digest, Exec=, Image=, Volume= or config\nvalue change. One error-message text in spire_agent_fed_attest.py\n(\"not in Tag-1 federation pair\" -> \"not in the federation pair\") with\nits matching pytest.raises(match=) in the sibling test. The\npersona-engine stub''s JSON \"successor\" note text changes (no test\npins it). bash -n / py_compile clean on all touched scripts.\n\nWorking regex now hits 0 files in infra (was 80 at 3beeea9).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(phase-4): keep test-pinned history anchors in Containerfile.real, clean scrub stubs (W5/Kai)\n\nThe pass-1 scrub removed Sprint-Pengine-13/14 and Tag-45/48/52 from the\npersona-engine Containerfile.real header. Two tests in the persona-engine\nsuite pin those literals (test_subscribe_mode_bug42.py,\ntest_manifest_0_5_2_final_pre_cutover.py), which turned three required\ncontexts red on the draft PR. Restore the literals in one explicitly\nmarked \"history anchors\" block (documented allowlist candidate; drop\ntogether with the pins in W5 part 2) and replace the leftover scrub\nstubs with version anchors (0.5.0/0.5.1/0.5.2-pre-cutover, 0.3.0-pilot).\n\nNo FROM/digest, LABEL value or RUN change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(phase-4): restore test-pinned literals in tooling helpers, pilot bootstrap and OTS probe step name (W5/Kai)\n\nLocal full-suite run against the pass-1/pass-2 sweep surfaced seven\nfailures caused by this branch (six further failures reproduce on the\n3beeea9 baseline and are not touched here):\n\n- tests/audit t02 (4 files) pin the ''-- Reza'' signature line in\n  tooling/audit/verify_{capability_token_layer_state,\n  cross_substrate_parity_spec,marathon_closeout,welle_7_final_sealing}.py\n  -> signature line restored, annotated as test-pinned.\n- tests/infra/test_pilot_bootstrap_bug_36_37_fixes.py pins\n  ''Reza-Cross-Review'' in infra/spire/federation/wakir-pilot-bootstrap.sh\n  -> literal restored inside the disagree-note comment, annotated.\n- tests/observability/test_ots_probe_workflow_hygiene_tag70.py pins the\n  step name ''Run hermetic Tag-59 test-suite'' in\n  .github/workflows/ots-pre-anchor-activation-probe.yml -> step name\n  restored (step name only, not a job display name / required context);\n  leftover ''#:'' scrub stub in the same block cleaned.\n\nAll literals are documented allowlist candidates for the tests-zone\nsweep (W5 part 2). bash -n and YAML parse verified.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): drop dead bulk-activation and errata-pin helpers, neutralise drift-audit class name (W5/Kai)\n\nRemoves four helper scripts that belonged to closed one-off\noperations and are referenced by no test, workflow or runtime\npath:\n\n- tooling/audit/adr_errata_audit_pin_verifier.py\n- tooling/ci/shared/audit_trail_marker_constants.py\n- tooling/ops/_bulk_activate_required_checks.py\n- tooling/ops/bulk_activate_required_checks.sh\n\nRenames the drift-audit report dataclass to WaveStateMachineDrift.\nThe serialised field name (welle_state_machine_drift) and the\nauthority path stay byte-identical because the audit consumers\npin them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci(required-checks): remove path filters from the three path-filtered required workflows (W5/Kai)\n\nA required status context that never reports leaves the pull request\npending forever. Three workflows that feed required contexts still\ncarried `paths:` filters under both `push` and `pull_request`:\n\n- license-gate.yml       -> License-Hygiene Gate (ADR-0061)\n- tests.yml              -> wirelang suite with rfc8785 + jsonschema,\n                            wirelang suite without rfc8785 / jsonschema\n                            (shadow), production-vs-sandbox drift envelope\n- runtime-acceptance-gates.yml -> runtime acceptance gates\n\nA pull request that touches only paths outside those filters (for\nexample `wirelang/**/*.json`) therefore blocks on a context that can\nnever arrive. The filters are removed; `pull_request: {}` makes the\nunfiltered trigger explicit, matching cross-repo-compat.yml and\nproof-path.yml, which already carry this invariant.\n\nNo job `name:` changes: all 13 required job display-names stay\nbyte-identical.\n\nFollow-up for the aggregator owner (not changed here, `scripts/` is\nout of this zone): the `SUB_WORKFLOWS` inventory in\n`scripts/ci/ci_aggregator.py` still mirrors the now-removed filters\nfor these five rows and should become `(\"**\",)`, together with the\nexpectations in `tests/ci/test_ci_aggregator_workflow.py` (tests 5\nand 7). The stale inventory is not a safety hole - it can only mark a\nsub-workflow `skip-ok` that in fact ran, and each of these contexts is\nenforced directly by branch protection.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(phase-4): scrub remaining prose archaeology from tooling docstrings and comments (W5/Kai, pass 3)\n\nRemoves the last persona-name and calendar-week references from\ndocstring and comment prose in tooling/audit, tooling/ci and\ntooling/ots, and repairs the indentation artefacts the first pass\nleft behind. Domain references become zone or role names\n(WAT-core zone, identity-substrate zone, container-infra zone,\nQA domain) instead of people.\n\nNo code path, constant, CLI flag, exit code or serialised field\nchanges. The remaining regex hits in tooling are data literals and\nsignature lines that tests pin byte-for-byte; they are listed as\nallowlist candidates in the pull-request body and belong to the\ntest-side part of this sweep.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Kai Hoffmann <kai@wakir.dev>","tree":{"sha":"6cf9d282e45a1785f681cb81d2da06fc34114d3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/trees/6cf9d282e45a1785f681cb81d2da06fc34114d3a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/commits/f39f7b10e335b01ea3f0f9c686c97eada9e50dc0","verification":{"payload":"tree 6cf9d282e45a1785f681cb81d2da06fc34114d3a\nparent 3beeea93383c80b2072480a8fe8cacbcd7225a11\nauthor wakir-labs <xypu4r8e@addy.io> 1789329901 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789329901 +0200\n\nchore(phase-4): remove development archaeology from infra, quadlet, tooling and workflows (ADR-0072 W5/Kai) (#528)\n\n* chore(phase-4): scrub development archaeology from infra, quadlet, compose, config, bi