.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/f39f7b10e335b01ea3f0f9c686c97eada9e50dc0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/281068747?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs","id":281068747,"login":"wakir-labs","node_id":"U_kgDOEMDEyw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/3beeea93383c80b2072480a8fe8cacbcd7225a11/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T22:44:42Z","email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T22:44:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci(compat): replace byte-level drift audit with canonical cross-repo compatibility gate (ADR-0072 W4) (#526)\n\n* ci(compat): replace byte-level drift audit with canonical cross-repo compatibility gate (ADR-0072 W4)\n\nNew workflow `.github/workflows/cross-repo-compat.yml`, job display name\n`cross-repo compatibility (protocol ↔ runtime ↔ verify)`, on every PR and\npush to main, no path filter, permissions contents: read, actions pinned\nby commit SHA, clones wakir-protocol@main + wakir-verify@main (depth 1),\nenforcing from day one.\n\ntooling/compat/ (stdlib + rfc8785 + jsonschema):\n- compat_canonical: JCS digest after stripping `x-spdx-*` and\n  `description` at every level (16/16 mirrored schemas identical today;\n  top-level-only stripping leaves 7/16 red on prose).\n- compat_allowlist: time-boxed waivers (`path`, `until`, `tracking`);\n  missing/expired `until` fails the gate.\n- check_compat: schema level (canonical digests, protocol stubs\n  deferred), vector level (protocol proof-path vectors reproduced with\n  wat.merkle and wakir_verify.merkle_proof, tampered case must fail),\n  manifest level (demo-proof manifest vs protocol schema, MANIFEST_VERSION\n  pinned in $id + enum, wakir_verify loader roundtrip, constraint C1\n  version/hour_slot vs envelope/hour, wat.verify.cli rebuilds the sibling\n  path), proof level (proof.json vs protocol inclusion-proof schema with\n  documented fallback to the runtime draft while protocol ships a stub).\n\nRemoved: cross-repo-drift-audit.yml, cross-repo-drift-allowlist-audit.yml,\n.cross-repo-drift-allowlist.yaml, tooling/ci/audit_cross_repo_drift_allowlist.py\nand the tests that pinned them (tests/ci/test_audit_cross_repo_drift_allowlist.py,\ntests/infra/test_cross_repo_drift_{audit,enforce_readiness,state}.py).\nci_aggregator inventory, check-name audit tests, failure-rate tracker and\nthe branch-protection docs now carry the new context; the legacy\noperations docs got a superseded banner. docs/ci/branch-protection-\nrequired-checks.md §2.3 documents the operator context swap.\n\nHermetic tests in tests/compat/ (mock checkouts, no network).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci(compat): time-boxed allowlist bridge for the inclusion-proof mirror\n\nEntry for wirelang/schemas/wakir-inclusion-proof-v1.json until 2026-09-30,\ntracking PR #526, so a deviation between the incoming protocol canon and\nthe runtime draft does not block unrelated runtime PRs; the mirror PR\nremoves it. Unused today (protocol still ships a stub) and reported as\n`warn` by the gate.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci(compat): align with protocol W4 canon — string-valued strip, 5-field allowlist, inclusion-proof mirror, Zone-3 pin\n\n- compat_canonical: strip only *string-valued* `description` and\n  `x-spdx-*` members at every depth (five persona schemas define a\n  `description` property that is contract). Rule now byte-identical to\n  wakir-protocol PR #6 (`sha256(JCS(strip(doc)))`).\n- compat_allowlist: exactly the five mandatory members `repo`, `path`,\n  `reason`, `until`, `tracking` (wakir-labs PR/issue URL), no others.\n- wirelang/schemas/wakir-inclusion-proof-v1.json mirrors the protocol\n  canon from PR #6 (only `x-canonical-home` and `examples` changed vs.\n  the W2 draft); the time-boxed allowlist bridge is therefore removed\n  again (entries: []).\n- tests/fixtures/proof-path-vectors/: passive byte mirror of the\n  protocol vectors (PR #6 state, vector-2 root 1f465e05…) so protocol''s\n  mirror-map can flip `required: true`.\n- check_compat vector level: an embedded `manifest` must validate\n  against the protocol manifest schema, load through\n  wakir_verify.manifest and fold to the vector root.\n- Zone 3 decision (capability_token_hash \"\" vs ^[0-9a-f]{64}$): the\n  schema is right; pilot sentinel becomes the all-zero digest. Producer\n  change (bridge_audit_writer, cross-lang fixtures, Rust) is a tracked\n  follow-up; tests/compat/test_zone3_capability_token_hash.py pins the\n  current state on both sides.\n\nGate: protocol@main b7de631 → ok=25 deferred=2 fail=0; protocol PR #6\nhead 25961b8 → ok=27 deferred=0 fail=0; enum mutation → fail=1, exit 1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9ae4ce3717c66d6ea1c39066a3357b662a8eccb1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/trees/9ae4ce3717c66d6ea1c39066a3357b662a8eccb1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/com