\ntests/infra/test_cross_repo_drift_{audit,enforce_readiness,state}.py).\nci_aggregator inventory, check-name audit tests, failure-rate tracker and\nthe branch-protection docs now carry the new context; the legacy\noperations docs got a superseded banner. docs/ci/branch-protection-\nrequired-checks.md §2.3 documents the operator context swap.\n\nHermetic tests in tests/compat/ (mock checkouts, no network).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci(compat): time-boxed allowlist bridge for the inclusion-proof mirror\n\nEntry for wirelang/schemas/wakir-inclusion-proof-v1.json until 2026-09-30,\ntracking PR #526, so a deviation between the incoming protocol canon and\nthe runtime draft does not block unrelated runtime PRs; the mirror PR\nremoves it. Unused today (protocol still ships a stub) and reported as\n`warn` by the gate.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci(compat): align with protocol W4 canon — string-valued strip, 5-field allowlist, inclusion-proof mirror, Zone-3 pin\n\n- compat_canonical: strip only *string-valued* `description` and\n  `x-spdx-*` members at every depth (five persona schemas define a\n  `description` property that is contract). Rule now byte-identical to\n  wakir-protocol PR #6 (`sha256(JCS(strip(doc)))`).\n- compat_allowlist: exactly the five mandatory members `repo`, `path`,\n  `reason`, `until`, `tracking` (wakir-labs PR/issue URL), no others.\n- wirelang/schemas/wakir-inclusion-proof-v1.json mirrors the protocol\n  canon from PR #6 (only `x-canonical-home` and `examples` changed vs.\n  the W2 draft); the time-boxed allowlist bridge is therefore removed\n  again (entries: []).\n- tests/fixtures/proof-path-vectors/: passive byte mirror of the\n  protocol vectors (PR #6 state, vector-2 root 1f465e05…) so protocol''s\n  mirror-map can flip `required: true`.\n- check_compat vector level: an embedded `manifest` must validate\n  against the protocol manifest schema, load through\n  wakir_verify.manifest and fold to the vector root.\n- Zone 3 decision (capability_token_hash \"\" vs ^[0-9a-f]{64}$): the\n  schema is right; pilot sentinel becomes the all-zero digest. Producer\n  change (bridge_audit_writer, cross-lang fixtures, Rust) is a tracked\n  follow-up; tests/compat/test_zone3_capability_token_hash.py pins the\n  current state on both sides.\n\nGate: protocol@main b7de631 → ok=25 deferred=2 fail=0; protocol PR #6\nhead 25961b8 → ok=27 deferred=0 fail=0; enum mutation → fail=1, exit 1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpdXaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKmsQADjdYqjKp9NnElGZ2n/0FrRW\nGL873eIqac48IKJAhCLL6Hf99NqVYIXaJmyWmJVR6MwmWZmcqt2/ytzPRgIaZmMW\nHpwkmFPejSi8Rt04I0BVwlpkrVLu7eC1l0+XNCcBan/peCNEOWAarrhziZolEV/L\nfkL5W0udGT5SIHljQn74DFryK8BWba1enOeS15qT3BygiYgv5aJNWsbmB55P5iAa\no3722sevl1tSyJxgMI8lNxWyXNuWUgTwwTyadlQKzPhDtdf1yYZrQ/5oOLsZcrM0\nUqkSJEpcQ2NwG3A/Cqs5arpTPPksP6neSLAHDRPFRXQLmaaV4TnsvxZmc0aeVMf2\nTuO5UXcO5RMJTCV45Hr5TjehB9BiGiP1atXp+C4fmq445Ty/6Bypb5tHmkzalpm1\nMO3s2ymHJ/aG0w6wqGUT/q+MSEfTTl0mpjqopiH/JGcepqFesiwcXG6Wowsli2Nu\nDhaSNRmF2jdeJykbDtun8QdYo/kdK24Y+AjGisAEWOB9INJ3kSVJ2ppWX9N8lL5J\nmy/DVYEWPb3szCfZgHq5spAoZ+KYDb/YjQIDb1XpLwkOpOsPDBW2BQNLZWZLQ1Wj\nRl21xM38jM7zLQh3xGZwxQWezg6/HJbIpGT9Ox7dIHYoZoFozfNkQ0YI0Q0NDJv6\nvEkuhwDixfyUtcSPX3EH\n=d5dw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T22:44:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow