"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/6e26d4cc98fd8fecab60e6cf4dd759eeda960b16/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T22:43:53Z","email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T22:43:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci(security): add gitleaks secret-scan gate (ADR-0072 W7) (#525)\n\nPhase 4 Sub-Item 4f (security posture, external review §13).\n\n- .github/workflows/secret-scan.yml: job `secret-scan` on pull_request +\n  push to main, permissions contents: read, fetch-depth 0, checkout pinned\n  by commit SHA (v4.4.0). Downloads gitleaks v8.30.1 release tarball,\n  verifies pinned SHA-256 (551f6fc8...70eb from the release checksums\n  file), runs `gitleaks git --config .gitleaks.toml --redact --exit-code 1`\n  over the full history. Count-only output; no gitleaks-action, no\n  TruffleHog.\n- .gitleaks.toml: default rules + narrow, justified allowlist entries\n  (path AND content shape); reviewed against the 2026-09 history scan.\n- docs/security/secret-scan-2026-09.md: history-scan report for all\n  three repos (counts and classification only, no finding content).\n- resolve-image-pins-ci.yml: permissions audit, contents: write kept with\n  inline rationale (workflow_dispatch-only auto-PR branch push).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0b293d9b89ea0df4008fa28ea5dbaae4b42ac687","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/trees/0b293d9b89ea0df4008fa28ea5dbaae4b42ac687"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/commits/6e26d4cc98fd8fecab60e6cf4dd759eeda960b16","verification":{"payload":"tree 0b293d9b89ea0df4008fa28ea5dbaae4b42ac687\nparent b431f95cf17537c3435ef95ab7d27739631e1822\nauthor wakir-labs <xypu4r8e@addy.io> 1789253033 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 17892