vatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/6e26d4cc98fd8fecab60e6cf4dd759eeda960b16","node_id":"C_kwDOSVv36NoAKDZlMjZkNGNjOThmZDhmZWNhYjYwZTZjZjRkZDc1OWVlZGE5NjBiMTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/b431f95cf17537c3435ef95ab7d27739631e1822","sha":"b431f95cf17537c3435ef95ab7d27739631e1822","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/b431f95cf17537c3435ef95ab7d27739631e1822"}],"sha":"6e26d4cc98fd8fecab60e6cf4dd759eeda960b16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/6e26d4cc98fd8fecab60e6cf4dd759eeda960b16"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/281068747?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs","id":281068747,"login":"wakir-labs","node_id":"U_kgDOEMDEyw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/b431f95cf17537c3435ef95ab7d27739631e1822/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T08:54:44Z","email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T08:54:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci(proof-path): make the proof path a hard CI gate + refresh python:3.13-slim digest pin (ADR-0072 W3) (#523)\n\n* ci(proof-path): make the proof path a hard CI gate + refresh python:3.13-slim digest pin (ADR-0072 W3)\n\nAdds .github/workflows/proof-path.yml (job display name `proof-path`,\npull_request + push:main + workflow_dispatch, no path filter,\npermissions contents:read, actions pinned by SHA). The job installs\nwakir-runtime editable plus wakir-verify at commit 706d3e3, runs\n`make demo-proof` into $RUNNER_TEMP/demo, validates the report with\nscripts/ci/validate_demo_proof_report.py --require-external-verify-ok,\nenforces the driver exit code, shellchecks scripts/demo-proof.sh and\nuploads the report as an artifact.\n\nThe validator is stdlib-only and hard-fails (exit 1) on: wrong schema,\nnot exactly the five canonical steps in order, any `failed`/`not_run`\nstep, external_verify != ok (with the flag), commits.wakir_runtime !=\nGITHUB_SHA, top-level exit_code != 0. 22 hermetic tests in\ntests/ci/test_validate_demo_proof_report.py cover the rules and the\nCLI exit codes, and pin the step list to demo_proof_helpers.STEP_NAMES.\n\ndocs/ci/branch-protection-required-checks.md gains `proof-path` as\nrow 12 (PENDING-OPERATOR, add after first green run on main); the doc\nverifier''s expected row count moves 11 -> 12.\n\nPin refresh: python:3.13-slim was re-pushed upstream on 2026-09-02\n(Docker Hub tag metadata). The three Containerfiles move from\nsha256:e544a7fc...c00a to sha256:9d2e5553...0285, which is what\nskopeo and crane both report in the `digest-verify python:3.13-slim`\njob (run 34567647224) and what the registry HEAD returns for the\nmanifest list. This turns that job green again.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci(proof-path): disable errexit around make demo-proof so the validator step is the visible gate\n\nFirst fault-injection run (34569013343) went red in the demo step and\nskipped the validator: GitHub''s default `bash -e {0}` aborted before\n`set -uo pipefail` (which does not clear -e). Explicit `set +e` fixes\nthe ordering; the driver exit code is still enforced in the following\nstep.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5723293c96f958f3f6b3ea1554edc9217860a273","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/trees/5723293c96f958f3f6b3ea1554edc9217860a273"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/commits/b431f95cf17537c3435ef95ab7d27739631e1822","verification":{"payload":"tree 5723293c96f958f3f6b3ea1554edc9217860a273\nparent 8465c4933eba9607d8843f75e0a0475a524b8f1c\nauthor wakir-labs <xypu4r8e@addy.io> 1789116884 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789116884 +0200\n\nci(proof-path): make the proof path a hard CI gate + refresh python:3.13-slim digest pin (ADR-0072 W3) (#523)\n\n* ci(proof-path): make the proof path a hard CI gate + refresh python:3.13-slim digest pin (ADR-0072 W3)\n\nAdds .github/workflows/proof-path.yml (job display name `proof-path`,\npull_request + push:main + workflow_dispatch, no path filter,\npermissions contents:read, actions pinned by SHA). The job installs\nwakir-runtime editable plus wakir-verify at commit 706d3e3, runs\n`make demo-proof` into $RUNNER_TEMP/demo, validates the report with\nscripts/ci/validate_demo_proof_report.py --require-external-verify-ok,\nenforces the driver exit code, shellchecks scripts/demo-proof.sh and\nuploads the report as an artifact.\n\nThe validator is stdlib-only and hard-fails (exit 1) on: wrong schema,\nnot exactly the five canonical steps in order, any `failed`/`not_run`\nstep, external_verify != ok (with the flag), commits.wakir_runtime !=\nGITHUB_SHA, top-level exit_code != 0. 22 hermetic tests in\ntests/ci/test_validate_demo_proof_report.py cover the rules and the\nCLI exit codes, and pin the step list to demo_proof_helpers.STEP_NAMES.\n\ndocs/ci/branch-protection-required-checks.md gains `proof-path` as\nrow 12 (PENDING-OPERATOR, add after first green run on main); the doc\nverifier''s expected row count moves 11 -> 12.\n\nPin refresh: python:3.13-slim was re-pushed upstream on 2026-09-02\n(Docker Hub tag metadata). The three Containerfiles move from\nsha256:e544a7fc...c00a to sha256:9d2e5553...0285, which is what\nskopeo and crane both report in the `digest-verify python:3.13-slim`\njob (run 34567647224) and what the registry HEAD returns for the\nmanifest list. This turns that job green again.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci(proof-path): disable errexit around make demo-proof so the validator step is the visible gate\n\nFirst fault-injection run (34569013343) went red in the demo step and\nskipped the validator: GitHub''s default `bash -e {0}` aborted before\n`set -uo pipefail` (which does not clear -e). Explicit `set +e` fixes\nthe ordering; the driver exit code is still enforced in the following\nstep.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo8HUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnqQQADGHS0xXBQYh3fJkJEKGOMX6\nb/mQONDP5Ft8KeTS4njDke6Pg+UaUPXHfFp+0SeBYjzc3wS1qXBDZE5GzNyJgFwD\nAqv/s2t8mnBktRLD/f37JIFuGbf1ZJgsDT3VTiZenpnzAh5QPBQOLIj3gDFtT7IY\nQcGpDD2lgEIVbd2SDM4ZfG6++rdOuZOlS1c0p74rKrh8PH+7M1zF5CuLs5jqvo7e\nQlU+KhIW5J/4U2MXjHtx+ck+/xwo9cd1rdz5AXeHNlwaCrg7e810hAF8/HC3zvSF\nJzqDFHy+u21D8HEfpmAAqK/th9gokjbmUHMYQ/HoU2kLstAscooMx5rCLtWGxlvx\nh5VzJpbnz53n/xdCDXT2eeMOqD8b0O4GKXBLlYNoJrbEIe4pTObzR65iBt2xxeSH\n/OzTXcxXhPNycuX5LNOPj9268fIA2z1wgJFkjgkZ/KjaXryQRhk/PTtQwLuhOldh\n7uM/hh5DHvvmyE7r7rfV4N1JKljIx33JM2tHcAEkAA4FvhTnBCcynTIXe20Ar9eJ\nALpaZNc6X0mDytjaPOmOUeppvG0uSXvKa/Z6J0HrwvHSNAKCvPlrAcyRx+3kts74\n6e75dfHmAlCXrJj9l0xM3cT2Ay6I7XT5DGVEj/+Z4yvsBNKVD5DEiHL8g6TGSuXx\neBJpnhk0w7XY+t9v2N+n\n=MCd5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-11T08:54:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/b431f95cf17537c3435ef95ab7d27739631e1822","node_id":"C_kwDOSVv36NoAKGI0MzFmOTVjZjE3NTM3YzM0MzVlZjk1YWI3ZDI3NzM5NjMxZTE4MjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/8465c4933eba9607d8843f75e0a0475a524b8f1c","sha":"8465c4933eba9607d8843f75e0a0475a524b8f1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/8465c4933eba9607d8843f75e0a0475a524b8f1c"}],"sha":"b431f95cf17537c3435ef95ab7d27739631e1822","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/b431f95cf17537c3435ef95ab7d27739631e1822"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/281068747?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs","id":281068747,"login":"wakir-labs","node_id":"U_kgDOEMDEyw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/8465c4933eba9607d8843f75e0a0475a524b8f1c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T05:52:35Z","email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T05:52:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(demo-proof): seal proof path driver — rc propagation, JSON assembly, library-based external verify (ADR-0072 W2) (#521)\n\nSeal `make demo-proof` (ADR-0072 sub-item 4a, fix list F1-F13):\n\n- F1/F11: no bash-side JSON. Step records are built and validated by\n  the Python helper (`emit-step`); the `\"${4:-{}}\"` default is gone.\n- F2/F9: `\"${step}\" || rc=$?` instead of `if ! ${step}`; a failed\n  step now short-circuits and the process exits 10.\n- F3: drop jq entirely. bash + python3 is the whole requirement.\n- F4: report always carries all five steps in fixed order; steps\n  after a failure are `not_run` with a reason.\n- F5: step 5 verifies through the wakir-verify library\n  (`wakir_verify.manifest`, `wakir_verify.merkle_proof`); `skipped`\n  with reason when not importable. No CLI probe, no `--help` stub.\n- F6: ONLINE=1 without DEMO_PROOF_OTS_PROOF is an explicit skip.\n- F7: proof.json is a `wakir-inclusion-proof/v1` document with\n  sibling hashes and side markers; schema draft under\n  wirelang/schemas/ (canonical copy goes to wakir-protocol).\n- F8: exit 0 unless a step failed; skipped no longer fails the run.\n- F10/F13: README and runbook updated, development archaeology\n  removed from the touched files.\n- F12: portable mktemp form.\n\nTests: 25 in tests/scripts/test_demo_proof.py (13 new), including\nfault injection via DEMO_PROOF_FAIL_STEP (test mode only), a\npoison-jq run, schema validation and stdlib-only root recomputation\nover a three-leaf sibling path.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fce0cf8dadfbb864ea63066689f8e941ccd0677e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/trees/fce0cf8dadfbb864ea63066689f8e941ccd0677e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/commits/8465c4933eba9607d8843f75e0a0475a524b8f1c","verification":{"payload":"tree fce0cf8dadfbb864ea63066689f8e941ccd0677e\nparent 3e0d64fca1ed5ebceab9d951a8f22a910770e4ef\nauthor wakir-labs <xypu4r8e@addy.io> 1789105955 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789105955 +0200\n\nfix(demo-proof): seal proof path driver — rc propagation, JSON assembly, library-based external verify (ADR-0072 W2) (#521)\n\nSeal `make demo-proof` (ADR-0072 sub-item 4a, fix list F1-F13):\n\n- F1/F11: no bash-side JSON. Step records are built and validated by\n  the Python helper (`emit-step`); the `\"${4:-{}}\"` default is gone.\n- F2/F9: `\"${step}\" || rc=$?` instead of `if ! ${step}`; a failed\n  step now short-circuits and the process exits 10.\n- F3: drop jq entirely. bash + python3 is the whole requirement.\n- F4: report always carries all five steps in fixed order; steps\n  after a failure are `not_run` with a reason.\n- F5: step 5 verifies through the wakir-verify library\n  (`wakir_verify.manifest`, `wakir_verify.merkle_proof`); `skipped`\n  with reason when not importable. No CLI probe, no `--help` stub.\n- F6: ONLINE=1 without DEMO_PROOF_OTS_PROOF is an explicit skip.\n- F7: proof.json is a `wakir-inclusion-proof/v1` document with\n  sibling hashes and side markers; schema draft under\n  wirelang/schemas/ (canonical copy goes to wakir-protocol).\n- F8: exit 0 unless a step failed; skipped no longer fails the run.\n- F10/F13: README and runbook updated, development archaeology\n  removed from the touched files.\n- F12: portable mktemp form.\n\nTests: 25 in tests/scripts/test_demo_proof.py (13 new), including\nfault injection via DEMO_PROOF_FAIL_STEP (test mode only), a\npoison-jq run, schema validation and stdlib-only root recomputation\nover a three-leaf sibling path.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo5cjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAe4QQAAz7nrPmJiG86BhE3GleQHA2\nNYdXfEcxH8VU1o87aJYcsZsKIAueQuUj6qGCxWVQN0qjc4G5QRrWVxfsI03Al5ZR\n7/jbKCZguUMNsoRytscaTBqx5vgdejlasXhB1ss9hXNGGbPfyV6Ab7yre02RoHCW\nXUq1onuxReGNs0XXWV2Na1ME+gHSYoDHy2OHThv7kLhjTnW40WXLMSP9x2LW6k8f\n8Ph1QBX+1Q1ciwgdAOa2PisUNvIhnqilO4NAUKQtUQwC0k5E/flKXq0E+QdmA83q\ndVtzWSNRg17/W6S/53LlQedUPUKF6tPifNE3usGYBffKokG/GKIvTcZu6jbLFoOO\nOMB9qjPxYJlFYHmlNLjtLBi9ZL+zbormf3DI7vFid3RFsGb6roX6Uey/cMOiu3+l\nvUSmd/d/dU/K+j