e_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/d1f46ce377f0a9b9f8d3fdaeb656a90f81b1e9c8","node_id":"C_kwDOSVv36NoAKGQxZjQ2Y2UzNzdmMGE5YjlmOGQzZmRhZWI2NTZhOTBmODFiMWU5Yzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/ee912fc7799af6c690089d6fbb110deb84c05fc4","sha":"ee912fc7799af6c690089d6fbb110deb84c05fc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/ee912fc7799af6c690089d6fbb110deb84c05fc4"}],"sha":"d1f46ce377f0a9b9f8d3fdaeb656a90f81b1e9c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/d1f46ce377f0a9b9f8d3fdaeb656a90f81b1e9c8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/281068747?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs","id":281068747,"login":"wakir-labs","node_id":"U_kgDOEMDEyw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/ee912fc7799af6c690089d6fbb110deb84c05fc4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-20T12:13:24Z","email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-20T12:13:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"cutover(welle-2): flip svid_workload_identity default backend python → rust (#509)\n\n* cutover(welle-2): flip svid_workload_identity default backend python → rust (tag-80)\n\nPhase 3c Welle-2 Cutover per ADR-0065 + ADR-0066, analog Welle-1\n(#508 merged 084d083c).\n\nSubstanz-Patch:\n  - wirelang/persona_engine/rust_backend_switch.py\n    _validate_svid_workload_identity_backend: default PYTHON → RUST\n  - wirelang/tests/persona_engine/test_rust_backend_switch.py\n    3 svid-Tests angepasst (SVID01 unset, SVID07 empty-string,\n    SVID10 per-decision-logging)\n  - scripts/persona-engine/boot-self-test.py\n    RUST_DEFAULT_DOMAINS_POST_CUTOVER += \"svid_workload_identity\"\n\nLokal-Pytest: 12/12 svid-Tests + alle boot-self-test-checks grün.\n\nValidation-Workflow: phase-3c-welle-2-validation.yml Run 26161326459\nparallel ausgeführt — sollte ready_for_live_smoke=true ergeben\n(analog Welle-1 v4 Run 26160817746).\n\nWelle-3 (bridge_audit_writer) folgt nächste.\n\nRefs ADR-0065 Welle-2, ADR-0066 Phase-3c-Cutover-Plan,\ndocs/operations/phase-3c-welle-2-runbook.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Mira Kessler (CEO Sandbox-Operator-Hand)\n\n* cutover(welle-2): also patch test_engine_and_cli.py svid bin_path assertion\n\nWelle-2-Cutover macht svid_workload_identity rust-default. Resolver\nprobes den DEFAULT_RUST_SVID_WORKLOAD_IDENTITY_BIN-Pfad bevor er auf\npython fallt — bin_path im decision-record ist NICHT mehr None,\nsondern resolved zum kanonischen Pfad\n\"/opt/wakir/bin/wakir-persona-engine-svid-workload-identity\".\n\ntest_engine_boot_records_nine_backend_decisions asserted\n``bin_path is None`` für svid — wird mit Welle-2-Flip rot. Patch:\nexakter Pfad-Match statt None-Match.\n\nPattern wiederholt sich für Welle-3 (bridge_audit_writer Z. 260) und\nWelle-6 (subscribe_loop Z. 197) — folgen analog im jeweiligen Welle-PR.\n\nWelle-5 (fsm) + Welle-7 (recovery) haben keine bin_path-Assertion im\nengine-test, daher nicht betroffen. Welle-4 (state_backing) ist\nlazy-resolved und nicht als attribute asserted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Mira Kessler (CEO Sandbox-Operator-Hand)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Kai Hoffmann <kai@wakir.dev>","tree":{"sha":"463a19d3b073179c706efbd13099cbb2440893ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/trees/463a19d3b073179c706efbd13099cbb2440893ff"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/commits/ee912fc7799af6c690089d6fbb110deb84c05fc4","verification":{"payload":"tree 463a19d3b073179c706efbd13099cbb2440893ff\nparent 084d083cf05843b2dc6a3be64cd249427585c640\nauthor wakir-labs <xypu4r8e@addy.io> 1779279204 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779279204 +0200\n\ncutover(welle-2): flip svid_workload_identity default backend python → rust (#509)\n\n* cutover(welle-2): flip svid_workload_identity default backend python → rust (tag-80)\n\nPhase 3c Welle-2 Cutover per ADR-0065 + ADR-0066, analog Welle-1\n(#508 merged 084d083c).\n\nSubstanz-Patch:\n  - wirelang/persona_engine/rust_backend_switch.py\n    _validate_svid_workload_identity_backend: default PYTHON → RUST\n  - wirelang/tests/persona_engine/test_rust_backend_switch.py\n    3 svid-Tests angepasst (SVID01 unset, SVID07 empty-string,\n    SVID10 per-decision-logging)\n  - scripts/persona-engine/boot-self-test.py\n    RUST_DEFAULT_DOMAINS_POST_CUTOVER += \"svid_workload_identity\"\n\nLokal-Pytest: 12/12 svid-Tests + alle boot-self-test-checks grün.\n\nValidation-Workflow: phase-3c-welle-2-validation.yml Run 26161326459\nparallel ausgeführt — sollte ready_for_live_smoke=true ergeben\n(analog Welle-1 v4 Run 26160817746).\n\nWelle-3 (bridge_audit_writer) folgt nächste.\n\nRefs ADR-0065 Welle-2, ADR-0066 Phase-3c-Cutover-Plan,\ndocs/operations/phase-3c-welle-2-runbook.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Mira Kessler (CEO Sandbox-Operator-Hand)\n\n* cutover(welle-2): also patch test_engine_and_cli.py svid bin_path assertion\n\nWelle-2-Cutover macht svid_workload_identity rust-default. Resolver\nprobes den DEFAULT_RUST_SVID_WORKLOAD_IDENTITY_BIN-Pfad bevor er auf\npython fallt — bin_path im decision-record ist NICHT mehr None,\nsondern resolved zum kanonischen Pfad\n\"/opt/wakir/bin/wakir-persona-engine-svid-workload-identity\".\n\ntest_engine_boot_records_nine_backend_decisions asserted\n``bin_path is None`` für svid — wird mit Welle-2-Flip rot. Patch:\nexakter Pfad-Match statt None-Match.\n\nPattern wiederholt sich für Welle-3 (bridge_audit_writer Z. 260) und\nWelle-6 (subscribe_loop Z. 197) — folgen analog im jeweiligen Welle-PR.\n\nWelle-5 (fsm) + Welle-7 (recovery) haben keine bin_path-Assertion im\nengine-test, daher nicht betroffen. Welle-4 (state_backing) ist\nlazy-resolved und nicht als attribute asserted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Mira Kessler (CEO Sandbox-Operator-Hand)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Kai Hoffmann <kai@wakir.dev>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqDaVkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAogYQAANpcrfdJuCQo6+mITCkWGrY\nMZVIaGduYdOzTSXUnInpsxByJfq9w952TiLzgcwajcdn7SgBYPpilqVHyWmZX82g\nNxqCIMIu0r4xnGxhU/EVaw9IZaKHCu8Omlx/VEmIhu+YUHNU6GtX7OsVTiTDpBqS\nY1R2tiGyvLGGbTwpRBq+baxKaRHEBkBhCM2pgUQd0SOM5rutr+0vnhxpQc6/5UZI\nTOz4Vjq51zJrt8P8CDUd45sX3iTT9Enh3HZuJ79q7WSZfhYlX865Cd06CJTfVPXV\n4VITLDaAjnr1qrek48udIIbFZcm7Zgnlv86lZ5/JTSXOo/rCCYxFAE9BPnkR2yB5\n2CHnt7CJJPVjeb0QqRcuQ7554CXO5aOHDGcGa7K+a+gzuhQwB/gDIbl/syXkjGUQ\nryHfEDmfRIEOcgH/TVMsO6jPy2hQujWoSPxUu7xyWBEv2yr+A3Dv7ywBi6DbiosT\n3Xk5b2w3Oo24pmLXeQnBowLg4c+PSQ7cJhz9P34z77te0lrPGpTXlao6iVkcisr2\nN7EW2Io+Uv9vm89lZYxl2lr9n3KPR2xmzA0GBUwIlLGvOy4DprpSW5eYjKMgW06L\nJ+I1jaX9CxpSTUajc4N4HS9VEp57aP7Y6cpcrbrr12lmMwAlbYUN0arK+GGkcr2E\nxjVm7G2/8ACtDDbbnzrE\n=Gn14\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-20T12:13:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"