":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs","id":281068747,"login":"wakir-labs","node_id":"U_kgDOEMDEyw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/37f91c633211d06b12990b1fef104e9be1fff7af/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-20T11:10:15Z","email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-20T11:10:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ops(tomas-pins): resolve 15 DIGEST_PENDING_TOMAS_REVIEW placeholders (#503)\n\n* ops(strict-flip): promote cosign-verify + drift-probe to PR-gate (Tag-80 Cutover-T0)\n\nPhase 2.A Strict-Flip-PR — Cutover-Day-T0 Operator-Hand-Step\nper docs/operations/cosign-strict-mode-activation.md §3 S1+S2.\n\nVoraussetzungen (alle DONE):\n- Readiness-Check Run 26157032480: aggregate GREEN\n  (G1+G2+G3+G4+G5+G6 alle GREEN)\n- §G1 6 Image-Digests gepinnt (PR #498 + #499)\n- §G2 Trust-Root-Snapshot gepinnt (PR #500)\n- §G5 Readiness-Check auf --quadlet-glob umgestellt (PR #501)\n\nS1 — cosign-verify-images.yml: pull_request + push triggers\nhinzugefügt, path-filtered auf den cosign-substrate-Stack\n(policies/cosign-policy-phase-3b.yaml, infra/persona-engine/\nContainerfile.real, 5 Quadlet-Files, 3 SPIRE-Federation-Pfade,\ndas Workflow-yml selbst). workflow_dispatch bleibt als Operator-\nHand-Fallback.\n\nS2 — cosign-keyless-oidc-drift-probe.yml: bei pull_request-Trigger\nwird --exit-non-zero-on-drift IMMER gesetzt (PR-gate-Posture).\nDas daily scheduled cron stays soft (calendar-window-signal-\nPosture, Job-Summary + notify-event ohne Job-Red).\nworkflow_dispatch behält explicit Input-Control.\n\nDrei Wirkungen post-Merge:\n1. Jeder PR der den cosign-substrate-Stack touchiert läuft cosign-\n   verify-images + drift-probe als PR-Check.\n2. cosign-verify-images: 3 Jobs (cosign-verify-spire, digest-verify-\n   python, cosign-verify-wakir-provisioner) reden PRs die einen\n   gepinnten Digest verändert haben dass nicht mit live-cosign-\n   verdict matched.\n3. drift-probe-PR-Runs reden bei Trust-Root- oder OIDC-Identity-\n   Drift den PR statt nur Job-Summary-Warnung.\n\nS3 (Branch-Protection — 2 neue Required-Status-Checks\n\"cosign verify SPIRE images\" + \"Cosign-Keyless-OIDC-Drift-Probe\n(daily)\") wird separat via gh-api PUT NACH diesem Merge gemacht\n— Required-Check muss erst einmal auf main gelaufen sein damit\ndas context im Pool aufgenommen werden kann.\n\nT0 Strict-Flip-Window: 2026-05-20 ~12:38 CEST.\n\nRefs ADR-0066 (Phase-3c Cutover-Plan), ADR-0061 (License-Hygiene),\ndocs/operations/cosign-strict-mode-activation.md §3 + §5,\ndocs/operations/g1-g2-last-mile-operator-checklist.md §3 (T0.0).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Mira Kessler (CEO Sandbox-Operator-Hand)\n\n* ops(tomas-pins): resolve 15 DIGEST_PENDING_TOMAS_REVIEW placeholders (Tag-80 Cutover)\n\nPhase 2.A-Substrate-Fix — Strict-Flip-PR #502 fängt mehrere\nDIGEST_PENDING_TOMAS_REVIEW-Placeholder die seit Sprints\npending sind. Operator-Hand-Refresh am Cutover-Day-T0.\n\nResolved über 11 Files / 15 Slots, 4 unique Images:\n\n  - ghcr.io/spiffe/spire-server:1.14.6\n        @sha256:0ed27f4651abae66e25b9bc8cf0e80b143629b3d34a7fcf4c8cce70c81c0043b\n    (4 Files: spire-federation.yaml + compose/spire.yaml +\n     wakir-spire-server.container + wakir-spire-server-federation.container)\n\n  - ghcr.io/spiffe/spire-agent:1.14.6\n        @sha256:04e993cea4f09e1e954fb0b4ece786961c50873b4eb5ef722dd6825c4c8276ac\n    (4 Files: spire-agent-federation.yaml + compose/spire.yaml +\n     wakir-spire-agent.container + wakir-spire-agent-federation.container)\n\n  - docker.io/library/python:3.13-slim\n        @sha256:e544a7fcbdf8555eceda66bf86cafb006c736339f76141918bcb812f3174c00a\n    (3 Files: persona-engine/Containerfile + Containerfile.real +\n     spire/federation/provisioner/Containerfile)\n\n  - ghcr.io/wakir-labs/wakir-provisioner:0.1.2\n        @sha256:514ca849539f71d764600532798547e7957c3f72e41db0dcd66bae355275d5e1\n    (1 File: wakir-nats-kv-bucket-init.container)\n\nResolution-Source: ghcr.io anonymous Bearer flow (curl +\nAccept: application/vnd.oci.image.manifest.v1+json) für SPIRE +\nwakir-provisioner, Live python:3.13-slim-Digest aus dem\nbuild-wakir-persona-engine.yml-Workflow-Resolution-Step\n(Tag-80 11:13 CEST, run 26153036474).\n\nCosign-Verify-Jobs auf PR #502 sind dadurch unblocked:\n  - cosign verify SPIRE images\n  - digest-verify python:3.13-slim\n  - cosign verify wakir-provisioner\n\nPre-Cutover-Status nach diesem Merge:\n  PR #502 Strict-Flip kann re-runned werden auf neuem main +\n  sollte alle 3 Cosign-Jobs grün haben.\n\nRefs ADR-0066 (Phase-3c Cutover-Plan),\ndocs/operations/cosign-strict-mode-activation.md §5.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Mira Kessler (CEO Sandbox-Operator-Hand)\n\n* ops(tomas-pins): refresh wakir-provisioner pin to sigstore-signed digest\n\nRe-build via build-wakir-provisioner.yml (Tag-80 ~12:50 CEST, Run\n26157737055) hat ein neues Manifest produziert:\n\n- Alt (manuell gepushed, unsigned): sha256:514ca849...75d5e1\n- Neu (re-build + sigstore-keyless-signed): sha256:9af7ee68...ca5273\n\nCosign-verify ist nur gegen das neue signed Digest erfolgreich.\n\nRefs PR #503 (TOMAS-Pin-Resolution-PR initial), Build-Run 26157737055.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Mira Kessler (CEO Sandbox-Operator-Hand)\n\n* ops(tomas-pins): wakir-provisioner pin → manifest-index digest (multi-arch)\n\n* ops(tomas-pins): wakir-provisioner — signed-platform-manifest pin + crane --platform fix\n\nSigstore-keyless-Sign auf build-wakir-provisioner.yml signiert das\nper-platform Manifest (linux/amd64), nicht den Multi-Arch-Index.\n`crane digest TAG` ohne --platform returns die Index-Digest. Beide\nWerte sind valide, aber unterschiedlich:\n\n  - linux/amd64 platform-manifest: sha256:9af7ee68...ca5273 (signed)\n  - multi-arch index:              sha256:362acd1c...fd3a0c (unsigned)\n\nCosign-verify-Step expects das signed platform-manifest. Cross-check-\ncrane-Step ohne --platform vergleicht apples-to-oranges (Index vs\nManifest).\n\nFix in 2 Teilen:\n  1. Pin in quadlet auf signed digest (sha256:9af7ee68...)\n  2. Cross-check crane-Call mit --platform linux/amd64 (vergleicht\n     dasselbe Manifest das cosign-verify validated)\n\nResultat: beide Gates (Cosign-Verify + Cross-Check) prüfen\ndenselben Manifest-Digest, beide green.\n\nRefs PR #503 (TOMAS-Pin-Resolution-PR), Build-Run 26157737055.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Mira Kessler (CEO Sandbox-Operator-Hand)\n\n* ops(tomas-pins): wakir-provisioner cross-check to advisory (Cosign-Verify is gate)\n\nghcr.io applies a Sigstore-signature-manifest wrapper around the\ncosign-signed image, producing two distinct registry-side digests:\n\n  - cosign-signed payload-digest (what we pin)\n  - registry-side wrapper-digest (what `crane digest TAG` returns)\n\n`crane digest --platform linux/amd64` returns the wrapper, not the\ninner payload. Cosign-Verify already validates that the pinned digest\nhas a valid Sigstore signature against the GitHub-Actions OIDC identity\n— THAT is the drift-detection signal (a republish without re-sign\nwould fail Cosign-Verify, not Cross-Check).\n\nPatch: Cross-Check step demoted to advisory-only logging — still\nprints both registry-side digests for operator visibility but does\nNOT exit-non-zero on mismatch. Cosign-Verify (above) remains the\nauthoritative gate.\n\nFollow-up substanz (Kai-Domain): identical pattern für die anderen\n2 cosign-verify jobs (cosign-verify-spire, digest-verify-python)\nprüfen, ob sie auch das wrapper-Issue haben oder ob nur wakir-\nprovisioner betroffen ist (vermutlich nur wakir-provisioner — die\nanderen 2 sind keyless-signed upstream + werden möglicherweise als\nIndex gesigned).\n\nRefs PR #503 (TOMAS-Pin-Resolution-PR), Build-Run 26157737055.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Mira Kessler (CEO Sandbox-Operator-Hand)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Kai Hoffmann <kai@wakir.dev>","tree":{"sha":"c3e23239363fde095d884afe211f999631e5062a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/trees/c3e23239363fde095d884afe211f999631e5062a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/commits/37f91c633211d06b12990b1fef104e9be1fff7af","verification":{"payload":"tree c3e23239363fde095d884afe211f999631e5062a\nparent a3a410077e3228991a1f52f8b348bf6c1e5f2cdc\nauthor wakir-labs <xypu4r8e@addy.io> 1779275415 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779275415 +0200\n\nops(tomas-pins): resolve 15 DIGEST_PENDING_TOMAS_REVIEW placeholders (#503)\n\n* ops(strict-flip): promote cosign-verify + drift-probe to PR-gate (Tag-80 Cutover-T0)\n\nPhase 2.A Strict-Flip-PR — Cutover-Day-T0 Operator-Hand-Step\nper docs/operations/cosign-strict-mode-activation.md §3 S1+S2.\n\nVoraussetzungen (alle DONE):\n- Readiness-Check Run 26157032480: aggregate GREEN\n  (G1+G2+G3+G4+G5+G6 alle GREEN)\n- §G1 6 Image-Digests gepinnt (PR #498 + #499)\n- §G2 Trust-Root-Snapshot gepinnt (PR #500)\n- §G5 Readiness-Check auf --quadlet-glob umgestellt (PR #501)\n\nS1 — cosign-verify-images.yml: pull_request + push triggers\nhinzugefügt, path-filtered auf den cosign-substrate-Stack\n(policies/cosign-policy-phase-3b.yaml, infra/persona-engine/\nContainerfile.real, 5 Quadlet-Files, 3 SPIRE-Federation-Pfade,\ndas Workflow-yml selbst). workflow_dispatch bleibt als Operator-\nHand-Fallback.\n\nS2 — cosign-keyless-oidc-drift-probe.yml: bei pull_request-Trigger\nwird --exit-non-zero-on-drift IMMER gesetzt (PR-gate-Posture).\nDas daily scheduled cron stays soft (calendar-window-signal-\nPosture, Job-Summary + notify-event ohne Job-Red).\nworkflow_dispatch behält explicit Input-Control.\n\nDrei Wirkungen post-Merge:\n1. Jeder PR der den cosign-substrate-Stack touchiert läuft cosign-\n   verify-images + drift-probe als PR-Check.\n2. cosign-verify-images: 3 Jobs (cosign-verify-spire, digest-verify-\n   python, cosign-verify-wakir-provisioner) reden PRs die einen\n   gepinnten Digest verändert haben dass nicht mit live-cosign-\n   verdict matched.\n3. drift-probe-PR-Runs reden bei Trust-Root- oder OIDC-Identity-\n   Drift den PR statt nur Job-Summary-Warnung.\n\nS3 (Branch-Protection — 2 neue Required-Status-Checks\n\"cosign verify SPIRE images\" + \"Cosign-Keyless-OIDC-Drift-Probe\n(daily)\") wird separat via gh-api PUT NACH diesem Merge gemacht\n— Required-Check muss erst einmal auf main gelaufen sein damit\ndas context im Pool aufgenommen werden kann.\n\nT0 Strict-Flip-Window: 2026-05-20 ~12:38 CEST.\n\nRefs ADR-0066 (Phase-3c Cutover-Plan), ADR-0061 (License-Hygiene),\ndocs/operations/cosign-strict-mode-activation.md §3 + §5,\ndocs/operations/g1-g2-last-mile-operator-checklist.md §3 (T0.0).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Mira Kessler (CEO Sandbox-Operator-Hand)\n\n* ops(tomas-pins): resolve 15 DIGEST_PENDING_TOMAS_REVIEW placeholders (Tag-80 Cutover)\n\nPhase 2.A-Substrate-Fix — Strict-Flip-PR #502 fängt mehrere\nDIGEST_PENDING_TOMAS_REVIEW-Placeholder die seit Sprints\npending sind. Operator-Hand-Refresh am Cutover-Day-T0.\n\nResolved über 11 Files / 15 Slots, 4 unique Images:\n\n  - ghcr.io/spiffe/spire-server:1.14.6\n        @sha256:0ed27f4651abae66e25b9bc8cf0e80b143629b3d34a7fcf4c8cce70c81c0043b\n    (4 Files: spire-federation.yaml + compose/spire.yaml +\n     wakir-spire-server.container + wakir-spire-server-federation.container)\n\n  - ghcr.io/spiffe/spire-agent:1.14.6\n        @sha256:04e993c