-05-19). Seven alerts\nsurface the Marathon-Closeout-Layer-Verdicts that aggregate the\nper-welle final-sealing outcomes (Welle-1..7) into THREE layer-\nverdicts plus the Phase-3-COMPLETE-Marker-Fire signal:\n\n  * WakirMarathonCloseoutReady       (info)\n  * WakirMarathonCloseoutPartial     (warning)\n  * WakirMarathonCloseoutDefect      (page)\n  * WakirMarathonFinalIntact         (info)\n  * WakirMarathonFinalDrift          (warning)\n  * WakirMarathonFinalDefect         (page)\n  * WakirPhase3CompleteMarkerFire    (info)\n\nNew trinary routing-class family marathon-closeout-{info,warning,\npage} added to the bridge (VALID_ROUTING_CLASSES,\nROUTING_CLASS_CHANNELS, ROUTING_CLASS_ESCALATION_SECONDS). Channel\nsets:\n  marathon-closeout-info    -> ntfy:ar-hand-info, activity-log:append\n  marathon-closeout-warning -> ntfy:ar-hand, activity-log:append\n  marathon-closeout-page    -> pagerduty:sre-oncall, ntfy:ar-hand,\n                               activity-log:append\n\nSource recording rules (Reza PR #479 Tag-76 Closeout-Aggregator;\nTomás PR #484 Phase-3-COMPLETE-Marker-Audit-Bundle):\n  * wakir_marathon_closeout_verdict_class (0/1/2)\n  * wakir_marathon_final_verdict_class (0/1/2)\n  * wakir_phase_3_complete_marker_fire (0/1, latched)\n\nCross-repo-mirror byte-equal (wirelang/specs/protocol-mirror-seed/).\n\nNoa-Tag-76-Lehre: _TAG78_MARATHON_CLOSEOUT_ALERTS pin-set added to\ntests/ci/test_welle_n_specific_alerts.py with cross-layer-\ncontamination guard (Tag-78 alerts MUST NOT appear in welle-N\ngroups). _TAG78_GROUP_CONTRACT pins the marathon-closeout-routing\ngroup to exactly 7 rules at 30s interval.\n\nGroup-count pins bumped 20 -> 21 in\ntests/ci/test_phase_3_marathon_failure_mode_alerts.py and\ntests/ci/test_pre_existing_failures_fix_tag68.py.\n\nTest surface: 35 tests in\ntests/observability/test_marathon_closeout_routing_tag78.py\n(YAML surface, bridge catalog, mirror equality, cross-reference\nchecks, regression guards). All 4082 observability+ci tests pass.\n\nCo-authored-by: Noa Bergstroem <noa@wakir.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f8a360734f6fa4305373ea04026cb83edef54e0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/trees/f8a360734f6fa4305373ea04026cb83edef54e0a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/commits/8d50124b3a6c8c6f9d4c06b905bfda58ab4dfc7a","verification":{"payload":"tree f8a360734f6fa4305373ea04026cb83edef54e0a\nparent 04e7ee0b78fc8569fbb5deebbd1b3c43716a5789\nauthor wakir-labs <xypu4r8e@addy.io> 1779218338 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779218338 +0200\n\nfeat(observability): Tag-78 Marathon-Closeout-Alert-Routing-Erweiterung (Noa SRE, 35 tests) (#495)\n\nContinuous-Mode-Marathon-Polish (Tag-78, 2026-05-19). Seven alerts\nsurface the Marathon-Closeout-Layer-Verdicts that aggregate the\nper-welle final-sealing outcomes (Welle-1..7) into THREE layer-\nverdicts plus the Phase-3-COMPLETE-Marker-Fire signal:\n\n  * WakirMarathonCloseoutReady       (info)\n  * WakirMarathonCloseoutPartial     (warning)\n  * WakirMarathonCloseoutDefect      (page)\n  * WakirMarathonFinalIntact         (info)\n  * WakirMarathonFinalDrift          (warning)\n  * WakirMarathonFinalDefect         (page)\n  * WakirPhase3CompleteMarkerFire    (info)\n\nNew trinary routing-class family marathon-closeout-{info,warning,\npage} added to the bridge (VALID_ROUTING_CLASSES,\nROUTING_CLASS_CHANNELS, ROUTING_CLASS_ESCALATION_SECONDS). Channel\nsets:\n  marathon-closeout-info    -> ntfy:ar-hand-info, activity-log:append\n  marathon-closeout-warning -> ntfy:ar-hand, activity-log:append\n  marathon-closeout-page    -> pagerduty:sre-oncall, ntfy:ar-hand,\n                               activity-log:append\n\nSource recording rules (Reza PR #479 Tag-76 Closeout-Aggregator;\nTomás PR #484 Phase-3-COMPLETE-Marker-Audit-Bundle):\n  * wakir_marathon_closeout_verdict_class (0/1/2)\n  * wakir_marathon_final_verdict_class (0/1/2)\n  * wakir_phase_3_complete_marker_fire (0/1, latched)\n\nCross-repo-mirror byte-equal (wirelang/specs/protocol-mirror-seed/).\n\nNoa-Tag-76-Lehre: _TAG78_MARATHON_CLOSEOUT_ALERTS pin-set added to\ntests/ci/test_welle_n_specific_alerts.py with cross-layer-\ncontamination guard (Tag-78 alerts MUST NOT appear in welle-N\ngroups). _TAG78_GROUP_CONTRACT pins the marathon-closeout-routing\ngroup to exactly 7 rules at 30s interval.\n\nGroup-count pins bumped 20 -> 21 in\ntests/ci/test_phase_3_marathon_failure_mode_alerts.py and\ntests/ci/test_pre_existing_failures_fix_tag68.py.\n\nTest surface: 35 tests in\ntests/observability/test_marathon_closeout_routing_tag78.py\n(YAML surface, bridge catalog, mirror equality, cross-reference\nchecks, regression guards). All 4082 observability+ci tests pass.\n\nCo-authored-by: Noa Bergstroem <noa@wakir.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqDLeiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxN0QABqZlz3eDKhZiVSvdGJ/0auc\nk5oIy4uM1nS+fZXhVLkFJEwdexFJGFIEsTLsVst8Nl/wL0OQCWhswr2hE2vhcBpt\nBP575uPafaEOgesr+luuUJj8wyyAqp+1jRWustbpRp5/0ynskkfa9ZSyMjIh74uF\nZMjDGFusq1qVI1lgIWUL+ZGPtgzLw0PiKp9mwlIpxjIg5/xzXmKzMtcBQJzM8+GT\nDnPTYemcsURcJsvolvH+7zTcJN7TwkvS9jdvGncE+LXpLeHOgq99bASYTZmkg842\nw1JS9BZZ+Ajq25DvwJetr+lFKzv04u70YDeJjxa8AU2l1gVIgFRKbdW+EFRuq7D0\nwIvTAmXuRfvIaTSZj16sV3DQhfHgVrl3J15NLZKbW0NkdC11r1C2Cyh12ttcFDY9\nm/bZYuLpoBfnIl7Zmljjx2un3xKEzHGBoCsmWxFZ/n4FZQfrBz8fAAjQVPs44QXu\navuSexBssx9fcNOrK5XHc5AVjaZfuIjHWbzuRs8Tl/D49vfcf2Lp8AKzonbbDUan\nDGLyhb7LFjW314x8aDrszv4gCXP4zLlI6yja7TTcD4BXEI5KF0B4+e1jArDqU0uQ\nqHkxoMdaibGWPcxcovZ4WJH8emsbrqs6PZFFzdBEmWp3F/EyV+Chtg+NSS0Tg4pF\nknmcLg/2qt4EIKWcmflS\n=Fmn6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-19T19:18:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/8d50124b3a6c8c6f9d4c06b905bfda58ab4dfc7a","node_id":"C_kwDOSVv36NoAKDhkNTAxMjRiM2E2YzhjNmY5ZDRjMDZiOTA1YmZkYTU4YWI0ZGZjN2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/04e7ee0b78fc8569fbb5deebbd1b3c43716a5789","sha":"04e7ee0b78fc8569fbb5deebbd1b3c43716a5789","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/04e7ee0b78fc8569fbb5deebbd1b3c43716a5789"}],"sha":"8d50124b3a6c8c6f9d4c06b905bfda58ab4dfc7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/8d50124b3a6c8c6f9d4c06b905bfda58ab4dfc7a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/281068747?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs","id":281068747,"login":"wakir-labs","node_id":"U_kgDOEMDEyw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/04e7ee0b78fc8569fbb5deebbd1b3c43716a5789/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-19T19:11:44Z","email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-19T19:11:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci(tag-78): operator-items health-check workflow + helper + tests (Kai) (#491)\n\nTag-78 Marathon-Polish-Phase substrate: hermetic daily Pre-Cutover-Eve\nreadiness probe for the ten Operator-Hand Pending-Items I1..I10\nconsolidated in Tag-77 PR #486.\n\nThree stages\n------------\n\n* Stage 1 parses the Tag-77 master-doc\n  (docs/operations/operator-hand-pending-items-konsolidat.md) and\n  extracts the ten Item-IDs + Prerequisites narrative bullets,\n  confirming the helper''s static recipes are in sync.\n* Stage 2 evaluates the static per-item recipe (doc-presence,\n  workflow-presence, helper-presence, state-dir-presence) against\n  the runtime-repo HEAD and emits per-item status green/yellow/red\n  with a missing-primitive list.\n* Stage 3 aggregates the ten statuses into a single envelope:\n  OPERATOR-ITEMS-READY  (all ten green),\n  OPERATOR-ITEMS-CAUTION  (1..2 yellow, zero red),\n  OPERATOR-ITEMS-BLOCKED  (any red, OR 3+ yellow).\n\nThe envelope JSON is uploaded as a build artifact. BLOCKED exits\nthe workflow non-zero so the Actions UI surfaces a red signal;\nCAUTION emits a warning annotation.\n\nTrigger surface\n---------------\n\n* workflow_dispatch -- operator-hand / AR-Hand manual run with\n  optional verbose flag.\n* schedule: cron \"0 6 * * *\" -- daily 06:00 UTC, runs from Tag-78\n  through the Pre-Cutover-Eve stichtag (2026-06-26 Fr) and across\n  the Marathon-Lauf to surface drift in I6/I7 carry-forward items.\n* push (path-filtered) -- master-doc / helper / tests / workflow\n  changes re-probe immediately.\n\nHermetic posture\n----------------\n\nStrict hermetic: stdlib + filesystem only. Live-VM-only primitives\n(cosign verify, systemctl restart, podman pull, gh api PUT) are\nexplicitly OUT of scope -- per the Live-Bring-up Sandbox-Gap memo\n(2026-05-13), those remain Operator-Hand on the Live-VM and are\nrecorded in the Closure-Record files referenced in Tag-77 §1..§8.\n\nNot a required status check\n---------------------------\n\nPer feedback_branch_protection_check_names.md the workflow is NOT\nlisted as a required status check -- it gates a calendar-window\n(Pre-Cutover-Eve 2026-06-26 Fr), not individual PRs.\n\nFiles\n-----\n\n* .github/workflows/operator-items-health-check.yml -- three-stage\n  workflow with dispatch + daily 06:00 UTC cron + path-filtered\n  push, minimal contents-read permissions, concurrency-pinned.\n* tooling/ci/health_check_operator_items.py -- stdlib-only helper\n  with parse_master_doc_items, parse_master_doc_prerequisites,\n  check_all_items, aggregate_verdict, build_envelope, main CLI\n  (exit 0 READY/CAUTION, exit 1 BLOCKED, exit 2 master-doc missing).\n* tests/observability/test_operator_items_health_check_tag78.py --\n  27 hermetic tests (T-A parser, T-B per-item + aggregator,\n  T-C workflow file shape, INT helper x doc/workflow cross-check).\n\nTest status\n-----------\n\n27/27 green on Python 3.14. Helper executed on actual repo emits\nBLOCKED verdict as expected (5 weeks ahead of stichtag, helpers\nlike tooling/ci/snapshot_trust_root.py and tooling/ots/stamp_commit.py\nwill land in subsequent spawns; the daily probe surfaces that drift\nto AR + Mira).\n\nCo-authored-by: Kai Hoffmann <kai@wakirlabs.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Kai Hoffmann (DevOps) <kai@wakir-labs.dev>","tree":{"sha":"df50813fc8b6edefc139ff09ee5adb03a47222f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/trees/df50813fc8b6edefc139ff09ee5adb03a47222f0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/commits/04e7ee0b78fc8569fbb5deebbd1b3c43716a5789","verification":{"payload":"tree df50813fc8b6edefc139ff09ee5adb03a47222f0\nparent 7d25485fcfe03cd07a450dd02177a960d9949452\nauthor wakir-labs <xypu4r8e@addy.io> 1779217904 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779217904 +0200\n\nci(tag-78): operator-items health-check workflow + helper + tests (Kai) (#491)\n\nTag-78 Marathon-Polish-Phase substrate: hermetic daily Pre-Cutover-Eve\nreadiness probe for the ten Operator-Hand Pending-Items I1..I10\nconsolidated in Tag-77 PR #486.\n\nThree stages\n------------\n\n* Stage 1 parses the Tag-77 master-doc\n  (docs/operations/operator-hand-pending-items-konsolidat.md) and\n  extracts the ten Item-IDs + Prerequisites narrative bullets,\n  confirming the helper''s static recipes are in sync.\n* Stage 2 evaluates the static per-item recipe (doc-presence,\n  workflow-presence, helper-presence, state-dir-presence) against\n  the runtime-repo HEAD and emits per-item status green/yellow/red\n  with a missing-primitive list.\n* Stage 3 aggregates the ten statuses into a single envelope:\n  OPERATOR-ITEMS-READY  (all ten green),\n  OPERATOR-ITEMS-CAUTION  (1..2 yellow, zero red),\n  OPERATOR-ITEMS-BLOCKED  (any red, OR 3+ yellow).\n\nThe envelope JSON is uploaded as a build artifact. BLOCKED exits\nthe workflow non-zero so the Actions UI surfaces a red signal;\nCAUTION emits a warning annotation.\n\nTrigger surface\n---------------\n\n* workflow_dispatch -- operator-hand / AR-Hand manual run with\n  optional verbose flag.\n* schedule: cron \"0 6 * * *\" -- daily 06:00 UTC, runs from Tag-78\n  through the Pre-Cutover-Eve stichtag (2026-06-26 Fr) and across\n  the Marathon-Lauf to surface drift in