.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/7d25485fcfe03cd07a450dd02177a960d9949452","sha":"7d25485fcfe03cd07a450dd02177a960d9949452","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/7d25485fcfe03cd07a450dd02177a960d9949452"}],"sha":"04e7ee0b78fc8569fbb5deebbd1b3c43716a5789","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/04e7ee0b78fc8569fbb5deebbd1b3c43716a5789"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/281068747?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs","id":281068747,"login":"wakir-labs","node_id":"U_kgDOEMDEyw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/7d25485fcfe03cd07a450dd02177a960d9949452/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-19T19:10:56Z","email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-19T19:10:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"audit(persona-engine): Tag-78 engine-migration-drift audit (Selin, 23 tests, audit-only) (#494)\n\nPin the migration-consistency contract between the Python Stage-1\nauthority (wirelang/persona_engine/welle_state_producer.py + engine.py\n+ engine_async.py and 17 sibling authority modules) and the Rust\nStage-2 plan substrate (the persona-engine-* crates in the\nwirelang-rust workspace).\n\nThe helper walks four orthogonal drift dimensions: Python-authority\nsymbol coverage (D1), Rust-crate parity-anchor declaration (D2),\ncross-side drift classification (D3 -- rust-pendant-present /\nrust-pendant-absent / stale-anchor), and the Welle-state-machine\ndrift block (D4 -- the welle_state_producer + engine + engine_async\nhave no Rust pendant by design at Tag-78; that is the post-cutover\nStage-2 migration map). Emits a stable JSON drift envelope; pure\nstdlib; no subprocess; no git invocation; no network.\n\nThe test suite ships 23 tests across six lemma-families (envelope\nshape, Python-authority counter, Rust-crate anchor extractor,\ncross-side drift classification, Welle-state-machine block, CLI\nexit-code contract). Manufactures the authority + crate skeleton\nin tmp_path; no coupling to the runtime tip.\n\nAudit-only. No migration step. No Python or Rust source mutation.\nNo persona-definition (Aisha-Domaene), WAT-core (Tomas), identity-\nsubstrate (Reza), container-infra (Kai) touch. Marathon-Polish-\nPhase Continuous-Mode.\n\nCo-authored-by: pengine-eng <pengine@wakir.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b9026e0d8eb323a47fe0face06cfaef815f9c1c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/trees/b9026e0d8eb323a47fe0face06cfaef815f9c1c3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/commits/7d25485fcfe03cd07a450dd02177a960d9949452","verification":{"payload":"tree b9026e0d8eb323a47fe0face06cfaef815f9c1c3\nparent 7bb8783ec71e70f78399ad48cbb93256d187c13f\nauthor wakir-labs <xypu4r8e@addy.io> 1779217856 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779217856 +0200\n\naudit(persona-engine): Tag-78 engine-migration-drift audit (Selin, 23 tests, audit-only) (#494)\n\nPin the migration-consistency contract between the Python Stage-1\nauthority (wirelang/persona_engine/welle_state_producer.py + engine.py\n+ engine_async.py and 17 sibling authority modules) and the Rust\nStage-2 plan substrate (the persona-engine-* crates in the\nwirelang-rust workspace).\n\nThe helper walks four orthogonal drift dimensions: Python-authority\nsymbol coverage (D1), Rust-crate parity-anchor declaration (D2),\ncross-side drift classification (D3 -- rust-pendant-present /\nrust-pendant-absent / stale-anchor), and the Welle-state-machine\ndrift block (D4 -- the welle_state_producer + engine + engine_async\nhave no Rust pendant by design at Tag-78; that is the post-cutover\nStage-2 migration map). Emits a stable JSON drift envelope; pure\nstdlib; no subprocess; no git invocation; no network.\n\nThe test suite ships 23 tests across six lemma-families (envelope\nshape, Python-authority counter, Rust-crate anchor extractor,\ncross-side drift classification, Welle-state-machine block, CLI\nexit-code contract). Manufactures the authority + crate skeleton\nin tmp_path; no coupling to the runtime tip.\n\nAudit-only. No migration step. No Python or Rust source mutation.\nNo persona-definition (Aisha-Domaene), WAT-core (Tomas), identity-\nsubstrate (Reza), container-infra (Kai) touch. Marathon-Polish-\nPhase Continuous-Mode.\n\nCo-authored-by: pengine-eng <pengine@wakir.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqDLXACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtfYQADg/GSD9N7X/VvdVV1H1+p4e\nxXskIPC7y/4/335GjQz8rs6jzac4Rih1ifcgcvX8ftT8HHs6/OTwHT33h1GiOGBX\n1rcKiwnykZtCww/qzw6aVkNxLNwrNwqnGP1dJa31dYMYtLBzWMOHdAkx8PvuVKeU\nSUadVyEYssy7QTgS4myuWYAvGv8Xbe/1LMfYISCAU5Aiw0hXXsBasjO7TCmglVnY\nMV90WLAG+iY9ebCE+Xgp9q4ZGLqy5Olv+MMVMTrGYu410OFRNFVacFg5ju1J2PbT\nicYKAbP7Dg7PpTN+qSpP1KiieVz0ZZhuLqPPEEzbuX0WbSFAhcik6Psdw/FcAS27\nzRh195BBJ756FGyBPpsQ7JkYk/FP7s9owZvbYVH/CuPT+BJahiMfmNMDzMmsnkw3\nOkKBkfVQtAdHlWROf/tWbJMgalBBW6hHUvmumG7UVunxVaWML/fLpmHU7cLCHznl\nQI+Pp6ZBRGJAVQ7l599XvscDiaw1M3ijQRo6