tps://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs","id":281068747,"login":"wakir-labs","node_id":"U_kgDOEMDEyw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/a54d7abb82381938b7292a9627d22d2ce7d3f8ad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-19T18:31:48Z","email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-19T18:31:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci(marathon): Tag-77 Marathon-Final-Smoke E2E (Amara, Continuous-Mode) (#489)\n\nUmbrella hermetic Marathon-Polish-Phase smoke that consolidates\nthe entire Tag-69..Tag-76 substrate-set into a single end-to-end\nMARATHON-FINAL verdict (INTACT / DRIFT / DEFECT):\n\n  Stages 1..7  -- seven per-Welle-Integration-Smoke envelopes\n                  (Welle-1+2 audit-anchor stand-ins, Welle-3..7\n                  canonical Tag-71..Tag-75 aggregator outputs).\n  Stage 8      -- Tag-76 Cross-Welle-Stability-Pin (Amara #483).\n  Stage 9      -- Tag-76 Marathon-Closeout-Aggregator (Reza #479).\n  Stage 10     -- Tag-76 Phase-3-COMPLETE-Marker-Audit-Bundle\n                  (Tomas #484).\n  Stage 11     -- Aggregated MARATHON-FINAL verdict.\n\nFiles:\n\n  .github/workflows/marathon-final-smoke-e2e.yml -- 11-stage\n    hermetic workflow with drift_inject + defect_inject probe\n    surfaces for each stage.\n  tooling/ci/aggregate_marathon_final_smoke.py -- stdlib-only\n    aggregator (build_envelope + decide + CLI). Reads ten input\n    envelopes, emits trinary verdict. Read-only over Tag-76\n    substrate verdicts; no substrate logic re-implemented.\n  tests/ci/test_marathon_final_smoke_tag77.py -- 57 hermetic\n    unittest cases covering aggregator decision rule, envelope\n    schema (top-level keys, per-Welle anchors, stage provenance,\n    Brief-vs-canonical reconciliation), CLI smoke, workflow\n    shape (11 stages, dispatch inputs, terminal-status gate,\n    artifact uploads).\n\nAnchors\n\n  docs/quality-gates/pre-cutover-acceptance-run-order.md §3\n    -- 7 Welle-Datumsanker (cross-Welle sequencing contract).\n  docs/quality-gates/phase-3-marathon-anti-patterns.md §AP-9\n    -- Welle-3 Rollback-Cascade (consumed indirectly via Stage 8).\n  decisions/0066-marathon-cadence-vier-wochen.md §Beschluss\n    -- Doppel-Welle PAR-path (consumed indirectly via Stage 8).\n\nBrief-vs-canonical reconciliation\n\n  * Brief \"7 Welle-Integration-Smokes\": canonical = five\n    aggregators on main (Welle-3..7), Welle-1+2 audit-anchor-only\n    stand-ins; surfaced in stage_provenance.\n  * Brief \"Stage 9 Closeout + Stage 10 Bundle\": canonical = two\n    distinct Tag-76 substrates with distinct verdict maps\n    (MARATHON-CLOSEOUT-READY vs BUNDLE-READY); both surfaced\n    as separate stages.\n\nSandbox-boundary\n\n  stdlib only, no network IO, no actual Welle dispatch, no\n  gh workflow run, no Phase-3-COMPLETE-marker emit, no closeout\n  signing. Hermetic by construction. Live dispatch on the\n  Marathon Cutover-Mittwoche (2026-06-10/17/24, 2026-07-01) is\n  operator-hand.\n\nNot a required status check per feedback_branch_protection_check_names.\n\nTests: 57 hermetic cases, all pass locally.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kai Hoffmann <kai@wakir.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8aeb4062d2bfbf177150c7d1a8d2f700f22225f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/trees/8aeb4062d2bfbf177150c7d1a8d2f700f22225