wakir-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/8347f897129a3da0e50e7ca665806b4843d2ea22/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-19T18:24:43Z","email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-19T18:24:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"audit(reza): Tag-77 v0.4.4 Promotion Pre-Vorbereitung Substrate (Schluss-Stein, 24 tests, audit-only) (#485)\n\nSchluss-Stein of the Tag-63..Tag-72 v0.4.4 Reserve-Item substrate\ntrilogy. Aggregates the ten per-axis audit-only artefacts pinned\nacross Tag-63 (draft baseline, PR #403), Tag-64 (sample-block\ncoverage, PR #407), Tag-65 (sequencing doc, PR #414), Tag-66\n(RES-D OTS-probe coverage, PR #421), Tag-67 (activation pre-mortem,\nPR #428), Tag-68 (pre-mortem coverage, PR #433), Tag-69 (RES-D4\ndeep-dive, PR #440), Tag-70 (HD-1 OTS substrate, PR #446),\nTag-71 (HD-2 Peer-Roster substrate, PR #452), and Tag-72 (HD-3\nAudit-Coverage substrate, PR #458) into a single per-RES-Dn\nPromotion-Pre-Readiness-Score (0..5) plus a global verdict.\n\nScore methodology (audit-only, advisory-only):\n\n  Dim 1 substrate-pinned          (Tag-63 + Tag-64)   - reachable\n  Dim 2 ots-probe-coverage        (Tag-66)            - reachable\n  Dim 3 pre-mortem-covered        (Tag-67 + Tag-68)   - reachable\n  Dim 4 hard-dep-substrate-prep   (Tag-70/71/72)      - reachable\n  Dim 5 ceo-triage-authorisation  (per-item ADR)      - FROZEN-FALSE\n\nDim 5 is FROZEN-FALSE in the Tag-77 audit-only snapshot. The\nSandbox-Hand score ceiling is 4/5 by construction; flipping to 5\nrequires Operator-Hand / AR-authorisation under ADR-0023a +\nADR-0023b and is OUT OF SCOPE for this helper.\n\nAggregate result over RES-D1..D5 at Tag-77: all five items at\nscore 4/5 (substrate trilogy complete, ceo-triage authorisation\npending). Verdict: substrate-complete-ceo-triage-pending. The\nverdict does NOT authorise promotion - it only states that the\nsubstrate trilogy reached its Sandbox ceiling.\n\nSubstanz delivered:\n\n  - tooling/audit/spec-v0-4-4-promotion-pre-readiness-snapshot.json\n    (audit-only snapshot stub; per-item + aggregate; sandbox-\n    boundary recital; what-this-is-not negations; emit-discipline)\n  - tooling/audit/prepare_spec_v0_4_4_promotion_substrate.py\n    (stdlib helper; validates snapshot; prints advisory-only\n    score table; refuses to alter env flags; no side-channels)\n  - docs/operations/wirelang-spec-v0-4-4-promotion-sequencing.md\n    extended with new §8 Tag-77 Promotion Pre-Readiness Score\n    (Schluss-Stein) - §8.1 motivation, §8.2 methodology,\n    §8.3 snapshot result, §8.4 what-this-is-not, §8.5 sandbox-\n    boundary recital, §8.6 cross-anchor\n  - tests/audit/test_spec_v0_4_4_promotion_pre_vorbereitung_tag77.py\n    (24 hermetic stdlib+pytest tests across three axes: snapshot\n    shape invariants, helper subprocess mutilation suite, doc §8\n    cross-anchor presence; >=18 tests requested)\n\nDiscipline:\n\n  - Audit-only; indefinite-deferral remains default for all items.\n  - No promotion-PR opening, no AR-authorisation request, no\n    draft-ADR, no Pin-Pack edit, no NATS-KV schema flip, no OTS\n    activation, no notify-log / activity-log / audit-sample-\n    rotation emit.\n  - Helper writes to stdout only; advisory-only score.\n  - Tag-65 verifier still green (no regression on doc §1..§7).\n  - REUSE-lint clean (Apache-2.0 default catch-all for new files;\n    no new annotations needed).\n\nTest verdict locally: 24/24 green for Tag-77; 362/362 green over\nthe full Tag-63..Tag-77 v0.4.4 substrate trilogy.\n\nCo-authored-by: Mira Kessler <mira@wakir.local>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3cca0cc80bae4cbeab66a8e16b012cc0866abbe5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/trees/3cca0cc80bae4cbeab66a8e16b012cc0866abbe5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/commits/8347f897129a3da0e50e7ca665806b4843d2ea22","verification":{"payload":"tree 3cca0cc80bae4cbeab66a8e16b012cc0866abbe5\nparent dd979315ce351d01ce39b408520bdb9cbbd4ecb0\nauthor wakir-labs <xypu4r8e@addy.io> 1779215083 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779215083 +0200\n\naudit(reza): Tag-77 v0.4.4 Promotion Pre-Vorbereitung Substrate (Schluss-Stein, 24 tests, audit-only) (#485)\n\nSchluss-Stein of the Tag-63..Tag-72 v0.4.4 Reserve-Item substrate\ntrilogy. Aggregates the ten per-axis audit-only artefacts pinned\nacross Tag-63 (draft baseline, PR #403), Tag-64 (sample-block\ncoverage, PR #407), Tag-65 (sequencing doc, PR #414), Tag-66\n(RES-D OTS-probe coverage, PR #421), Tag-67 (activation pre-mortem,\nPR #428), Tag-68 (pre-mortem coverage, PR #433), Tag-69 (RES-D4\ndeep-dive, PR #440), Tag-70 (HD-1 OTS substrate, PR #446),\nTag-71 (HD-2 Peer-Roster substrate, PR #452), and Tag-72 (HD-3\nAudit-Coverage substrate, PR #458) into a single per-RES-Dn\nPromotion-Pre-Readiness-Score (0..5) plus a global verdict.\n\nScore methodology (audit-only, advisory-only):\n\n  Dim 1 substrate-pinned          (Tag-63 + Tag-64)   - reachable\n  Dim 2 ots-probe-coverage        (Tag-66)            - reachable\n  Dim 3 pre-mortem-covered        (Tag-67 + Tag-68)   - reachable\n  Dim 4 hard-dep-substrate-prep   (Tag-70/71/72)      - reachable\n  Dim 5 ceo-triage-authorisation  (per-item ADR)      - FROZEN-FALSE\n\nDim 5 is FROZEN-FALSE in the Tag-77 audit-only snapshot. The\nSandbox-Hand score ceiling is 4/5 by construction; flipping to 5\nrequires Operator-Hand / AR-authorisation under ADR-0023a +\nADR-0023b and is OUT OF SCOPE for this helper.\n\nAggregate result over RES-D1..D5 at Tag-77: all five items at\nscore 4/5 (substrate trilogy complete, ceo-triage authorisation\npending). Verdict: substrate-complete-ceo-triage-pending. The\nverdict does NOT authorise promotion - it only states that the\nsubstrate trilogy reached its Sandbox ceiling.\n\nSubstanz delivered:\n\n  - tooling/audit/spec-v0-4-4-promotion-pre-readiness-snapshot.json\n    (audit-only snapshot stub; per-item + aggregate; sandbox-\n    boundary recital; what-this-is-not negations; emit-discipline)\n  - tooling/audit/prepare_spec_v0_4_4_promotion_substrate.py\n    (stdlib helper; validates snapshot; prints advisory-only\n    score table; refuses to alter env flags; no side-channels)\n  - docs/operations/wirelang-spec-v0-4-4-promotion-sequencing.md\n    extended with new §8 Tag-77 Promotion Pre-Readiness Score\n    (Schluss-Stein) - §8.1 motivation, §8.2 methodology,\n    §8.3 snapshot result, §8.4 what-this-is-not, §8.5 sandbox-\n    boundary recital, §8.6 cross-anchor\n  - tests/audit/test_spec_v0_4_4_promotion_pre_vorbereitung_tag77.py\n    (24 hermetic stdlib+pytest tests across three axes: snapshot\n    shape invariants, helper subprocess mutilation suite, doc §8\n    cross-anchor presence; >=18 tests requested)\n\nDiscipline:\n\n  - Audit-only; indefinite-deferral remains default for all items.\n  - No promotion-PR opening, no AR-authorisation request, no\n    draft-ADR, no Pin-Pack edit, no NATS-KV schema flip, no OTS\n    activation, no notify-log / activity-log / audit-sample-\n    rotation emit.\n  - Helper writes to stdout only; advisory-only score.\n  - Tag-65 verifier still green (no regression on doc §1..§7).\n  - REUSE-lint clean (Apache-2.0 default catch-all for new files;\n    no new annotations needed).\n\nTest verdict locally: 24/24 green for Tag-77; 362/362 green over\nthe full Tag-63..Tag-77 v0.4.4 substrate trilogy.\n\nCo-authored-by: Mira Kessler <mira@wakir.l