":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/281068747?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs","id":281068747,"login":"wakir-labs","node_id":"U_kgDOEMDEyw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/af8966a7d131d7809e5d0f7a263e54a6628e865f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-19T17:57:48Z","email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-19T17:57:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(persona-engine): Tag-76 Welle-1..7 Production-Bringup-Verifier (Selin, 31 tests) (#481)\n\nTag-75 (PR #475) shipped the Welle-7 producer-path closing the producer-\nsubstrate for all six per-Welle marker-families. Tag-76 (this PR) adds\nthe cross-Welle **Production-Bringup-Verifier** -- the seventh disjoint\ntrigger-family in the audit-stream.\n\nSubstanz\n--------\n\n- `WelleStateProducer.handle_phase_3_complete_event` (read-only cross-\n  Welle aggregate verifier). Checks that all required Wellen (default\n  `{1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7}`) are in canonical signed-off State with non-\n  empty `cutover_iso` + `signoff_iso`, and that cross-Welle\n  `cutover_iso` ordering is monotone non-decreasing in welle_number.\n  On green: emits a `Phase3CompleteAuditRecord` (cross-Welle aggregate,\n  disjoint from `WelleAuditRecord`). On red: raises\n  `Phase3CompleteVerifierError`.\n- `wirelang.persona_engine.engine.handle_phase_3_complete_event` --\n  top-level sync handler.\n- `wirelang.persona_engine.engine_async.handle_phase_3_complete_event`\n  -- async wrapper (default-loop thread-pool executor).\n\nThe verifier is the **engine-side gate-input** for the downstream\n`PHASE_3_COMPLETE_VIA_DOPPEL_WELLE_6_7` marker emission (per\n`docs/quality-gates/phase-3c-doppel-welle-6-7.md` §4.1). The marker\nemission itself is audit-trail-consumer-territory (Henrik Internal\nAudit Zone-N), NOT this verifier''s responsibility.\n\nDisjointness pins\n-----------------\n\n- `trigger=\"phase-3-complete-verify\"` is disjoint from all six per-\n  Welle marker-family trigger-literals (`cutover`, `sealing`,\n  `snapshot-restore`, `capability-token-rotation`,\n  `cross-substrate-parity`, `final-sealing`) + vanilla `sign-off` +\n  `rollback`.\n- `verdict=\"phase-3-complete-verified\"` is disjoint from all per-Welle\n  marker-literals (`sealed`, `restored`, `rotated`, `verified`,\n  `confirmed`, `rollback-authorized`, `designated`, `signed-off`).\n- `Phase3CompleteAuditRecord` carries cross-Welle-aggregate fields\n  (`verified_wellen`, `earliest_cutover_iso`, `latest_signoff_iso`);\n  the `WelleAuditRecord` carries single-Welle fields. Downstream\n  consumers (Henrik Zone-N) distinguish by `trigger`.\n\nTests\n-----\n\n31 tests in `wirelang/tests/persona_engine/test_production_bringup_verifier_tag76.py`:\n\n- 8 module-shape pins (constants, exports, error-hierarchy, async-\n  coroutine-shape).\n- 4 happy-path tests (verdict, emitter, idempotency, canonical-JSON).\n- 6 per-Welle-precondition refusal tests (pending/in-progress/rolled-\n  back, empty cutover_iso/signoff_iso, missing state-file).\n- 2 cross-Welle-invariant tests (non-monotone refusal, equal-cutover\n  tolerance for KW-26-Welles 4/5/6).\n- 4 parametric tests (subset, empty-set, invalid welle_number,\n  invalid verify_iso).\n- 3 top-level sync handler tests.\n- 2 async handler tests.\n- 2 disjointness pins.\n\nScope discipline (Selin)\n------------------------\n\n- Read-only: no state-file mutation.\n- No marker-file mutation (audit-trail-consumer-territory).\n- No persona-definition mutation (Aisha-Domaene).\n- No WAT-core coupling (Tomas, Zone-K).\n- No identity-substrate coupling (Reza, Zone-L).\n- No container-infra coupling (Kai, Zone-J).\n\nCo-authored-by: pengine-eng <pengine@wakir.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e0ac2e9265979ce2fc34976d8e2f1a0b54eb45f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/trees/e0ac2e9265979ce2fc34976d8e2f1a0b54eb45f9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/commits/af8966a7d131d7809e5d0f7a263e54a6628e865f","verification":{"payload":"tree e0ac2e9265979ce2fc34976d8e2f1a0b54eb45f9\nparent c44e454060c52e1d87ff1ecdc112f5a3ce4be8f2\nauthor wakir-labs <xypu4r8e@addy.io> 1779213468 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779213468 +0200\n\nfeat(persona-engine): Tag-76 Welle-1..7 Production-Bringup-Verifier (Selin, 31 tests) (#481)\n\nTag-75 (PR #475) shipped the Welle-7 producer-path closing the producer-\nsubstrate for all six per-Welle marker-families. Tag-76 (this PR) adds\nthe cross-Welle **Production-Bringup-Verifier** -- the seventh disjoint\ntrigger-family in the audit-stream.\n\nSubstanz\n--------\n\n- `WelleStateProducer.handle_phase_3_complete_event` (read-only cross-\n  Welle aggregate verifier). Checks that all required Wellen (default\n  `{1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7}`) are in canonical signed-off State with non-\n  empty `cutover_iso` + `signoff_iso`, and that cross-Welle\n  `cutover_iso` ordering is monotone non-decreasing in welle_number.\n  On green: emits a `Phase3CompleteAuditRecord` (cross-Welle aggregate,\n  disjoint from `WelleAuditRecord`). On red: raises\n  `Phase3CompleteVerifierError`.\n- `wirelang.persona_engine.engine.handle_phase_3_complete_event` --\n  top-level sync handler.\n- `wirelang.persona_engine.engine_async.handle_phase_3_complete_event`\n  -- async wrapper (default-loop thread-pool executor).\n\nThe verifier is the **engine-side gate-input** for the downstream\n`PHASE_3_COMPLETE_VIA_DOPPEL_WELLE_6_7` marker emission (per\n`docs/quality-gates/phase-3c-doppel-welle-6-7.md` §4.1). The marker\nemission itself is audit-trail-consumer-territory (Henrik Internal\nAudit Zone-N), NOT this verifier''s responsibility.\n\nDisjointness pins\n-----------------\n\n- `trigger=\"phase-3-complete-verify\"` is disjoint from all six per-\n  Welle marker-family trigger-literals (`cutover`, `sealing`,\n  `snapshot-restore`, `capability-token-rotation`,\n  `cross-substrate-parity`, `final-sealing`) + vanilla `sign-off` +\n  `rollback`.\n- `verdict=\"phase-3-complete-verified\"` is disjoint from all per-Welle\n  marker-literals (`sealed`, `restored`, `rotated`, `verified`,\n  `confirmed`, `rollback-authorized`, `designated`, `signed-off`).\n- `Phase3CompleteAuditRecord` carries cross-Welle-aggregate fields\n  (`verified_wellen`, `earliest_cutover_iso`, `latest_signoff_iso`);\n  the `WelleAuditRecord` carries single-Welle fields. Downstream\n  consumers (Henrik Zone-N) distinguish by `trigger`.\n\nTests\n-----\n\n31 tests in `wirelang/tests/persona_engine/test_production_bringup_verifier_tag76.py`:\n\n- 8 module-shape pins (constants, exports, error-hierarchy, async-\n  coroutine-shape).\n- 4 happy-path tests (verdict, emitter, idempotency, canonical-JSON).\n- 6 per-Welle-precondition refusal tests (pending/in-progress/rolled-\n  back, empty cutover_iso/signoff_iso, missing state-file).\n- 2 cross-Welle-invariant tests (non-monotone refusal, equal-cutover\n  tolerance for KW-26-Welles 4/5/6).\n- 4 parametric tests (subset, empty-set, invalid welle_number,\n  invalid verify_iso).\n- 3 top-level sync handler tests.\n- 2 async handler tests.\n- 2 disjointness pins.\n\nScope discipline (Selin)\n------------------------\n\n- Read-only: no state-file mutation.\n- No marker-file mutation (audit-trail-consumer-territory).\n- No persona-definition mutation (Aisha-Domaene).\n- No WAT-core coupling (Tomas, Zone-K).\n- No identity-substrate coupling (Reza, Zone-L).\n- No container-infra coupling (Kai, Zone-J).\n\nCo-authored-by: pengine-eng <pengine@wakir.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqDKScCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADTIQAK4iuNP/PJ7M9cxvz3hDJbdJ\nqC19DSPCM1x5+5FwPrQbCywPWQsCYkA6P78x7vcdhwB4JRIX08/DYiAWoAP9gDaC\nUmNEdH0lPfwGhQ+FNChtPZV1r2xKQAUYuAFikp8tIRqZctIpQjSb3Y3D5+aT88yZ\nJ65tuJYFG+H5PRdu0Tgu+v+BDnGWOsMmQYzff5LyWLIAv9zTN7DxeHIbkcrpXnyC\nsU0ViXIb6WVw+w/ZYX0+WrGWoLKmptFKSF3loDl3qh9k9dFZfBdVniM6CSABP3N+\n1F/6TxONxHRF0lurhjxyQDlDlGd8Qq237Tcca24SaR2A+PaOw9Q1ZlDBv8lruEUl\ndLeIYpu/j01RmXBng0rjzmBAw5pG1HewvnU/i5g7DWu5m6qq8p2CwYWoxRy95RSP\nksAhGUpmZo899EX6AmHCCtHpmd7f3iOdcb3tw1Dtg+JIx/+lYEf/awgKOG5d4N5s\nnbbHF8ngRB/7fbUNwuRZ2NfrA1Dowf0YNwE22NKoEZ30fZqGV0AK3M8Wg/L4GFtW\nXEAjhb02nAk2TROBly2p23jBPDL+JvmKBfhMncrCJrrAhFWoGo6r1ORoWf1GiAyN\ns2JTvTs4pbqbRZzPDwKUtFKxGopPnE8qnFqpxjJvw2cu9qgFHiyNktPtyE9tKgeL\nXojlMKd+STXwLZOIvGhC\n=IbkJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-19T17:57:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/af8966a7d131d7809e5d0f7a263e54a6628e865f","node_id":"C_kwDOSVv36NoAKGFmODk2NmE3ZDEzMWQ3ODA5ZTVkMGY3YTI2M2U1NGE2NjI4ZTg2NWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/c44e454060c52e1d87ff1ecdc112f5a3ce4be8f2","sha":"c44e454060c52e1d87ff1ecdc112f5a3ce4be8f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/c44e454060c52e1d87ff1ecdc112f5a3ce4be8f2"}],"sha":"af8966a7d131d7809e5d0f7a263e54a6628e865f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/af8966a7d131d7809e5d0f7a263e54a6628e865f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/281068747?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs","id":281068747,"login":"wakir-labs","node_id":"U_kgDOEMDEyw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/c44e454060c52e1d87ff1ecdc112f5a3ce4be8f2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-19T17:57:40Z","email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-19T17:57:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): Tag-76 cardinality-Failures auf origin/main (5+1 Hotspot, Noa SRE) (#482)\n\nTomás-Tag-75-Side-Befund: 6 pre-existing cardinality-Failures auf\norigin/main durch Tag-72/73/74/75 routing-extensions die in die\nwelle-N-alerts groups appended wurden ohne dass der Tag-50-Contract\nin tests/ci/test_welle_n_specific_alerts.py mitwächst.\n\nSymptom (pre-fix, origin/main, 154 tests, 6 failed):\n- test_welle_group_alarm_count_in_range[welle-4-alerts]   (5 > max=3)\n- test_welle_group_alarm_count_in_range[welle-5-alerts]   (5 > max=3)\n- test_welle_group_alarm_count_in_range[welle-6-alerts]   (4 > max=3)\n- test_welle_group_alarm_count_in_range[welle-7-alerts]   (5 > max=3)\n- test_tag50_alert_names_disjoint_from_tag45             (8 overlap)\n- test_tag50_count_equals_eighteen                        (got 26)\n\nFix:\n1. _TAG50_GROUP_CONTRACT max bumped welle-4..7 (3->5/5/4/5) so\n   each cap = Tag-50-originals + Tag-72/73/74/75 extensions.\n2. tag50_alerts_by_name fixture restricts to _TAG50_ALERTS set\n   so the Tag-50 disjointness + count-18 contract stays scoped\n   to the originals (Tag-7X extensions filtered out cleanly).\n\nAnti-Regression-Pins (5 neue Tests, alle gruen):\n- test_tag7x_extension_count_pinned_per_welle (parametrize x7):\n  per welle: residual = group_rules - _TAG50_ALERTS MUST equal\n  pinned _TAG7X_EXTENSION_COUNT_PER_WELLE entry.\n- test_tag7x_extension_inventory_exhaustive: every alert in\n  welle-N-alerts groups MUST be Tag-50 original OR pinned\n  Tag-7X extension; no drift permitted.\n- test_tag7x_extension_total_count_equals_eight: 0+0+0+2+2+2+2=8\n  total Tag-7X extensions.\n- test_tag7x_extension_uses_wakirphase3_prefix (parametrize x8):\n  naming-convention pin.\n- test_tag50_group_contract_max_accommodates_pinned_extensions:\n  cross-check max >= Tag-50-originals + Tag-7X-extensions per welle.\n\nPost-fix: 172 passed in test file, 3756 passed (+1 skipped) across\ntests/ci/ + tests/observability/.\n\nDisziplin:\n- main-Tip pre-Cutover-T0 grün-Pflicht erfüllt.\n- Pure test-side fix, kein Substrate-Code touched.\n\nCo-authored-by: Noa Bergstroem <noa@wakir.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bb6d129d4d50c5029871347972ecf6beb67e68e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/trees/bb6d129d4d50c5029871347972ecf6beb67e68e9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/commits/c44e454060c52e1d87ff1ecdc112f5a3ce4be8f2","verification":{"payload":"tree bb6d129d4d50c5029871347972ecf6beb67e68e9\nparent 6f2759826a5f9e6fb465fb708323e89ef0f56817\nauthor wakir-labs <xypu4r8e@addy.io> 1779213460 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779213460 +0200\n\nfix(ci): Tag-76 cardinality-Failures auf origin/main (5+1 Hotspot, Noa SRE) (#482)\n\nTomás-Tag-75-Side-Befund: 6 pre-existing cardinality-Failures auf\norigin/main durch Tag-72/73/74/75 routing-extensions die in die\nwelle-N-alerts groups appended wurden ohne dass der Tag-50-Contract\nin tests/ci/test_welle_n_specific_alerts.py mitwächst.\n\nSymptom (pre-fix, origin/main, 154 tests, 6 failed):\n- test_welle_group_alarm_count_in_range[welle-4-alerts]   (5 > max=3)\n- test_welle_group_alarm_count_in_range[welle-5-alerts]   (5 > max=3)\n- test_welle_group_alarm_count_in_range[welle-6-alerts]   (4 > max=3)\n- test_welle_group_alarm_count_in_range[welle-7-alerts]   (5 > max=3)\n- test_tag50_alert_names_disjoint_from_tag45             (8 overlap)\n- test_tag50_count_equals_eighteen                        (got 26)\n\nFix:\n1. _TAG50_GROUP_CONTRACT max bumped welle-4..7 (3->5/5/4/5) so\n   each cap = Tag-50-originals + Tag-72/73/74/75 extensions.\n2. tag50_alerts_by_name fixture restricts to _TAG50_ALERTS set\n   so the Tag-50 disjointness + count-18 contract stays scoped\n   to the originals (Tag-7X extensions filtered out cleanly).\n\nAnti-Regression-Pins (5 neue Tests, alle gruen):\n- test_tag7x_extension_count_pinned_per_welle (parametrize x7):\n  per welle: residual = group_rules - _TAG50_ALERTS MUST equal\n  pinned _TAG7X_EXTENSION_COUNT_PER_WELLE entry.\n- test_tag7x_extension_inventory_exhaustive: every alert in\n  welle-N-alerts groups MUST be Tag-50 original OR pinned\n  Tag-7X extension; no drift permitted.\n- test_tag7x_extension_total_count_equals_eight: 0+0+0+2+2+2+2=8\n  total Tag-7X extensions.\n- test_tag7x_extension_uses_wakirphase3_prefix (parametrize x8):\n  naming-convention pin.\n- test_tag50_group_contract_max_accommodates_pinned_extensions:\n  cross-check max >= Tag-50-originals + Tag-7X-extensions per welle.\n\nPost-fix: 172 passed in test file, 3756 passed (+1 skipped) across\ntests/ci/ + tests/observability/.\n\nDisziplin:\n- main-Tip pre-Cutover-T0 grün-Pflicht erfüllt.\n- Pure test-side fix, kein Substrate-Code touched.\n\nCo-authored-by: Noa Bergstroem <noa@wakir.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqDKSVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMMUQACBnoZrkLJG5IpvmETUVA+7a\nCAsiOcILo/sGcqie1B1CaycM2i6gN5p3/La/6r5haGcn5ku0yTuh34uouVvbho5j\nMhdagWurMgnVHVE2+cM0ZuKzD7PggWZwZ6jCieAR4AWnF7CUt/J3IpS8zjFZ0BRH\notBHo2BsOmogvBudiYNt0TfCeS/pBo5CRxpg6Ezm3JI5D9ztSun4fCbZpUb/g3LO\nQeTaqzzoPZbPBGtSVXcuGfhOKFvJoKA7OfeLuO7/cMzu3GEEjlvGbwuMVr3nM+kL\nrYHPOYdQa4i1aGSOHL4YwmlBJ4lVJ0yh5/Didb2x843uBJkFY9cZ/4NxdfyqHJU/\n3g+GLUOeEdLvs3zdel5RrLwXuf1FoRKHya/SkDytf/7jtuRF7KW2FJFrnvnAHmDM\nlKrWv3TTXZNulWAjkJFKuEDP7/jg04qq7qaEeKsheDRSA3fd2kDS4zeBBQLGGk+E\nH0rAi2zoMmW/Y6LjPeQKkp1ywWDqKRUc1gXKmHHVqs7UapeHgazezZu4fAPjwfQm\nup2wfYiercNWpNHXf5vGShslbrY19H70Z7VMspjnSwwA9huv1ozHqsFPJo/2Bo8Y\nONKy2AQy+2Cvu8H8tQTJOhVzEO6HYTJCEHSzKAY+sMTSgOAikv