:"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-19T17:27:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ci): Tag-75 Welle-7 Audit-Trail-Anchor-Integration (FINAL Welle, Tomás, 27 tests) (#477)\n\nTag-75 Continuous-Mode-Spawn: FINAL Welle of the Phase-3c-Welle-Marathon.\nMirror of Tag-69..Tag-74 wiring for the Welle-7 audit-trail-anchor\n(KW-27 Doppel-Welle-6+7 entry, Cutover-Mittwoch 2026-07-01, Sign-off-\nFreitag 2026-07-03 = Global Acceptance-Verdict per\ndocs/quality-gates/pre-cutover-acceptance-run-order.md §3.2).\n\nSubstanz:\n\n  - emit_manifest_hash_ots_marker.py:\n    * --mode welle-7-audit-anchor with --welle-7-{rollup,sign-off,\n      validation,pre-auditor} flags.\n    * compute_welle_7_audit_anchor_hash (recipe-identical to\n      Welle-1..6 per Cross-Substrate-Parity-Markers).\n    * derive_phase_3_final_sealing_tracking deriving the six-field\n      tracking block (active / status / iso / global-verdict-recorded\n      / Phase-3-COMPLETE-marker-ready / evidence-ref). Status enum:\n      pending / sealed / escalated / unknown (PHASE_3_FINAL_SEALING_\n      STATUS_VALUES).\n    * build_welle_7_audit_anchor_marker emitting two Pre-Auditor-\n      Final-Sealing-Signaling-Markers:\n        - pre_auditor_signaling_ready (pre-auditor present)\n        - pre_auditor_final_sealing_signaling_ready (above AND\n          global_acceptance_verdict_recorded == True).\n      Second flag is the canonical Tomás -> Henrik hand-off signal\n      for Phase-3-COMPLETE-marker readiness at Post-Welle-7 sign-off.\n    * load_welle_7_bundle (mirror of Welle-1..6).\n    * WELLE_7_BUNDLE_ORDER / WELLE_7_BUNDLE_REQUIRED /\n      WELLE_7_KIND_MARKER / WELLE_7_KIND_ENVELOPE constants.\n\n  - tooling/ci/wire_welle_7_audit_trail_anchor.py:\n    Single-purpose producer-envelope wire helper for Selin''s Tag-75\n    persona-engine batch-writer (welle=7). Stdlib-only, no-network,\n    no-subprocess. Mirrors Tag-69..Tag-74 wire-helper shape;\n    envelope kind = welle-7-audit-trail-anchor-producer-envelope.\n\n  - tests/ci/test_welle_7_audit_anchor_tag75.py (27 tests, >= 12\n    per Tag-75 auftrag):\n    * Hash determinism + Welle-1..7 recipe-identity pin (t04).\n    * Bundle-shape validation (welle-7 error messages, t05/t06).\n    * Phase-3-Final-Sealing-Tracking derivation (active/inactive\n      defaults, status-enum collapse to unknown, sign-off\n      precedence for verdict + Phase-3-COMPLETE-marker flags).\n    * Pre-Auditor-Final-Sealing-Signaling-Markers four\n      combinatorial cases (t11).\n    * Marker + envelope shape pins (welle_number=7, kind strings,\n      tracking block, signaling flags, anchors block).\n    * CLI surface tests (emit_helper happy path / missing flags /\n      hygiene-inactive defaults; wire_helper full / minimal /\n      missing-file / malformed-JSON).\n    * Welle-1..7-Kind-Disjointness-Pin (t23, auftrag-mandatory):\n      7 distinct marker kinds + 7 distinct envelope kinds.\n    * Sandbox-boundary invariants (stdlib-only, no-network).\n    * Cross-Substrate-Parity-Markers list pin (full Welle-1..7\n      lineage on marker + envelope anchors).\n\nSandbox-Boundary:\n\n  Stdlib-only. No third-party imports. No network. No OTS-CLI\n  subprocess. Marker / envelope files are local writes only.\n\nCross-coord (separate PR, Selin):\n\n  Selin''s Tag-75 producer (engine.py::backfill_audit_trail_anchors,\n  welle=7) reads the marker/envelope and writes\n  audit_trail_anchor into state/welle-7.json.\n\nCross-coord (separate PR, Henrik):\n\n  Henrik''s Zone-N Audit-Evidence-Index consumes the pre_auditor_\n  final_sealing_signaling_ready flag as the hand-off signal for\n  Phase-3-COMPLETE-marker readiness gating.\n\nPre-existing failures (NOT caused by this PR): five Welle-N-specific-\nalerts cardinality-pin tests fail on stash baseline (Noa-domain,\nout-of-scope here).\n\nAnchors:\n  - ADR-0066 (Four-Wochen-Cadence KW-24..KW-27)\n  - ADR-0058 §Nachtrag (Live-VM acceptance-lane operator-hand)\n  - pre-cutover-acceptance-run-order.md §3.2 (Welle-7 sign-off-\n    Freitag = Global Acceptance-Verdict)\n  - phase-3-marathon-final-acceptance.md (Surface-1..5 conjunction)\n  - Tag-69..Tag-74 audit-anchor PRs (#439, #445, #450, #457, #464,\n    #470)\n\n— Tomás\n\nCo-authored-by: Mira Kessler <mira@wakir.local>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"36f5fba432cb0ed052b23dedbd7853de46ce89d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/trees/36f5fba432cb0ed052b23dedbd7853de46ce89d9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/commits/8f0072edce70dbc98c90ccccea3cb8adf3c92064","verification":{"payload":"tree 36f5fba432cb0ed052b23dedbd7853de46ce89d9\nparent 710d6e7e133d43893837483e72c252e1a7ac4c1f\nauthor wakir-labs <xypu4r8e@addy.io> 1779211639 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779211639 +0200\n\nfeat(ci): Tag-75 Welle-7 Audit-Trail-Anchor-Integration (FINAL Welle, Tomás, 27 tests) (#477)\n\nTag-75 Continuous-Mode-Spawn: FINAL Welle of the Phase-3c-Welle-Marathon.\nMirror of Tag-69..Tag-74 wiring for the Welle-7 audit-trail-anchor\n(KW-27 Doppel-Welle-6+7 entry, Cutover-Mittwoch 2026-07-01, Sign-off-\nFreitag 2026-07-03 = Global Acceptance-Verdict per\ndocs/quality-gates/pre-cutover-acceptance-run-order.md §3.2).\n\nSubstanz:\n\n  - emit_manifest_hash_ots_marker.py:\n    * --mode welle-7-audit-anchor with --welle-7-{rollup,sign-off,\n      validation,pre-auditor} flags.\n    * compute_welle_7_audit_anchor_hash (recipe-identical to\n      Welle-1..6 per Cross-Substrate-Parity-Markers).\n    * derive_phase_3_final_sealing_tracking deriving the six-field\n      tracking block (active / status / iso / global-verdict-recorded\n      / Phase-3-COMPLETE-marker-ready / evidence-ref). Status enum:\n      pending / sealed / escalated / unknown (PHASE_3_FINAL_SEALING_\n      STATUS_VALUES).\n    * build_welle_7_audit_anchor_marker emitting two Pre-Auditor-\n      Final-Sealing-Signaling-Markers:\n        - pre_auditor_signaling_ready (pre-auditor present)\n        - pre_auditor_final_sealing_signaling_ready (above AND\n          global_acceptance_verdict_recorded == True).\n      Second flag is the canonical Tomás -> Henrik hand-off signal\n      for Phase-3-COMPLETE-marker readiness at Post-Welle-7 sign-off.\n    * load_welle_7_bundle (mirror of Welle-1..6).\n    * WELLE_7_BUNDLE_ORDER / WELLE_7_BUNDLE_REQUIRED /\n      WELLE_7_KIND_MARKER / WELLE_7_KIND_ENVELOPE constants.\n\n  - tooling/ci/wire_welle_7_audit_trail_anchor.py:\n    Single-purpose producer-envelope wire helper for Selin''s Tag-75\n    persona-engine batch-writer (welle=7). Stdlib-only, no-network,\n    no-subprocess. Mirrors Tag-69..Tag-74 wire-helper shape;\n    envelope kind = welle-7-audit-trail-anchor-producer-envelope.\n\n  - tests/ci/test_welle_7_audit_anchor_tag75.py (27 tests, >= 12\n    per Tag-75 auftrag):\n    * Hash determinism + Welle-1..7 recipe-identity pin (t04).\n    * Bundle-shape validation (welle-7 error messages, t05/t06).\n    * Phase-3-Final-Sealing-Tracking derivation (active/inactive\n      defaults, status-enum collapse to unknown, sign-off\n      precedence for verdict + Phase-3-COMPLETE-marker flags).\n    * Pre-Auditor-Final-Sealing-Signaling-Markers four\n      combinatorial cases (t11).\n    * Marker + envelope shape pins (welle_number=7, kind strings,\n      tracking block, signaling flags, anchors block).\n    * CLI surface tests (emit_helper happy path / missing flags /\n      hygiene-inactive defaults; wire_helper full / minimal /\n      missing-file / malformed-JSON).\n    * Welle-1..7-Kind-Disjointness-Pin (t23, auftrag-mandatory):\n      7 distinct marker kinds + 7 distinct envelope kinds.\n    * Sandbox-boundary invariants (stdlib-only, no-network).\n    * Cross-Substrate-Parity-Markers list pin (full Welle-1..7\n      lineage on marker + envelope anchors).\n\nSandbox-Boundary:\n\n  Stdlib-only. No third-party imports. No network. No OTS-CLI\n  subprocess. Marker / envelope files are local writes only.\n\nCross-coord (separate PR, Selin):\n\n  Selin''s Tag-75 producer (engine.py::backfill_audit_trail_anchors,\n  welle=7) reads the marker/envelope and writes\n  audit_trail_anchor into state/welle-7.json.\n\nCross-coord (separate PR, Henrik):\n\n  Henrik''s Zone-N Audit-Evidence-Index consumes the pre_auditor_\n  final_sealing_signaling_ready flag as the hand-off signal for\n  Phase-3-COMPLETE-marker readiness gating.\n\nPre-existing failures (NOT caused by this PR): five Welle-N-specific-\nalerts cardinality-pin tests fail on stash baseline (Noa-domain,\nout-of-scope here).\n\nAnchors:\n  - ADR-0066 (Four-Wochen-Cadence KW-24..KW-27)\n  - ADR-0058 §Nachtrag (Live-VM acceptance-lane operator-hand)\n  - pre-cutover-acceptance-run-order.md §3.2 (Welle-7 sign-off-\n    Freitag = Global Acceptance-Verdict)\n  - phase-3-marathon-final-acceptance.md (Surface-1..5 conjunction)\n  - Tag-69..Tag-74 audit-anchor PRs (#439, #445, #450, #457, #464,\n    #470)\n\n— Tomás\n\nCo-authored-by: Mira Kessler <mira@wakir.local>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqDJ13CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAn5AQAHXyE+9aH2u1T/YYhxHaxZ7F\nZZucxmO6jXp4Z02wsU2MJYqhF8d0DW/6UdoHxlE/m8Ps8R+EYyLXpF2psG5Av9mR\nKrOUOw2QtnIadb21esXx2ZsAehEktXZUdOabLLlD1fMKahwdvnmhjhb4U4f+bVd7\ndsLuUWaJafB+vzGUQlegDi3dD8ij15rJ3qaQ2F6V7R3oN1imnzd9iEfOEH9AoliP\n6167a6j3aAl045b8UoiVx09j+F7+c8n5Fsm4P9tiRGDdOcXONw0DEGqpPIe5KKZR\nlGTNVuUtdoZ7g8hFR7xPjA7yiSbkpDc8c7QyU/fnNcwTGUjlNe0M6TbNzkz4t3uc\ngjPeqM3faWhHpqbiDjsOtOSqRRaJowLHaSo+6puc6nafEkrLqOdM6+LtpuK78Ha0\nyo8nG0MOyPqGOkP9NybOQX3CLY16b5OxFMfFPPSDPvtW6T90JCD6EskeOMYHXoCI\nnKtrIeh3oFnefJrIbhh2klE6HqcPs2oX6z7jYs0+wHdadmpHWOAPIwwCUu1fxmX7\nG/6fU8AqdqQblIRJjyVO3RoAzTC6UnbGbV9DWPjr5aE8kBLCi1mn7ybsyqM2MslR\nVGBHBZ6gAkqkoBGIE/lcLDZUttn3N2sjsSfEFyPy8aqGIMEqJj74Fkb8iMlg4IAA\nvV5kTz9YucP//P59mf99\n=RQNa\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-19T17:27:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/8f0072edce70dbc98c90ccccea3cb8adf3c92064","node_id":"C_kwDOSVv36NoAKDhmMDA3MmVkY2U3MGRiYzk4YzkwY2NjY2VhM2NiOGFkZjNjOTIwNjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/710d6e7e133d43893837483e72c252e1a7ac4c1f","sha":"710d6e7e133d43893837483e72c252e1a7ac4c1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/710d6e7e133d43893837483e72c252e1a7ac4c1f"}],"sha":"8f0072edce70dbc98c90ccccea3cb8adf3c92064","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/8f0072edce70dbc98c90ccccea3cb8adf3c92064"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/281068747?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs","id":281068747,"login":"wakir-labs","node_id":"U_kgDOEMDEyw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/710d6e7e133d43893837483e72c252e1a7ac4c1f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-19T17:20:22Z","email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-19T17:20:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Tag-75 Welle-7 Integration-Smoke (Amara, 33 tests) (#478)\n\n* ci(welle-7): Tag-75 Welle-7 Integration-Smoke (Amara, 33 tests)\n\nHermetic end-to-end simulation of the five Welle-7 substrates that\nfire on the canonical KW-27 Mi 2026-07-01 Welle-7 recovery_workflow\nDoppel-Welle-6+7 Cutover-Mittwoch + KW-27 Fr 2026-07-03 Post-Welle-7\nGlobal-Acceptance pipeline (per pre-cutover-acceptance-run-order.md\n§3 row Welle-7 + phase-3-marathon-final-acceptance.md row KW-27 +\nphase-3-marathon-rollback-runbook.md J2).\n\nWelle-7 is the FINAL-SEALING Welle. Post-Welle-7 is the only slot\nwhere the Global Acceptance-Verdict fires (L1-full + L3-full +\nL2-record-validation across Welle-1..7). Tag-75 simulates the\nfinal-sealing substrate-trio + Welle-7''s distinctive IIA-1130\nPre-Auditor gate (AP-7 substitute-control for Henrik self-audit\ntrap; Welle-7 is the ORIGINAL IIA-1130 case per Henrik Tag-39).\n\nStages\n------\n\n  S1 Welle-7-Producer simulation (Selin Tag-75): state-file\n     render + schema-pin + welle-number=7 + status=pending.\n  S2 Welle-7-Audit-Anchor simulation (Tomas Tag-75): SHA-256\n     bundle anchor across canonical JSON; 64-hex hash invariant.\n  S3 Doppel-Welle-6+7 Coupling-Gate W7 side (Amara): partner=W6\n     subscribe_loop READY/PARTNER-MISSING/PARTNER-DEFECT trinary.\n  S4 IIA-1130 Pre-Auditor-Gate (Amara, Tag-75 distinctive):\n     state/welle-7-pre-auditor-decision.json presence + schema +\n     APPROVED/PENDING/REJECTED/MISSING/MALFORMED quinary.\n  S5 Final-Sealing-Verification (Amara, Tag-75 distinctive):\n     Post-Welle-7 Global-Acceptance Layer-anchor discoverability\n     (L1 Tag-40 + L3 Tag-43 + L2 Tag-41); READY/PARTIAL/BREAK.\n  S6 Aggregate WELLE-7-INTACT/DRIFT/DEFECT.\n\nForward-cascade\n---------------\n\nA Welle-7 DEFECT blocks (6,7) under Doppel-Welle-6+7 PAR-path\nsymmetric coupling. Same tuple as Tag-74 Welle-6 cascade --\nattests the symmetric coupling on the W7 side.\n\nBrief-vs-canonical reconciliation (Tag-71+72+73+74 lehre)\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\nThree reconciliations surfaced on the envelope:\n\n  * Brief: \"Welle-7 = Final-Sealing-Welle\" framing.\n    Canonical: substrate_modul=recovery_workflow (J2);\n    schedule_role=final_sealing_welle. Both framings surfaced.\n  * Brief: cited \"ADR-0066 vs KW-24-Acceptance §7\".\n    Canonical: ADR-0066 wins; KW-24-Acceptance §7 surfaced as\n    parallel-view evidence.\n  * Brief: \"§11 Pre-Auditor-Disziplin\".\n    Canonical: full anchor-chain surfaced (AP-7 + hot-spot-\n    probe Check-4 + Henrik Tag-39 Pre-Audit-Bundle + IIA-1130\n    Independence-and-Objectivity standard).\n\nFiles\n-----\n\n  .github/workflows/welle-7-integration-smoke.yml\n  tooling/ci/aggregate_welle_7_integration.py\n  tests/ci/test_welle_7_integration_tag75.py (33 tests)\n\nSandbox posture\n---------------\n\nHermetic (stdlib + workflow-dispatch + on-disk synthetic\nbundles). No gh workflow run; no NATS; no SPIRE; no actual\nWelle-7 dispatch; no AR-Hand Pre-Auditor-Decision emission. The\nactual Welle-7 trigger on 2026-07-01 is operator-hand; the\nPre-Auditor-Decision is AR-Hand-Governance.\n\nCross-Review-Markers\n--------------------\n\n  Zone-M: QA x Selin (producer S1, final-sealing L2 Tag-41)\n  Zone-M: QA x Tomas (audit-anchor S2, final-sealing L1+L3\n          Tag-40/Tag-43)\n  Zone-M: QA x Selin+Tomas (doppel-coupling-gate S3 partner=W6)\n  Zone-N: QA x Henrik (IIA-1130 Pre-Auditor-Gate S4 substitute-\n          control; aggregated WELLE-7 envelope as audit-evidence)\n\nContinuous-Mode (Mira, 2026-05-19); not a required status check.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci(welle-7): Tag-75 Stage-5 bash-to-python bool conversion fix\n\nStage-5 Final-Sealing-Verification heredoc was substituting bash\nbool strings (true/false) directly into Python literals, causing\nNameError: name ''true'' is not defined at runtime.\n\nFix: convert via \"$var\" == \"true\" comparison inside the Python\nblock before assigning to Python identifiers.\n\nNo semantic change; verdict logic and envelope shape unchanged.\nTests still 33/33 green locally (no test exercised the heredoc\nsubstitution; the existing tests parse-only the workflow YAML).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Kai Hoffmann <kai@wakir.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8e6969bcd52788da5e4435910b179057571d3f0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/trees/8e6969bcd52788da5e4435910b179057571d3f0d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/commits/710d6e7e133d43893837483e72c252e1a7ac4c1f","verification":{"payload":"tree 8e6969bcd52788da5e4435910b179057571d3f0d\nparent 56b4bc1c171e4085f774059a8bbc0bd67b0c9ce5\nauthor wakir-labs <xypu4r8e@addy.io> 1779211222 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779211222 +0200\n\nTag-75 Welle-7 Integration-Smoke (Amara, 33 tests) (#478)\n\n* ci(welle-7): Tag-75 Welle-7 Integration-Smoke (Amara, 33 tests)\n\nHermetic end-to-end simulation of the five Welle-7 substrates that\nfire on the canonical KW-27 Mi 2026-07-01 Welle-7 recovery_workflow\nDoppel-Welle-6+7 Cutover-Mittwoch + KW-27 Fr 2026-07-03 Post-Welle-7\nGlobal-Acceptance pipeline (per pre-cutover-acceptance-run-order.md\n§3 row Welle-7 + phase-3-marathon-final-acceptance.md row KW-27 +\nphase-3-marathon-rollback-runbook.md J2).\n\nWelle-7 is the FINAL-SEALING Welle. Post-Welle-7 is the only slot\nwhere the Global Acceptance-Verdict fires (L1-full + L3-full +\nL2-record-validation across Welle-1..7). Tag-75 simulates the\nfinal-sealing substrate-trio + Welle-7''s distinctive IIA-1130\nPre-Auditor gate (AP-7 substitute-control for Henrik self-audit\ntrap; Welle-7 is the ORIGINAL IIA-1130 case per Henrik Tag-39).\n\nStages\n------\n\n  S1 Welle-7-Producer simulation (Selin Tag-75): state-file\n     render + schema-pin + welle-number=7 + status=pending.\n  S2 Welle-7-Audit-Anchor simulation (Tomas Tag-75): SHA-256\n     bundle anchor across canonical JSON; 64-hex hash invariant.\n  S3 Doppel-Welle-6+7 Coupling-Gate W7 side (Amara): partner=W6\n     subscribe_loop READY/PARTNER-MISSING/PARTNER-DEFECT trinary.\n  S4 IIA-1130 Pre-Auditor-Gate (Amara, Tag-75 distinctive):\n     state/welle-7-pre-auditor-decision.json presence + schema +\n     APPROVED/PENDING/REJECTED/MISSING/MALFORMED quinary.\n  S5 Final-Sealing-Verification (Amara, Tag-75 distinctive):\n     Post-Welle-7 Global-Acceptance Layer-anchor discoverability\n     (L1 Tag-40 + L3 Tag-43 + L2 Tag-41); READY/PARTIAL/BREAK.\n  S6 Aggregate WELLE-7-INTACT/DRIFT/DEFECT.\n\nForward-cascade\n---------------\n\nA Welle-7 DEFECT blocks (6,7) under Doppel-Welle-6+7 PAR-path\nsymmetric coupling. Same tuple as Tag-74 Welle-6 cascade --\nattests the symmetric coupling on the W7 side.\n\nBrief-vs-canonical reconciliation (Tag-71+72+73+74 lehre)\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\nThree reconciliations surfaced on the envelope:\n\n  * Brief: \"Welle-7 = Final-Sealing-Welle\" framing.\n    Canonical: substrate_modul=recovery_workflow (J2);\n    schedule_role=final_sealing_welle. Both framings surfaced.\n  * Brief: cited \"ADR-0066 vs KW-24-Acceptance §7\".\n    Canonical: ADR-0066 wins; KW-24-Acceptance §7 surfaced as\n    parallel-view evidence.\n  * Brief: \"§11 Pre-Auditor-Disziplin\".\n    Canonical: full anchor-chain surfaced (AP-7 + hot-spot-\n    probe Check-4 + Henrik Tag-39 Pre-Audit-Bundle + IIA-1130\n    Independence-and-Objectivity standard).\n\nFiles\n-----\n\n  .github/workflows/welle-7-integration-smoke.yml\n  tooling/ci/aggregate_welle_7_integration.py\n  tests/ci/test_welle_7_integration_tag75.py (33 tests)\n\nSandbox posture\n---------------\n\nHermetic (stdlib + workflow-dispatch + on-disk synthetic\nbundles). No gh workflow run; no NATS; no SPIRE; no actual\nWelle-7 dispatch; no AR-Hand Pre-Auditor-Decision emission. The\nactual Welle-7 trigger on 2026-07-01 is operator-hand; the\nPre-Auditor-Decision is AR-Hand-Governance.\n\nCross-Review-Markers\n--------------------\n\n  Zone-M: QA x Selin (producer S1, final-sealing L2 Tag-41)\n  Zone-M: QA x Tomas (audit-anchor S2, final-sealing L1+L3\n          Tag-40/Tag-43)\n  Zone-M: QA x Selin+Tomas (doppel-coupling-gate S3 partner=W6)\n  Zone-N: QA x Henrik (IIA-1130 Pre-Auditor-Gate S4 substitute-\n          control; aggregated WELLE-7 envelope as audit-evidence)\n\nContinuous-Mode (Mira, 2026-05-19); not a required status check.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci(welle-7): Tag-75 Stage-5 bash-to-python bool conversion fix\n\nStage-5 Final-Sealing-Verification heredoc was substituting bash\nbool strings (true/false) directly into Python literals, causing\nNameError: name ''true'' is not defined at runtime.\n\nFix: convert via \"$var\" == \"true\" comparison inside the Python\nblock before assigning to Python identifiers.\n\nNo semantic change; verdict logic and envelope shape unchanged.\nTests still 33/33 green locally (no test exercised the heredoc\nsubstitution; the existing tests parse-only the workflow YAML).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Kai Hoffmann <kai@wakir.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqDJvWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUSkQAJYFqRoVOa3rfGvXG8s/+pDR\nyv0QBz4CdU0FdwIsNAFdB+pHjPCsvUQKRFW2S15uvA79OD1ztDQu2y/kaJXB1xDj\nUAwwfM6IriU+wWfORvPQMOvrGJkas3w/XY/62o+g0UIeel39kPfUDjf99HC25cHY\nT1fg4nzrCv/CBK+/Q92ippPx2Q2ICdQidxl1nAuqpSYd+EnEn6gWk+O7DBreZUUB\nicg+PeaJYVpR8PORzgEIVvsjIoMeEHTUpV2xURtXYSndp6SJvAv3SRZsJZuksttm\nJCuZ/S+GRkxn5zv4I9cecXsuxsIF+BK3Kv5DIpUg7n28QS/M9U+QFxMlXDwLC0Mt\noZV4Spd3XTABDtNEihf00geWjJhYE3XjYX8eMS1uUmhjHxkfgxX5Y98aSUKRf5XW\n+5KAH52CIyfr1EOgOnsGDQ1W9uRPhbHghY2578TCT13rYpTOo/EvuLQTFerTW3VX\nQ9pNSBJC9d7MPWBqumXQmNo7F4jW5L6+95Oa0kOIVekwCVbjoPJjKY3elLpCT7rO\nLtSlXEUpuAKOgjQB6WA02AJSYmYql2byFl9AQBd97uG+OfJ3jViE1yN1E3r9HEW1\njm/5XmHUVG/z+5EHQcTHL5kdwwp8nTl6BmfIb9yJJ+dDXdi6kg6+IpdlAdyo0pPe\n59rQvCIErpVCLzLlEQWf\n=HJ5w\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-19T17:20:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/710d6e7e133d43893837483e72c252e1a7ac4c1f","node_id":"C_kwDOSVv36NoAKDcxMGQ2ZTdlMTMzZDQzODkzODM3NDgzZTcyYzI1MmUxYTdhYzRjMWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/56b4bc1c171e4085f774059a8bbc0bd67b0c9ce5","sha":"56b4bc1c171e4085f774059a8bbc0bd67b0c9ce5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/56b4bc1c171e4085f774059a8bbc0bd67b0c9ce5"}],"sha":"710d6e7e133d43893837483e72c252e1a7ac4c1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/710d6e7e133d43893837483e72c252e1a7ac4c1f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/281068747?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs","id":281068747,"login":"wakir-labs","node_id":"U_kgDOEMDEyw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/56b4bc1c171e4085f774059a8bbc0bd67b0c9ce5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-19T17:10:44Z","email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-19T17:10:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(persona-engine): Tag-75 Welle-7 Final-Sealing producer (Selin, 38 tests) (#475)\n\nWelle-7 is the terminal Welle of the Phase-3c-Welle-Marathon (KW-27 per\ndocs/quality-gates/pre-cutover-acceptance-run-order.md §3 + canonical\ndocs/quality-gates/phase-3c-doppel-welle-6-7.md §4 Phase-3-Marathon-\nSchluss-Acceptance). The sign-off carries TWO hot-spot axes:\n\n  1. Pre-Auditor-Guard (Henrik-cannot-self-sign-off, analog Welle-3)\n  2. Final-Sealing-Marker-Guard (Phase-3-Marathon-Schluss-Acceptance)\n\nSubstanz\n--------\n\n* WelleStateProducer.handle_welle_7_signoff_event with all three\n  preconditions (sign-off-marker + pre-auditor-decision + final-sealing-\n  marker). Trigger=\"final-sealing\" (sixth disjoint marker-family).\n* engine.handle_welle_7_signoff_event top-level dispatcher.\n* engine_async.handle_welle_7_signoff_event async wrapper.\n* FinalSealingError + FINAL_SEALING_CONFIRMED + FINAL_SEALING_GUARDED_WELLEN\n  constants. \"confirmed\" is intentionally distinct from Welle-2''s \"sealed\".\n* Stricter-idempotency: a retried sign-off with degraded preconditions is\n  refused EVEN IF the state-file already reports signed-off (audit-trail\n  forensic invariant; differs from W2/4/5/6 idempotency).\n\nTests (38, all green)\n---------------------\n\n* §1 Public-API surface invariants (6 tests).\n* §2 Six-marker-family disjointness with intentional W7 pre-auditor x\n  final-sealing overlap pinned (4 tests).\n* §3 Producer-method direct-call (13 tests covering happy path, all three\n  marker refusals, refusal-order determinism, pre-auditor + final-sealing\n  stricter-idempotency, time-invariants, atomic write).\n* §4 Top-level sync handler (4 tests).\n* §5 Async wrapper (3 tests).\n* §6 Rollback after Welle-7 sign-off (1 test).\n* §7 Six-marker-family triggers pairwise-distinct (2 tests, the\n  Tag-75-specific 6-family pin).\n* §8 Audit-record canonical-JSON byte-stability (1 test).\n* §9 FinalSealingError inherits from WelleProducerError (1 test).\n* §10 state/welle-7.json KW-27 on-disk anchor pin (2 tests).\n\nHermetic\n--------\n\nNo network, no NATS, no SPIRE, no subprocess. Pure stdlib file I/O on\ntmp_path fixtures. Mirrors Tag-69/70/71/72/73/74 producer-test\nconventions verbatim. REUSE 3.3 compliant.\n\nCross-substrate boundary\n------------------------\n\nThis PR pins only the engine-side producer-substrate (\"final-sealing\"\ntrigger emission + state-file transition). The downstream\nPHASE_3_COMPLETE_VIA_DOPPEL_WELLE_6_7 marker emission lives at the\naudit-trail-consumer level (phase-3c-doppel-welle-6-7.md §4.1); this\nproducer does NOT couple to marker-emission semantics. Zone-K\n(Tomas WAT) / Zone-L (Reza Identity) / Zone-J (Kai Container) +\nAisha (HR Persona-Defs) boundaries preserved.\n\nVerification\n------------\n\n* 1694/1694 persona_engine tests pass (1656 baseline + 38 Tag-75 new).\n* REUSE 3.3 compliant.\n* No regression on Tag-74 Welle-6 producer or W5-anchor-fix tests.\n\nRefs\n----\n\n* docs/quality-gates/pre-cutover-acceptance-run-order.md §3 (KW-27)\n* docs/quality-gates/phase-3c-doppel-welle-6-7.md §4 + §4.1\n* Tag-71 Welle-3 Pre-Auditor-Guard (mirror)\n* Tag-74 Welle-6 Cross-Substrate-Parity producer (mirror)\n\nCo-authored-by: pengine-eng <pengine@wakir.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6c985e9fe33990e5c2400cc1bf3d295b0854f115","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/trees/6c985e9fe33990e5c2400cc1bf3d295b0854f115"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/commits/56b4bc1c171e4085f774059a8bbc0bd67b0c9ce5","verification":{"payload":"tree 6c985e9fe33990e5c2400cc1bf3d295b0854f115\nparent 8fc24d380f1eb45c72b70ea282c92b56e40b2f15\nauthor wakir-labs <xypu4r8e@addy.io> 1779210644 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779210644 +0200\n\nfeat(persona-engine): Tag-75 Welle-7 Final-Sealing producer (Selin, 38 tests) (#475)\n\nWelle-7 is the terminal Welle of the Phase-3c-Welle-Marathon (KW-27 per\ndocs/quality-gates/pre-cutover-acceptance-run-order.md §3 + canonical\ndocs/quality-gates/phase-3c-doppel-welle-6-7.md §4 Phase-3-Marathon-\nSchluss-Acceptance). The sign-off carries TWO hot-spot axes:\n\n  1. Pre-Auditor-Guard (Henrik-cannot-self-sign-off, analog Welle-3)\n  2. Final-Sealing-Marker-Guard (Phase-3-Marathon-Schluss-Acceptance)\n\nSubstanz\n--------\n\n* WelleStateProducer.handle_welle_7_signoff_event with all three\n  preconditions (sign-off-marker + pre-auditor-decision + final-sealing-\n  marker). Trigger=\"final-sealing\" (sixth disjoint marker-family).\n* engine.handle_welle_7_signoff_event top-level dispatcher.\n* engine_async.handle_welle_7_signoff_event async wrapper.\n* FinalSealingError + FINAL_SEALING_CONFIRMED + FINAL_SEALING_GUARDED_WELLEN\n  constants. \"confirmed\" is intentionally distinct from Welle-2''s \"sealed\".\n* Stricter-idempotency: a retried sign-off with degraded preconditions is\n  refused EVEN IF the state-file already reports signed-off (audit-trail\n  forensic invariant; differs from W2/4/5/6 idempotency).\n\nTests (38, all green)\n---------------------\n\n* §1 Public-API surface invariants (6 tests).\n* §2 Six-marker-family disjointness with intentional W7 pre-auditor x\n  final-sealing overlap pinned (4 tests).\n* §3 Producer-method direct-call (13 tests covering happy path, all three\n  marker refusals, refusal-order determinism, pre-auditor + final-sealing\n  stricter-idempotency, time-invariants, atomic write).\n* §4 Top-level sync handler (4 tests).\n* §5 Async wrapper (3 tests).\n* §6 Rollback after Welle-7 sign-off (1 test).\n* §7 Six-marker-family triggers pairwise-distinct (2 tests, the\n  Tag-75-specific 6-family pin).\n* §8 Audit-record canonical-JSON byte-stability (1 test).\n* §9 FinalSealingError inherits from WelleProducerError (1 test).\n* §10 state/welle-7.json KW-27 on-disk anchor pin (2 tests).\n\nHermetic\n--------\n\nNo network, no NATS, no SPIRE, no subprocess. Pure stdlib file I/O on\ntmp_path fixtures. Mirrors Tag-69/70/71/72/73/74 producer-test\nconventions verbatim. REUSE 3.3 compliant.\n\nCross-substrate boundary\n------------------------\n\nThis PR pins only the engine-side producer-substrate (\"final-sealing\"\ntrigger emission + state-file transition). The downstream\nPHASE_3_COMPLETE_VIA_DOPPEL_WELLE_6_7 marker emission lives at the\naudit-trail-consumer level (phase-3c-doppel-welle-6-7.md §4.1); this\nproducer does NOT couple to marker-emission semantics. Zone-K\n(Tomas WAT) / Zone-L (Reza Identity) / Zone-J (Kai Container) +\nAisha (HR Persona-Defs) boundaries preserved.\n\nVerification\n------------\n\n* 1694/1694 persona_engine tests pass (1656 baseline + 38 Tag-75 new).\n* REUSE 3.3 compliant.\n* No regression on Tag-74 Welle-6 producer or W5-anchor-fix tests.\n\nRefs\n----\n\n* docs/quality-gates/pre-cutover-acceptance-run-order.md §3 (KW-27)\n* docs/quality-gates/phase-3c-doppel-welle-6-7.md §4 + §4.1\n* Tag-71 Welle-3 Pre-Auditor-Guard (mirror)\n* Tag-74 Welle-6 Cross-Substrate-Parity producer (mirror)\n\nCo-authored-by: pengine-eng <pengine@wakir.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqDJmUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5eoQAF4LzD9jqBoDdmWxcE8E+hnJ\nDOBySsMFzBq9YKmP9NHs5eFpmr8uHb3ZTWLIv6K/w919I5BAzOZ3k0tMyi0BzrPd\nDdCbbfk4b53zDIxrZise8tqVoUDrZDVhmLB4HmOeICGj92KFW1b0PsxPHr8Dt3lw\nJfF2XFzoJICUnPtFdIe8G6dBWxzjIIpQg+TxwyEeUlaiK1UiRtteYkK7iR13Yh/W\nsY9wdcxosUo9Y0TsSBMGMuWzcdShN0z59WxsHHzn9wbFRCto9Fn8CV0X62OJJzUb\nUcjY0Gz/D694bAs5S74uyvDs/cBr4EcKwh2t8SU2gMLxJZlIlFM1SjAP2zyQ4rpL\nnG9fmCKUI6Lj9mvqHsHXhh4U3nUJF1LvYsGYzcLqtGVkUuaL+mji6zfL9lf7IFu1\nSNdMzxJLPp+4gvijvbV7zITLV1K3nnOnzSKsTPCFwCxUqM70dfHlADrdVQgQycse\ndpfpD5bBjpxc1jl7R/D70rEDSB38Jo09/6eDNZ6NDHcA+ohmyevE