liation-tag74.md documents the two-canonical-views\n    (run-order vs acceptance-criteria) and the resolution rule:\n    engine-side runtime artefacts align to run-order view; the\n    kw-24-acceptance aggregator stays as the parallel-substrate-view.\n  - Conventions test test_06_welle_345_kw_anchor (Tag-67-era pin\n    \"all three on KW-25\") updated to per-Welle expected-map.\n  - Tag-73 aggregate_welle_5_integration.py BRIEF_VS_CANONICAL\n    resolution updated: \"NOT patched\" -> \"PATCHED in Tag-74\"\n    (the Tag-73-era ''state-file not patched'' resolution is\n    superseded).\n\nTeil 2 - Welle-6 Cross-Substrate-Parity sign-off shorthand:\n  - WelleStateProducer.handle_welle_6_signoff_event: structural\n    in-progress -> signed-off with two markers:\n    sign_off_marker_status == \"signed-off\" AND\n    cross_substrate_parity_marker_status == \"verified\". Audit-record\n    trigger=\"cross-substrate-parity\" (5th disjoint trigger family).\n  - CROSS_SUBSTRATE_PARITY_GUARDED_WELLEN = {6} + CROSS_SUBSTRATE_\n    PARITY_VERIFIED = \"verified\" + CrossSubstrateParityError.\n  - engine.handle_welle_6_signoff_event + engine_async wrapper.\n  - 32 tests test_welle_6_producer_w5_fix_tag74.py including 5-marker-\n    family pairwise-distinct + W5-anchor-fix verification.\n\n195 producer-test green + 1656 persona-engine-test green + 236 modified-\ntest green. REUSE-clean.\n\nScope discipline: kw-anchor-agnostic producer (no transition-machine\ngate on kw_cutover_anchor); the engine-side runtime alignment is to\nrun-order view per the reconciliation rule.\n\nCo-authored-by: pengine-eng <pengine@wakir.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"70d96789fb7a65e0772fc079beb480210b82d6c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/trees/70d96789fb7a65e0772fc079beb480210b82d6c8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/commits/72c05813a78b0e56991826c68176fba2903ae0eb","verification