ithub.com/users/wakir-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs","id":281068747,"login":"wakir-labs","node_id":"U_kgDOEMDEyw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/beb125ab20762c871b123fa6dddde406078c9eea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-19T16:45:21Z","email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-19T16:45:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(operations): Tag-74 Operator-Hand Welle-6 Day-of-Recipe-Patch (Kai, 28 tests, doc-form-only) (#469)\n\nWelle-6 Day-of-Recipe-Patch (subscribe_loop, KW-27-Mi 2026-06-24) als\nchirurgische Patch-Lage ueber dem Tag-66 Eve-Recipe §4.5 + dem\nphase-3c-welle-6-runbook §3. Folgt dem Welle-5-Patch-Pattern\n(Tag-73 PR #463, 26 Tests) und Welle-3-Patch-Pattern (Tag-71, IIA-1130\nPre-Auditor-Discipline).\n\nWelle-6 hat zwei verschraenkte Hot-Spot-Achsen (dual-axis wie Welle-5):\n\n* nats-subscribe-mode      -- NATS-Subscribe-Mode-Live-Check; Henrik\n                              Tag-46 A8-Lineage (NATS-JetStream-\n                              Loss-Recovery), Live-Mode-Verification\n                              gegen Produktions-JetStream-Cluster.\n* subscribe-loop-cascade   -- Subscribe-Loop-Cascade-into-Welle-7\n                              Replay-Divergenz; Cascading-Drift\n                              zwischen Rust- und Python-Subscribe-\n                              Loop-Resolver.\n\n**Strukturelle KW-27-vs-KW-26-Asymmetrie**: anders als die KW-26-\nDoppel-Welle (Welle-4+Welle-5, symmetrische Cross-Modul-Schnittstellen,\ninline-Cross-Modul-Stress-Step) ist die KW-27-Doppel-Welle\n(Welle-6+Welle-7) **gerichtet-asymmetrisch** -- Welle-6 -> Welle-7. Der\nCross-Modul-Stress laeuft **out-of-band** via Phase-2-Acceptance-Gate\ndaily rollup (axis: cross-modul-subscribe-loop-recovery-workflow).\nDiese Asymmetrie ist explizit in §2, R-W6-D und §6 (TP-W6-3) codifiziert.\n\nLiefer-Artefakte:\n\n* docs/operations/operator-hand-welle-6-eve-recipe-patch.md\n  -- 9 Sections (§0..§9), 5 P-Steps (P1..P5), 4 Rollback-Pfade\n  (R-W6-A..D, einschliesslich R-W6-D KW-27-Doppel-Welle-Decouple\n  mit Cascade-Directionality-Asymmetrie), 3 AR-Hand-Touchpoints\n  (TP-W6-1..3), 8 Aggregate-Verdict-Marker.\n\n* tooling/ci/verify_welle_6_recipe_patch_doc.py\n  -- Tag-74 hermetic verifier, stdlib-only Python, 12 hard-checks\n  H1..H12 + 3 soft-checks S1..S3, exit 0/1/2.\n\n* tests/observability/test_welle_6_recipe_patch_tag74.py\n  -- 28 hermetic tests (9 doc-substance A1..A9 + 19 verifier\n  B1..B19), stdlib + pytest only, kein Netzwerk-IO, kein\n  Side-Effekt. Inkl. directional-cascade-asymmetry-Test (B19) als\n  strukturelle Differenzierung zur Welle-5-Patch-Symmetrie.\n\nSandbox-Disziplin: doc-form-only (ADR-0058 + AR-Direktive Tag-44\n+ Tag-66 + Tag-71 + Tag-73). Keine Subprozess-PR-Mutationen, keine\nState-File-Commits aus diesem PR -- nur Doc + Verifier + Tests.\n\nTag-74 Continuous-Mode-Spawn (Marathon). Welle-3 -> Welle-5 ->\nWelle-6 Patch-Kaskade haelt; naechste Folge ist Welle-7-Patch\n(Tag-75, KW-27-Doppel-Welle-Partner).\n\nCo-authored-by: Kai Hoffmann (DevOps) <kai@wakir-labs.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f3c111a3ee48328553675d0ac37e762ab72054ad","url":"https://api.github.com/r