r-runtime/commits/60a4c25200e1ae8cb3dd05266ee882803fdf6303/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-19T16:42:27Z","email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-19T16:42:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(observability,ci): Tag-74 Welle-6 cross-substrate-parity alert-routing + Tag-73 reuse-lint enforce-hook (Noa SRE) (#468)\n\nTeil 1 -- Welle-6 Cross-Substrate-Parity-Alert-Routing-Erweiterung:\ntwo additional Welle-6 subscribe-loop alerts close the positive-\nconfirmation + consumer-lag routing gap surfaced during the KW-27\ndoppel-cutover audit. Both alerts carry the new routing-class\n`welle-6-subscribe-loop-info` -> ntfy:ar-hand-info + activity-log\n(no on-call page; existing Welle-6 page-level alerts cover\nhard failure).\n\n  * WakirPhase3Welle6SubscribeLoopHealthy   (info)\n  * WakirPhase3Welle6JetStreamConsumerLag   (warning)\n\nTeil 2 -- Tomas Tag-73 follow-up: existing Tag-61 hint-mode\n`reuse-wrap-pre-merge-lint` hook caught drift advisorily but did\nNOT block commits; four Tag-66/68/71 drift episodes slipped\nthrough. Tag-74 adds a second hook bound to the same lint helper\nin `--mode enforce`, scoped narrowly to `tests/observability/**`\nand `tests/phase_3c/**` where drift recurs. Tag-61 hint-mode hook\nremains for broader test-tree advisory coverage (additive, not\nreplacement).\n\nBridge ALERT_CATALOG + ROUTING_CLASS_CHANNELS + VALID_ROUTING_CLASSES\n+ ROUTING_CLASS_ESCALATION_SECONDS extended. Protocol-mirror-seed\ncopies of dashboards + bridge updated byte-equal.\n\nTests: 28 hermetic tests covering YAML alert surface, bridge\ncatalog, routing-class table shape, cross-repo-mirror byte-\nequality, alert<->catalog cross-reference, and the\n`.pre-commit-config.yaml` enforce-mode hook structure.\n\nCo-authored-by: Noa Bergstroem <noa@wakir.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6dd022f059fe3d8930c5f411dfc1608f19dee5b5",