b.com/users/wakir-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs","id":281068747,"login":"wakir-labs","node_id":"U_kgDOEMDEyw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/155861868e0be7de9695b7dcd43c268b31fcbb9f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-19T16:18:34Z","email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-19T16:18:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Tag-73 Welle-5 Audit-Trail-Anchor-Integration (Tomás, 25 tests) (#464)\n\n* feat(ci): Tag-73 Welle-5 Audit-Trail-Anchor-Integration (Tomás, 25 tests)\n\nTag-73 Welle-5 State-File Audit-Trail-Anchor-Integration:\n\n  * tooling/ots/emit_manifest_hash_ots_marker.py: adds\n    --mode welle-5-audit-anchor + compute_welle_5_audit_anchor_hash\n    + build_welle_5_audit_anchor_marker + load_welle_5_bundle +\n    derive_capability_token_rotation_tracking. Same hash recipe as\n    Welle-1..4; welle-5-specific kind strings + welle_number=5;\n    capability_token_rotation_tracking block surfaces rotation-\n    discipline cadence + last-rotation-iso + replay-window-closed\n    flag + rotation-evidence-ref. Reza Sprint-9 cross-coord\n    (Capability-Token-Rotation+Replay sub).\n\n  * tooling/ci/wire_welle_5_audit_trail_anchor.py: producer-facing\n    envelope helper for Selin''s Tag-73 persona-engine batch-writer.\n    Stdlib-only, no network, no subprocess. Mirrors Tag-72 surface.\n\n  * tests/ci/test_welle_5_audit_anchor_tag73.py: 25 tests covering\n    hash determinism, cross-welle recipe identity (Welle-1..5),\n    bundle-shape validation, tracking derivation (active / unknown /\n    replay-window-precedence), marker + envelope shape, CLI surface\n    (happy + error paths), kind-disjointness pin (Welle-1..5), Tag-67\n    verifier regex round-trip, sandbox-boundary invariants.\n\nHermetic audit-only: no network I/O, no OTS calendar call, no\nsubprocess outside test fixtures. Real OTS calendar stamping\nremains Operator-Hand on a network-attached host (separate runbook\nstep). Cross-Review-Zone-K (PEngine producer wiring).\n\nSelin Tag-73 follow-up (separate PR) wires this marker into the\nengine.py backfill_audit_trail_anchors welle=5 path.\n\nAnchors: decisions/0007-internal-audit-trail-ots.md, Amara Tag-67\nstate-file conventions, Tomás Tag-69/70/71/72 prior audit-anchor\nwiring (PRs #439, #445, #450, #457).\n\n— Tomás\n\n* fix(reuse): wrap SPDX literal in Tag-73 capability-token verifier test\n\nThe Tag-73 capability-token-layer verifier test (Reza #461) carries\na bare ``SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0`` literal inside an\nassertion message. ``reuse lint`` flags this as an invalid SPDX\nlicense expression, breaking the License-Hygiene Gate (ADR-0061)\non rebased PRs.\n\nWrap the literal with ``# REUSE-IgnoreStart`` / ``# REUSE-IgnoreEnd``\nmarkers per REUSE-3.3 convention. The assertion itself is unchanged.\n\n— Tomás\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mira Kessler <mira@wakir.local>","tree":{"sha":"9c530b2e33f8d844056db836ad6bc72f17822d36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/trees/9c530b2e33f8d844056db836ad6bc72f17822d36"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/commits/155861868e0be7de9695b7dcd43c268b31fcbb9f","verification":{"payload":"tree 9c530b2e33f8d844056db836ad6bc72f17822d36\nparent 3a6927cb21efee250ace73ebb05d49291599fefd\nauthor wakir-labs <xypu4r8e@addy.io> 1779207514 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779207514 +0200\n\nTag-73 Welle-5 Audit-Trail-Anchor-Integration (Tomás, 25 tests) (#464)\n\n* feat(ci): Tag-73 Welle-5 Audit-Trail-Anchor-Integration (Tomás, 25 tests)\n\nTag-73 Welle-5 State-File Audit-Trail-Anchor-Integration:\n\n  * tooling/ots/emit_manifest_hash_ots_marker.py: adds\n    --mode welle-5-audit-anchor + compute_welle_5_audit_anchor_hash\n    + build_welle_5_audit_anchor_marker + load_welle_5_bundle +\n    derive_capability_token_rotation_tracking. Same hash recipe as\n    Welle-1..4; welle-5-specific kind strings + welle_number=5;\n    capability_token_rotation_tracking block surfaces rotation-\n    discipline cadence + last-rotation-iso + replay-window-closed\n    flag + rotation-evidence-ref. Reza Sprint-9 cross-coord\n    (Capability-Token-Rotation+Replay sub).\n\n  * tooling/ci/wire_welle_5_audit_trail_anchor.py: producer-facing\n    envelope helper for Selin''s Tag-73 persona-engine batch-writer.\n    Stdlib-only, no network, no subprocess. Mirrors Tag-72 surface.\n\n  * tests/ci/test_welle_5_audit_anchor_tag73.py: 25 tests covering\n    hash determinism, cross-welle recipe identity (Welle-1..5),\n    bundle-shape validation, tracking derivation (active / unknown /\n    replay-window-precedence), marker + envelope shape, CLI surface\n    (happy + error paths), kind-disjointness pin (Welle-1..5), Tag-67\n    verifier regex round-trip, sandbox-boundary invariants.\n\nHermetic audit-only: no network I/O, no OTS calendar call, no\nsubprocess outside test fixtures. Real OTS calendar stamping\nremains Operator-Hand on a network-attached host (separate runbook\nstep). Cross-Review-Zone-K (PEngine producer wiring).\n\nSelin Tag-73 follow-up (separate PR) wires this marker into the\nengine.py backfill_audit_trail_anchors welle=5 path.\n\nAnchors: decisions/0007-internal-audit-trail-ots.md, Amara Tag-67\nstate-file conventions, Tomás Tag-69/70/71/72 prior audit-anchor\nwiring (PRs #439, #445, #450, #457).\n\n— Tomás\n\n* fix(reuse): wrap SPDX literal in Tag-73 capability-token verifier test\n\nThe Tag-73 capability-token-layer verifier test (Reza #461) carries\na bare ``SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0`` literal inside an\nassertion message. ``reuse lint`` flags this as an invalid SPDX\nlicense expression, breaking the License-Hygiene Gate (ADR-0061)\non rebased PRs.\n\nWrap the literal with ``# REUSE-IgnoreStart`` / ``# REUSE-IgnoreEnd``\nmarkers per REUSE-3.3 convention. The assertion itself is unchanged.\n\n— Tomás\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mira Kessler <mira@wakir.local>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqDI1aCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAK9QQAKR80Z/YSf8wL1bJeOAcbMFX\noSk2ENVc0UmacyRVPdXdtl5MRGUJD89NxR318SkzucpH7oKZdmubHiEnjoPxasV7\niAUeJYNKeTNO2bII1rnjMjXKxSuuaPsSD6UI+LPRPF51lSWqje8awoo3W+c8aERK\nV9X40m8JjB8NZQfuLlviEFWyblp1W/vIclS2TPgGynXTs65M7q5jKPUJWaAnLgdu\nWCvRjPXjB7kQmRwv0F3mOs3G+aXboBSdoHq5uhDemXXhHh/iakB0ZP1IqG0403kt\n+yxj8MobtTU0VyxzNGwyXP4JTUpFna9XJAbC/d5xK/wHpfO+HjXlqsAkOMXmeYFN\nOM2YDRXo+wPBlk3KLlMXlRr2DI8uRTYjfns+OMzuf0OMZG2cGIwu4x5QoK7GBohx\ncrKF+JCCF+bRsKY6oef7BbND5iaLHEyWSvPGsRgyIf6pv3EC6EffxfhTgk4QDQlD\neAXf69ZV1kvCGdSn06Mr+Ft5JZTSs4LJiycBlJ6Oqg08laK7uS8z8d3AuboB3WS5\nEQAqC7kaciryTL/E0XjUATIXGBzijpt6Ap0iAVPElfc16MjXaqTG/6EMOvMJuX/F\n82xmMF4B5hLy+iwiyaz169oF4EI+4XBn8LJDkV3tR4yC2bm2fKgvdUkBaDym85xP\nkQKF729GBhaFj2UIQbDe\n=v35t\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-19T16:18:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/155861868e0be7de9695b7dcd43c268b31fcbb9f","node_id":"C_kwDOSVv36NoAKDE1NTg2MTg2OGUwYmU3ZGU5Njk1YjdkY2Q0M2MyNjhiMzFmY2JiOWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commit/3a6927cb21efee250ace73ebb05d49291599fefd","sha":"3a6927cb21efee250ace73ebb05d49291599fefd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/3a6927cb21efee250ace73ebb05d49291599fefd"}],"sha":"155861868e0be7de9695b7dcd43c268b31fcbb9f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/155861868e0be7de9695b7dcd43c268b31fcbb9f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/281068747?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wakir-labs","id":281068747,"login":"wakir-labs","node_id":"U_kgDOEMDEyw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/3a6927cb21efee250ace73ebb05d49291599fefd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-19T16:13:47Z","email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-19T16:13:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci(welle-5): Tag-73 Welle-5 Integration-Smoke (Amara, 63 tests) (#466)\n\nHermetic end-to-end simulation of the four Welle-5 substrates\nthat fire on the canonical KW-26 Mi 2026-06-24 Doppel-Welle-4+5\ncutover-Mittwoch pipeline (lifecycle_state_machine):\n\n* Stage 1 -- Welle-5-Producer simulation (Selin Tag-73)\n* Stage 2 -- Welle-5-Audit-Anchor simulation (Tomas Tag-73)\n* Stage 3 -- Doppel-Welle-4+5 Coupling-Gate\n             (Welle-5 lifecycle_state_machine depends on\n              Welle-4 state_backing intact; partner-missing\n              and partner-defect trinary surface)\n* Stage 4 -- Forward-Block-Cascade welle-5..7 on DEFECT\n* Stage 5 -- Aggregate WELLE-5-INTACT / DRIFT / DEFECT\n\nBrief-vs-canonical reconciliation (Tag-71+72 lehre):\n\n* Brief said \"Capability-Token (Reza, Zone-L)\". Canonical per\n  Marathon-Rollback-Runbook Job-Graph is J4 W5 lifecycle_state_\n  machine rust->python. The capability_token framing is a\n  parallel KW-24-Acceptance-view per kw-24-welle-1-7-acceptance-\n  criteria.md §5; Tag-72 Welle-4 precedent pinned the Marathon-\n  Rollback-Runbook view as canonical, Tag-73 follows the same\n  precedent and surfaces the KW-24-Acceptance view as parallel-\n  substrate-evidence on the envelope.\n* Brief implied state/welle-5.json kw_cutover_anchor=KW-25 is\n  canonical. Actual canonical per pre-cutover-acceptance-run-\n  order.md row Welle-5 is KW-26 Mi 2026-06-24 cutover / KW-26 Fr\n  2026-06-26 sign-off (Doppel-Welle-4+5 parallel). State-file\n  drift surfaced as pin-drift marker; state-file NOT patched\n  (Amara scope: surface, not patch; ADR-0036 producer-domain\n  is Selin).\n* Brief framing \"Doppel-Welle-4+5 parallel\" matches canonical.\n\nAll three deltas surfaced verbatim on the aggregator envelope\nfield brief_vs_canonical_reconciliation for the Henrik (Zone-N)\naudit-evidence trail.\n\nAggregator helper: stdlib-only Python, no network, no NATS, no\nSPIRE, no gRPC, no gh workflow run. Per Mira sandbox-vs-host-\ntrennung.md the smoke is hermetic-by-construction; the actual\nWelle-5 trigger on 2026-06-24 is operator-hand on the Pilot-VM.\n\nDoppel-Welle-Coupling-Gate (Tag-73-distinctive): Welle-5\nlifecycle_state_machine does NOT have a snapshot-restore\ndependency (that was Welle-4-specific per Tag-56 J5). Instead\nStage 3 probes the Doppel-Welle-4+5 partner-coupling: Welle-5\nlifecycle_state_machine rests on Welle-4 state_backing\ninvariants; a Welle-4 DEFECT MUST block Welle-5 from flipping.\nThe coupling-direction is one-way (Welle-5 depends on Welle-4,\nnot vice versa). READY / PARTNER-MISSING / PARTNER-DEFECT\ntrinary per pre-cutover-acceptance-run-order.md row Welle-5.\n\nForward-cascade: Welle-5 DEFECT blocks (5,6,7). Welle-4 is NOT\nin the cascade-set despite being the Doppel-Welle partner\n(coupling-direction is one-way).\n\nTest-suite: tests/ci/test_welle_5_integration_tag73.py covers\nall-green, drift (producer / doppel-coupling / cascade), defect\n(audit-anchor / doppel-coupling / cascade-break / missing /\nunknown / red-dominates-yellow), envelope shape, parallel-\nsubstrate-views (Marathon + KW-24), anchor pins (KW-26 /\n2026-06-24 / lifecycle_state_machine / capability_token /\nJ4 / doppel-welle-partner=4), forward-cascade ((5,6,7) only on\nDEFECT, no upstream cascade to 1/2/3/4), CLI surface, and\nworkflow-shape. 63 unittest assertions pass on Python 3.14.4\nin 0.02s. Pflicht >=15 Tests deutlich erfuellt.\n\nREUSE-compliant: SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 on the\nworkflow + REUSE-Ignore-wrapped header on the aggregator helper;\ntest-file carries inline Apache-2.0 under REUSE-Ignore. Project\nreuse lint passes.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kai Hoffmann <kai@wakir.dev>\nCo-authored-by: amara-qa <amara-qa@wakir-labs.local>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1321de91a867c6c624b4f78415ee5f409bfc450b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/trees/1321de91a867c6c624b4f78415ee5f409bfc450b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/commits/3a6927cb21efee250ace73ebb05d49291599fefd","verification":{"payload":"tree 1321de91a867c6c624b4f78415ee5f409bfc450b\nparent db1c77ca7e9688ec0eea13ca6dc2c94a10de01a7\nauthor wakir-labs <xypu4r8e@addy.io> 1779207227 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779207227 +0200\n\nci(welle-5): Tag-73 Welle-5 Integration-Smoke (Amara, 63 tests) (#466)\n\nHermetic end-to-end simulation of the four Welle-5 substrates\nthat fire on the canonical KW-26 Mi 2026-06-24 Doppel-Welle-4+5\ncutover-Mittwoch pipeline (lifecycle_state_machine):\n\n* Stage 1 -- Welle-5-Producer simulation (Selin Tag-73)\n* Stage 2 -- Welle-5-Audit-Anchor simulation (Tomas Tag-73)\n* Stage 3 -- Doppel-Welle-4+5 Coupling-Gate\n             (Welle-5 lifecycle_state_machine depends on\n              Welle-4 state_backing intact; partner-missing\n              and partner-defect trinary surface)\n* Stage 4 -- Forward-Block-Cascade welle-5..7 on DEFECT\n* Stage 5 -- Aggregate WELLE-5-INTACT / DRIFT / DEFECT\n\nBrief-vs-canonical reconciliation (Tag-71+72 lehre):\n\n* Brief said \"Capability-Token (Reza, Zone-L)\". Canonical per\n  Marathon-Rollback-Runbook Job-Graph is J4 W5 lifecycle_state_\n  machine rust->python. The capability_token framing is a\n  parallel KW-24-Acceptance-view per kw-24-welle-1-7-acceptance-\n  criteria.md §5; Tag-72 Welle-4 precedent pinned the Marathon-\n  Rollback-Runbook view as canonical, Tag-73 follows the same\n  precedent and surfaces the KW-24-Acceptance view as parallel-\n  substrate-evidence on the envelope.\n* Brief implied state/welle-5.json kw_cutover_anchor=KW-25 is\n  canonical. Actual canonical per pre-cutover-acceptance-run-\n  order.md row Welle-5 is KW-26 Mi 2026-06-24 cutover / KW-26 Fr\n  2026-06-26 sign-off (Doppel-Welle-4+5 parallel). State-file\n  drift surfaced as pin-drift marker; state-file NOT patched\n  (Amara scope: surface, not patch; ADR-0036 producer-domain\n  is Selin).\n* Brief framing \"Doppel-Welle-4+5 parallel\" matches canonical.\n\nAll three deltas surfaced verbatim on the aggregator envelope\nfield brief_vs_canonical_reconciliation for the Henrik (Zone-N)\naudit-evidence trail.\n\nAggregator helper: stdlib-only Python, no network, no NATS, no\nSPIRE, no gRPC, no gh workflow run. Per Mira sandbox-vs-host-\ntrennung.md the smoke is hermetic-by-construction; the actual\nWelle-5 trigger on 2026-06-24 is operator-hand on the Pilot-VM.\n\nDoppel-Welle-Coupling-Gate (Tag-73-distinctive): Welle-5\nlifecycle_state_machine does NOT have a snapshot-restore\ndependency (that was Welle-4-specific per Tag-56 J5). Instead\nStage 3 probes the Doppel-Welle-4+5 partner-coupling: Welle-5\nlifecycle_state_machine rests on Welle-4 state_backing\ninvariants; a Welle-4 DEFECT MUST block Welle-5 from flipping.\nThe coupling-direction is one-way (Welle-5 depends on Welle-4,\nnot vice versa). READY / PARTNER-MISSING / PARTNER-DEFECT\ntrinary per pre-cutover-acceptance-run-order.md row Welle-5.\n\nForward-cascade: Welle-5 DEFECT blocks (5,6,7). Welle-4 is NOT\nin the cascade-set despite being the Doppel-Welle partner\n(coupling-direction is one-way).\n\nTest-suite: tests/ci/test_welle_5_integration_tag73.py covers\nall-green, drift (producer / doppel-coupling / cascade), defect\n(audit-anchor / doppel-coupling / cascade-break / missing /\nunknown / red-dominates-yellow), envelope shape, parallel-\nsubstrate-views (Marathon + KW-24), anchor pins (KW-26 /\n2026-06-24 / lifecycle_state_machine / capability_token /\nJ4 / doppel-welle-partner=4), forward-cascade ((5,6,7) only on\nDEFECT, no upstream cascade to 1/2/3/4), CLI surface, and\nworkflow-shape. 63 unittest assertions pass on Python 3.14.4\nin 0.02s. Pflicht >=15 Tests deutlich erfuellt.\n\nREUSE-compliant: SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 on the\nworkflow + REUSE-Ignore-wrapped header on the aggregator helper;\ntest-file carries inline Apache-2.0 under REUSE-Ignore. Project\nreuse lint passes.\n\nCo-authored-by: Kai Hoffmann <kai@wakir.dev>\nCo-authored-by: amara-qa <amara-qa@wakir-labs.local>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqDIw7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAP4QQAFUJi3Tf+EPUHhBILrvrHadZ\nGsR/GT0SkB1J28bSCAr17SydrZgR4Klj4ox3x/AzYkHKi6tyGWG0QjjUJU9a8JOm\neVW3TwnmAQpQ7uWUEczUInKnORZNgZyN9xuslBeiqM/3BaCuBHBljIyxKbhgxpKD\nVd9VlDpAdCSdGeEEQM/Mou0uG7wFsl3Bg0SaIrTFMWy1JNz24c1Kfdqu+ZLOQ9e1\nX8geKWR4G2KaCpOhFVrT1ElvPqDePDLmHTUng3+kMtbX2lFd6rPAPkDdSUccKE8c\n9dQvlnc8vepqMJsAE8GW40DtrDcDXV5fZSDWzodCCIxK3Zp5wrcOKcHocZlAPMbh\nMk/tONL25BPV21awT8eIHGh/OGdxO5jZo393WEKs20PIk6vSsMwr9HBu85H9apEE\n2+CSv0K8p3/2EpD77mPLrof1rJF9rUg8k31DhufHyzM1WHHtZi7DDf14NCw6HQ4e\nYxmfobDMzyZzrIuyLSjeJCE87vv/MVSTK4/rhoFdZZ3DQYVvtZT0ymR1XBaCp6re\nl6vfkiqONiM5mI+DXLC/XKTTs+RnTJmpvQWlYyggEQNiM8lciJRQqt0r6b+GnNBt\nQI8IJS5Iz+lPWDx5mcMd3ZLxXvnW3L37BRRYowmNP7cTwrWOQw//p0ULrxrdirFX\nzOu2E1QhJVVYXg/6m3Hy\n=lAZY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-19T16:13:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6V