s://api.github.com/users/wakir-labs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/commits/db1c77ca7e9688ec0eea13ca6dc2c94a10de01a7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-19T16:12:47Z","email":"xypu4r8e@addy.io","name":"wakir-labs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-19T16:12:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(welle-5): Tag-73 Welle-5 Capability-Token producer + handler (Selin) (#465)\n\nAdds the engine-side producer-path for the Welle-5 Capability-Token\nsign-off (KW-25 Fr 2026-06-19, Reza-Zone-L). Mirrors the Tag-72\nWelle-4 design with a new marker-family (capability-token-rotation-\nmarker == \"rotated\") and audit-trigger \"capability-token-rotation\".\n\nSubstanz:\n- welle_state_producer.py: CAPABILITY_TOKEN_ROTATION_GUARDED_WELLEN\n  ({5}), CAPABILITY_TOKEN_ROTATED (\"rotated\"),\n  CapabilityTokenRotationError, handle_welle_5_signoff_event method.\n- engine.py: handle_welle_5_signoff_event top-level dispatch.\n- engine_async.py: async wrapper via thread-pool executor.\n- test_welle_5_producer_tag73.py: 26 hermetic tests (>=18 required),\n  including marker-family-disambiguation across all four Wellen\n  (W2 sealing / W3+W7 sign-off / W4 snapshot-restore / W5 capability-\n  token-rotation).\n\nSchema-pin unchanged (Tag-67). Rotation-iso lives in the audit-stream\nper the Tag-72 convention. No persona-definitions, WAT-core,\nidentity-substrate, or container-infra changes (Zone-J/K/L respected;\nReza-Zone-L rotation-marker contract consumed verbatim).\n\nFull wirelang test suite: 3234 passed, 16 skipped, 0 failed (was\n1624/1624 persona_engine, 1598/1598 pre-Tag-73 producer baseline).\n\nRefs: kw-24-welle-1-7-acceptance-criteria §5 (probes W5-S1..S4),\nphase-3c-doppel-welle-4-5.md §3.2, ADR-0066.\n\nCo-authored-by: pengine-eng <pengine@wakir.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"df0820f4a830f0085f041183361f8a085edd117c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/trees/df0820f4a830f0085f041183361f8a085edd117c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/git/commits/db1c77ca7e9688ec0eea13ca6dc2c94a10de01a7","verification":{"payload":"tree df0820f4a830f0085f041183361f8a085edd117c\nparent 24666b719603f7857dec332c96edddb62927a9f3\nauthor wakir-labs <xypu4r8e@addy.io> 1779207167 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779207167 +0200\n\nfeat(welle-5): Tag-73 Welle-5 Capability-Token producer + handler (Selin) (#465)\n\nAdds the engine-side producer-path for the Welle-5 Capability-Token\nsign-off (KW-25 Fr 2026-06-19, Reza-Zone-L). Mirrors the Tag-72\nWelle-4 design with a new marker-family (capability-token-rotation-\nmarker == \"rotated\") and audit-trigger \"capability-token-rotation\".\n\nSubstanz:\n- welle_state_producer.py: CAPABILITY_TOKEN_ROTATION_GUARDED_WELLEN\n  ({5}), CAPABILITY_TOKEN_ROTATED (\"rotated\"),\n  CapabilityTokenRotationError, handle_welle_5_signoff_event method.\n- engine.py: handle_welle_5_signoff_event top-level dispatch.\n- engine_async.py: async wrapper via thread-pool executor.\n- test_welle_5_producer_tag73.py: 26 hermetic tests (>=18 required),\n  including marker-family-disambiguation across all four Wellen\n  (W2 sealing / W3+W7 sign-off / W4 snapshot-restore / W5 capability-\n  token-rotation).\n\nSchema-pin unchanged (Tag-67). Rotation-iso lives in the audit-stream\nper the Tag-72 convention. No persona-definitions, WAT-core,\nidentity-substrate, or container-infra changes (Zone-J/K/L respected;\nReza-Zone-L rotation-marker contract consumed verbatim).\n\nFull wirelang test suite: 3234 passed, 16 skipped, 0 failed (was\n1624/1624 persona_engine, 1598/1598 pre-Tag-73 producer baseline).\n\nRefs: kw-24-welle-1-7-acceptance-criteria §5 (probes W5-S1..S4),\nphase-3c-doppel-welle-4-5.md §3.2, ADR-0066.\n\nCo-authored-by: pengine-eng <pengine@wakir.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <n