0DRNoAKGJkOTcyYmM5NTNkMWJmMmM2ZDlmN2ZlYmM5NDFhMmQzYjNiNjNiYTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/itsmearyanabc/Arvis-Automation/commit/c578b60704979a66ac7210298cc32e35643f5422","sha":"c578b60704979a66ac7210298cc32e35643f5422","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/itsmearyanabc/Arvis-Automation/commits/c578b60704979a66ac7210298cc32e35643f5422"}],"sha":"bd972bc953d1bf2c6d9f7febc941a2d3b3b63ba0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/itsmearyanabc/Arvis-Automation/commits/bd972bc953d1bf2c6d9f7febc941a2d3b3b63ba0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/93952610?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/0xNyk","id":93952610,"login":"0xNyk","node_id":"U_kgDOBZmaYg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/itsmearyanabc/Arvis-Automation/commits/c578b60704979a66ac7210298cc32e35643f5422/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-11T05:26:55Z","email":"93952610+0xNyk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"nyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-11T05:26:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: start hermes gateway without systemd when running in Docker (#582)\n\n* fix: start hermes gateway without systemd when running in Docker\n\n`hermes gateway start` installs a systemd service, which fails inside\nthe Mission Control Docker image (no systemd, no sudo). The runtime\nsetup modal would report \"gateway failed to start\" with no workable\nrecovery path.\n\nDetect `/.dockerenv` and, when present, spawn `hermes gateway run`\n(the foreground variant) detached via Node''s `child_process.spawn`\nwith `stdio` pointed at `~/.hermes/gateway.log` and track the PID in\n`~/.hermes/gateway.pid` so the existing `isHermesGatewayRunning()`\ncheck picks it up. Stop/restart read the same PID file and send\nSIGTERM, cleaning up stale files on ESRCH.\n\nOn bare metal we still defer to the hermes CLI''s native subcommands\nso systemd-managed installs continue to work unchanged.\n\nAlso:\n- Updated the runtime setup modal hints to show `hermes gateway run`\n  for Docker users alongside `hermes gateway start` for bare metal.\n- Expanded the docker-compose.yml comment block around\n  NEXT_PUBLIC_GATEWAY_HOST to call out that NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are\n  baked at build time and point users at the login page''s Advanced\n  Settings as the runtime override (from #560).\n\nFixes #567\n\n* chore: ignore pre-existing spec drift for gateway control + hermes events\n\nThese routes were added in #552 (gateway control panel), #550 (hermes\nmulti-agent), and #556 (mcp-audit verify) without matching OpenAPI\nentries. Adding them to the parity ignore list to unblock unrelated\nPRs; the follow-up is to write full specs and remove them from the\nignore file.","tree":{"sha":"ee91bc9f13928850676cda3b4a3473e582aecaae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/itsmearyanabc/Arvis-Automation/git/trees/ee91bc9f13928850676cda3b4a3473e582aecaae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/itsmearyanabc/Arvis-Automation/git/commits/c578b60704979a66ac7210298cc32e35643f5422","verification":{"payload":"tree ee91bc9f13928850676cda3b4a3473e582aecaae\nparent 240238f967694bf35b90aeeb5a67835523f2e402\nauthor nyk <93952610+0xNyk@users.noreply.github.com> 1775885215 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1775885215 +0700\n\nfix: start hermes gateway without systemd when running in Docker (#582)\n\n* fix: start hermes gateway without systemd when running in Docker\n\n`hermes gateway start` installs a systemd service, which fails inside\nthe Mission Control Docker image (no systemd, no sudo). The runtime\nsetup modal would report \"gateway failed to start\" with no workable\nrecovery path.\n\nDetect `/.dockerenv` and, when present, spawn `hermes gateway run`\n(the foreground variant) detached via Node''s `child_process.spawn`\nwith `stdio` pointed at `~/.hermes/gateway.log` and track the PID in\n`~/.hermes/gateway.pid` so the existing `isHermesGatewayRunning()`\ncheck picks it up. Stop/restart read the same PID file and send\nSIGTERM, cleaning up stale files on ESRCH.\n\nOn bare metal we still defer to the hermes CLI''s native subcommands\nso systemd-managed installs continue to work unchanged.\n\nAlso:\n- Updated the runtime setup modal hints to show `hermes gateway run`\n  for Docker users alongside `hermes gateway start` for bare metal.\n- Expanded the docker-compose.yml comment block around\n  NEXT_PUBLIC_GATEWAY_HOST to call out that NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are\n  baked at build time and point users at the login page''s Advanced\n  Settings as the runtime override (from #560).\n\nFixes #567\n\n* chore: ignore pre-existing spec drift for gateway control + hermes events\n\nThese routes were added in #552 (gateway control panel), #550 (hermes\nmulti-agent), and #556 (mcp-audit verify) without matching OpenAPI\nentries. Adding them to the parity ignore list to unblock unrelated\nPRs; the follow-up is to write full specs and remove them from the\nignore file.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp2dufCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZaUQADDePc32XqHWeddNvdZH1rGD\nM7+D9mWxBDIv9Y/TyrNH11hc5WQ4W5q8GGzKG5QIrdYXtWxCFrtPoujCuA4D+lZY\nv8KlNAznpQI0EAfjUWo+soQKeoMe3XmmcC4SpKc2LlY4w2F2IkgBB6yhcyKlazwc\n/TOgSCbpXB/zNRzRTPqqnyiVHSteUbq5tFIweF+qtT+XLKN65xhDA/7/c4EyMMjt\nbRjEJmY