37900792ab5974475d01f58"}],"sha":"17b5dad01b87c3071b8531aac532b67e86ee42ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/17b5dad01b87c3071b8531aac532b67e86ee42ee"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95","id":36343085,"login":"masonstevens95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQzMDg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/d6f488ac43a8b6ff637900792ab5974475d01f58/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-08T02:58:37Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-08T02:58:37Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"message":"feat(remote): watershed dilation preserves gaps between adjacent fg features\n\nPreviously dilateSubject did a uniform 4-neighbor fattening pass per\nradius pixel — fine in open bg, but in narrow channels between two\nforeground features (e.g. tripod legs) the two sides grew toward each\nother and merged. The mortar''s three legs read as one fat blob at\nhigh dilation values.\n\nWatershed approach: replace the iterative O(N*R) expansion with a\ndistance-transform-based O(N) pass. Compute Chebyshev distance from\neach bg pixel to its nearest fg pixel (two-pass chamfer), plus the\nseed coordinate so RGB can be propagated. Then for each bg pixel\nwithin R distance: if it''s a strict local max on the distance map\n(= medial axis between two fg regions), keep bg; otherwise mark fg\nwith RGB copied from the nearest fg seed.\n\nEffect: the subject grows by R pixels into open bg, but in channels\nbetween two fg regions growth halts at the gap centerline, leaving a\n~1 px bg ridge. Tripod legs stay distinguishable even at large R.\nPerformance: dilation is now O(N) regardless of radius (was O(N*R)) —\na R=30 dilate is ~10x faster than before on large sources.\n\nBoundary cleanup pre-erode (BOUNDARY_CLEANUP=2) is preserved.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fde4a237d795e163b0876d1f6f8d4468eacc3139","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/trees/fde4a237d795e163b0876d1f6f8d4468eacc3139"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/commits/d6f488ac43a8b6ff637900792ab5974475d01f58","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95","id":36343085,"login":"masonstevens95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQzMDg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/received_events","