"email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-08T01:41:10Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"message":"chore(remote): raise exposed-chunk ceiling to 50 KB for v4.2\n\nv4 → v4.2 delta is ~+7900 bytes raw, all from cartoon-shaping UI\nsurface (7 new dials × per-filter preset fields, hook plumbing,\nSilhouetteControl JSX). Pipeline modules go into the worker bundle,\nnot the exposed chunk. The React-internals / ORT / MediaPipe grep\nguards still pass — growth is feature surface, not accidental\nbundling.\n\nCeiling: 41000 → 50000 (v4.2-measured + ~4 KB headroom).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4a0da9fbf76fe25ced8730f3f0b2cb714556cb7e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/trees/4a0da9fbf76fe25ced8730f3f0b2cb714556cb7e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/commits/7817da339188b54ff6e44433204cf70b1aa1e4fd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95","id":36343085,"login":"masonstevens95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQzMDg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commit/7817da339188b54ff6e44433204cf70b1aa1e4fd","node_id":"C_kwDOSV4urtoAKDc4MTdkYTMzOTE4OGI1NGZmNmU0NDQzMzIwNGNmNzBiMWFhMWU0ZmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commit/eb94e4850e453529e0ef0fb0d1646c20f590e44c","sha":"eb94e4850e453529e0ef0fb0d1646c20f590e44c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/eb94e4850e453529e0ef0fb0d1646c20f590e44c"}],"sha":"7817da339188b54ff6e44433204cf70b1aa1e4fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/7817da339188b54ff6e44433204cf70b1aa1e4fd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95","id":36343085,"login":"masonstevens95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQzMDg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/eb94e4850e453529e0ef0fb0d1646c20f590e44c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-08T01:32:52Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-08T01:32:52Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"message":"feat(remote): cartoon shaping toggles (close, dilate, tight crop, flat fill)\n\nFive new pipeline stages, each independently togglable, all\nidentity-at-default so v3/v4 invariants stay byte-identical.\n\n- silhouetteMorph.closeMask: dilate-then-erode at source resolution to\n  fill U2-Net mask holes and fuse fragmented foreground regions.\n- silhouetteMorph.dilateMask: pure 4-neighbor dilation that fattens\n  thin features (tripod legs, weapon handles) before downscale so they\n  survive at 48-128 px output instead of compressing to 1px strokes.\n- tightCrop: re-frames image+mask to the foreground bbox + margin,\n  with a sub-toggle for square pad vs subject-aspect output. Subject\n  fills the canvas instead of being lost in source-photo padding.\n- flatFill: k-means LAB clustering on foreground pixels (alpha>0\n  only). Replaces photographic gradient with N-color cel shading.\n- silhouetteOutline (v4.1 carryover): strokes the alpha 0/255 boundary\n  after the mask applies, sealing the chunky silhouette.\n\nPipeline order: silhouette mask -> close -> dilate -> tight crop ->\nposterize -> downscale (subject-aware) -> quantize -> outline -> mask\napply -> flat-fill -> silhouette boundary outline -> chunky.\n\nAsset filter opts into the full stack (close=1, dilate=2, tight crop\nwith 5% margin + square pad, flat-fill=4 colors). Other filters keep\nv4.1 behavior. UI groups the five knobs under \"Cartoon shaping\" in\nSilhouetteControl, gated on Remove background being enabled.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"79e4241e50082387e28ee5a55a8a7fd7dd714319","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/trees/79e4241e50082387e28ee5a55a8a7fd7dd714319"},"url":"https