_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commit/654a25f6f8340382d8fe1fda97d8b3a751facf56","node_id":"C_kwDOSV4urtoAKDY1NGEyNWY2ZjgzNDAzODJkOGZlMWZkYTk3ZDhiM2E3NTFmYWNmNTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commit/8e977bf14a26051d4a2d80b5a9c6d3c1eaeb9c66","sha":"8e977bf14a26051d4a2d80b5a9c6d3c1eaeb9c66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/8e977bf14a26051d4a2d80b5a9c6d3c1eaeb9c66"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commit/6746c27c4b81b2e3853398356b6fd0ceb2446cc2","sha":"6746c27c4b81b2e3853398356b6fd0ceb2446cc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/6746c27c4b81b2e3853398356b6fd0ceb2446cc2"}],"sha":"654a25f6f8340382d8fe1fda97d8b3a751facf56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/654a25f6f8340382d8fe1fda97d8b3a751facf56"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95","id":36343085,"login":"masonstevens95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQzMDg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/6746c27c4b81b2e3853398356b6fd0ceb2446cc2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-07T23:23:28Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-07T23:23:28Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"message":"feat(remote): U9 v4 invariant + bundle ceiling + build fix\n\nFinal v4 unit. Three deliverables:\n\n1. Build fix (vite.config.ts): worker.format=''es'' so dynamic imports\n   inside the worker (onnxruntime-web/wasm and @mediapipe/tasks-vision)\n   can code-split. Default ''iife'' rejects code-splitting builds — fix\n   was required after U1''s lazy ORT import broke the production build.\n\n2. Bundle ceiling (verify-build.sh): raised 34000→41000 raw bytes.\n   Actual v4 exposed chunk: 38149 bytes (only +6980 from v3''s 31169\n   because lazy imports kept ORT JS adapter, MediaPipe shim, and\n   worker code in separate chunks). The v4 plan''s 110 KB upper bound\n   was speculative; the contingency ladder didn''t need to fire.\n\n   Added ML-not-bundled multi-pronged check:\n   - No .onnx or .task files in dist/assets\n   - No direct ORT (onnxruntime-web/InferenceSession.create) or\n     MediaPipe (FaceLandmarker/FilesetResolver) references in the\n     exposed chunk\n   - ORT and MediaPipe lazy chunks DO exist as separate files\n     (proves the imports are split, not just absent)\n\n3. v4-default invariant test (R12): extended v1-invariant.test.ts with\n   v4 default-off path. Negative controls confirm smoothness=high and\n   faceAwareEnabled=true with non-null landmarks both produce\n   not-byte-equal output, proving the identity short-circuits aren''t\n   masking regressions. Reference-equality check verifies bilateral\n   and faceBoost return input by reference at default.\n\n4. docs/deploy.md updates: v4 model hosting, Cache Storage version-bump\n   procedure, CDN trust + supply-chain notes, ML-disabled smoke test,\n   worker output format requirement.\n\nTests: 363 passing (was 358; +5 new v4 invariant scenarios).\nTypecheck/lint/build all clean. VERIFY OK.","tree":{"sha":"f1addea50a010fdf0aa004e503a2ce6ecef4c6cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/trees/f1addea50a010fdf0aa004e503a2ce6ecef4c6cf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/commits/6746c27c4b81b2e3853398356b6fd0ceb2446cc2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95","id":36343085,"login":"masonstevens95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQzMDg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commit/6746c27c4b81b2e3853398356b6fd0ceb2446cc2","node_id":"C_kwDOSV4urtoAKDY3NDZjMjdjNGI4MWIyZTM4NTMzOTgzNTZiNmZkMGNlYjI0NDZjYzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commit/1a9b0d93e7413c5dbb43ec109109b2284ebab3d6","sha":"1a9b0d93e7413c5dbb43ec109109b2284ebab3d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/1a9b0d93e7413c5dbb43ec109109b2284ebab3d6"}],"sha":"6746c27c4b81b2e3853398356b6fd0ceb2446cc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/6746c27c4b81b2e3853398356b6fd0ceb2446cc2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95","id":36343085,"login":"masonstevens95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQzMDg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/1a9b0d93e7413c5dbb43ec109109b2284ebab3d6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-07T21:04:16Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-07T21:04:16Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"message":"feat(remote): U8 model-load UX surfaces\n\nSurface ML loading / failure / first-render states to the user as three\nsmall components with the worker→main-thread protocol additions they need.\n\nComponents\n- ModelLoadIndicator: compact \"Loading enhanced features…\" panel + a CSS-\n  only indeterminate progress sliver, rendered below the StyleSelector\n  whenever ANY ML stage (segmentation OR face-landmarks) is in the\n  ''loading'' phase. Reserved-slot layout (`min-h-10` on the outer wrapper\n  regardless of state) so loading→ready transitions don''t jitter the\n  surrounding controls. role=\"status\" + aria-live=\"polite\".\n- DegradedModeNotice: per-stage amber banner shown when an ML stage\n  failed. Sticky-dismiss is tracked as a `Set<MLStage>` so dismissing the\n  segmentation banner does not also hide a later face-landmarks failure\n  banner — and a stage that''s been dismissed stays hidden if its status\n  re-flips to ''failed'' in the same session. role=\"status\" +\n  aria-live=\"polite\".\n- FirstRenderSpinner: absolute-positioned overlay rendered inside the\n  RESULT pane only of SideBySidePreview, leaving the source pane clear\n  so the user still sees the file they dropped while the heavy first\n  pass runs. Centered spinner + \"Processing image…\" caption.\n  role=\"status\" + aria-label=\"Processing image\".\n\nWorker emits\n- first-render-start { sourceId } / first-render-end { sourceId }: new\n  outbound message types in `protocol.ts` plus matching type guards.\n  The worker tracks `firstRenderStartedSourceIds: Set<string>` and emits\n  the pair at most once per (worker lifetime, sourceId), bracketing the\n  source-cached stages (rasterize → bilateral → face landmarks →\n  segmentation). Subsequent dispatches for the same source hit the\n  cache and skip the emits — the spinner only appears for the\n  perceptible-cost first render.\n- ml-status loading / ready emits already shipped in U5 / U6 along the\n  success paths; U8 simply consumes them via the existing one-shot-per-\n  stage memo.\n\nState / wiring\n- usePixelArtPipeline: PipelineState gains `firstRenderActive: boolean`,\n  toggled by the new first-render-* messages. mlStatus tracking from U5\n  is unchanged.\n- PixelArtApp: renders ModelLoadIndicator + DegradedModeNotice directly\n  below the StyleSelector and threads `state.firstRenderActive` into\n  SideBySidePreview, which positions the spinner inside its existing\n  result-pane container.\n\nTests (all 358 green)\n- New: ModelLoadIndicator / DegradedModeNotice / FirstRenderSpinner\n  component tests covering happy paths, multi-stage visibility, ARIA\n  roles, the layout-reserved slot, and per-stage sticky dismiss.\n- Extended: protocol.test.ts now covers isMLStatusMessage,\n  isMLErrorMessage, isFirstRenderStartMessage, isFirstRenderEndMessage.\n- Extended: usePixelArtPipeline.test.ts adds integration scenarios\n  for ml-status loading/ready/failed transitions and the\n  first-render-start/end → firstRenderActive boolean flip (Covers F3,\n  F5, AE8).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"54fff755407193c39f4da2235d7f887c922495a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/trees/54fff755407193c39f4da2235d7f887c922495a3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/commits/1a9b0d93e7413c5dbb43ec109109b2284ebab3d6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95","id":36343085,"login":"masonstevens95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQzMDg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commit/1a9b0d93e7413c5dbb43ec109109b2284ebab3d6","node_id":"C_kwDOSV4urtoAKDFhOWIwZDkzZTc0MTNjNWRiYjQzZWMxMDkxMDliMjI4NGViYWIzZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commit/f7b6c5b38aa2cb5214cb2eeda751baca40539d34","sha":"f7b6c5b38aa2cb5214cb2eeda751baca40539d34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/f7b6c5b38aa2cb5214cb2eeda751baca40539d34"}],"sha":"1a9b0d93e7413c5dbb43ec109109b2284ebab3d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/1a9b0d93e7413c5dbb43ec109109b2284ebab3d6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95","id":36343085,"login":"masonstevens95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQzMDg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/f7b6c5b38aa2cb5214cb2eeda751baca40539d34/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-07T20:53:17Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-07T20:53:17Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"message":"feat(remote): U7 filter re-tuning + face-aware wiring\n\nExtend FilterPreset with three v4 fields (smoothness, faceAwareEnabled,\nsilhouetteQuality) and re-tune per-filter defaults per the v4 plan\ntable (line 654 of the cartoon-quality plan):\n\n- Custom (R12 invariant baseline): smoothness=off, faceAwareEnabled=\n  false, silhouetteQuality=fast. All v3 dial values preserved byte-\n  identical.\n- Art piece / Environment (painterly): smoothness=off, no face boost,\n  fast silhouette. v3 values unchanged (no smoothing on gradient art).\n- Portrait: resolution raised 128 -> 192 long edge so face features\n  survive quantization; smoothness=medium; faceAwareEnabled=true; thin\n  black outline + posterize 6 retained.\n- Units: smoothness=medium; v3 dials unchanged (thick outline, posterize\n  4, chunky 2).\n- Asset: smoothness=low; silhouetteQuality=smart (the only filter where\n  the user-visible default opts into ML segmentation); resolution stays\n  48 with thick black outline + posterize 4.\n\ndialsMatchPreset extended with string-equality checks for smoothness\nand silhouetteQuality, and strict boolean equality for faceAwareEnabled.\nRemoved the optional-chain fallback U3 added — smoothness is now\nrequired on FilterPreset proper.\n\nPixelArtApp applyFilter handler batches three new setState calls for\nthe v4 dials (React 18 batches them into one render). Modified-state\ndetection useEffect passes the three new dial values through to\ndialsMatchPreset.\n\nTests: filters.test.ts presetDials helper extended; new assertions\ncover the v4 schema (every filter declares all three fields), Asset\nsilhouetteQuality=smart (AE2), Portrait resolution=192 + faceAware=true\n(AE4), painterly filters keep smoothness=off, and three new\ndialsMatchPreset edge cases (smoothness, faceAwareEnabled,\nsilhouetteQuality each individually flip to \"modified\").\n\n330 tests pass; typecheck + lint clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"97be8053be4fb097387fa9ec2840e004aa1a7f22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/trees/97be8053be4fb097387fa9ec2840e004aa1a7f22"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/commits/f7b6c5b38aa2cb5214cb2eeda751baca40539d34","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95","id":36343085,"login":"masonstevens95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQzMDg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commit/f7b6c5b38aa2cb5214cb2eeda751baca40539d34","node_id":"C_kwDOSV4urtoAKGY3YjZjNWIzOGFhMmNiNTIxNGNiMmVlZGE3NTFiYWNhNDA1MzlkMzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commit/a8350e722b4cec6cf882a0994ec72e8e78d6ac36","sha":"a8350e722b4cec6cf882a0994ec72e8e78d6ac36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/a8350e722b4cec6cf882a0994ec72e8e78d6ac36"}],"sha":"f7b6c5b38aa2cb5214cb2eeda751baca40539d34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/f7b6c5b38aa2cb5214cb2eeda751baca40539d34"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95","id":36343085,"login":"masonstevens95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQzMDg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/a8350e722b4cec6cf882a0994ec72e8e78d6ac36/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-07T20:47:59Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-07T20:47:59Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"message":"feat(remote): U6 ML face landmarker + landmark-aware contrast boost\n\nAdd MediaPipe Face Landmarker integration with R12-gated worker call site\nand a landmark-aware contrast boost stage that runs after bilateral and\nbefore saturation, source-cached.\n\n- @mediapipe/tasks-vision pinned to 0.10.18 (exact version, not caret).\n  Doc-review security requirement: jsDelivr resolves `latest` at edge so\n  a compromised npm release would propagate without us noticing. The CDN\n  URLs in faceLandmarks.ts interpolate the same exact version.\n\n- Worker R12 GATE (load-bearing): pixelArtWorker.ts skips\n  detectLandmarks entirely when faceAwareEnabled !== true. No\n  @mediapipe/tasks-vision import, no .task fetch, no fileset download\n  on the default path. Without this gate the ~3-4 MB MediaPipe bundle\n  would lazy-load on every R12-default new-source dispatch.\n\n- applyFaceBoost is identity-by-reference at !enabled OR null landmarks.\n  Both empty-result shapes from MediaPipe (faceLandmarks: [] AND\n  faceLandmarks: [[]]) normalize to null at the detectLandmarks layer\n  so callers branch on a single sentinel.\n\n- SourceCache extended with `landmarksAttempted: boolean` to distinguish\n  \"never attempted\" from \"attempted, no face found\" so the worker\n  doesn''t redundantly invoke MediaPipe on faceless sources. Type-only\n  import of NormalizedLandmark from @mediapipe/tasks-vision so the\n  runtime bundle stays out until first use.\n\n- runAndCacheLandmarks mirrors U5''s runAndCacheSegmentation cancellation\n  guard: stale sourceId on resolve drops the write-back without\n  poisoning the new cache entry.\n\n- FaceBoostToggle component follows the SilhouetteControl mlAvailable\n  pattern; default off (R12 baseline; U7 will default on for Portrait).\n  Added to AdvancedControlsPanel after SmoothnessControl.\n\nTests: +30 (faceBoost identity + firing path + edge cases, faceLandmarks\nmocked detector + cancellation guard + both empty-array normalizations,\nFaceBoostToggle component, sourceCache landmarksAttempted default +\neviction reset). 320/320 pass; pnpm typecheck + lint clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"83cfee6098f9765ea4b75cf704733c4bd29dbac0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/trees/83cfee6098f9765ea4b75cf704733c4bd29dbac0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/commits/a8350e722b4cec6cf882a0994ec72e8e78d6ac36","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95","id":36343085,"login":"masonstevens95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQzMDg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commit/a8350e722b4cec6cf882a0994ec72e8e78d6ac36","node_id":"C_kwDOSV4urtoAKGE4MzUwZTcyMmI0Y2VjNmNmODgyYTA5OTRlYzcyZThlNzhkNmFjMzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commit/92ca6ebd59fabdd97f53581ceb132d7095ae443f","sha":"92ca6ebd59fabdd97f53581ceb132d7095ae443f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/92ca6ebd59fabdd97f53581ceb132d7095ae443f"}],"sha":"a8350e722b4cec6cf882a0994ec72e8e78d6ac36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/a8350e722b4cec6cf882a0994ec72e8e78d6ac36"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95","id":36343085,"login":"masonstevens95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQzMDg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/92ca6ebd59fabdd97f53581ceb132d7095ae443f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-07T20:33:58Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-07T20:33:58Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"message":"feat(remote): U5 ML segmentation integration (U2-NetP)\n\nLazy-loads U2-NetP via the U1 ORT runtime on first Smart-quality\nsilhouette dispatch and produces a binary alpha mask through inference,\nreplacing naive corner-sample as the v4 default cutout strategy. The\nv3 corner-sample stays available as the Fast quality fallback.\n\nKey pieces:\n\n- ml/segmentation.ts: prepareInput/runSegmentation split so jsdom-based\n  unit tests can stub the OffscreenCanvas-dependent resize step. The\n  orchestrator handles ORT session, ImageNet normalization, threshold\n  + nearest-neighbor upscale to source dims, and a runAndCacheSegmentation\n  wrapper that guards write-back against the active SourceCacheManager\n  (in-flight inference for stale sourceId no longer poisons the cache).\n\n- pipeline/pixelArtWorker.ts: Smart route emits ml-status (loading/ready/\n  failed) and falls back to Fast + one-shot ml-error on MLRuntimeError.\n  R12 gate preserved: silhouetteEnabled=false skips the ML path entirely\n  (no getOrtSession, no fetch). cropMaskToMatch trims the source-dims ML\n  mask to the cropped image dims so applyMask sees matching sizes.\n\n- pipeline/protocol.ts: adds optional silhouetteQuality field to\n  ProcessRequest, plus MLStatusMessage / MLErrorMessage outbound types\n  with type guards. The ''face-landmarks'' stage is included in the union\n  up front so U6 lands its emit sites without further protocol churn.\n\n- components/SilhouetteControl.tsx: Quality radio (Fast / Smart) with\n  Smart as the visual default. Smart radio is disabled with descriptive\n  copy when mlAvailable=false. Quality radios are gated by the enabled\n  checkbox so users can''t change quality on a no-op silhouette.\n\n- hooks/usePixelArtPipeline.ts: subscribes to ml-status / ml-error,\n  surfaces them via mlStatus / mlError on PipelineState, and forwards\n  silhouetteQuality on dispatch.\n\n- exposes/PixelArtApp.tsx: silhouetteQuality state defaults to ''fast''\n  for the v3 invariant; ml-availability flows from state.mlStatus into\n  the SilhouetteControl prop.\n\nTests: 290 / 290 pass (was 283; +13 SilhouetteControl + 16 segmentation =\n+23 net, accounting for 6 superseded SilhouetteControl assertions).\ntypecheck + lint clean. R12 v1-invariant test still passes since the\nsilhouetteEnabled=false default never reaches the ML path.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5ac1c16a43f1de7b2694494e1ef7556a0c7d3c21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/trees/5ac1c16a43f1de7b2694494e1ef7556a0c7d3c21"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/commits/92ca6ebd59fabdd97f53581ceb132d7095ae443f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95","id":36343085,"login":"masonstevens95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQzMDg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commit/92ca6ebd59fabdd97f53581ceb132d7095ae443f","node_id":"C_kwDOSV4urtoAKDkyY2E2ZWJkNTlmYWJkZDk3ZjUzNTgxY2ViMTMyZDcwOTVhZTQ0M2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commit/28188c210e16bca41fd93aa5746f572ac01b74e7","sha":"28188c210e16bca41fd93aa5746f572ac01b74e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/28188c210e16bca41fd93aa5746f572ac01b74e7"}],"sha":"92ca6ebd59fabdd97f53581ceb132d7095ae443f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/92ca6ebd59fabdd97f53581ceb132d7095ae443f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95","id":36343085,"login":"masonstevens95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQzMDg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/28188c210e16bca41fd93aa5746f572ac01b74e7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-07T20:17:45Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-07T20:17:45Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"message":"feat(remote): U4 XDoG outline replacement (post-quantize)\n\nSwap the Sobel-based edge detector inside applyOutline for a Winnemöller\nXDoG implementation, and move the outline pass in pixelArtWorker from\npre-quantize to post-quantize so the configured outline color survives\nunchanged in the output (no palette-bucket absorption).\n\n- New `apps/remote/src/pipeline/xdog.ts`: pure function over a Float32\n  luminance buffer, returns a binary 0/255 edge mask. Uses two separable\n  Gaussian blurs (σ and k·σ), a centered DoG (D = τ·(B_σ − B_kσ)) to keep\n  flat regions at zero regardless of luminance, and a tanh threshold on\n  |D|. Defaults match Winnemöller 2012: σ=0.4, k=1.6, τ=0.99, ε=0.1, φ=200,\n  exposed via an optional `params` arg for future tuning.\n- `outline.ts`: internals swap only — same `OutlineOptions` API, same\n  enabled=false identity short-circuit, same dilation logic for thicker\n  lines via `width − 1` 4-neighbor passes, same alpha-bypass overlay.\n  The <3-dim short-circuit is kept for explicit small-input behavior.\n- `pixelArtWorker.ts`: outline call site moves from after-downscale /\n  before-quantize to after-quantize / before-silhouette-mask. Quantize\n  now runs on the un-outlined image; the configured outline color is\n  applied on top of palette-quantized pixels and reaches output exact.\n- Tests: new `tests/pipeline/xdog.test.ts` covering flat-input no-edges\n  (including dark-flat where the standard Winnemöller formulation would\n  spuriously fire), high-contrast subject outline, sparse-mask noise\n  signature, small-input safety (1×1, 3×3), and ε monotonicity. Existing\n  `tests/pipeline/outline.test.ts` kept its R12 / width-stack / alpha /\n  small-input assertions; only Sobel-specific phrasing was reworded.\n- The v1-invariant negative-control for outlineEnabled=true continues to\n  pass: XDoG output on a random fixture still differs from v1.","tree":{"sha":"4803e80c7196fe17b431f0396a1e037cf7a8ba76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/trees/4803e80c7196fe17b431f0396a1e037cf7a8ba76"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/commits/28188c210e16bca41fd93aa5746f572ac01b74e7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95","id":36343085,"login":"masonstevens95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQzMDg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commit/28188c210e16bca41fd93aa5746f572ac01b74e7","node_id":"C_kwDOSV4urtoAKDI4MTg4YzIxMGUxNmJjYTQxZmQ5M2FhNTc0NmY1NzJhYzAxYjc0ZTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commit/0f173cffbf6fd17b0ba23df2a2a7dc4ba7943f97","sha":"0f173cffbf6fd17b0ba23df2a2a7dc4ba7943f97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/0f173cffbf6fd17b0ba23df2a2a7dc4ba7943f97"}],"sha":"28188c210e16bca41fd93aa5746f572ac01b74e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/28188c210e16bca41fd93aa5746f572ac01b74e7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95","id":36343085,"login":"masonstevens95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQzMDg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/0f173cffbf6fd17b0ba23df2a2a7dc4ba7943f97/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-07T20:00:11Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-07T20:00:11Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"message":"feat(remote): U3 bilateral filter + Smoothness control\n\nAdd the cartoon-smoothing pipeline stage and its UI dropdown, source-cached\nvia the U2 SourceCacheManager. Smoothness ''off'' (default) short-circuits\ninside bilateralFilter to return the input ImageData by reference, which\nis the R12 invariant contribution — the v3-default pipeline still produces\nbyte-identical output.\n\n- bilateral.ts: naive O(N·r²) Tomasi-Manduchi bilateral. Smoothness levels\n  map to (spatial-σ, range-σ, window radius): low→(1.0, 25, 2),\n  medium→(2.0, 35, 4), high→(3.0, 50, 6). Per-channel range Gaussian,\n  alpha bypassed, edge-clamped window.\n- Worker integration: bilateral runs as a source-cached stage right after\n  rasterize, before saturation. Cache key ''bilateral:<level>'' on\n  cache.smoothnessKey; cache slot cache.bilateralOutput. Smoothness change\n  recomputes; sourceId change evicts the whole cache (segmentation/landmarks\n  slots untouched, per the cache''s typed-struct design).\n- Protocol: optional ProcessRequest.smoothness field, undefined treated as\n  ''off'' so absence preserves prior behavior.\n- SmoothnessControl: dropdown matching the labeled-default-option pattern\n  from ChunkyPixelsControl; \"Off (default)\" makes the no-op state self-\n  describing. Disabled when no image loaded.\n- PixelArtApp: smoothness state defaulting to ''off'', threaded through\n  ProcessOptions and the modified-state detection. dialsMatchPreset\n  defaults missing preset.smoothness to ''off'' so v3 presets still match\n  cleanly until U7 lifts smoothness onto FilterPreset proper.\n\nTests: bilateral covers R12 short-circuit (reference equality), edge\npreservation on a black/white split, variance reduction on flat noise,\nalpha bypass, 1×1 / 3×3 edge cases, and non-mutation. SmoothnessControl\ncovers all 4 options, default label, change emission, disabled state, and\nARIA association.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"be246e565929cf0a537e053fa2a0fc7fa9f74a58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/trees/be246e565929cf0a537e053fa2a0fc7fa9f74a58"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/commits/0f173cffbf6fd17b0ba23df2a2a7dc4ba7943f97","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95","id":36343085,"login":"masonstevens95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQzMDg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commit/0f173cffbf6fd17b0ba23df2a2a7dc4ba7943f97","node_id":"C_kwDOSV4urtoAKDBmMTczY2ZmYmY2ZmQxN2IwYmEyM2RmMmEyYTdkYzRiYTc5NDNmOTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commit/3c5f6fc964660edd57de60b622dcb3681b3c79f6","sha":"3c5f6fc964660edd57de60b622dcb3681b3c79f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/3c5f6fc964660edd57de60b622dcb3681b3c79f6"}],"sha":"0f173cffbf6fd17b0ba23df2a2a7dc4ba7943f97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/0f173cffbf6fd17b0ba23df2a2a7dc4ba7943f97"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95","id":36343085,"login":"masonstevens95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQzMDg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/3c5f6fc964660edd57de60b622dcb3681b3c79f6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-07T19:50:25Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-07T19:50:25Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"message":"feat(remote): U2 source-cache scaffolding in worker\n\nAdds per-source-id worker-side cache manager and the protocol field\nthat drives it. No consumers yet — U3 will populate bilateralOutput,\nU5 segmentationMask, U6 landmarks.\n\n- SourceCacheManager is a typed struct (not Record<string, unknown>),\n  per doc-review consensus: closed three-slot consumer set buys\n  static field shapes and legible invalidation rules at the call\n  sites.\n- Single-entry LRU: any new sourceId evicts the previous entry, so\n  memory bound is exactly one SourceCache regardless of how many\n  source switches occur.\n- ProcessRequest.sourceId is required (not optional). Every dispatch\n  path — component, hook, tests — mints/forwards an id. No v3-compat\n  optional path; correctness is enforced at the type boundary.\n- PixelArtApp mints sourceId via crypto.randomUUID() in the existing\n  sourceFile-change effect; same file = same id, new file = new id.\n- Worker termination addendum test added to usePixelArtPipeline.test\n  to assert that terminate() leaves no shared state with a freshly-\n  constructed worker (jobId counter resets, message ledger isolated)\n  — doc-review flagged that no unit explicitly owned this assertion.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"700e40dfb226ea69c06ee99e2c8290174a39b12a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/trees/700e40dfb226ea69c06ee99e2c8290174a39b12a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/commits/3c5f6fc964660edd57de60b622dcb3681b3c79f6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95","id":36343085,"login":"masonstevens95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQzMDg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commit/3c5f6fc964660edd57de60b622dcb3681b3c79f6","node_id":"C_kwDOSV4urtoAKDNjNWY2ZmM5NjQ2NjBlZGQ1N2RlNjBiNjIyZGNiMzY4MWIzYzc5ZjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commit/42eb8deaf4074a2c4e248adc4321787c0092b77c","sha":"42eb8deaf4074a2c4e248adc4321787c0092b77c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/42eb8deaf4074a2c4e248adc4321787c0092b77c"}],"sha":"3c5f6fc964660edd57de60b622dcb3681b3c79f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/3c5f6fc964660edd57de60b622dcb3681b3c79f6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95","id":36343085,"login":"masonstevens95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQzMDg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/42eb8deaf4074a2c4e248adc4321787c0092b77c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-07T19:41:44Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-07T19:41:44Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"message":"feat(remote): U1 ML runtime adapter + model cache layer\n\nAdd the ONNX Runtime Web adapter and Cache Storage helper that v4''s\nML stages (U5 segmentation, U6 face landmarks) build on. No model is\nloaded yet — this unit is purely additive infrastructure.\n\n- src/ml/runtime.ts: lazy `import(''onnxruntime-web/wasm'')` (tree-shakes\n  WebGPU/WebGL paths), `ort.env.wasm.wasmPaths` set to a jsDelivr CDN\n  constant, `numThreads = 1` (no COOP/COEP in MF host), and a\n  per-modelUrl session promise cache so repeat callers share one init.\n  Includes the corrupt-cache self-heal: if `InferenceSession.create()`\n  rejects a cached ArrayBuffer, evict + refetch + retry exactly once,\n  and surface a typed `MLRuntimeError(''model_load_failed'')` on the\n  second failure. Without this, one bad cache write would permanently\n  degrade the user until the next cache version bump.\n\n- src/ml/modelCache.ts: `pixelart-models-v1` cache, `fetchModel` reads\n  the response body fully into ArrayBuffer BEFORE `cache.put` so a\n  network drop never persists a truncated entry. `QuotaExceededError`\n  is swallowed (caller still gets bytes; persistence missed).\n  `evictModel` for the runtime self-heal path. `purgeOldCaches` is\n  prefix-scoped — only deletes caches starting with `pixelart-models-`\n  not in the current allow-list, so host-page caches are never touched.\n\n- src/ml/types.ts: `ModelDescriptor`, `InferenceSessionWrapper`, and a\n  typed `MLRuntimeError` with codes `model_fetch_failed | model_load_failed\n  | inference_failed | cors_blocked | quota_exceeded` so U8''s degraded-mode\n  UI can route each failure mode distinctly.\n\n- tests/ml/modelCache.test.ts: 9 vitest cases covering happy path,\n  QuotaExceededError fallback, prefix-scoped purge (incl. assertion\n  that non-prefixed caches are preserved), network + CORS-opaque\n  error paths, mid-read body failure (no partial cache write), and\n  evictModel re-download.\n\n- package.json: `onnxruntime-web ^1.19.0` added as a runtime dep;\n  pnpm-lock.yaml updated.","tree":{"sha":"616a20c43d9f63d0760ec187a2971371dff5af27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/trees/616a20c43d9f63d0760ec187a2971371dff5af27"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/commits/42eb8deaf4074a2c4e248adc4321787c0092b77c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95","id":