hub.com/users/masonstevens95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/b848953212428cba178b72bfcd5f69a09718e55e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-06T22:51:24Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-06T22:51:24Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"message":"chore(v2): pin image-q, refresh README, mark v2 plan completed\n\nPin image-q from ^4.0.0 to ~4.0.0 in both apps/remote and\napps/harness. The Wu quantizer''s tie-breaking on near-identical\nhistogram bins is implementation-dependent if the dependency is\nbumped — the v1-invariant byte-equality test in U5 implicitly relies\non Wu being deterministic across runs. ~ pins to patch updates only,\nwhich is tighter than ^ and protects the invariant from a routine\n''pnpm install'' minor bump (per feasibility doc-review feedback).\n\nREADME updates from ''v1 currently live'' framing to a unified ''What\nit does'' list covering all six controls (drop, resolution, aspect,\npalette, brand, saturation) — accurate for the first time since the\nfile was written. v1 and v2 plan history move into an\n''Implementation history'' section that points at both plan documents.\n\nv2 plan status flips active → completed (the only allowed plan\nmutation during ce-work, per the skill spec).\n\nFinal quality gates: typecheck clean, lint clean, 123 tests across\n19 test files passing, both apps build cleanly with verify scripts\ngreen.","tree":{"sha":"e172c8bc0142118b537a6f448142b4c2b703fa23","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/trees/e172c8bc0142118b537a6f448142b4c2b703fa23"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/commits/b848953212428cba178b72bfcd5f69a09718e55e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95","id":36343085,"login":"masonstevens95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQzMDg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commit/b848953212428cba178b72bfcd5f69a09718e55e","node_id":"C_kwDOSV4urtoAKGI4NDg5NTMyMTI0MjhjYmExNzhiNzJiZmNkNWY2OWEwOTcxOGU1NWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commit/c5a9238b5e38966aae0ba510c01ddce6a4cb2d50","sha":"c5a9238b5e38966aae0ba510c01ddce6a4cb2d50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/c5a9238b5e38966aae0ba510c01ddce6a4cb2d50"}],"sha":"b848953212428cba178b72bfcd5f69a09718e55e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/b848953212428cba178b72bfcd5f69a09718e55e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95","id":36343085,"login":"masonstevens95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQzMDg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/c5a9238b5e38966aae0ba510c01ddce6a4cb2d50/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-06T22:49:58Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-06T22:49:58Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"message":"feat(remote): U5+U6 — brand-color injection + v1-invariant integration test\n\nFolds the v2 plan''s U6 (v1-invariant test + bundle audit) into U5 per\nscope-guardian doc-review feedback (a single integration test + script\nedit didn''t earn standalone-unit status).\n\nBrandColorsTextarea reuses parsePalette from U4 — same hex format,\nsame forgiving parser, same silent-truncation-at-64. Adds a\ncontext-sensitive UX hint (per design-lens doc-review feedback): when\nthe active palette is curated/custom AND brand colors are non-empty,\nsurfaces ''Brand colors merge with the active palette — the result may\nnot look like a pure curated set.'' Quiet otherwise. role=''alert'' on\nthe parse-error container for screen-reader announcement.\n\nPixelArtApp threads brand colors through the existing pipeline plumbing\nlanded in U4. The brandColors pass-through is the last piece of the v2\nworker protocol — all four v2 features now live behind optional\nProcessRequest fields with v1-equivalent defaults. ProcessOptions\nshape stays stable.\n\nv1-invariant test (folded from U6) lives at\napps/remote/tests/pipeline/v1-invariant.test.ts — exercises the v2\npipeline stages with all defaults (saturation=0 short-circuits,\naspectRatio=undefined skips crop, no fixedPalette, no brandColors)\nand asserts byte-identical output against a v1-equivalent\n''downscale → quantize'' reference computed inline. Includes a negative\ncontrol (saturation=-1 must NOT match v1) so a real regression in\nthe short-circuit logic would surface as a test failure.\n\nverify-build.sh ceiling raised from v1''s 50 KB to a hard 23 KB cap\n(per scope-guardian''s enforcement-not-aspiration recommendation).\nSizing rationale documented in the script: v1 exposed chunk was 8886\nbytes raw / ~3 KB gzipped; v2 ships at 20810 bytes raw / ~6.6 KB\ngzipped. v1→v2 delta is +3.6 KB gzipped, under R7''s +5 KB target.\n23 KB = v2 measured + 2 KB headroom. Builds exceeding 23 KB fail loud.\n\nTests: 9 BrandColorsTextarea + 4 v1-invariant. 136 passing total.","tree":{"sha":"31ab67d0163d4fe9d7b20d914754819c031f11de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/trees/31ab67d0163d4fe9d7b20d914754819c031f11de"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/commits/c5a9238b5e38966aae0ba510c01ddce6a4cb2d50","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95","id":36343085,"login":"masonstevens95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQzMDg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commit/c5a9238b5e38966aae0ba510c01ddce6a4cb2d50","node_id":"C_kwDOSV4urtoAKGM1YTkyMzhiNWUzODk2NmFhZTBiYTUxMGMwMWRkY2U2YTRjYjJkNTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commit/1116e60c0b97d3ab1d14e0c49f98adad46cfa091","sha":"1116e60c0b97d3ab1d14e0c49f98adad46cfa091","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/1116e60c0b97d3ab1d14e0c49f98adad46cfa091"}],"sha":"c5a9238b5e38966aae0ba510c01ddce6a4cb2d50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/c5a9238b5e38966aae0ba510c01ddce6a4cb2d50"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95","id":36343085,"login":"masonstevens95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQzMDg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/1116e60c0b97d3ab1d14e0c49f98adad46cfa091/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-06T22:46:59Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-06T22:46:59Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"message":"feat(remote): U4 — curated and custom palette modes\n\npalettes.ts ships three retro classics: Game Boy DMG (4 colors),\nPICO-8 (16), EGA-16 (16). Per scope-guardian doc-review feedback,\nday-one catalog is intentionally narrow — adding more palettes is\ndata-only with no code changes. RGB tuples cite their canonical\nreferences in the source file.\n\nparsePalette is forgiving but bounded:\n- Whitespace and comma separators interchangeably\n- Optional leading #, 3-digit shorthand or 6-digit hex, case-insensitive\n- Two distinct overflow paths (resolved during planning):\n    * Index ≥ 64: silent truncation, returns ok with truncated:true\n    * Malformed token: returns ok:false with the bad token highlighted\n- The truncated:true flag drives the ''Truncated to first 64 colors''\n  inline notice in PaletteModeControl\n\nquantize.ts grows from (input, paletteSize) to (input, options):\n- options.fixedPalette → skip Wu, apply supplied RGB tuples via\n  iq.utils.Palette.add(Point.createByRGBA(r,g,b,255))\n- options.brandColors → prepend to whatever palette is active. Auto\n  mode: Wu builds at size max(2, paletteSize − brandColors.length)\n  so its quality function isn''t wasted on slots that get evicted\n  (per the KTD↔U5 contradiction reconciled in the plan-patch commit).\n  Fixed-palette modes: trailing entries evicted on overflow.\n- mergeBrandColors handles dedup (exact RGB equality) + truncation\n- countDistinctColors retained for tests\n- v1 path preserved: quantizePalette(image) with no options reproduces\n  v1 behavior exactly\n\nPaletteModeControl uses native <input type=radio> in <fieldset>/\n<legend> per design-lens doc-review feedback — gives keyboard nav\n(arrow keys between options) and screen-reader semantics for free,\nno custom ARIA. Mode sub-state preserved across switches: switching\nCustom → Auto → Custom keeps the user''s pasted hex intact (only\nvisibility toggles, values persist). role=''alert'' on parse-error\ncontainer so screen readers announce invalid hex tokens.\n\nWorker protocol grows fixedPalette and brandColors as optional\nreadonly RGB-tuple arrays. Worker routes to quantize options based\non presence; v1 defaults (both undefined) reproduce v1 path.\n\nTests: 11 palettes/parsePalette + 10 quantize (including the v1\ninvariant: brandColors=[] + no fixedPalette = v1 byte-identical) +\n9 PaletteModeControl. 110 passing total.","tree":{"sha":"1b4812062515a106a387536e190f76d2a422407f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/trees/1b4812062515a106a387536e190f76d2a422407f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/commits/1116e60c0b97d3ab1d14e0c49f98adad46cfa091","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95","id":36343085,"login":"masonstevens95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQzMDg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commit/1116e60c0b97d3ab1d14e0c49f98adad46cfa091","node_id":"C_kwDOSV4urtoAKDExMTZlNjBjMGI5N2QzYWIxZDE0ZTBjNDlmOThhZGFkNDZjZmEwOTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commit/9b888d42971912e52c32e757dd12d84007f07f87","sha":"9b888d42971912e52c32e757dd12d84007f07f87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/9b888d42971912e52c32e757dd12d84007f07f87"}],"sha":"1116e60c0b97d3ab1d14e0c49f98adad46cfa091","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/1116e60c0b97d3ab1d14e0c49f98adad46cfa091"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95","id":36343085,"login":"masonstevens95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQzMDg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/9b888d42971912e52c32e757dd12d84007f07f87/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-06T22:41:49Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-06T22:41:49Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"message":"feat(remote): U3 — aspect-ratio selector + center-crop pipeline stage\n\ncenterCrop is a pure function on ImageData: largest centered rectangle\nmatching the target W/H ratio. Source-already-matches case (within 1\nsource pixel) returns the input unchanged — so ''preserves source\naspect'' (the v1 default) costs zero work and produces v1-bit-identical\noutput.\n\nWorker pipeline gains a new conditional stage between saturation and\ndownscale: msg.aspectRatio !== undefined ? centerCrop(...) : skip.\nThe downscale step then computes target dims from the cropped image,\nso the resolution slider''s long-edge target applies to the cropped\nresult (e.g. 4000x3000 source + 1:1 + target 64 = 64x64, not 64x48).\n\nAspectRatioSelect ships Source / Square / Portrait (3:4) / Landscape\n(4:3) / Custom. Custom uses two number inputs — no arbitrary [1,50]\nupper bound (per scope-guardian doc-review feedback; the real\nconstraint is post-crop dims ≥ 1×1, which centerCrop validates\ngeometrically). Helper text ''Enter ratio parts (16 and 9 for 16:9)''\naddresses the design-lens hint-copy gap. Inline error via role=alert\nwhen W or H is non-positive.\n\nCustom mode emits 16/9 immediately on selection (defaults populated)\nso users see a result without typing anything; subsequent edits flow\nthrough tryApplyCustom which validates before emitting.\n\nProcessOptions grows aspectRatio?: number; ProcessRequest grows\naspectRatio?. Both optional with v1-equivalent defaults (undefined →\nno crop). v1 invariant preserved end-to-end.\n\nTests: 14 new (8 crop pure-function + 6 AspectRatioSelect). 71\npassing total.","tree":{"sha":"55e5e0a09fe9b00fd8a11150e07ce7fce906e541","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/trees/55e5e0a09fe9b00fd8a11150e07ce7fce906e541"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/commits/9b888d42971912e52c32e757dd12d84007f07f87","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95","id":36343085,"login":"masonstevens95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQzMDg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commit/9b888d42971912e52c32e757dd12d84007f07f87","node_id":"C_kwDOSV4urtoAKDliODg4ZDQyOTcxOTEyZTUyYzMyZTc1N2RkMTJkODQwMDdmMDdmODc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commit/7786855660a1cd6b369f1c2f33acf04320e12859","sha":"7786855660a1cd6b369f1c2f33acf04320e12859","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/7786855660a1cd6b369f1c2f33acf04320e12859"}],"sha":"9b888d42971912e52c32e757dd12d84007f07f87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/9b888d42971912e52c32e757dd12d84007f07f87"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95","id":36343085,"login":"masonstevens95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQzMDg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/7786855660a1cd6b369f1c2f33acf04320e12859/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-06T22:39:42Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-06T22:39:42Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"message":"feat(remote): U2+U1 — saturation slider + HSL transform + advanced panel\n\nFolds the v2 plan''s U1 (Advanced panel scaffold) into U2 per scope-\nguardian doc-review feedback (an empty disclosure unit produced no\nshippable value alone).\n\nPipeline addition: saturationAdjust (HSL space) runs after rasterize\nand before downscale. The function explicitly short-circuits at\namount === 0 and returns the input ImageData unchanged — required to\nmake the byte-equality unit test reachable, since RGB→HSL→RGB on\nalready-rounded 8-bit values is otherwise lossy by ~1 unit per\nchannel. The worker also pre-checks (msg.saturation ?? 0) so v1\ndefaults skip the function entirely.\n\nUI: AdvancedControlsPanel uses native <details>/<summary> for free\nkeyboard accessibility and zero JS state. Marker suppressed via CSS,\nreplaced with a chevron that rotates 180° on open via the [open]\nattribute selector. Closed by default — v1 simple flow stays the\nprimary surface.\n\nSaturationSlider provides a continuous -1..+1 control with 0.05 step,\nexplicit-sign formatting (+0.40 / 0.00 / -0.30), a center tick mark\non the track, and muted readout color when the value is exactly 0 —\nboth visual cues for the neutral-state ambiguity flagged in design-\nlens doc review.\n\nPer design-lens doc-review feedback, the Advanced controls follow a\nuniform ''rendered-but-disabled when no image is loaded'' policy\n(matching ResolutionSlider). Removes implementer ambiguity on no-image\nstate across U2-U5.\n\nWorker protocol: saturation is the first of v2''s optional fields on\nProcessRequest; absence reproduces v1 behavior. Hook forwards via a\nProcessOptions object so adding the remaining v2 fields (aspectRatio,\npaletteMode, brandColors) doesn''t require yet another positional\nargument.\n\nTests: 15 new (7 saturation pure-function + 5 SaturationSlider + 3\nAdvancedControlsPanel). 57 passing total. R5 invariant assertion\n(saturation=0 returns input.data byte-identical via short-circuit) is\nthe most load-bearing — explicit it == input check, not just data\nequality.","tree":{"sha":"885de2c400767909ee2d95fd0c906a323b1f1585","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/trees/885de2c400767909ee2d95fd0c906a323b1f1585"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/commits/7786855660a1cd6b369f1c2f33acf04320e12859","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95","id":36343085,"login":"masonstevens95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQzMDg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commit/7786855660a1cd6b369f1c2f33acf04320e12859","node_id":"C_kwDOSV4urtoAKDc3ODY4NTU2NjBhMWNkNmIzNjlmMWMyZjMzYWNmMDQzMjBlMTI4NTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commit/3c01a7689e5bfc366763472f09725a61e9c70181","sha":"3c01a7689e5bfc366763472f09725a61e9c70181","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/3c01a7689e5bfc366763472f09725a61e9c70181"}],"sha":"7786855660a1cd6b369f1c2f33acf04320e12859","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/7786855660a1cd6b369f1c2f33acf04320e12859"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95","id":36343085,"login":"masonstevens95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQzMDg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/commits/3c01a7689e5bfc366763472f09725a61e9c70181/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-06T22:36:04Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-06T22:36:04Z","email":"mason.c.stevens@gmail.com","name":"masonstevens95"},"message":"docs(plan): patch v2 plan to resolve doc-review P1 algorithmic contradictions\n\nPre-execution patches addressing the four findings most likely to cause\ndivergent implementations or test-construction errors:\n\n1. Brand-color injection algorithm — KTD and U5 contradicted on Auto mode\n   (build-full-then-truncate vs build-reduced-then-merge). Reconciled to\n   the build-reduced-then-merge strategy: Wu sees target size directly\n   so its quality function optimizes the slots that survive.\n2. Auto vs Curated truncation strategy — algorithmic divergence is\n   intentional (Wu can be parameterized; curated catalogs are fixed\n   data) but was unexplained. Documented the rationale in KTD.\n3. saturationAdjust function-level identity short-circuit — U2''s\n   byte-identical-at-saturation=0 test required the function itself to\n   short-circuit, not just the worker-level skip. Spelled out.\n4. parsePalette overflow vs invalid-token paths — KTD said inline error,\n   U4 test said silent truncation. Two distinct paths now: overflow at\n   index 64 silently drops; malformed tokens surface inline errors.\n\nNES palette ''54 vs ~25'' contradiction was auto-applied silently during\ndoc-review''s safe_auto pass earlier this turn.\n\nOther doc-review findings (no-image state policy, mode persistence,\nfocus management, ARIA roles, mobile breakpoints, swatch previews,\nunit collapsing) are deliberately left unpatched in the plan and will\nbe applied as code-time decisions during execution, called out in\ntheir respective unit commits.","tree":{"sha":"c4352bdb96bbb61b45dfbac69a4d1ad4b54e0bff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/trees/c4352bdb96bbb61b45dfbac69a4d1ad4b54e0bff"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masonstevens95/picture-to-pixel-art/git/commits/3c01a7689e5bfc366763472f09725a61e9c70181","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36343085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/masonstevens95","id":36343085,"login":"masonstevens95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzQzMDg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masonstevens95/received