m/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/4e06e9e206d64a1535dae5ecbf00e849cbe3f93f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-14T20:26:13Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-14T20:26:13Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-7e): address Codex review round 8 (P3 fixes)\n\nTwo doc-hygiene findings, no behaviour change:\n\n- **[P3] `design.md` §4 + gate list still claimed\n  the status-based `PARTIAL_CONTENT` skip is the\n  current model.** §4 said \"Range pre-emption stays\n  intact via the explicit `if parts.status ==\n  StatusCode::PARTIAL_CONTENT` check INSIDE\n  `maybe_apply`\", and the §4 gate list still had a\n  step 5 reading \"`parts.status == PARTIAL_CONTENT`\n  → return with `Vary` set, body untouched\". Codex\n  round 4 P2 removed that skip; 206 now follows the\n  same threshold gate as 200. Rewrote both sites to\n  describe the current unified-gate semantics and\n  preserve the round-4 historical citation.\n\n- **[P3] `proposal.md` slice-4 summary still listed\n  \"Range pre-emption\" as a current `http-compression`\n  spec deliverable.** That bullet is a current-state\n  description of what the change package''s spec\n  covers — but the spec now describes the\n  threshold-gate composition with Stage 7c, not\n  Range pre-emption. Rewrote the bullet to mention\n  \"206 / threshold-gate composition with Stage 7c\n  — small ranges pass through uncompressed with Vary;\n  large ranges encode like 200s, per the Codex round\n  4 P2 refinement\".\n\nVerification:\n\n- `npx @fission-ai/openspec validate --all --strict`\n  — 26 passed / 0 failed.\n- No code changed; `cargo` unchanged from rounds 6-7\n  (362 / 81-2-0 / 26 still holds).\n\nFinal sweep for \"Range pre-empts compression\" /\n\"PARTIAL_CONTENT short-circuit\" returns only:\n- Correct current-state mentions (\"no status-based\n  206 skip\" — design.md §4, http-compression spec\n  Range Requirement, decisions.md D-020 \"What is\n  contractual\", open-questions.md Q-002 closure).\n- Historical narrative inside `tasks.md`''s round-4\n  P2 entry (correct — describes the fix).\n- The kickoff plan file\n  `docs/features/0019_PLAN_stage7e_compression.md`\n  (frozen at plan-time per stage methodology — plan\n  files are kickoff records, not current-state\n  documentation).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"137b20e864083a17aa820ca51ac1bc65fd0b55b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/137b20e864083a17aa820ca51ac1bc65fd0b55b9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/4e06e9e206d64a1535dae5ecbf00e849cbe3f93f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/4e06e9e206d64a1535dae5ecbf00e849cbe3f93f","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDRlMDZlOWUyMDZkNjRhMTUzNWRhZTVlY2JmMDBlODQ5Y2JlM2Y5M2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/34a7ba3bccfce58ecb12d5234cee26951595cac4","sha":"34a7ba3bccfce58ecb12d5234cee26951595cac4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/34a7ba3bccfce58ecb12d5234cee26951595cac4"}],"sha":"4e06e9e206d64a1535dae5ecbf00e849cbe3f93f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/4e06e9e206d64a1535dae5ecbf00e849cbe3f93f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/34a7ba3bccfce58ecb12d5234cee26951595cac4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-14T20:19:20Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-14T20:19:20Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-7e): address Codex review round 7 (P3 fixes)\n\nTwo doc-hygiene findings, no behaviour change:\n\n- **[P3] D-020 \"Forward note\" still cited \"10 affected\n  snapshots\".** Same entry''s #1 and #4 bullets were\n  bumped to 12 in round 6, but the Forward-note\n  sentence at the end of D-020 was missed. Bumped to\n  12 to match the current state of\n  `tools/probe/cases/compression-raw.json`''s\n  `runner.l0.bodyMayDiffer` array.\n\n- **[P3] proposal.md slice-2 block was anachronistic\n  after round 6.** Round 6 bumped the \"10 compressed\n  anchors\" count to 12 inside a slice-2 historical\n  description, which broke the surrounding context\n  (\"Slice 2 added 20 anchors\", \"ORC-191..ORC-210\" were\n  left at the slice-2 numbers). Reverted that one\n  number to 10 — the slice-2 block now consistently\n  describes the state at commit `d1b9a15` (20 anchors,\n  10 compressed, ORC-191..ORC-210, dispatcher seam in\n  `build_file_or_304`) — and appended a one-sentence\n  forward pointer to the current-state counts (23 / 12\n  / ORC-191..ORC-213) for readers who want the latest\n  numbers. Source of truth for current state stays\n  in D-020 / `openspec/specs/http-compression/spec.md`\n  Compatibility notes / `docs/reference/serve/inventory.md`\n  SRV-CLI-012 entry.\n\nVerification:\n\n- `npx @fission-ai/openspec validate --all --strict`\n  — 26 passed / 0 failed.\n- No code changed; `cargo` unchanged from round 6\n  (362 / 81-2-0 / 26 still holds).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b99e58d6251c229d8ae972c956a87484a7a60909","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/b99e58d6251c229d8ae972c956a87484a7a60909"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/34a7ba3bccfce58ecb12d5234cee26951595cac4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/34a7ba3bccfce58ecb12d5234cee26951595cac4","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDM0YTdiYTNiY2NmY2U1OGVjYjEyZDUyMzRjZWUyNjk1MTU5NWNhYzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/2dd3b6f483fecd127a878d6a2f8f615f7eb95a02","sha":"2dd3b6f483fecd127a878d6a2f8f615f7eb95a02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/2dd3b6f483fecd127a878d6a2f8f615f7eb95a02"}],"sha":"34a7ba3bccfce58ecb12d5234cee26951595cac4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/34a7ba3bccfce58ecb12d5234cee26951595cac4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/2dd3b6f483fecd127a878d6a2f8f615f7eb95a02/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-14T19:57:39Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-14T19:57:39Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-7e): address Codex review round 6 (P3 fixes)\n\nTwo doc-hygiene findings, no behaviour change:\n\n- **[P3] CLI OpenSpec described the pre-round-4\n  contract.** `openspec/specs/cli/spec.md` (canonical\n  baseline) and `openspec/changes/015-compression/specs/cli/spec.md`\n  (change-package delta) both:\n  - Listed \"Range pre-emption\" as an L3 skip\n    condition. Replaced with the round-4-P2 \"206 /\n    threshold-gate composition\" wording (small ranges\n    pass through uncompressed with Vary; large ranges\n    encode like 200s).\n  - Cited `ORC-191..ORC-210` / \"20 anchors\". Bumped\n    to `ORC-191..ORC-213` / \"23 anchors\" — covering\n    round-3 P2''s identity / non-identity passthrough\n    pair (ORC-211, ORC-212) and round-4 P2''s\n    above-threshold-range encode case (ORC-213).\n  - Change-package delta still claimed the seam was\n    in `build_file_or_304` \"before Range pre-emption\".\n    Rewrote to the round-1-P2 centralized\n    `server::handler` seam (between `apply_cors` and\n    the request log) and dropped the stale\n    \"before Range pre-emption\" phrase. Added the\n    skip-list entries for round-3 P2 (already-encoded\n    non-identity `Content-Encoding` passthrough).\n\n- **[P3] Several current compatibility notes still\n  said \"10 compressed anchors\".** Bumped to \"12\":\n  - `docs/reference/serve/decisions.md` D-020 #1 (the\n    framing divergence''s `bodyMayDiffer` description).\n  - `docs/reference/serve/decisions.md` D-020 #4 (the\n    body-bytes divergence''s `bodyMayDiffer`\n    description — both occurrences within the entry).\n  - `docs/reference/serve/inventory.md` SRV-CLI-012\n    compatibility note.\n  - `openspec/specs/http-compression/spec.md`\n    Compatibility note on body bytes (D-020 #4).\n  - `openspec/changes/015-compression/specs/http-compression/spec.md`\n    same note in the delta.\n  - `openspec/changes/015-compression/proposal.md`\n    out-of-scope #4 description.\n  - `openspec/changes/015-compression/design.md` D-020\n    inline summary.\n\nThe post-round-3 / post-round-4 anchor count is 12:\nthe 10 slice-2 compressed anchors\n(`big_html_gzip_deflate_br`, `big_html_gzip`,\n`big_html_deflate`, `big_html_gzip_q0`,\n`big_css_gzip_deflate_br`, `big_js_gzip_deflate_br`,\n`data_json_gzip_deflate_br`,\n`vector_svg_gzip_deflate_br`, `wasm_gzip_deflate_br`,\n`options_big_html_gzip`) plus round-3-P2''s\n`user_ce_identity_above_threshold` and round-4-P2''s\n`range_big_html_above_threshold`. Source of truth:\n`tools/probe/cases/compression-raw.json`''s\n`runner.l0.bodyMayDiffer` array.\n\nSlice-2 historical narrative entries in\n`openspec/changes/015-compression/{proposal,design,tasks}.md`\nthat describe what slice 2 added (20 anchors / 10\ncompressed at slice-2 commit time) are left as\nhistorical context — they describe a past state, not\nthe current one. The \"current state\" claims (in D-020\n/ Compatibility notes / canonical capability spec /\ninventory / CLI baseline) all reflect post-round-4\ncounts.\n\nVerification:\n\n- `cargo test --workspace --lib` — 362 passed\n  (unchanged; doc-only round).\n- `cargo test --test oracle` — 81 passed / 2 skipped\n  / 0 failed (unchanged).\n- `npx @fission-ai/openspec validate --all --strict`\n  — 26 passed / 0 failed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5006e4794b0ae6ca95949ab599ccebdeb148943b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/5006e4794b0ae6ca95949ab599ccebdeb148943b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/2dd3b6f483fecd127a878d6a2f8f615f7eb95a02","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/2dd3b6f483fecd127a878d6a2f8f615f7eb95a02","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDJkZDNiNmY0ODNmZWNkMTI3YTg3OGQ2YTJmOGY2MTVmN2ViOTVhMDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/3c2444a57e49e878aec9a77f54b476964cfa808a","sha":"3c2444a57e49e878aec9a77f54b476964cfa808a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/3c2444a57e49e878aec9a77f54b476964cfa808a"}],"sha":"2dd3b6f483fecd127a878d6a2f8f615f7eb95a02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/2dd3b6f483fecd127a878d6a2f8f615f7eb95a02"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/3c2444a57e49e878aec9a77f54b476964cfa808a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-14T19:45:12Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-14T19:45:12Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-7e): address Codex review round 5 (P3 fixes)\n\nOne finding, pure doc-hygiene:\n\n- **[P3] Stale comments and docs claiming \"Range\n  pre-empts compression entirely\".** Codex round 4 P2\n  removed the status-based 206 skip — 206 now follows\n  the same threshold gate as 200 (mirroring\n  `compression/index.js:177` which checks `chunkLength\n  < threshold` uniformly across statuses). But six\n  committed references still described the old model:\n\n  Code comments rewritten:\n  - `crates/irserve-core/src/compression.rs` module\n    doc — replaced the \"Range requests pre-empt\n    compression entirely\" bullet with the threshold-\n    gate description plus an explicit note that\n    small ranges fail the threshold gate naturally\n    and large ranges encode normally.\n  - `crates/irserve-core/src/compression.rs`\n    `maybe_apply` rustdoc — removed the dead\n    \"On 206 Partial Content (Range): nothing\n    (pre-emption — body is already a sliced range\n    and Content-Range would lie after re-compression)\"\n    bullet from the mutation list.\n  - `crates/irserve-core/src/server.rs::handler` —\n    rewrote the centralized-compression comment to\n    enumerate the current skip set (including the\n    round 3 P2 identity passthrough) and the round\n    4 P2 unified 206-threshold-gate semantics.\n  - `crates/irserve-core/src/dispatch.rs` — rewrote\n    the no-Range tail comment to reflect that the\n    Range branch''s 206 / 416 outputs DO flow through\n    `compression::maybe_apply` at the handler-level\n    seam (vs the stale \"Range path below still\n    short-circuits compression\").\n\n  Reference docs rewritten:\n  - `docs/reference/serve/open-questions.md` Q-002\n    closure — split the skip-conditions bullet to\n    include the round 3 P2 identity passthrough and\n    added a dedicated 206 bullet with the round 4 P2\n    threshold-gate semantics.\n  - `docs/reference/serve/decisions.md` D-020''s\n    \"What is contractual\" paragraph — refreshed to\n    mention the 206 / threshold-gate composition,\n    the identity passthrough, and the corrected\n    ORC range (ORC-191..ORC-213, was ORC-191..ORC-210).\n  - `docs/stage7_l3_capabilities.md` row 7e —\n    rewrote the skip-conditions list and Range\n    interaction to current state; bumped anchor\n    counts 22 → 23 and ORC range; added the round 4\n    P2 commit citation alongside the round 1/2/3\n    history.\n  - `openspec/changes/015-compression/design.md`\n    §1 — refreshed the Range bullet to enumerate\n    both sub-cases (below threshold → no encode,\n    above threshold → encode with Content-Range\n    retained); bumped the anchor-count footnote to\n    23.\n  - `openspec/changes/015-compression/tasks.md`\n    slice 0 anchor list — clarified\n    `range_big_html_gzip` is the \"below-threshold\n    sub-case\" (vs the stale \"Range pre-empts\n    compression\").\n\nVerification:\n\n- `cargo test --workspace --lib` — 362 passed\n  (unchanged; doc-only round).\n- `cargo test --test oracle` — 81 passed / 2 skipped\n  / 0 failed (unchanged).\n- `npx @fission-ai/openspec validate --all --strict`\n  — 26 passed / 0 failed.\n\nFinal sweep for \"Range pre-empts compression\" / \"206\nnever enters maybe_apply\" / \"pre-empts compression\nentirely\" returned only historical narrative inside\n`tasks.md`''s round 2 P2 / round 3 P3 entries\n(describing the old text being rewritten by those\nrounds) — kept as historical context. The Stage 7c\n\"Range pre-empts the 304 short-circuit\" mentions\n(separate semantic) are still accurate and unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"57ebeb2099fcba42e0905deec2758349ffd2402d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/57ebeb2099fcba42e0905deec2758349ffd2402d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/3c2444a57e49e878aec9a77f54b476964cfa808a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/3c2444a57e49e878aec9a77f54b476964cfa808a","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDNjMjQ0NGE1N2U0OWU4NzhhZWM5YTc3ZjU0YjQ3Njk2NGNmYTgwOGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/1c526ebb92f58904ea013fd4046ff7202dc512e2","sha":"1c526ebb92f58904ea013fd4046ff7202dc512e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/1c526ebb92f58904ea013fd4046ff7202dc512e2"}],"sha":"3c2444a57e49e878aec9a77f54b476964cfa808a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/3c2444a57e49e878aec9a77f54b476964cfa808a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/1c526ebb92f58904ea013fd4046ff7202dc512e2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-14T19:35:47Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-14T19:35:47Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-7e): address Codex review round 4 (P2 fix)\n\nOne finding, valid:\n\n- **[P2] Above-threshold 206 Partial Content ranges\n  were not compressed.** Initial Stage 7e wiring\n  carried an explicit `if status ==\n  StatusCode::PARTIAL_CONTENT` short-circuit in\n  `maybe_apply` — a deliberate safety measure based\n  on the slice-0 probe of a 16-byte range (which\n  naturally fails the 1024-byte threshold gate\n  anyway). Codex round 4 P2 surfaced empirically\n  that the reference has NO status-based 206 skip:\n  `serve-handler/src/index.js:749` sets\n  `Content-Length` to the range size before\n  `writeHead`, and `compression/index.js:177`\n  evaluates `chunkLength < threshold` uniformly\n  across statuses. A `Range: bytes=0-1499` on a\n  4723-byte HTML file in reference returns `206 +\n  Content-Encoding: br + Transfer-Encoding: chunked`.\n  The previous OpenSpec text now explicitly claimed\n  \"no encode regardless of range size\" — false for\n  reference.\n\n  Fix: removed the status-based 206 skip from\n  `crates/irserve-core/src/compression.rs`. 206\n  responses now follow the same gate ordering as\n  200s; small ranges naturally fail the threshold\n  gate; large ranges encode normally with\n  `Content-Range` retained verbatim (the RFC 9110\n  §15.3.7 quirk where `Content-Range` addresses the\n  ORIGINAL bytes while the wire body is the\n  encoded form — both targets share this surface).\n\n  Verification:\n  - Renamed `maybe_apply_partial_content_keeps_vary_skips_encoding`\n    → `maybe_apply_partial_content_below_threshold_keeps_vary_skips_encoding`\n    (and adjusted the body to 16 bytes, which is what\n    the 16-byte-range case actually carries).\n  - Added `maybe_apply_partial_content_above_threshold_compresses`\n    — a 1500-byte 206 body asserts `Content-Encoding: br`\n    is set, `Content-Range` retained verbatim, and\n    compressed body length is < 1500.\n  - New raw dual-target probe anchor\n    `range_big_html_above_threshold` (Range:\n    `bytes=0-1199` → 1200-byte slice on `big.html`)\n    in `compression-raw.json`. Added ORC-213.\n    `bodyMayDiffer` per D-020 #4. Reference snapshot\n    re-recorded — pins `206 + Content-Range: bytes\n    0-1199/1494 + Vary + Content-Encoding: br +\n    Transfer-Encoding: chunked` on reference (vs\n    `Content-Length: <compressed>` on irserve, per\n    the existing D-020 #1 framing entry — no new\n    D-020 entry needed).\n  - Updated ORC-206 must-match text to clarify the\n    no-`Content-Encoding` outcome is due to the\n    threshold gate, not a status-based skip.\n  - Updated `openspec/specs/http-compression/spec.md`:\n    rewrote the Range Requirement to say \"206 follows\n    the same threshold gate as 200\" with two\n    concrete sub-cases (below / above threshold),\n    added a new Scenario for the above-threshold\n    case, and refreshed the Implementation gate\n    list (no `PARTIAL_CONTENT` step). Mirrored in\n    the change-package delta. Bumped anchor counts\n    22 → 23 in `inventory.md`.\n\nVerification:\n\n- `cargo test --workspace --lib` — 362 passed (was\n  361; +1 unit test for above-threshold 206 encode).\n- `cargo test --test oracle` — 81 passed / 2 skipped\n  / 0 failed (compression-raw now verifies 23\n  requests; the new ORC-213 anchor lands inside the\n  existing case).\n- `npx @fission-ai/openspec validate --all --strict`\n  — 26 passed / 0 failed.\n- Manual smoke against `big.html` (2226 bytes):\n  - `Range: bytes=0-15` → 206 + Vary +\n    Content-Length: 16 + no Content-Encoding.\n  - `Range: bytes=0-1499` → 206 + Vary +\n    Content-Encoding: br + Content-Length: 87\n    (compressed from 1500 raw bytes).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"09d97049d975af4845704f62c193849280875166","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/09d97049d975af4845704f62c193849280875166"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/1c526ebb92f58904ea013fd4046ff7202dc512e2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/1c526ebb92f58904ea013fd4046ff7202dc512e2","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDFjNTI2ZWJiOTJmNTg5MDRlYTAxM2ZkNDA0NmZmNzIwMmRjNTEyZTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/a49609c4a56c36094710803e98c4be37a422b200","sha":"a49609c4a56c36094710803e98c4be37a422b200","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/a49609c4a56c36094710803e98c4be37a422b200"}],"sha":"1c526ebb92f58904ea013fd4046ff7202dc512e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/1c526ebb92f58904ea013fd4046ff7202dc512e2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/a49609c4a56c36094710803e98c4be37a422b200/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-14T19:25:58Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-14T19:25:58Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-7e): address Codex review round 3 (P2 + P3 fixes)\n\nTwo findings, both valid:\n\n- **[P2] `Content-Encoding: identity` was incorrectly\n  treated as already-encoded.** Round 2 P2''s\n  initial truthy-check skip (`contains_key`) was a\n  divergence from reference, which does\n  `encoding = res.getHeader(''Content-Encoding'') ||\n  ''identity''; if (encoding !== ''identity'') skip` at\n  `compression/index.js:182-188`. With a user\n  `headers` rule setting `Content-Encoding: identity`,\n  reference compresses normally (overwriting `identity`\n  with the chosen encoder); round-2 irserve skipped\n  and emitted `Content-Encoding: identity` + raw body.\n\n  Fix: refine the gate in `maybe_apply` to compare\n  against the literal `identity` string (case-\n  sensitive, mirroring JS strict equality):\n  ```rust\n  let existing = parts.headers.get(CONTENT_ENCODING).and_then(|v| v.to_str().ok());\n  if let Some(value) = existing {\n      if value != \"identity\" {\n          return Response::from_parts(parts, body);\n      }\n  }\n  ```\n  New unit test\n  `maybe_apply_existing_identity_falls_through_and_compresses`\n  pins the round-trip — user-set `identity` is\n  ignored by the passthrough gate, the body is\n  encoded, and `Content-Encoding` is overwritten to\n  `br`. Renamed the existing test\n  `maybe_apply_existing_content_encoding_passthrough`\n  to\n  `maybe_apply_existing_non_identity_content_encoding_passthrough`\n  for symmetry.\n\n  Locked dual-target via two new raw probes in\n  `compression-raw.json`:\n  - `user_ce_identity_above_threshold` — user-set\n    `identity` → reference and irserve both compress\n    (Content-Encoding: br, body brotli-encoded).\n    `bodyMayDiffer` per D-020 #4.\n  - `user_ce_br_above_threshold` — user-set `br` →\n    reference and irserve both skip (Content-Encoding:\n    br preserved, body served raw — Content-Length\n    matches the raw fixture size). Body must-match\n    (no compression on either side).\n  Added ORC-211 and ORC-212 to `oracle-matrix.md`.\n  Re-snapped the reference (case file now 22\n  anchors).\n\n- **[P3] Stale doc references to the old pre-round-1\n  architecture outside OpenSpec.**\n  - `docs/stage7_l3_capabilities.md` row 7e: rewrote\n    to reflect the centralized `server::handler` seam\n    (vs the original `build_file_or_304` slice-2\n    wiring) plus the Codex round 1 / 2 / 3\n    evolution. Bumped `brotli` version `\"7\"` → `\"8\"`\n    (was a transcription error in the meta slice).\n    Bumped \"20 anchors\" → \"22 anchors\" (new round-3\n    additions).\n  - `docs/reference/serve/oracle-matrix.md` ORC-206:\n    rewrote to say \"206 DOES enter `maybe_apply`,\n    gets `Vary` set, then short-circuits on\n    `PARTIAL_CONTENT`\" (vs the stale \"206 never\n    enters maybe_apply\"). Mirrors the reference''s\n    middleware ordering: `vary()` runs before any\n    status / threshold filter.\n  - `docs/reference/serve/inventory.md` SRV-CLI-012:\n    bumped anchor counts (20 → 22) with a note that\n    the +2 came from round 3 P2.\n  - `openspec/specs/http-compression/spec.md` and the\n    change-package delta: refreshed the\n    Implementation step 7 (`existing_encoding !=\n    None && existing_encoding != Some(\"identity\")`),\n    refreshed the Compatibility note on\n    already-encoded passthrough to the case-sensitive\n    identity-comparison rule, and added the two new\n    anchor names to the dual-target evidence.\n  - `openspec/changes/015-compression/proposal.md`:\n    refreshed out-of-scope #8 with the round 3\n    refinement.\n\nVerification:\n\n- `cargo test --workspace --lib` — 361 passed (was 360;\n  one new unit test for identity-fall-through).\n- `cargo test --test oracle` — 81 passed / 2 skipped\n  / 0 failed (unchanged at case-file level; the 2 new\n  anchors land inside the existing `compression-raw`\n  case).\n- `npx @fission-ai/openspec validate --all --strict`\n  — 26 passed / 0 failed.\n- Manual smoke: with `serve.json` setting\n  `Content-Encoding: identity` via a `headers` rule,\n  irserve responds with `content-encoding: br`,\n  `vary: Accept-Encoding`, `content-length: 111`\n  (compressed from a 2226-byte raw fixture).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2829ddbfe0e99d2cf7d7c94510afd0095e45f436","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/2829ddbfe0e99d2cf7d7c94510afd0095e45f436"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/a49609c4a56c36094710803e98c4be37a422b200","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/a49609c4a56c36094710803e98c4be37a422b200","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKGE0OTYwOWM0YTU2YzM2MDk0NzEwODAzZTk4YzRiZTM3YTQyMmIyMDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/47d7f25dad53657af1b79ea0b64174d4223d180b","sha":"47d7f25dad53657af1b79ea0b64174d4223d180b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/47d7f25dad53657af1b79ea0b64174d4223d180b"}],"sha":"a49609c4a56c36094710803e98c4be37a422b200","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/a49609c4a56c36094710803e98c4be37a422b200"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/47d7f25dad53657af1b79ea0b64174d4223d180b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-14T19:12:57Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-14T19:12:57Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-7e): address Codex review round 2 (P2 + P3 fixes)\n\nThree findings, all valid:\n\n- **[P2] Existing Content-Encoding from user `headers` is not\n  honored.** A user `headers` rule (Stage 6f) can set\n  `Content-Encoding` on the merged response via\n  `apply_custom_headers`; the centralized compression pass\n  previously ignored the existing value and re-encoded the\n  body, overwriting the user''s choice. Reference''s\n  `compression@1.8.1` middleware skips already-encoded\n  responses at `compression/index.js:183-189`. Fix: added a\n  new gate (step 7 in `maybe_apply`''s ordered checks) that\n  short-circuits when `response.headers().contains_key(\n  CONTENT_ENCODING)`. Vary stays set (the check sits AFTER\n  the Vary append in step 4, mirroring the reference''s\n  `vary()` call order at `compression/index.js:174`). Any\n  non-empty string value triggers the skip, including\n  `identity` (JS truthy semantics). New unit test\n  `maybe_apply_existing_content_encoding_passthrough` pins\n  the round-trip — user-set `Content-Encoding: br` survives\n  unchanged, body is NOT re-encoded, `Content-Length` stays\n  at the original byte count.\n\n- **[P2] OpenSpec described the old pre-round-1 architecture.**\n  The canonical `openspec/specs/http-compression/spec.md`\n  still claimed `maybe_apply` was called from\n  `build_file_or_304`, set `Vary` only if missing, and that\n  206 responses NEVER entered the pass. All three are stale\n  — round 1 P2 moved compression to a centralized\n  post-dispatch pass in `server::handler`, switched Vary to\n  append semantics via `append_vary_accept_encoding`, and\n  put the `PARTIAL_CONTENT` short-circuit AFTER the Vary set\n  so 206 anchors carry the negotiation hook. Rewrote the\n  Implementation gate-order list, the Range Requirement, and\n  the Compatibility notes (already-encoded and body-bytes\n  entries) in both `openspec/specs/http-compression/spec.md`\n  and the change-package delta at\n  `openspec/changes/015-compression/specs/http-compression/spec.md`.\n\n- **[P3] Reference docs claimed `bodyMayDiffer` strips\n  `content-encoding`.** Round 1 P1 intentionally separated\n  the overlays — `bodyMayDiffer` strips only body fields +\n  `content-length`; `content-encoding` is stripped only by\n  the explicit per-anchor `contentEncodingMayDiffer`\n  partition. The narrative survived in D-020 #1 and #4\n  (`docs/reference/serve/decisions.md`), in\n  `inventory.md`''s SRV-CLI-012 compatibility note, in\n  ORC-191 (`oracle-matrix.md`), and in\n  `openspec/changes/015-compression/{proposal,design}.md`.\n  Reworded every site to call out the round-1 P1 separation\n  explicitly and to clarify that the 10 compressed anchors\n  in `compression-raw.json` do NOT opt into\n  `contentEncodingMayDiffer` (encoder CHOICE is contractual\n  even though encoder OUTPUT is not).\n\nVerification:\n\n- `cargo test --workspace --lib`: 360 passed (was 359; new\n  unit test for the Content-Encoding passthrough).\n- `cargo test --test oracle`: 81 passed / 2 skipped / 0\n  failed (unchanged; doc / catalogue / one-gate edits don''t\n  shift the contract).\n- `npx @fission-ai/openspec validate --all --strict`: 26\n  passed / 0 failed.\n- Manual smoke: with `serve.json` setting\n  `Content-Encoding: br` via a `headers` rule, irserve\n  responds with `content-encoding: br`, `vary:\n  Accept-Encoding`, and `content-length` matching the raw\n  fixture size (no re-encoding).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1f7fbe9aa8333d3d74301ee55384d4f6104ef377","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/1f7fbe9aa8333d3d74301ee55384d4f6104ef377"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/47d7f25dad53657af1b79ea0b64174d4223d180b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/47d7f25dad53657af1b79ea0b64174d4223d180b","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDQ3ZDdmMjVkYWQ1MzY1N2FmMWI3OWVhMGI2NDE3NGQ0MjIzZDE4MGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/2105a90ae098349c7f8e4a18dff0f1dce7f285ff","sha":"2105a90ae098349c7f8e4a18dff0f1dce7f285ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/2105a90ae098349c7f8e4a18dff0f1dce7f285ff"}],"sha":"47d7f25dad53657af1b79ea0b64174d4223d180b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/47d7f25dad53657af1b79ea0b64174d4223d180b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/2105a90ae098349c7f8e4a18dff0f1dce7f285ff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-14T17:25:01Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-14T17:25:01Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-7e): address Codex review round 1 (P1 + P2 + P3 fixes)\n\nFour findings, all valid:\n\n- **[P3] OpenSpec validation red.** First Requirement in\n  `openspec/specs/http-compression/spec.md` led with\n  `When the server is run without ...,` so the validator\n  read only that fragment and flagged \"must contain SHALL\n  or MUST\" despite the wrapped next line carrying `SHALL`.\n  Reshaped to `The server SHALL ... when ...`. Same edit\n  in the change-package delta. `npx @fission-ai/openspec\n  validate --all --strict` now: 26 passed / 0 failed.\n\n- **[P2] Vary append.** Reference''s `vary()` utility\n  appends `Accept-Encoding` to any existing `Vary` header;\n  the initial slice-2 implementation only inserted when\n  missing, which is cache-incorrect when a user `headers`\n  rule already set e.g. `Vary: Cookie` (downstream caches\n  would key only on Cookie and serve a brotli body to\n  identity clients). New `append_vary_accept_encoding`\n  in `crates/irserve-core/src/compression.rs`: appends\n  to existing Vary, dedupes `Accept-Encoding`\n  case-insensitively, leaves `Vary: *` alone. Three new\n  unit tests cover the append / dedup / wildcard paths.\n  The old `maybe_apply_existing_vary_preserved` test\n  was retired (its assertion locked in the wrong\n  behavior).\n\n- **[P2] Compression seam widened to listings and\n  errors.** Initial slice-2 wired\n  `compression::maybe_apply` inside\n  `build_file_or_304` so directory-listing and error\n  responses bypassed compression — the reference''s\n  middleware fires on every response. Moved to a\n  centralized post-dispatch pass in\n  `crates/irserve-core/src/server.rs::handler` between\n  `apply_cors` and the request log. The pass is async\n  (consumes the response body via\n  `axum::body::to_bytes`); Range pre-emption stays via\n  an explicit `StatusCode::PARTIAL_CONTENT`\n  short-circuit AFTER Vary is set, so 206 responses\n  carry the negotiation hook without re-encoding the\n  sliced body. Reverted the `req_method` parameter\n  previously threaded through `build_file_or_304` and\n  its 36 test callsites — back to the pre-7e shape.\n\n- **[P1] Oracle assertions tightened.** Two seams were\n  masking the main compression contract:\n  - `''vary''` was in `L0_EXTRA_VOLATILE_HEADERS`\n    (stripped on every L0 comparison) so the Vary\n    must-match invariant was invisible across all\n    probes. Dropped from the global mask now that the\n    centralized seam fix above makes irserve emit Vary\n    everywhere the reference does.\n  - `bodyMayDiffer` overlay also stripped\n    `content-encoding`. The compression-raw probe\n    marks 10 compressed anchors as `bodyMayDiffer`\n    because their body bytes differ at the bit level\n    per D-020 #4 — but the compression DECISION (which\n    encoder is picked, whether Content-Encoding is\n    emitted) is contractual. Stripping\n    content-encoding from bodyMayDiffer let those\n    anchors pass even when irserve emitted no\n    Content-Encoding at all. Reverted; bodyMayDiffer\n    is body-only again.\n  - Added a new `contentEncodingMayDiffer` partition\n    to the runner + the case schema for the narrower\n    scenario \"the body content is implementation-\n    defined per D-002 / D-003 so the compression\n    decision is too\" (4xx error pages, directory\n    listings — reference emits a 1.6 KiB HTML body\n    that crosses the threshold and gets compressed;\n    irserve emits a 23-byte `<h1>` line that stays\n    below threshold). 20 legacy probes got\n    `contentEncodingMayDiffer` mirroring their\n    `bodyMayDiffer`.\n\nCatalogue updates:\n\n- `openspec/changes/015-compression/proposal.md`: out-of-\n  scope #5 rewritten (Vary is now appended).\n- `openspec/changes/015-compression/design.md`: §4\n  rewritten (centralized handler seam, not the\n  in-dispatcher build_file_or_304 site); negotiation\n  algorithm gate ordering updated (206 short-circuits\n  AFTER Vary).\n- `openspec/changes/015-compression/tasks.md`: appended a\n  \"Codex review round 1\" section.\n- `openspec/specs/http-compression/spec.md` + the\n  change-package delta: Compatibility note on Vary\n  rewritten to reflect append semantics.\n\nVerification:\n\n- `cargo test --workspace --lib` — 359 passed (was 356;\n  three new unit tests for append / dedup / wildcard).\n- `cargo test --test oracle` — 81 passed / 2 skipped /\n  0 failed (unchanged total; tighter assertions).\n- `npx @fission-ai/openspec validate --all --strict` —\n  26 passed / 0 failed.\n- Manual smoke: `Vary: Cookie` + `Accept-Encoding: br`\n  → response carries `vary: Cookie, Accept-Encoding`\n  and `content-encoding: br`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"072ca71f09fdeb2852f2b53f8a4ab01c70b1e0b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/072ca71f09fdeb2852f2b53f8a4ab01c70b1e0b8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/2105a90ae098349c7f8e4a18dff0f1dce7f285ff","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/2105a90ae098349c7f8e4a18dff0f1dce7f285ff","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDIxMDVhOTBhZTA5ODM0OWM3ZjhlNGExOGRmZjBmMWRjZTdmMjg1ZmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/5b73ce24cb09f0eeffc54b9e3361158e54d23962","sha":"5b73ce24cb09f0eeffc54b9e3361158e54d23962","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/5b73ce24cb09f0eeffc54b9e3361158e54d23962"}],"sha":"2105a90ae098349c7f8e4a18dff0f1dce7f285ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/2105a90ae098349c7f8e4a18dff0f1dce7f285ff"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/5b73ce24cb09f0eeffc54b9e3361158e54d23962/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-14T16:59:43Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-14T16:59:43Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-7e): add 015-compression change package + spec deltas\n\nSlice 4 of Stage 7e. Pure prose / spec / catalogue — no code touched.\n\nNew change package `openspec/changes/015-compression/`:\n\n- proposal.md: Why (closes SRV-CLI-012 + Q-002; transitions D-006\n  from `adapted` to implemented; adds D-020) / What (slice 0 / 2 /\n  4 narrative) / Out of scope (D-020''s four divergences + five\n  inherited non-divergences) / Risks (anti-hallucination #9 declared\n  parity scope, body-bytes drift, Stage 7d composition, encoder\n  defaults drift). Mirrors 7d''s voice.\n- design.md: §1 Reference behavior (verbatim `server.ts:8,25,71-72`\n  + slice 0 empirical anchors) / §2 Negotiation algorithm /\n  §3 MIME filter (D2) / §4 Dispatcher seam / §5 Probe-runner\n  adaptations / §6 D-020 inline summary / §7 Why this stage shape\n  (D1 / D2 / D3 fork rationale).\n- tasks.md: slice-by-slice `[x]` per the 7c / 7d convention.\n- specs/cli/spec.md (MODIFIED): ADDED Requirements entry for\n  SRV-CLI-012. Style mirrors the SRV-CLI-010 (`--cors`) entry\n  (flag-presence + capability-spec pointer).\n- specs/http-compression/spec.md (ADDED): new capability. Covers\n  encoder set + preference, threshold, MIME filter, Vary semantics,\n  skip conditions, Range pre-emption; Compatibility notes enumerate\n  D-020 + the five inherited non-divergences.\n\nMirrored as a canonical capability spec at\n`openspec/specs/http-compression/spec.md`.\n\nCatalogue updates:\n\n- `docs/reference/serve/decisions.md`: appended D-020 (date\n  2026-05-14, status adapted, four enumerated divergences —\n  framing, mime-db, q-rank within (0, 1), compressed body bytes).\n  D-006 stays as historical record. Notes that D-020 supersedes\n  D-006''s deferral rationale.\n- `docs/reference/serve/inventory.md`: SRV-CLI-012 entry — struck\n  the Q-002 open-question reference (closed), flipped the \"MAY\n  ship without compression\" hedge to past tense, cites D-020.\n  Status stays `verified`.\n- `docs/reference/serve/oracle-matrix.md`: flipped ORC-058 to\n  dual-target with the \"Promoted in Stage 7e slice 2\" annotation;\n  appended ORC-191..ORC-210 (20 new rows — one per\n  compression-raw anchor, ordered by MIME-allowlist /\n  per-encoder / non-compressible / skip-conditions /\n  negotiation-corners).\n- `README.md`: added the 7e-done line to the status list, flipped\n  the 7e stage-map row from `todo` to `done`, added a compression\n  demo block in \"Try IrServe\" (br / gzip negotiation + --no-compression\n  skip), and trimmed `gzip compression` from the \"What is NOT yet\n  observable\" list (now reads \"still deferred to L4: symlink\n  resolution, TLS\").\n- `docs/stage7_l3_capabilities.md`: 7e table row rewritten to\n  past-tense DONE with slice 0 / slice 2 / slice 4 commit citations\n  and the empirical anchors enumerated.\n\nOracle harness unchanged: 81 passed / 2 skipped / 0 failed\n(slice 4 is prose-only).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cbe625d676157bf93ca3e4215d1815ec7bf3c07a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/cbe625d676157bf93ca3e4215d1815ec7bf3c07a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/5b73ce24cb09f0eeffc54b9e3361158e54d23962","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/5b73ce24cb09f0eeffc54b9e3361158e54d23962","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDViNzNjZTI0Y2IwOWYwZWVmZmM1NGI5ZTMzNjExNThlNTRkMjM5NjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/d1b9a15544cc09f5a29f883c483a8b3fcad25dba","sha":"d1b9a15544cc09f5a29f883c483a8b3fcad25dba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/d1b9a15544cc09f5a29f883c483a8b3fcad25dba"}],"sha":"5b73ce24cb09f0eeffc54b9e3361158e54d23962","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/5b73ce24cb09f0eeffc54b9e3361158e54d23962"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/d1b9a15544cc09f5a29f883c483a8b3fcad25dba/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-14T16:42:07Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-14T16:42:07Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"feat(stage-7e): implement HTTP compression (SRV-CLI-012)\n\nSlice 2 of Stage 7e. Lands the irserve compression module and wires\nit into the static-file pipeline, closes SRV-CLI-012 (`-u` /\n`--no-compression`), and flips ORC-058 + the compression-raw probe\nfrom reference-only to dual-target.\n\nRust crates:\n\n- `crates/irserve-core/src/compression.rs` (new): negotiation +\n  encoder + MIME-allowlist gate, mirroring `compression@1.8.1`''s\n  surface as pinned in `tools/probe/snapshots/compression-raw.json`.\n  - Preference order: brotli > gzip > deflate (per\n    `compression/index.js:44-45` when Node has brotli support).\n  - Threshold: 1024 bytes (reference default).\n  - MIME compressible: curated allowlist (`text/*`, `application/json`,\n    `application/javascript`, `application/wasm`, `image/svg+xml`)\n    + regex fallback `^text/|\\+(?:json|text|xml)$` per\n    `compressible/index.js:23`. The full `mime-db` table is NOT\n    ported — out of scope per D-020.\n  - Vary: Accept-Encoding always set when compressible MIME passes\n    the no-transform gate, including the HEAD / below-threshold /\n    identity-only / all-q-zero skip paths (mirrors reference).\n  - Skips: HEAD (vary kept, body emptied by axum/hyper),\n    `Cache-Control: no-transform`, body below threshold,\n    `Accept-Encoding: identity`-only, `*;q=0` wildcard rejection.\n  - 18 unit tests cover negotiation corners (q=0, wildcard, missing\n    header, preference order), MIME-filter decisions, and the\n    `maybe_apply` skip / compress paths.\n- `crates/irserve-core/src/dispatch.rs`: integrate\n  `compression::maybe_apply` in `build_file_or_304` between\n  `apply_custom_headers` and the no-Range return path. Range\n  pre-empts compression (the `let Some(range_value)` tail bypasses\n  the call), mirroring reference. Threads `req.method()` through\n  so HEAD can be detected. Tests fix to pass `&Method::GET`.\n- `crates/irserve-core/src/config.rs`: add `compression: Option<bool>`\n  to `ServeConfig`, marked `#[serde(skip)]` so it''s not part of the\n  `serve.json` schema — the reference exposes the flag only on the\n  CLI.\n- `crates/irserve/src/main.rs`: wire `-u`/`--no-compression` to\n  `serve_config.compression = Some(false)`. Mirrors the\n  `--no-etag` plumbing from Stage 7b.\n- `crates/irserve-core/Cargo.toml`: add `flate2 = \"1\"` and\n  `brotli = \"8\"`.\n\nProbe runner + cases:\n\n- `tools/probe/run.mjs`: drop `content-encoding` from\n  `L0_EXTRA_VOLATILE_HEADERS` (the slice-0 temporary mask is no\n  longer needed now that irserve emits compression). Extend the\n  `bodyMayDiffer` overlay to ALSO strip `content-encoding` per\n  anchor — when a body''s content is may-differ (custom error pages\n  per D-002 / D-003), the compression outcome is necessarily\n  may-differ too, since the compression decision is a function of\n  body length vs threshold.\n- `tools/probe/cases/compression-raw.json`: add `runner.l0.clean`\n  covering all 20 anchors plus `bodyMayDiffer` on the 10 compressed\n  anchors (their body bytes differ between Node zlib/brotli and\n  Rust `flate2` / `brotli` crates at their respective defaults —\n  D-020).\n- `tools/probe/cases/compression-default.json`: add\n  `runner.l0.clean: [\"with_accept_encoding\"]` so the legacy single-\n  anchor probe becomes dual-target.\n\nResult: oracle harness now reports 81 passed / 2 skipped / 0 failed\n(was 79 / 3 / 0 at end of Stage 7d). Manual smoke confirms wire-\nlevel br/gzip/deflate negotiation, q=0 exclusion, identity / no-\naccept-encoding skipping, and `--no-compression` flag flipping.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ed17bb2dd12c1440cd174333e5693214b5e2fbfe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/ed17bb2dd12c1440cd174333e5693214b5e2fbfe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/d1b9a15544cc09f5a29f883c483a8b3fcad25dba","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/d1b9a15544cc09f5a29f883c483a8b3fcad25dba","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKGQxYjlhMTU1NDRjYzA5ZjVhMjlmODgzYzQ4M2E4YjNmY2FkMjVkYmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/9bd52f0916ba59754956aa97402ccc7b07a1db4a","sha":"9bd52f0916ba59754956aa97402ccc7b07a1db4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/9bd52f0916ba59754956aa97402ccc7b07a1db4a"}],"sha":"d1b9a15544cc09f5a29f883c483a8b3fcad25dba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/d1b9a15544cc09f5a29f883c483a8b3fcad25dba"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/9bd52f0916ba59754956aa97402ccc7b07a1db4a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-14T16:27:58Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-14T16:27:58Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"probe(stage-7e): pin reference compression surface (Q-002 closure)\n\nSlice 0 of Stage 7e (HTTP compression). Pure reference reconnaissance —\nno irserve code yet, only probe-runner extension + new raw-socket probe\n+ Q-002 resolution.\n\nChanges:\n\n- tools/probe/run.mjs: add `content-encoding` to TRACKED_RESPONSE_HEADERS\n  so the reference''s wire-level compression behavior is observable.\n  L0_EXTRA_VOLATILE_HEADERS gains `content-encoding` as a temporary\n  blanket mask until slice 2 lands the irserve implementation\n  (otherwise every probe whose reference response is > 1024 bytes of\n  compressible MIME would now diverge against irserve''s\n  no-compression L0 state).\n- tools/probe/cases/compression-raw.json (new) — 20 raw-socket anchors\n  covering threshold, encoder preference (br > gzip > deflate),\n  q=0 / wildcard q=0 exclusions, identity-only, MIME allowlist\n  (text/html, text/css, application/javascript, application/json,\n  application/wasm, image/svg+xml) vs non-compressible\n  (image/png, font/woff2, video/mp4), HEAD / OPTIONS / no-transform\n  skip conditions, and Range pre-emption.\n- tools/probe/snapshots/compression-raw.json (new) — reference\n  snapshot pinning the empirical behavior. Case has no `runner.l0`\n  block, so it''s reference-only until slice 2 promotes it.\n- 21 existing reference snapshots re-recorded: the `content-encoding`\n  addition surfaced `content-encoding: gzip` on every 4xx error page\n  (1.6 KiB HTML > 1024-byte threshold) and a few other compressible\n  responses the runner was previously silently stripping. Pure\n  fidelity improvement, no behavior change.\n- docs/reference/serve/open-questions.md: close Q-002 with the\n  empirically-determined threshold (1024 B), encoder preference\n  (br > gzip > deflate), compressible MIME set, and skip conditions.\n\nEmpirical surprises captured:\n\n- `Vary: Accept-Encoding` is set IFF content-type is compressible\n  (mime-db lookup or regex fallback). Non-compressible MIMEs exit\n  before vary() so PNG / WOFF2 / MP4 responses carry no Vary.\n- `Cache-Control: no-transform` skips compression AND Vary (the\n  middleware''s shouldTransform check fires before vary()).\n- HEAD requests keep Vary and the ORIGINAL Content-Length, body\n  empty.\n- OPTIONS routes through GET (Stage 7d composition) so OPTIONS\n  responses ARE compressed.\n- Range pre-empts compression — 206 with raw body slice and\n  Content-Range, Vary still set.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ba0a7a9911c7ea93f863e34ba50dede7fc44da03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/ba0a7a9911c7ea93f863e34ba50dede7fc44da03"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/9bd52f0916ba59754956aa97402ccc7b07a1db4a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/9bd52f0916ba59754956aa97402ccc7b07a1db4a","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDliZDUyZjA5MTZiYTU5NzU0OTU2YWE5NzQwMmNjYzdiMDdhMWRiNGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/66b35c07c9927a5b2ac6fa56bd835318188988a3","sha":"66b35c07c9927a5b2ac6fa56bd835318188988a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/66b35c07c9927a5b2ac6fa56bd835318188988a3"}],"sha":"9bd52f0916ba59754956aa97402ccc7b07a1db4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/9bd52f0916ba59754956aa97402ccc7b07a1db4a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/66b35c07c9927a5b2ac6fa56bd835318188988a3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-14T16:08:26Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-14T16:08:26Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-7e): plan for HTTP compression (-u/--no-compression)\n\nProbe-first slice 0 against the `compression@1.8.1` middleware vendored\nin third_party/serve; full gzip+deflate+brotli parity with the reference\npreference order; curated MIME allowlist + compressible regex fallback.\nAnticipated D-020 covers Content-Length-vs-chunked framing and the\nmime-db port omission.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f82c210d5aa82b5417d744f45c8572f77f860a84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/f82c210d5aa82b5417d744f45c8572f77f860a84"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/66b35c07c9927a5b2ac6fa56bd835318188988a3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/66b35c07c9927a5b2ac6fa56bd835318188988a3","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDY2YjM1YzA3Yzk5MjdhNWIyYWM2ZmE1NmJkODM1MzE4MTg4OTg4YTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/073a6e749633d590f10122d12786e01001516721","sha":"073a6e749633d590f10122d12786e01001516721","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/073a6e749633d590f10122d12786e01001516721"}],"sha":"66b35c07c9927a5b2ac6fa56bd835318188988a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/66b35c07c9927a5b2ac6fa56bd835318188988a3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/073a6e749633d590f10122d12786e01001516721/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-14T15:42:08Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-14T15:42:08Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-7d): address Codex review round 2 (P3 fixes)\n\n**P3 (stale `Accept-Ranges` in change-package prose).**\nAfter round 1 removed `Accept-Ranges: bytes` from the cors\nspec Requirement bodies and the OPTIONS Scenario, two prose\nmentions still incorrectly listed it among the headers\nirserve emits on a `200 OK` OPTIONS response:\n\n- `proposal.md:55` claimed the irserve-side OPTIONS response\n  yields \"200 OK with the file body + the four CORS headers\n  + ETag + Content-Type + Accept-Ranges.\"\n- `tasks.md:55` similarly described the verify-step output\n  as \"200 + file body + four CORS headers + ETag +\n  Content-Type + Accept-Ranges.\"\n\nBoth are wrong: irserve does NOT emit `Accept-Ranges`\n(`file_response` at `dispatch.rs` only sets Content-Type,\nETag, Last-Modified) and the probe runner explicitly masks\nthe header via `L0_EXTRA_VOLATILE_HEADERS` at\n`tools/probe/run.mjs:41`. The reference snapshot does\ncontain `Accept-Ranges: bytes` (per the verbatim\n`defaultHeaders` block at `serve-handler/src/index.js:219`,\nwhich the round-1 design.md and the new http-cache delta\nboth correctly quote), but it is non-contractual under\ndual-target verification.\n\nRewrite the two prose spots to drop `+ Accept-Ranges` from\nthe irserve-side listing and add a parenthesised note that\nthe header appears in the reference snapshot only, masked\nby the runner. Other `Accept-Ranges` mentions in `design.md`\n(L170, L203, L294) and `specs/http-cache/spec.md` (L51) are\ncorrectly scoped to reference-source citations and are not\nmodified.\n\nValidation green: `npx -y @fission-ai/openspec@latest\nvalidate --all --strict --concurrency 12` reports 24 passed,\n0 failed. No Rust changes; no test runs affected.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"43d4ddd2baeb19d30d4cd457a5861ea320e78619","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/43d4ddd2baeb19d30d4cd457a5861ea320e78619"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/073a6e749633d590f10122d12786e01001516721","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/073a6e749633d590f10122d12786e01001516721","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDA3M2E2ZTc0OTYzM2Q1OTBmMTAxMjJkMTI3ODZlMDEwMDE1MTY3MjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/fa659b388a054d90bd943f95e5ed724989399091","sha":"fa659b388a054d90bd943f95e5ed724989399091","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/fa659b388a054d90bd943f95e5ed724989399091"}],"sha":"073a6e749633d590f10122d12786e01001516721","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/073a6e749633d590f10122d12786e01001516721"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/fa659b388a054d90bd943f95e5ed724989399091/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-14T15:31:38Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-14T15:31:38Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-7d): address Codex review round 1 (P1 + P2 fixes)\n\n**P1 (OpenSpec validation green).** Two issues flagged by\n`npx -y @fission-ai/openspec@latest validate --all --strict`:\n\n- `change/014-cache-headers-and-preflight`: the\n  `specs/cors/spec.md` was authored as a full spec (with\n  `## Purpose` / `## Requirements` / `## Compatibility\n  notes`) rather than as an `## ADDED Requirements` delta.\n  Rewrite the change-package delta to contain only\n  `# Delta for cors` + `## ADDED Requirements` + the two\n  Requirement bodies (with Scenarios). The full-spec prose\n  stays in the canonical `openspec/specs/cors/spec.md`.\n- `spec/cors`: Requirement #0''s body wrapped before `SHALL`\n  (line 1 was \"When the server is started with the `-C` /\n  `--cors` CLI\", SHALL on line 2). Validator parses the\n  first body line for the SHALL/MUST keyword. Reword to\n  \"Every response under `-C` / `--cors` SHALL carry the\n  following four headers:\" so SHALL lands on line 1.\n- Tasks.md: mark the validation checkbox `[x]` with a note\n  on what round 1 fixed.\n\nValidator now reports `Totals: 24 passed, 0 failed`.\n\n**P1 (Accept-Ranges falsehood removed).** Both versions of\nthe cors spec (delta + canonical) asserted\n`AND the response carries Accept-Ranges: bytes` on the\nOPTIONS scenario, but irserve does NOT emit `Accept-Ranges`\non file responses — `file_response` in `dispatch.rs` only\nsets `Content-Type`, `ETag`/`Last-Modified`, and the probe\nrunner explicitly masks `accept-ranges` via\n`L0_EXTRA_VOLATILE_HEADERS` (`tools/probe/run.mjs:41`). ORC-\n044 records the same non-emission. Strip the header from the\nRequirement body and from the OPTIONS Scenario. Promoting\n`Accept-Ranges` to a real contract would require a separate\nchange (emission code + ORC reclassification + probe\npartition).\n\n**P2 (phantom `Access-Control-Allow-Methods` claim).**\n`design.md` §1 quoted a fabricated `Access-Control-Allow-Methods:\nGET, POST, PUT, DELETE, PATCH, OPTIONS` `setHeader` line as\n\"verbatim\" from `third_party/serve/source/utilities/server.ts:65-70`.\nThe actual pinned source sets exactly four headers there\n(verified at `server.ts:65-70`). The cors spec compatibility\nnotes repeated the same falsehood. Rewrite the design block\nto quote the four actual `setHeader` lines verbatim. Rewrite\nthe cors Compatibility note to state simply: \"The reference''s\n`--cors` block at `server.ts:65-70` contains only the four\n`setHeader` calls catalogued above\" without inventing\ndivergence.\n\n**P2 (OPTIONS spec narrowed to verified surface).** The\nprevious Requirement body asserted SHALL clauses for missing-\npath 404, 304 short-circuit, and Range 206/416 under OPTIONS,\nand one Scenario pinned `OPTIONS /no-such-file -> 404` — but\nonly `cors-preflight#preflight_options` (existing file) is\nactually probed at L0. Demote the derivative behaviors from\nprescriptive SHALL bullets to descriptive prose: \"Because\nOPTIONS walks the same pipeline as GET, all downstream\nbehaviors apply identically. Those derivative behaviors are\nNOT separately pinned by Stage 7d; the contractual surface in\n7d is the pipeline routing observable via the cors-preflight\nprobe.\" Drop the missing-path Scenario. The single remaining\nOPTIONS Scenario (existing file under `--cors`) is what\nORC-056 pins. Add a Compatibility note pointing future stages\nat the right place to add probe anchors\n(`preflight_on_missing`, `preflight_with_inm`,\n`preflight_with_range`) if they want to pin OPTIONS-specific\nedge cases.\n\nRegression: `cargo test --test oracle` green (79 passed, 3\nskipped, 0 failed); no Rust changes in this round.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e6276cc7d7bb2d7a90462cf70fa8c0a1c2b334df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/e6276cc7d7bb2d7a90462cf70fa8c0a1c2b334df"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/fa659b388a054d90bd943f95e5ed724989399091","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/fa659b388a054d90bd943f95e5ed724989399091","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKGZhNjU5YjM4OGEwNTRkOTBiZDk0M2Y5NWU1ZWQ3MjQ5ODkzOTkwOTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/3baedf5e36341f06fd1e773148d8f2176432dbed","sha":"3baedf5e36341f06fd1e773148d8f2176432dbed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/3baedf5e36341f06fd1e773148d8f2176432dbed"}],"sha":"fa659b388a054d90bd943f95e5ed724989399091","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/fa659b388a054d90bd943f95e5ed724989399091"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/3baedf5e36341f06fd1e773148d8f2176432dbed/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-14T14:05:12Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-14T14:05:12Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-7d): spec deltas + cors capability + meta\n\nAuthor the change package\n`openspec/changes/014-cache-headers-and-preflight/`:\n\n- `proposal.md` — closes SRV-CACHE-005 (verification-only,\n  no Rust change since 6f) and SRV-CORS-001 (OPTIONS routing\n  added in slice 1); out-of-scope covers HEAD body\n  suppression, other HTTP methods at 405, the three\n  not-emitted CORS headers, Stage 7e compression, and\n  default Cache-Control emission.\n- `design.md` — §1 OPTIONS routing as GET (verbatim reference\n  proof points at `serve-handler/src/index.js:548-769`, CLI\n  at `server.ts:42-93`, irserve seam at `dispatch.rs:91-108`\n  before/after); §2 Cache-Control absence-of-default\n  (verbatim `getHeaders` block at `index.js:194-254` with\n  the no-default observation); §3 why no D-NNN.\n- `tasks.md` — slice plan with `[x]` for slices 0/1/2/3.\n- `specs/http-cache/spec.md` — MODIFIED delta adding the\n  Cache-Control absence-of-default Requirement (6 Scenarios,\n  one per probe anchor).\n- `specs/cors/spec.md` — ADDED capability spec with two\n  Requirements (four-header surface + OPTIONS routing),\n  5 Scenarios, and 7 Compatibility notes.\n\nMirror the deltas into the live tree:\n\n- `openspec/specs/http-cache/spec.md` — update Purpose to\n  past-tense for 7d, append the Cache-Control Requirement\n  with all 6 Scenarios before `## Compatibility notes`.\n- `openspec/specs/cors/spec.md` — new live capability spec,\n  identical to the change-package delta.\n\nInventory update at `docs/reference/serve/inventory.md` —\nstrike the SRV-CORS-001 open question (\"adopt or diverge\nfrom no-preflight-short-circuit\"); resolved to **adopt** in\nStage 7d slice 1 (commit `381f9bd`). Compatibility note on\nthe same SRV entry rewritten to reflect the live behavior.\n\nREADME updates: flip the Stage 7d status bullet (Status\nsection) and stage map row to `done`; trim the \"What is NOT\nyet observable\" footer to drop default `Cache-Control` and\nCORS preflight (both now observable / dual-target); add two\ncurl examples to \"Try IrServe\" — an OPTIONS preflight under\n`--cors` (200 + body + four CORS headers, no 204\nshort-circuit) and a Cache-Control absence check.\n\nNo D-NNN entry. Mirror semantics across both SRVs (same\nshape as Stage 7c). Slice 2 audit collapsed to no-op because\nthe other four `cors-*` probes already carried L0-clean\npartitions. Last D-NNN stays at D-018 (Stage 7b).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cb5218a438431814f476c46ff17106172b37ebc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/cb5218a438431814f476c46ff17106172b37ebc3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/3baedf5e36341f06fd1e773148d8f2176432dbed","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/3baedf5e36341f06fd1e773148d8f2176432dbed","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDNiYWVkZjVlMzYzNDFmMDZmZDFlNzczMTQ4ZDhmMjE3NjQzMmRiZWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/381f9bd716c4922b1b89059f31b76306cb0ce21b","sha":"381f9bd716c4922b1b89059f31b76306cb0ce21b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/381f9bd716c4922b1b89059f31b76306cb0ce21b"}],"sha":"3baedf5e36341f06fd1e773148d8f2176432dbed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/3baedf5e36341f06fd1e773148d8f2176432dbed"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/381f9bd716c4922b1b89059f31b76306cb0ce21b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-14T13:53:20Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-14T13:53:20Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"feat(stage-7d): route OPTIONS through the static pipeline (SRV-CORS-001)\n\nAllow OPTIONS through the dispatcher''s method gate alongside\nGET/HEAD. Mirrors the reference: `serve-handler/src/index.js`\nnever inspects `request.method`, so an `OPTIONS /asset.css` under\n`--cors` walks phases 3..13 and yields 200 + file body + the four\n`access-control-*` headers applied post-dispatch by `apply_cors`\n(Stage 6h). Pinned by `tools/probe/snapshots/cors-preflight.json`\n(7-byte `body{}\\n`, ETag, content-type, accept-ranges, and the\nfour CORS headers).\n\nSide-effects (mirroring reference, not additional code):\n- An OPTIONS with a matching `If-None-Match` short-circuits to 304\n  through the same `build_file_or_304` path GET uses — reference''s\n  304 check at `serve-handler/src/index.js:760` does not gate on\n  method either.\n- A Range-bearing OPTIONS yields 206/416 via the existing 7c path.\n\nNo D-NNN: mirror semantics, not adaptation. SRV-CORS-001''s prior\nopen question (\"adopt or diverge from no-preflight-short-circuit\")\nis settled by this commit — adopt.\n\nProbe verification: `cors-preflight` green dual-target\n(`runner.l0.clean: [\"preflight_options\"]`); full oracle harness\n(`cargo test --test oracle`) green with 79/82 passing, 0 failed,\nno regressions. ORC-056 promoted to dual-target in\n`oracle-matrix.md` with the Stage 7d slice 1 note.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fc26d22deccf1fc3ab72923cc1ddc48c02c94b0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/fc26d22deccf1fc3ab72923cc1ddc48c02c94b0d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/381f9bd716c4922b1b89059f31b76306cb0ce21b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/381f9bd716c4922b1b89059f31b76306cb0ce21b","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDM4MWY5YmQ3MTZjNDkyMmIxYjg5MDU5ZjMxYjc2MzA2Y2IwY2UyMWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/47a56f9683b77a2a6db9169ea1347505d5b4b6d7","sha":"47a56f9683b77a2a6db9169ea1347505d5b4b6d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/47a56f9683b77a2a6db9169ea1347505d5b4b6d7"}],"sha":"381f9bd716c4922b1b89059f31b76306cb0ce21b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/381f9bd716c4922b1b89059f31b76306cb0ce21b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/47a56f9683b77a2a6db9169ea1347505d5b4b6d7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-14T13:49:50Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-14T13:49:50Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"probe(stage-7d): promote cache-control-default to dual-target (ORC-047..052)\n\nAdd `runner.l0` partition to `tools/probe/cases/cache-control-default.json`:\nall six anchors (`default_file_no_rule`, `default_listing_html`,\n`default_listing_json`, `default_404_html`, `default_404_json`,\n`rule_applies_cache_control`) listed under `clean`; the four anchors\nwhose body shape is not contractual (listing HTML/JSON, 404 HTML/JSON)\nalso listed under `bodyMayDiffer` per ORC-049''s pre-existing\n\"may-differ: body\" note and D-002 (404 page shape implementation-defined).\n\nVerified empirically: `node tools/probe/run.mjs cache-control-default\n--target=irserve --snapshot=verify` green on all 6 anchors; reference\ntarget unchanged. irserve already emits zero default Cache-Control\n(grep across `crates/` returns no matches); the only `Cache-Control`\nentry point remains the user `headers` rule via `apply_custom_headers`\n(Stage 6f, SRV-HDR-001) — the `rule_applies_cache_control` anchor\nexercises this byte-for-byte.\n\nFlip ORC-047..052 in `docs/reference/serve/oracle-matrix.md` from\nreference-only to dual-target with \"Promoted to dual-target in Stage\n7d slice 0.\" Extend may-differ notes on ORC-050..052 to surface the\nvolatile-body partition (ORC-049 already carried it).\n\nCloses SRV-CACHE-005 contractually under both targets. No Rust\nchanges — verification-only slice.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a63ec67143b532ad53dede8b4786349ce914a793","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/a63ec67143b532ad53dede8b4786349ce914a793"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/47a56f9683b77a2a6db9169ea1347505d5b4b6d7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VX