rl":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/238bd0c49659ff847181bb3a9f2d70d251ca6b51/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-14T13:49:36Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-14T13:49:36Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-7d): add plan file for cache headers + preflight\n\nVerbatim copy of the plan-mode artifact at\n.claude/plans/7d-modular-lagoon.md, dropped under docs/features/\nper the 0001..0017 convention. Will be referenced from the change\npackage and Codex review rounds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d03d17c79828a2a6afb81b0b7095dbe4a2b4ea42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/d03d17c79828a2a6afb81b0b7095dbe4a2b4ea42"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/238bd0c49659ff847181bb3a9f2d70d251ca6b51","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/238bd0c49659ff847181bb3a9f2d70d251ca6b51","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDIzOGJkMGM0OTY1OWZmODQ3MTgxYmIzYTlmMmQ3MGQyNTFjYTZiNTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/572e0ff17c296a81278a30f0e3183ca6dfda77c9","sha":"572e0ff17c296a81278a30f0e3183ca6dfda77c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/572e0ff17c296a81278a30f0e3183ca6dfda77c9"}],"sha":"238bd0c49659ff847181bb3a9f2d70d251ca6b51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/238bd0c49659ff847181bb3a9f2d70d251ca6b51"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/572e0ff17c296a81278a30f0e3183ca6dfda77c9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T19:59:16Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T19:59:16Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-7c): address Codex review round 4 (P3 fixes)\n\nTwo doc-hygiene leftovers from rounds 1-3 — no behavioral change,\nno new tests, no new probes, no new D-NNN.\n\nP3 — Range Requirement intro overstated header ordering as\nuniversally last-write-wins. The opening paragraph in both\ncanonical openspec/specs/http-cache/spec.md and the change\npackage''s specs/http-cache/spec.md still claimed that\n\"range-emitted headers are last-write-wins over user rules,\nmirroring reference''s post-getHeaders injection at\nindex.js:749-752\". That was true for 206 only; round 1 made 416\nfirst-write-wins (user Content-Range rule wins) via\nentry().or_insert_with, and round 3 already documented the\nasymmetry path-by-path in the 206 / 416 response-shape paragraphs\nand in the Compatibility notes. The intro was the last place\nthat universalised the 206 rule. Replaced with neutral wording\nthat defers to the per-path paragraphs below: \"the per-path\nordering rules ... are documented in the 206 and 416\nresponse-shape paragraphs below — the two paths take opposite\nstances on user-rule overrides for those keys, mirroring the\nreference''s asymmetric setHeader / writeHead ordering\".\n\nP3 — Inventory entry for SRV-CACHE-004 was stuck at slice-2\nstate: 8 anchors, ORC-173..177 only, \"mirrors via\nrest.split('','').next()\" wording for multi-range. Rewrote the\nProbe / Oracle / Compatibility-note bullets to reflect the\npost-rounds-1-2-3 reality:\n\n- Probe: 21 anchors (18 clean + 3 divergent), enumerated the\n  three growth batches (slice 0 +5, round 1 +3, round 2 +7,\n  round 3 +3) so the change-history is recoverable from a\n  single read; bodyMayDiffer carve-out for the 404\n  range_on_missing_file anchor mentioned.\n- Oracle: ORC-044/045/046 + ORC-173..ORC-187 (single-range,\n  dual-target) + ORC-188..ORC-190 (multi-range, reference-only\n  per D-019).\n- Requirement (draft) gained a paragraph distinguishing the\n  contract single-range surface from the partially-adapted\n  multi-range surface; cites D-019.\n- Compatibility notes: replaced \"irserve mirrors via\n  rest.split('','').next()\" wording with the explicit D-019\n  \"first-segment-only\" divergence note and a forward-pointer\n  to the divergent probes + ~10 LOC future-close path. Added\n  the round-1 P2 416-user-override and round-1 P1 empty-file\n  contracts as their own bullets so the inventory entry is\n  self-contained.\n\nStatus stays `verified` per the SRV-CACHE-003 precedent: the\ninventory line records \"what the reference does and what\nirserve agrees on\" at the wire; the irserve-side adaptation is\ncaptured in the Requirement and Compatibility notes pointing at\nD-019 (same pattern SRV-CACHE-003 uses to record D-018).\n\nValidation: cargo test --workspace 327 passed (unchanged from\nround 3); cargo test --test oracle green; openspec validate\n--all --strict 22/22 passed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5cd4ce79a1979e5a27b520478f9e9ea8973209d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/5cd4ce79a1979e5a27b520478f9e9ea8973209d2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/572e0ff17c296a81278a30f0e3183ca6dfda77c9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/572e0ff17c296a81278a30f0e3183ca6dfda77c9","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDU3MmUwZmYxN2MyOTZhODEyNzhhMzBmMGUzMTgzY2E2ZGZkYTc3Yzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/279b7b731ee36c675c0efef61a83e7210974da22","sha":"279b7b731ee36c675c0efef61a83e7210974da22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/279b7b731ee36c675c0efef61a83e7210974da22"}],"sha":"572e0ff17c296a81278a30f0e3183ca6dfda77c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/572e0ff17c296a81278a30f0e3183ca6dfda77c9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/279b7b731ee36c675c0efef61a83e7210974da22/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T19:50:44Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T19:50:44Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-7c): address Codex review round 3 (P2 + P3 fixes)\n\nThis is the third consecutive Codex review round landing on the\nsame fine-grained aspect — the `Range` header parser surface.\nAnti-hallucination rule #9 (\"Stop after 3+ consecutive review\nrounds on the same aspect → pause, declare parity scope,\ndocument divergences in BOTH the D-NNN decision AND the spec\ndelta''s Compatibility note, ask the user\") fires here. The user\nchose Option (i) — declare divergence + D-019 — over Option (ii)\nmirror.\n\nP2 — Multi-range comma list. Reference''s range-parser iterates\nALL comma-segments at index.js:42-71 and skips invalid ones via\nthe `continue` at :63; serve-handler then takes `range[0]` from\nthe resulting list of VALID parsed ranges at index.js:724.\nirserve''s parse_range consults only `rest.split('','').next()`\nand returns 416 if that segment alone is invalid, regardless of\nwhether later segments would be valid. Codex pinned three smoke\ncases:\n  - bytes=999-1000,0-3 → reference 206 bytes 0-3/11, irserve 416\n  - bytes=10-1,0-3     → reference 206 bytes 0-3/11, irserve 416\n  - bytes=abc,0-3      → reference 206 bytes 0-3/11, irserve 416\nThis stage''s resolution is \"declare scope, don''t keep mirroring\":\n\n- D-019 (Date: 2026-05-12, Affected: SRV-CACHE-004, Status:\n  adapted) added to docs/reference/serve/decisions.md. Records\n  the full rationale: three rounds running → rule #9 → pause.\n  Lists the three smoke cases as the canonical divergence\n  surface and points at the ~10 LOC future-close path\n  (\"iterate `rest.split('','')`, keep the first `InRange`\n  outcome\") for whoever wants to flip D-019 from `adapted` to\n  `mirrored`.\n\n- Three new probe anchors added to range-request.json under\n  `runner.l0.divergent` (reference-only): `range_multi_first_invalid`,\n  `range_multi_first_unsatisfiable`, `range_multi_first_alpha_only`.\n  Probes pin the reference-side 206 outcome; irserve-side\n  outcome unit-tested separately (3 new tests in range::tests\n  with names ending `_irserve_side` so a future \"mirror\" flip\n  reliably surfaces them for deletion).\n\n- ORC-188/189/190 added to oracle-matrix.md (reference-only,\n  citing D-019).\n\n- `range.rs::parse_range` gains a multi-line comment at the\n  `rest.split('','').next()` site explaining the intentional\n  divergence and pointing at D-019.\n\n- Compatibility notes in both change package and canonical\n  spec rewritten: the parser-grammar bullet on multi-range no\n  longer claims to \"mirror reference''s range[0]\"; a new\n  Compatibility note `Multi-range comma list is\n  first-segment-only (D-019)` documents the divergence.\n\nNo code change to parse_range. The single-range surface stays\nbyte-identical to the reference (rounds 1+2 mirrored every\nparseInt/split/clip/suffix corner); only the multi-range\ncomma-iteration is out-of-parity-scope.\n\nP3 — Doc inconsistency. Round 1 made 416 user `Content-Range`\noverride the default (via `entry().or_insert_with`), but two\ndocs/comments still claimed \"Range-emitted headers are\nlast-write-wins over user rules\" as a universal statement:\n  - range.rs::apply rustdoc (above the function signature)\n  - openspec/specs/http-cache/spec.md Compatibility notes\nBoth rewritten to spell out the 206 vs 416 asymmetry explicitly:\n206 uses `insert` (last-write-wins), 416 uses\n`entry().or_insert_with` (first-write-wins / user rule wins).\nMirrors reference''s setHeader-before-getHeaders ordering for\n416 at index.js:730-732,746,767 vs post-getHeaders injection\nfor 206 at index.js:749-752.\n\nValidation: cargo test --workspace 327 passed (+3 over round\n2 — three irserve-side multi-range tests). cargo test --test\noracle green. node tools/probe/run.mjs range-request green\nunder both targets (21 anchors: 18 clean + 3 divergent +\nrange_on_missing_file bodyMayDiffer carve-out). openspec\nvalidate --all --strict 22/22 passed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cd196a4706c8b0ad936248a202628c6db6bf6192","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/cd196a4706c8b0ad936248a202628c6db6bf6192"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/279b7b731ee36c675c0efef61a83e7210974da22","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/279b7b731ee36c675c0efef61a83e7210974da22","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDI3OWI3YjczMWVlMzZjNjc1YzBlZmVmNjFhODNlNzIxMDk3NGRhMjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/be6c040fe50984240d2f298a6b1af165322c96ad","sha":"be6c040fe50984240d2f298a6b1af165322c96ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/be6c040fe50984240d2f298a6b1af165322c96ad"}],"sha":"279b7b731ee36c675c0efef61a83e7210974da22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/279b7b731ee36c675c0efef61a83e7210974da22"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/be6c040fe50984240d2f298a6b1af165322c96ad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T19:29:35Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T19:29:35Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-7c): address Codex review round 2 (P2 fix)\n\nRound 1 claimed `parse_digit_prefix` mirrors JS `parseInt`, but\nCodex round 2 enumerated five inputs where it doesn''t — and one\nof those revealed that `split_once(''-'')` is the wrong primitive\nfor mirroring `range-parser`''s `arr[i].split(''-'')[0|1]` shape\non double-hyphen inputs. Reading range-parser/index.js verbatim\n(third_party/serve/node_modules/.pnpm/range-parser@1.2.0/...)\nsurfaced two more gaps the original recon missed: `isNaN(start)`\nrepurposes any unparseable start as a suffix-form request\n(so `bytes=abc-3` → 206 bytes 8-10/11, NOT 416), and the\nclip-end-to-size-1 step happens unconditionally BEFORE the\nstart>end / start<0 validation (so any u64-overflowing decimal\nliteral in the end slot is clipped before invalidation).\n\nMirror in full:\n\n- New `parse_int_js` helper replaces `parse_digit_prefix`.\n  Accepts optional `+`/`-` sign, then leading ASCII digits.\n  Parses magnitude via u128 and clamps to i64::MAX so a literal\n  like `184467440737095516160` saturates without panicking.\n  Returns `Option<i64>` (None ≡ JS NaN). Trailing non-digit\n  chars are silently ignored, matching parseInt.\n\n- `parse_range` reshaped to mirror range-parser/index.js:42-71\n  step-for-step: split on `,` (multi-range first-segment only,\n  unchanged from round 1); then split on **every** `-` (NOT\n  `split_once`) and consult positions [0] and [1] only; parseInt\n  both; `isNaN(start)` triggers suffix repurpose\n  (`start = size - end; end = size - 1`); `isNaN(end)` triggers\n  open-end (`end = size - 1`); clip end to `size - 1`\n  unconditionally; invalidate on `start > end` or `start < 0`.\n\n- 7 new range::tests cover sign prefix in start / end / suffix,\n  overflow saturation, double-hyphen→open-end, alpha-start→\n  suffix-repurpose, and the explicit \"suffix>total → 416\"\n  contract that contradicts RFC 7233 §2.1''s \"use entire\n  representation\" suggestion (range-parser doesn''t honor it;\n  irserve mirrors).\n\n- Two existing tests had to change because their previous\n  outcomes were divergent-from-reference, not mirroring:\n  * parse_suffix_larger_than_total_returns_full → renamed to\n    parse_suffix_larger_than_total_is_unsatisfiable. Was based\n    on a misreading of range-parser semantics; the round-1\n    spec wrongly cited RFC 7233 §2.1.\n  * parse_leading_garbage_is_unsatisfiable → renamed to\n    parse_alpha_start_is_treated_as_suffix. Was rejecting\n    `bytes=abc-3` but reference returns 206 via the isNaN(start)\n    suffix repurpose.\n\nProbes: 7 new anchors in range-request.json — sign-prefix in\nstart/end/suffix, overflow-end-clipped, double-hyphen-open-end,\nalpha-start-is-suffix, suffix-larger-than-total-is-416. Anchor\ntotal now 18. ORC-181..187 documented; ORC-180''s prose updated\nto call out the round-2 parser strengthening. Re-recorded\nreference snapshot; irserve verifies green.\n\nCompatibility notes (both change package and canonical spec)\nrewritten: the previous \"leading ASCII-digit prefix\" wording is\nreplaced with a full parseInt-shape description that calls out\nsign handling, saturation, the split(''-'')-not-split_once\ndistinction, and the isNaN(start)→suffix repurpose. The bogus\n\"suffix > total returns full representation\" note is replaced\nwith the accurate \"suffix > total is Unsatisfiable\" note.\n\nValidation: cargo test --workspace 324 passed (+6 over round 1);\ncargo test --test oracle passes (range-request 18/18 anchors\ngreen under both targets); openspec validate --all --strict\n22/22 passed.\n\nNo new D-NNN. The parser is now a more faithful mirror, not an\nintentional divergence.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c388ac9fb3a777f189ba8184f1f82447d288c601","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/c388ac9fb3a777f189ba8184f1f82447d288c601"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/be6c040fe50984240d2f298a6b1af165322c96ad","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/be6c040fe50984240d2f298a6b1af165322c96ad","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKGJlNmMwNDBmZTUwOTg0MjQwZDJmMjk4YTZiMWFmMTY1MzIyYzk2YWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/a9f62b39882df1fca15a6d519ebda692adf46ee4","sha":"a9f62b39882df1fca15a6d519ebda692adf46ee4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/a9f62b39882df1fca15a6d519ebda692adf46ee4"}],"sha":"be6c040fe50984240d2f298a6b1af165322c96ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/be6c040fe50984240d2f298a6b1af165322c96ad"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/a9f62b39882df1fca15a6d519ebda692adf46ee4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T19:06:03Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T19:06:03Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-7c): address Codex review round 1 (P1 + P2 fixes)\n\nThree wire-observable divergences from the pinned reference,\nall caught by Codex with targeted smokes. All three are pure\n\"mirror more faithfully\" fixes — no new D-NNN entry (last\nremains D-018 from Stage 7b).\n\nP1 — Empty file diverged from reference. Reference''s guard\n`if (request.headers.range && stats.size)` at\nserve-handler/src/index.js:720 skips Range processing entirely\non a 0-byte file (returns the normal 200 with no Content-Range);\nirserve was always calling range::apply and `total == 0` was\npinned as Unsatisfiable → 416 + Content-Range: bytes */0. Fix:\nadd a `total == 0 → return merged` guard in build_file_or_304\nright before range::apply. New probe anchor `range_on_empty_file`\n(ORC-178) pins the 200 + no-Content-Range outcome on both\ntargets. Integration test\n`dispatch::tests::range_on_empty_file_returns_200_not_416`.\n\nP2 — Manual parser was stricter than range-parser. Reference''s\nrange-parser uses JS `parseInt(start, 10)` and `parseInt(end, 10)`\nwhich accept a leading-digit prefix and ignore trailing garbage\n(`bytes=0-3x` parses as `0-3` → 206). irserve''s\n`.parse::<u64>()` rejected any non-digit and produced 416. Fix:\nintroduce `parse_digit_prefix` helper in range.rs that mirrors\nparseInt''s leading-digit semantics; route all three numeric\nparse sites (start, end, suffix N) through it. New probe anchor\n`range_trailing_garbage_in_end` (ORC-180) pins\n`Range: bytes=0-3x` → 206 + `bytes 0-3/11` on both targets.\nFour new unit tests in range::tests cover trailing garbage in\nend / start / suffix and the leading-non-digit fallback to\nUnsatisfiable. Integration test\n`dispatch::tests::range_trailing_garbage_value_emits_206`.\n\nP2 — 416 user Content-Range override was not honored. Reference\nsets `Content-Range: bytes */N` via `setHeader` BEFORE\n`getHeaders` returns; the subsequent `writeHead(status, headers)`\noverrides prior setHeader values for keys present in the merged\nmap, so a user `serve.json#headers` rule for `Content-Range`\nwins on 416 (Codex smoke: reference returns \"custom\"). irserve\nwas using `headers.insert(CONTENT_RANGE, ...)` post-merge,\nalways clobbering user values. Fix: switch to\n`headers.entry(CONTENT_RANGE).or_insert_with(...)` in\n`range::build_416` — the default `bytes */N` fills in only when\nthe merged response has no Content-Range yet. New probe anchor\n`range_416_user_content_range_override` (ORC-179) pins\n`content-range: custom-value` on both targets. Two new unit\ntests in range::tests + integration test\n`dispatch::tests::range_416_user_content_range_rule_wins`.\n\nThe 206 path keeps `insert` semantics (last-write-wins over\nuser rules) — that mirrors reference''s POST-getHeaders injection\nat index.js:749-752 for the 206 branch and is the only branch\nwhere reference clobbers user values. Stage 7c spec deltas\n(both change package and canonical) clarify the asymmetric\nordering: 206 = last-write-wins; 416 = first-write-wins via\nor_insert_with.\n\nProbe fixture grew by 2 files (empty.txt, tagged.txt) and 1\nserveJson entry (Content-Range rule scoped to tagged.txt).\nrunner.l0.clean grew to 11 anchors. Validation:\ncargo test --workspace 318 passed; cargo test --test oracle\npasses (range-request 11/11 anchors green); openspec validate\n--all --strict 22/22 passed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2a45878e88d39a091a0686f7dc7dd69ece40cafa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/2a45878e88d39a091a0686f7dc7dd69ece40cafa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/a9f62b39882df1fca15a6d519ebda692adf46ee4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/a9f62b39882df1fca15a6d519ebda692adf46ee4","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKGE5ZjYyYjM5ODgyZGYxZmNhMTVhNmQ1MTllYmRhNjkyYWRmNDZlZTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/bf4bdca90469fb487f93f4c0024a8e574a61e716","sha":"bf4bdca90469fb487f93f4c0024a8e574a61e716","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/bf4bdca90469fb487f93f4c0024a8e574a61e716"}],"sha":"a9f62b39882df1fca15a6d519ebda692adf46ee4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/a9f62b39882df1fca15a6d519ebda692adf46ee4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/bf4bdca90469fb487f93f4c0024a8e574a61e716/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T18:38:29Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T18:38:29Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-7c): spec deltas + oracle-matrix promotion + meta\n\nNew change package openspec/changes/013-range-requests/ with\nproposal / design / tasks / spec delta. Spec delta carries an\nADDED Requirement for SRV-CACHE-004 (Range / 206 / 416) with\n5 Scenarios, and a MODIFIED Requirement on the Stage 7b\nLast-Modified entry — the precursor `Range + matching IMS\nreturns 200` Scenario flips to `Range pre-empts the IMS 304 →\n206`. Mirrors the delta into the canonical\nopenspec/specs/http-cache/spec.md (added Range Requirement;\nupdated LM Requirement prose to document Range pre-emption;\nappended 7c-specific Compatibility notes).\n\nNo new D-NNN entry — D1 in the plan-mode AskUserQuestion\npicked Mirror (416 body is the full file per the reference''s\nfall-through and RFC 7233 §4.4); there is no intentional\ndivergence to record. Last D-NNN remains D-018 (Stage 7b).\n\nREADME: Stage 7c row flipped to `done`; \"What is NOT yet\nobservable\" footer trimmed (dropped Range requests); Range\ncurl demo added under \"Try IrServe\" with examples of in-range,\nsuffix-form, out-of-range, and the Range-pre-empts-304 note.\n\ninventory.md: SRV-CACHE-004 Probe bullet now lists the 8\nanchors (3 existing + 5 added in slice 0) and points at\nORC-044..046 + ORC-173..177 as dual-target oracle evidence;\nCompatibility notes expanded with the clip-vs-416 distinction,\nthe let-else 304 pre-emption, and the `Accept-Ranges`-not-\nemitted carve-out.\n\nValidation: cargo test --workspace passes (309 unit tests +\noracle harness 82 total, 77 passed, 5 skipped, 0 failed).\nopenspec validate --all --strict: 22 passed, 0 failed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dcef72618fb9577034de3a8591214c0035dd80de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/dcef72618fb9577034de3a8591214c0035dd80de"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/bf4bdca90469fb487f93f4c0024a8e574a61e716","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/bf4bdca90469fb487f93f4c0024a8e574a61e716","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKGJmNGJkY2E5MDQ2OWZiNDg3ZjkzZjRjMDAyNGE4ZTU3NGE2MWU3MTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/794fe6c4e06671b4baa17a638321970889456b2b","sha":"794fe6c4e06671b4baa17a638321970889456b2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/794fe6c4e06671b4baa17a638321970889456b2b"}],"sha":"bf4bdca90469fb487f93f4c0024a8e574a61e716","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/bf4bdca90469fb487f93f4c0024a8e574a61e716"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/794fe6c4e06671b4baa17a638321970889456b2b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T18:27:44Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T18:27:44Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"feat(stage-7c): slice 2 — emit 206/416 on Range requests\n\nWires range::apply into build_file_or_304: when a Range header\nis present the dispatcher clones the file bytes (no-Range path\nkeeps its single-alloc shape), pre-empts the 7a/7b 304\nshort-circuits via a let-else, and hands the merged response\nto range::apply which mutates it into 206 (partial body +\nContent-Range + Content-Length) or 416 (full body retained,\n+ Content-Range: bytes */<total>). Mirrors reference''s\npost-getHeaders injection at serve-handler/src/index.js:749-752\nand the Range-pre-empts-304 guard at index.js:760.\n\nPromotes all 8 range-request.json anchors to dual-target via\nrunner.l0.clean. range_on_missing_file''s 404 body diverges\nbetween targets (reference: 1641-byte vercel HTML; irserve:\n23-byte fallback `<h1>404 Not Found</h1>\\n`) — covered by\nbodyMayDiffer, same pattern as last-modified-roundtrip.json''s\nims_on_404 anchor.\n\nUpdated existing 7c-precursor tests in dispatch::tests\n(range_present_skips_304_even_on_match and\nrange_present_skips_ims_304_even_on_match): they previously\nasserted that Range presence keeps the 200 fall-through; with\nRange emission live they now pin StatusCode::PARTIAL_CONTENT.\n\nEight new integration tests in dispatch::tests cover:\n- in-range / tail / suffix → 206 with correct Content-Range\n- out-of-range → 416 with `bytes */16`\n- Range × IMS-match under --no-etag → 206 (Range pre-empts)\n- ETag preserved on both 206 and 416\n- user `headers` rule (ETag override) preserved on 206 and 416\n- user `Last-Modified: null` rule under --no-etag still 206s\n\nOracle harness: target=irserve total=82 passed=77 skipped=5\n(was passed=76 skipped=6 — range-request flipped from skipped\nto passed). ORC-044..046 and ORC-173..177 promoted to\ndual-target in oracle-matrix.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e25618a5bd9e0ec361ec3930834ca9a18d5017a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/e25618a5bd9e0ec361ec3930834ca9a18d5017a8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/794fe6c4e06671b4baa17a638321970889456b2b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/794fe6c4e06671b4baa17a638321970889456b2b","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDc5NGZlNmM0ZTA2NjcxYjRiYWExN2E2MzgzMjE5NzA4ODk0NTZiMmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/40fc032d6227566cc8377bb9e8fcdd88947ed3e7","sha":"40fc032d6227566cc8377bb9e8fcdd88947ed3e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/40fc032d6227566cc8377bb9e8fcdd88947ed3e7"}],"sha":"794fe6c4e06671b4baa17a638321970889456b2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/794fe6c4e06671b4baa17a638321970889456b2b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/40fc032d6227566cc8377bb9e8fcdd88947ed3e7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T18:21:54Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T18:21:54Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"feat(stage-7c): slice 1 — range parser module + apply helper (unit-tested, not yet wired)\n\nNew crates/irserve-core/src/range.rs with:\n- pub fn parse_range(value, total) -> RangeOutcome  — mirrors\n  the subset of vercel/serve-handler''s range-parser usage we\n  need: single-range, bytes unit, inclusive end, partial-overlap\n  clipping, suffix form `bytes=-N`. Wrong unit, malformed input,\n  and strictly-out-of-range all collapse to Unsatisfiable so the\n  caller routes everything non-OK through one 416 branch\n  (mirrors `index.js:730-732`).\n- pub fn apply(merged, range_header, bytes, total) -> Response\n  — mutates a merged 200 response into 206 (partial body +\n  `Content-Range: bytes <s>-<e>/<total>` + `Content-Length`) or\n  416 (full body retained per the reference, +\n  `Content-Range: bytes */<total>`). Content-Type, ETag,\n  Last-Modified, and user-rule custom headers carry over\n  unchanged; Content-Range / Content-Length are last-write-wins\n  (mirrors reference''s post-`getHeaders` injection at\n  `serve-handler/src/index.js:749-752`).\n\n21 unit tests in range::tests pin both layers (parser + apply).\nNot yet wired into dispatch.rs — that lands in slice 2.\n\nPlan §\"Slice 0\" added `runner.l0.clean` to range-request.json\ntogether with the new probes, but slice 0 had no irserve\nimplementation yet, so the partition turned target=irserve red.\nReverted the partition here; slice 2 re-adds it together with\nthe dispatch wiring so both ratchet up in lockstep.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a470414c7bb443b37ef7c1f2940cfe20824feaf7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/a470414c7bb443b37ef7c1f2940cfe20824feaf7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/40fc032d6227566cc8377bb9e8fcdd88947ed3e7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/40fc032d6227566cc8377bb9e8fcdd88947ed3e7","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDQwZmMwMzJkNjIyNzU2NmNjODM3N2JiOWU4ZmNkZDg4OTQ3ZWQzZTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/4d86eeb6ced4938884b765bcd38dc61863d0e269","sha":"4d86eeb6ced4938884b765bcd38dc61863d0e269","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/4d86eeb6ced4938884b765bcd38dc61863d0e269"}],"sha":"40fc032d6227566cc8377bb9e8fcdd88947ed3e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/40fc032d6227566cc8377bb9e8fcdd88947ed3e7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/4d86eeb6ced4938884b765bcd38dc61863d0e269/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T18:16:47Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T18:16:47Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"probe(stage-7c): extend range-request fixture with edge cases (suffix, single-byte, clip, 404, INM-interaction)\n\nAdds 5 anchors to tools/probe/cases/range-request.json with their\nrunner.l0.clean partition, records the reference snapshot, and\ndocuments ORC-173..177 in oracle-matrix.md.\n\nConfirmed empirically from the new reference snapshot:\n- bytes=-3 → 206 with Content-Range: bytes 8-10/11 (suffix form\n  resolves to start=total-n, end=total-1).\n- bytes=0-0 → 206 with Content-Range: bytes 0-0/11 (inclusive-end\n  semantics — one byte, not zero).\n- bytes=8-999 → 206 with Content-Range: bytes 8-10/11 (partial\n  overlap clips to total-1, NOT 416; the 416 boundary is strictly\n  out-of-range like bytes=999-1000).\n- Range + missing file → 404 (Range parsing is downstream of the\n  404 branch in the reference; same expected for irserve).\n- Range + matching If-None-Match → 206, NOT 304 (Range pre-empts\n  the conditional-GET 304 short-circuit per index.js:760; irserve\n  mirrors via dispatch.rs:771 guard).\n\nReference-only initially; promotion to dual-target lands in\nslice 2 once range::apply is wired into build_file_or_304.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8c40772191d304f256c6a47fb4a4efa0918073fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/8c40772191d304f256c6a47fb4a4efa0918073fb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/4d86eeb6ced4938884b765bcd38dc61863d0e269","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_t