e `## Validation`\nintro:\n\n- Round 5 heading: `(this commit)` placeholder replaced with\n  `(commit 7ed7fe4)`, matching the convention rounds 1–4\n  established (each round-N+1 commit pins round-N''s hash).\n- `## Validation` intro: `Latest totals at end of Stage 7b\n  (post-Codex round 4):` rephrased to drop the round qualifier.\n  Counts have been stable at 279/279 since Codex round 1 added\n  the IMS-gate test; rounds 2–6 are pure doc-hygiene with no\n  effect on lib-test, oracle, or openspec-validate totals. The\n  new intro reads: \"Latest totals at end of Stage 7b (refreshed\n  after every Codex round; rounds 5+ have been doc-hygiene only\n  and do not change the underlying counts).\" This makes the\n  section stable regardless of how many further hygiene rounds\n  happen.\n\nThis round also adds a Round 6 section to the round-log with the\nself-reference window made explicit. The round-N section, when\nfreshly committed, carries a `(commit pending; pinned in next\nround if any)` marker for itself; the next round (if any) pins\nthe hash. Stage 7b''s closing commit (if no further Codex rounds)\nleaves the last round''s hash unpinned in the doc but visible in\n`git log`. The marker phrasing eliminates the \"this commit\"\nambiguity Codex flagged in rounds 5 and 6.\n\nNo code, no spec content, no probe changes. Round-log hygiene\nonly.\n\nVerified:\n- `cargo test --workspace --lib` — 279/279 (unchanged).\n- `npx -y @fission-ai/openspec@latest validate --all --strict`\n  — 21/21 passed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"34123a83b62cd92e01cf6cbfb9d36ed6906655b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/34123a83b62cd92e01cf6cbfb9d36ed6906655b8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/7f219e184a6fad24a6be0721b6ae4abbd56a191b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"