documentation. Round 3\nhad updated inventory.md but missed five sites still carrying the\npre-promotion status text:\n\n- `openspec/specs/http-cache/spec.md:179` (canonical Evidence\n  line on the `Last-Modified` Requirement) — flipped both SRV\n  status fields from `accepted` to `verified`.\n- `openspec/changes/012-last-modified/specs/http-cache/spec.md:59`\n  (delta variant of the same Evidence line) — same flip.\n- `openspec/changes/012-last-modified/proposal.md:19,25` (Why\n  bullets that listed each SRV''s pre-stage status) — rewrote\n  the parenthetical to `accepted → verified via ORC-167`,\n  matching the inventory.md promotion event narrative.\n- `openspec/changes/012-last-modified/proposal.md:131`\n  (Documentation updates bullet that explicitly said the two\n  SRVs \"stay accepted\") — rewrote to describe the round-3\n  promotion outcome and cite README §Anti-hallucination rules\n  #2 as the taxonomy rationale (an SRV transitions to `verified`\n  when an Oracle test demonstrates the behavior; ORC-167 is that\n  test for both SRVs under `serveArgs: [\"--no-etag\"]`).\n- `docs/reference/serve/compatibility-levels.md:61,92` — Level 3\n  list entry rewritten from \"(`accepted` / verified by ORC-167)\"\n  to \"(`verified` via ORC-167)\"; Coverage gaps entry rewritten\n  from \"SRV-CLI-013 / SRV-CACHE-002 stay `accepted`\" to\n  \"promoted `accepted` → `verified`\".\n\nThe plan file `docs/features/0016_PLAN_stage7b_last_modified.md`\nkeeps its point-in-time `accepted` wording (same convention as\nthe 011-etag-conditional package''s historical citations — plan\nfiles are snapshots of intent at commit time).\n\n`tasks.md` round-log gains a Round 3 commit-hash (`cef7185`)\nand a Round 4 section recording this commit''s scope.\n\nVerified:\n- `cargo test --workspace --lib` — 279/279 unit tests green\n  (docs-only changes).\n- `cargo test --test oracle` — 82/76/6/0 unchanged.\n- `npx -y @fission-ai/openspec@latest validate --all --strict`\n  — 21/21 passed.\n- `grep -rnE ''SRV-(CACHE-002|CLI-013)[^\\n]{0,80}accepted''\n  openspec/ docs/reference/` — only transitional\n  \"`accepted` → `verified`\" phrasings remain (correct event\n  documentation, no stale standalone `accepted` status).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"54bf5ebfec7fdd98a44535ae3f6859871146de3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/54bf5ebfec7fdd98a44535ae3f6859871146de3f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/3437082594204ab31a5f339516b72b893c483feb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/3437082594204ab31a5f339516b72b893c483feb","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDM0MzcwODI1OTQyMDRhYjMxYTVmMzM5NTE2YjcyYjg5M2M0ODNmZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/cef71859e586abb2551d329ed2956244e5d7c5e1","sha":"cef71859e586abb2551d329ed2956244e5d7c5e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/cef71859e586abb2551d329ed2956244e5d7c5e1"}],"sha":"3437082594204ab31a5f339516b72b893c483feb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/3437082594204ab31a5f339516b72b893c483feb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/cef71859e586abb2551d329ed2956244e5d7c5e1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T12:25:05Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T12:25:05Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-7b): address Codex review round 3 (P3 fixes)\n\nP3 — `docs/reference/serve/compatibility-levels.md` had two stale\nlines contradicting Stage 7b''s outcome:\n- L61 listed `Last-Modified` / IMS status as `unknown` with\n  Q-009 open. Rewrote to reflect: SRV-CACHE-002 verified by\n  ORC-167; SRV-CACHE-003 verified for the reference path /\n  adapted for irserve per D-018; Q-009 closed in slice 0.\n- L92 \"Coverage gaps / `--no-etag` / Last-Modified path —\n  no probe\" flipped to strike-through \"closed in Stage 7b\"\n  with the ORC-167..172 + D-018 cross-link.\n\nP3 — `docs/reference/serve/inventory.md` had three stale\nevidence-field entries from before Stage 7b:\n- L398 SRV-CLI-013: \"Oracle test: planned\" → ORC-167 anchor.\n  Status promoted `accepted` → `verified` per the taxonomy\n  in README §Anti-hallucination rules #2: ORC-167 now\n  exercises the `--no-etag` → `Last-Modified` substitution\n  end-to-end via `last-modified-roundtrip.json#first_get`\n  under `serveArgs: [\"--no-etag\"]`, which is precisely the\n  contract SRV-CLI-013 captures.\n- L1400 SRV-CACHE-002: \"Probe: not run for this branch\" /\n  \"Oracle test: planned\" → cites `last-modified-roundtrip.json`\n  + ORC-167 (Last-Modified emitted, ETag absent under\n  `--no-etag` — the SRV-CACHE-002 contract). Status promoted\n  `accepted` → `verified` for the same reason: ORC-167''s\n  must-match assertion exercises the SRV-CACHE-002 wire surface\n  directly.\n- L1423 SRV-CACHE-003: already `verified` from slice 0; the\n  \"Oracle test: planned\" line replaced with the full ORC-167..172\n  enumeration + the irserve-side `dispatch::tests::ims_*` +\n  `etag_on_ignores_ims_even_with_user_lm_rule` cross-reference.\n\nThe status promotions follow the taxonomy literally as Codex\nsuggested: \"verified = Oracle test demonstrates the behavior\"\n(README §Compatibility levels / status). Both SRV-CLI-013 and\nSRV-CACHE-002 had been blocked at `accepted` only because the\noracle test was pending; ORC-167 closes that gap.\n\nP3 — `openspec/changes/012-last-modified/tasks.md:228`\nplaceholder `commit <this commit>` for the Round 1 section\nreplaced with the actual commit hash `13b66bb`. Added a Round 2\nsection (commit `60058e4`) and a Round 3 section (this commit)\nto keep the round log complete.\n\nVerified:\n- `cargo test --workspace --lib` — 279/279 unit tests green\n  (docs-only changes; no code touched).\n- `cargo test --test oracle` — 82/76/6/0 unchanged.\n- `npx -y @fission-ai/openspec@latest validate --all --strict`\n  — 21/21 passed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1ab26e02ae6da027f688f49ccbbae736add89724","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/1ab26e02ae6da027f688f49ccbbae736add89724"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/cef71859e586abb2551d329ed2956244e5d7c5e1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/cef71859e586abb2551d329ed2956244e5d7c5e1","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKGNlZjcxODU5ZTU4NmFiYjI1NTFkMzI5ZWQyOTU2MjQ0ZTVkN2M1ZTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/60058e4d8211edd763c4a301da8ae9ba2e8352da","sha":"60058e4d8211edd763c4a301da8ae9ba2e8352da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/60058e4d8211edd763c4a301da8ae9ba2e8352da"}],"sha":"cef71859e586abb2551d329ed2956244e5d7c5e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/cef71859e586abb2551d329ed2956244e5d7c5e1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/60058e4d8211edd763c4a301da8ae9ba2e8352da/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T12:13:49Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T12:13:49Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-7b): address Codex review round 2 (P3 fixes)\n\nP3 — `docs/reference/serve/oracle-matrix.md` Coverage gaps section\ninternally inconsistent. The three lines for SRV-CLI-013 /\nSRV-CACHE-002 / SRV-CACHE-003 still listed them as probe gaps with\nQ-009 `open`, even though slice 0 had added ORC-167..ORC-172 in\nthe same file pinning the surface, and Q-009 closed in\n`open-questions.md` / inventory. Flipped all three entries to\nstrike-through \"closed in Stage 7b\" with the ORC cross-link and\nthe D-018 note for SRV-CACHE-003''s irserve adaptation.\n\nP3 — `openspec/changes/012-last-modified/proposal.md:116` still\nnamed \"ORC-167/168/169\" as the dual-target promotion set.\nCorrect partition (matches `last-modified-roundtrip.json#runner.l0`\n+ tasks.md as fixed in round 1): `clean: ORC-167/170/171/172`\n(dual-target), `divergent: ORC-168/169` (reference-only,\nirserve diverges to 304 per D-018). Same fix as the round-1\ntasks.md edit; this is the proposal copy that the subagent\nemitted with the same swap.\n\nP3 — Stale `dispatch.rs:NNN` citations after the round-1 guard\ninsertion shifted line numbers in `build_file_or_304` and the\nIMS branch. Replaced across 5 files:\n\n| Was                       | Now                       | What it points to |\n|---------------------------|---------------------------|------------------|\n| `dispatch.rs:754`         | `dispatch.rs:758`         | `build_file_or_304` fn start |\n| `dispatch.rs:763-765`     | `dispatch.rs:767-769`     | emission seam (etag_value + last_modified_value + file_response) |\n| `dispatch.rs:776-792`     | `dispatch.rs:780-809`     | IMS 304 branch (comment + gate + parse + 304) |\n| `dispatch.rs:797-802`     | `dispatch.rs:814`         | `not_modified_response()` helper |\n| `dispatch.rs:797`         | `dispatch.rs:814`         | (proposal variant of same helper citation) |\n| `dispatch.rs:767`         | `dispatch.rs:771`         | `Range`-absent guard |\n| `dispatch.rs:736-748`     | `dispatch.rs:710-756`     | `build_file_or_304` doc-comment span |\n\nFiles touched:\n- `openspec/specs/http-cache/spec.md` (canonical, 5 sites)\n- `openspec/changes/012-last-modified/specs/http-cache/spec.md`\n  (delta, 5 sites)\n- `openspec/changes/012-last-modified/proposal.md` (4 sites)\n- `openspec/changes/012-last-modified/design.md` (4 sites)\n- `openspec/changes/012-last-modified/tasks.md` (5 sites)\n- `docs/reference/serve/decisions.md` (D-018, 2 sites)\n\nThe 011-etag-conditional change package''s historical citations\n(`dispatch.rs:687`, `:637`, `:320`, `:430`, etc.) are left\nuntouched — that package is a closed change record and its\ncitations should remain valid at the time it was written, not\nretroactively refreshed.\n\nThe two unchanged call-site citations (`dispatch.rs:346` for the\nFile/Index arm and `dispatch.rs:480` for the renderSingle branch)\nverified still accurate via `grep -nE \"build_file_or_304\\(\"`.\n\nVerified:\n- `cargo test --workspace --lib` — 279/279 unit tests green\n  (no code changes; the citations are docs-only).\n- `cargo test --test oracle` — 82/76/6/0 (unchanged).\n- `npx -y @fission-ai/openspec@latest validate --all --strict`\n  — 21/21 passed.\n- `grep -rnE ''dispatch\\.rs:(754\\b|763-765|776-792|797-802|797\\b|736-748)''\n  openspec/ docs/reference/` — no matches (all stale citations\n  cleared).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0ff707f207c691a933c221927a6c57de6ec864f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/0ff707f207c691a933c221927a6c57de6ec864f6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/60058e4d8211edd763c4a301da8ae9ba2e8352da","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/60058e4d8211edd763c4a301da8ae9ba2e8352da","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDYwMDU4ZTRkODIxMWVkZDc2M2M0YTMwMWRhOGFlOWJhMmU4MzUyZGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/13b66bb204b5b9afd39e604cce38d05ff9d7de0d","sha":"13b66bb204b5b9afd39e604cce38d05ff9d7de0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/13b66bb204b5b9afd39e604cce38d05ff9d7de0d"}],"sha":"60058e4d8211edd763c4a301da8ae9ba2e8352da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/60058e4d8211edd763c4a301da8ae9ba2e8352da"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/13b66bb204b5b9afd39e604cce38d05ff9d7de0d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T11:58:35Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T11:58:35Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-7b): address Codex review round 1 (P2 + P3 fixes)\n\nP2 — gate IMS branch on `serve_config.etag == Some(false)`.\n\nSlice 3 implemented the IMS 304 path symmetrically with ETag/INM:\n\"if merged response has Last-Modified, IMS can short-circuit.\" On\nreflection during plan-mode I considered both designs and the plan\nexplicitly chose the narrower \"gate on etag-off\" form (Decisions\ntaken without asking → `build_file_or_304` extension), then slice 3\ndeviated to the symmetric form during implementation. The deviation\ncontradicted the inventory rule for SRV-CACHE-003 (\"When ETag is\non, IMS is ignored — the 304 trigger is `If-None-Match` per\nSRV-CACHE-001\") that I wrote myself in slice 0, and widened\nD-018''s divergence from reference unnecessarily: a deployment with\ndefault ETag plus a user `serve.json#headers` rule supplying\n`Last-Modified` would 304 on irserve and 200 on reference.\n\nFix: explicit `if serve_config.etag == Some(false)` gate around\nthe IMS branch in `build_file_or_304`. Under ETag-on (default or\nexplicit `Some(true)`), the IMS branch is bypassed entirely —\neven when a user rule supplies `Last-Modified` on the merged\nresponse. The 304 trigger under ETag-on is exclusively\n`If-None-Match`. Mirrors plan + inventory.\n\nBehavior matrix after the gate:\n\n| `etag` config | user LM rule | IMS request | irserve | reference |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `None`/`true`    | absent  | any   | 200, ETag        | 200, ETag        |\n| `None`/`true`    | present | match | 200, ETag + LM   | 200, ETag + LM   |\n| `Some(false)`    | absent  | match | 304              | 200, LM, no ETag |\n| `Some(false)`    | absent  | < LM  | 200, LM          | 200, LM, no ETag |\n| `Some(false)`    | present | match | 304              | 200, LM, no ETag |\n\nD-018 now applies only to the bottom-three rows; the second row\n(the case Codex flagged) returns to reference parity. The widened\n\"symmetric\" design from slice 3 is removed without controversy:\nit was never the contract I wrote in the inventory or the plan.\n\nNew unit test `etag_on_ignores_ims_even_with_user_lm_rule` pins\nthe corner case: default ETag + user `Last-Modified` rule + IMS\nmatching the override → 200 (not 304). Updated spec.md ADDED\nRequirement + Compatibility note + canonical http-cache spec +\nD-018 in decisions.md to make the gate explicit. Existing 7 IMS\ntests unchanged (all use `cfg_etag(Some(false))`).\n\nP3 — `docs/stage7_l3_capabilities.md` flipped to past tense for\nStage 7b: the row description, the \"Methodological signals to\nwatch for / 7b / IMS semantics (Q-009 closure)\" bullet, and the\nreferences to Q-009 as `unknown` / `probe-first`. SRV-CACHE-003\nis `verified` since slice 0; D-018 cited; the round-1 gate\nreferenced in the row''s partition story.\n\nP3 — `tasks.md`: marked slice-4 \"Main agent only\" items as done\n(canonical spec merge, D-018, README, openspec validate, commit\n`9605bb5`); added a \"Codex review rounds / Round 1\" section\nlisting each P2/P3 fix; fixed the stale slice-0 summary line\nthat said \"ORC-167/168/169 promoted to dual-target\" — the\nactual slice-3 promotion was ORC-167/170/171/172 via `clean`,\nORC-168/169 stayed reference-only in `divergent`. The\noracle-matrix.md rows themselves were already correct; only\nthe tasks.md summary carried the stale formulation.\n\nP3 — removed unused `SystemTime` import in\n`crates/irserve-core/src/last_modified.rs::tests`. Build now\nclean.\n\nVerified:\n- `cargo build --workspace` — clean, no warnings.\n- `cargo test --workspace --lib` — 279/279 unit tests green\n  (was 278; +1 from `etag_on_ignores_ims_even_with_user_lm_rule`).\n- `cargo test --test oracle` — 82/76 passed / 6 skipped / 0\n  failed (unchanged from slice 3 — no probe changes in this\n  round; the partition still pins reference''s IMS-inert\n  behavior under `target=reference` for ORC-168/169).\n- `npx -y @fission-ai/openspec@latest validate --all --strict`\n  — 21/21 passed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2b39540f606c892d5fef30b77b4f072c36c4c677","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/2b39540f606c892d5fef30b77b4f072c36c4c677"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/13b66bb204b5b9afd39e604cce38d05ff9d7de0d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/13b66bb204b5b9afd39e604cce38d05ff9d7de0d","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDEzYjY2YmIyMDRiNWI5YWZkMzllNjA0Y2NlMzhkMDVmZjlkN2RlMGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/9605bb5ce4ce834537cbc53de6921f7a69ac5adf","sha":"9605bb5ce4ce834537cbc53de6921f7a69ac5adf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/9605bb5ce4ce834537cbc53de6921f7a69ac5adf"}],"sha":"13b66bb204b5b9afd39e604cce38d05ff9d7de0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/13b66bb204b5b9afd39e604cce38d05ff9d7de0d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/9605bb5ce4ce834537cbc53de6921f7a69ac5adf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T11:26:27Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T11:26:27Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-7b): spec deltas + D-018 + http-cache merge + README\n\nSlice 4 (meta) — closes Stage 7b on the documentation side:\n\nOpenSpec change package `openspec/changes/012-last-modified/`\n(authored by delegated subagent per kickoff template, main-agent\nreviewed):\n- `proposal.md` — Why / What / Out-of-scope mirroring 011''s shape.\n  Cites SRV-CLI-013, SRV-CACHE-002/003, Q-009 (closed in slice 0),\n  D-018; lists the 4-slice implementation with file:line anchors.\n- `design.md` — 7 numbered sections covering the ETag/LM mutex,\n  Last-Modified emission seam, the IMS 304 D-018 adaptation,\n  the --no-etag CLI flag, the probe partition + day-of-week\n  methodological signal, D-018 framing, verification matrix.\n- `tasks.md` — 5 slices with commit hashes pinned\n  (351b3a7 / 127b6ce / a3a0aaf / 40a58bc / this commit) and a\n  Validation section listing counts.\n- `specs/http-cache/spec.md` — ADDED Requirement for\n  SRV-CACHE-002 + SRV-CACHE-003 + SRV-CLI-013 with 7 Scenarios\n  covering first-GET emission, IMS match → 304, IMS < LM → 200,\n  user override drives 304, user `null` rule suppresses 304,\n  malformed IMS → 200, Range + matching IMS → 200. MODIFIED\n  Requirement on Stage-7a''s ETag spec to add the mutex\n  paragraph. Compatibility notes pin the D-018 divergence, the\n  whole-second comparison, the RFC 9111 §13.1.3 malformed-IMS\n  recipient guidance, the `--no-etag` vs `serve.json#etag`\n  precedence carryover from 7a, and the scope rules (listings,\n  redirects, error pages).\n\nCanonical http-cache spec merge\n(`openspec/specs/http-cache/spec.md`):\n- Purpose updated — Last-Modified/IMS now delivered (not future).\n- ETag Requirement gains the mutex paragraph + mentions\n  `--no-etag` CLI flag as a now-supported disabling form.\n- New `Last-Modified` Requirement and its 7 Scenarios added.\n- Compatibility notes section extended with the 8 new entries\n  from the delta; obsolete \"`--no-etag` not yet parsed\" note\n  removed.\n\nD-018 entry appended to `docs/reference/serve/decisions.md`:\n- Status: `adapted`. Rationale anchored in anti-hallucination\n  rule #5 + Q-009 closure outcome + symmetry with the ETag/INM\n  path. Documents the wire contract (IMS ≥ merged LM → 304 with\n  no body / no Content-Type / no LM echo, Range-absent guarded)\n  and what is NOT contractual (the literal Last-Modified date\n  string; the reference''s 200 path). Cross-links the unit tests\n  + `last-modified-roundtrip.json` partition + the `--no-etag`\n  precedence note from Stage 7a.\n\nREADME.md:\n- Stage 7b row flipped to `done` in both the Status list and\n  the Stage map table.\n- \"Try IrServe\" curl demo block gains a Stage-7b section\n  (--no-etag round-trip + malformed-IMS sanity) immediately\n  after the Stage-7a ETag demo.\n- \"What is NOT yet observable\" footer drops the\n  `Last-Modified`/`If-Modified-Since` line; the remaining\n  L3-polish items (Range, default Cache-Control, full L3 CORS\n  preflight, gzip, symlink, TLS) carry over to 7c-7e + L4.\n\nVerified:\n- `npx -y @fission-ai/openspec@latest validate --all --strict`:\n  21 passed, 0 failed.\n- `cargo test --workspace --lib`: 278/278 unit tests green.\n- `cargo test --test oracle`: 82 total, 76 passed, 6 skipped, 0\n  failed (carries over from slice 3 — no oracle changes in this\n  slice).\n\nORC-167..172 rows from slice 0''s oracle-matrix.md are unchanged\nin this slice; their forward-looking Layer-text from slice 0 is\nnow past-tense-accurate (the dual-target promotion happened in\nslice 3). No edits needed; future maintenance can refresh tense\nif Codex review flags it.\n\nStage 7b is complete. Next stage per the roadmap:\n7c (Range requests, `206`/`416`) — independent of 7a/7b,\nschedulable when ready.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cf339ec36476a88678f9f09d46f52a83b71b3789","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/cf339ec36476a88678f9f09d46f52a83b71b3789"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/9605bb5ce4ce834537cbc53de6921f7a69ac5adf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/9605bb5ce4ce834537cbc53de6921f7a69ac5adf","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDk2MDViYjVjZTRjZTgzNDUzN2NiYzUzZGU2OTIxZjdhNjlhYzVhZGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/40a58bc18b068e9c9559fd046b318566303883ee","sha":"40a58bc18b068e9c9559fd046b318566303883ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/40a58bc18b068e9c9559fd046b318566303883ee"}],"sha":"9605bb5ce4ce834537cbc53de6921f7a69ac5adf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/9605bb5ce4ce834537cbc53de6921f7a69ac5adf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/40a58bc18b068e9c9559fd046b318566303883ee/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T11:11:10Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T11:11:10Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"feat(stage-7b): slice 3 — 304 short-circuit on If-Modified-Since (D-018)\n\nirserve adaptation per D-018: under `etag: false` (i.e. `--no-etag`\nor `serve.json#etag: false`), a request whose `If-Modified-Since`\nis ≥ the merged `Last-Modified` short-circuits to 304 with no\nbody, no `Content-Type`, no `Last-Modified` echo — mirroring the\nETag/INM 304 shape from Stage 7a. The reference has no IMS branch\n(Q-009 closure in slice 0), so under `target=reference` the same\nrequest returns 200 with the full body. The divergence is deliberate\nand documented; the spec delta + D-018 entry land in slice 4.\n\nImplementation (`dispatch::build_file_or_304`):\n- New IMS branch after the existing INM branch; gated by the\n  same `Range`-absent guard (mirrors `index.js:760`; Range parsing\n  itself lands in 7c).\n- Parses both IMS request header and merged `Last-Modified`\n  response header via `httpdate::parse_http_date`. Compares\n  `SystemTime` values with `>=`. Malformed IMS or LM falls\n  through to 200 (RFC 9111 §13.1.3 — recipients SHOULD ignore\n  unparseable IMS). Whole-second comparison naturally falls out\n  of the formatter/parser round-trip.\n- Symmetric with the ETag path: reads the MERGED Last-Modified\n  value (after `apply_custom_headers`), so a user\n  `serve.json#headers` rule that overrides or deletes\n  `Last-Modified` drives the 304 decision against the override\n  (or suppresses 304 entirely under `Last-Modified: null`).\n- New `not_modified_response()` helper extracts the 304-shape\n  builder shared by the INM and IMS branches.\n\nTests (7 new in `dispatch::tests`, all green):\n- `ims_exact_match_returns_304` — round-trip via captured LM.\n- `ims_future_returns_304` — far-future static IMS (day-of-week\n  cross-checked: 2099-01-01 is Thursday, not Friday).\n- `ims_past_returns_200_with_last_modified` — epoch IMS.\n- `ims_malformed_returns_200` — unparseable IMS.\n- `range_present_skips_ims_304_even_on_match` — 7c precursor.\n- `user_last_modified_null_rule_suppresses_304` — SRV-HDR-002\n  prune deletes LM → no 304 possible.\n- `user_last_modified_override_drives_304_decision` — custom LM\n  rule wins; replay of override → 304, IMS predating override → 200.\n- New `compile_last_modified_override` helper parallels\n  `compile_etag_override`.\n\nProbe + snapshot (`last-modified-roundtrip`):\n- Fixed day-of-week: `Fri, 01 Jan 2099` → `Thu, 01 Jan 2099`\n  in `ims_future` and `ims_on_404` headers (slice 0 had it wrong;\n  reference ignores IMS so the malformed day-of-week was inert\n  under `target=reference`, but irserve''s strict\n  `httpdate::parse_http_date` rejects mismatched day-of-week per\n  RFC 7231 and fell through to 200, breaking the slice 3 unit\n  test mirroring the same date).\n- Snapshot re-recorded (only the `if-modified-since` request-header\n  string changed — response stays 200 since reference is IMS-inert).\n- New `runner.l0` partition promotes the case to dual-target:\n  - `clean: [first_get, ims_past, ims_malformed, ims_on_404]` —\n    irserve and reference agree on the response shape.\n  - `divergent: [ims_exact, ims_future]` — irserve returns 304,\n    reference returns 200; recorded under `target=reference` only,\n    irserve coverage via the new `dispatch::tests` suite.\n  - `bodyMayDiffer: [ims_on_404]` — both sides emit 404 but the\n    HTML body content is not contractual (D-002).\n\nVerified:\n- `cargo test --workspace --lib` 278/278 unit tests green\n  (was 271; +7 from this slice).\n- `cargo test --test oracle` 82 total, 76 passed, 6 skipped, 0\n  failed (was 75 passed / 7 skipped; the four `last-modified-\n  roundtrip` clean anchors promoted to dual-target).\n- `node tools/probe/run.mjs last-modified-roundtrip --target=reference\n  --snapshot=verify` green.\n- `node tools/probe/run.mjs last-modified-roundtrip --target=irserve\n  --snapshot=verify` green (with the L0 partition applied).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f8ce126650d3e07a44946bffb4a36e83bfb6721d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/f8ce126650d3e07a44946bffb4a36e83bfb6721d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/40a58bc18b068e9c9559fd046b318566303883ee","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/40a58bc18b068e9c9559fd046b318566303883ee","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDQwYTU4YmMxOGIwNjhlOWM5NTU5ZmQwNDZiMzE4NTY2MzAzODgzZWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/a3a0aafdeb355bdf5e71bfa3b40ddd305656e2da","sha":"a3a0aafdeb355bdf5e71bfa3b40ddd305656e2da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/a3a0aafdeb355bdf5e71bfa3b40ddd305656e2da"}],"sha":"40a58bc18b068e9c9559fd046b318566303883ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/40a58bc18b068e9c9559fd046b318566303883ee"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/a3a0aafdeb355bdf5e71bfa3b40ddd305656e2da/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T11:02:15Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T11:02:15Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"feat(stage-7b): slice 2 — emit Last-Modified header under --no-etag\n\nNew module `crates/irserve-core/src/last_modified.rs` with\n`last_modified_value(serve_config, meta) -> Option<HeaderValue>`,\ngated on `serve_config.etag == Some(false)` (mutex with ETag —\ndirect mirror of `serve-handler/src/index.js:227-236`''s `if (etag)\n/ else` branches). The reference uses `stats.mtime.toUTCString()`;\nirserve uses `httpdate::fmt_http_date(SystemTime)` (RFC 7231\nIMF-fixdate, whole-second resolution, \"GMT\" suffix). Workspace gains\n`httpdate = \"1\"` (pinned-stable 1.0.3).\n\nDispatcher changes (`dispatch.rs`):\n- `file_response` takes a new `last_modified: Option<HeaderValue>`\n  parameter and emits the header when `Some`. ETag and Last-Modified\n  are written independently so user `headers` rules later (via\n  `apply_custom_headers`) can override either — mutex is upstream\n  in the two value helpers, not in the response builder.\n- `build_file_or_304` gains a `meta: Option<&Metadata>` parameter\n  (post-`bytes`, pre-`header_rules`); computes both `etag_value`\n  and `last_modified_value` from the same `ServeConfig.etag`\n  predicate, so exactly one of the two ends up `Some` per call.\n  304 logic unchanged in this slice; IMS short-circuit is slice 3.\n- Both call sites (File/Index arm and renderSingle branch) now\n  `tokio::fs::metadata(&p).await.ok()` alongside the bytes read.\n  A metadata failure degrades gracefully to \"no Last-Modified\";\n  a read failure still surfaces as 404. Two-syscall pattern is\n  the smallest diff and TOCTOU on mtime is immaterial at\n  whole-second IMF-fixdate resolution.\n\nTests:\n- 4 new unit tests in `last_modified.rs`: known-mtime → fixed wire\n  string, ETag-on suppresses LM (both default and explicit `true`),\n  ETag-off emits LM with shape sanity, ETag-off without meta → None.\n- 2 new tests in `dispatch::tests`: `etag_off_emits_last_modified_from_meta`\n  (LM present, no ETag, IMF-fixdate shape) and\n  `etag_on_suppresses_last_modified_even_with_meta` (ETag present,\n  LM absent under default config). All 10 existing dispatch tests\n  updated to pass `None` for the new `meta` argument (they exercise\n  the ETag-on path and don''t need a real mtime).\n\nVerified:\n- `cargo test --workspace` 271/271 unit tests green (was 265 in\n  slice 1; +6 = 4 LM + 2 dispatch).\n- `cargo test --test oracle` 82 total, 75 passed, 7 skipped (the\n  `last-modified-roundtrip` partition still reference-only; slice 3\n  promotes its scenarios to dual-target after the IMS 304 lands).\n- `cargo build --workspace` green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3c2ce2c1dc34f34ef386be8e6a5fc98340562589","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/3c2ce2c1dc34f34ef386be8e6a5fc98340562589"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/a3a0aafdeb355bdf5e71bfa3b40ddd305656e2da","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/a3a0aafdeb355bdf5e71bfa3b40ddd305656e2da","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKGEzYTBhYWZkZWIzNTViZGY1ZTcxYmZhM2I0MGRkZDMwNTY1NmUyZGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/127b6ce8540e73b232051fbad59caf1c8ce4f465","sha":"127b6ce8540e73b232051fbad59caf1c8ce4f465","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/127b6ce8540e73b232051fbad59caf1c8ce4f465"}],"sha":"a3a0aafdeb355bdf5e71bfa3b40ddd305656e2da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/a3a0aafdeb355bdf5e71bfa3b40ddd305656e2da"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/127b6ce8540e73b232051fbad59caf1c8ce4f465/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T10:54:23Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T10:54:23Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"feat(stage-7b): slice 1 — --no-etag CLI flag wired through to ServeConfig\n\nAdds `--no-etag: bool` (long-only, no short alias) to `Cli` and a\npost-parse override forcing `serve_config.etag = Some(false)` when\nthe flag is set. Mirrors `third_party/serve/source/utilities/cli.ts:155`\n+ `config.ts:140` (`config.etag = !args[''--no-etag'']`).\n\nPrecedence semantics: the flag wins over a `serve.json` `etag`\nvalue when set; when unset, the serve.json field (if any) is\nhonored. Diverges from reference''s stricter `force-true-without-flag`\nbehavior but preserves the 7a-established serve.json contract — no\ntest surface changes.\n\nNo new unit tests in this slice (the threading is a single boolean\noverride; behavioral coverage lands in slices 2 and 3 with\nLast-Modified emission and the IMS short-circuit). The planned\ndedicated `no-etag-flag.json` smoke probe is dropped — redundant\nwith `last-modified-roundtrip.json#first_get` from slice 0.\n\nVerified:\n- `cargo build --workspace` green.\n- `cargo test --workspace` 265/265 unit tests green.\n- `cargo test --test oracle` 82 total, 75 passed, 7 skipped (the\n  `last-modified-roundtrip` probe is in the skipped bucket; slice 3\n  promotes its `l0.clean` partition).\n- `cargo run -- --help` lists `--no-etag` with the SRV-CLI-013\n  doc comment.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a2c197d7f682ae88c8c1fe7c366cf211582c578f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/a2c197d7f682ae88c8c1fe7c366cf211582c578f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/127b6ce8540e73b232051fbad59caf1c8ce4f465","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/127b6ce8540e73b232051fbad59caf1c8ce4f465","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDEyN2I2Y2U4NTQwZTczYjIzMjA1MWZiYWQ1OWNhZjFjOGNlNGY0NjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/351b3a747ab65c288ee45141b0722d67c44dafd7","sha":"351b3a747ab65c288ee45141b0722d67c44dafd7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/351b3a747ab65c288ee45141b0722d67c44dafd7"}],"sha":"127b6ce8540e73b232051fbad59caf1c8ce4f465","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/127b6ce8540e73b232051fbad59caf1c8ce4f465"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/351b3a747ab65c288ee45141b0722d67c44dafd7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T10:51:35Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T10:51:35Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"probe(stage-7b): close Q-009 — reference IMS handling under --no-etag\n\nNew probe `last-modified-roundtrip.json` (6 requests, `serveArgs: [\"--no-etag\"]`)\nrecords pinned reference behavior:\n- `first_get` — `Last-Modified` present, `ETag` absent (mutex per\n  `serve-handler/src/index.js:227-236`).\n- `ims_exact` (via `$fromResponse` capture-replay), `ims_future`,\n  `ims_past`, `ims_malformed` — all return 200 with the full body.\n  Confirms `serve-handler/src/index.js:758-765` only branches on\n  `if-none-match`; there is no `if-modified-since` branch.\n- `ims_on_404` — 404 unchanged; IMS is inert on missing files.\n\nQ-009 closed (open-questions.md) with the snapshot citation;\nSRV-CACHE-003 flipped `unknown` → `verified` in inventory.md.\nCompatibility notes anticipate D-018 (Stage 7b slice 3): irserve\nwill short-circuit to 304 on IMS ≥ floor(mtime, sec) under\n`--no-etag`, a deliberate divergence from the reference''s 200 path.\nSix new ORC rows (ORC-167..ORC-172) record reference behavior;\nslice 3 will promote ORC-167/168/169 to dual-target and pin the\nD-018 divergence in their Layer text.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"650323653fe232b87136075f46c54e08c21a1c6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/650323653fe232b87136075f46c54e08c21a1c6d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/351b3a747ab65c288ee45141b0722d67c44dafd7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_ur