rivacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/c70ac3aee8ccb584f39720d1bc89a9a3e3bf934c","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKGM3MGFjM2FlZThjY2I1ODRmMzk3MjBkMWJjODlhOWEzZTNiZjkzNGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/75f9619fd3d8a15141d0e275ef69b708196dda61","sha":"75f9619fd3d8a15141d0e275ef69b708196dda61","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/75f9619fd3d8a15141d0e275ef69b708196dda61"}],"sha":"c70ac3aee8ccb584f39720d1bc89a9a3e3bf934c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/c70ac3aee8ccb584f39720d1bc89a9a3e3bf934c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/75f9619fd3d8a15141d0e275ef69b708196dda61/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T08:55:42Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T08:55:42Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-7a): address Codex review round 4 (P3 design.md polish)\n\nRound 3 introduced two inaccuracies in design.md §7 that round 4\ncatches:\n\n1. `cargo test -p irserve-core etag` was described as \"etag.rs\n   module tests + the four `dispatch::tests::etag_*` cases\" — 8\n   tests. The filter actually runs **11**: it also matches the\n   two `dispatch::tests::custom_etag_*` cases (which contain\n   the `etag` substring) and `config::tests::etag_field_accepted`.\n\n2. design.md §7 said `dispatch::tests` \"or just `etag`\" can be\n   used for exhaustive 304 coverage. The `etag` filter MISSES\n   `range_present_skips_304_even_on_match` and\n   `no_if_none_match_returns_200` (neither has `etag` in the\n   name) — so it catches 6 of the 8 dispatch 304-related tests,\n   not all 8. Only `dispatch::tests` is exhaustive.\n\nReworded §7 to list three filters precisely, each with its\nactual scope and a note on what it does NOT cover. The\nexhaustive filter for the 304 surface is\n`cargo test -p irserve-core dispatch::tests`; the\nsubstring-based `etag` filter is useful for the 11 tests it\ncatches but not for 304 surface coverage; the narrow\n`dispatch::tests::etag` matches only the 4 `etag_*`-prefixed\ntests and is included for completeness.\n\nNumbers re-verified empirically:\n- `cargo test -p irserve-core etag`: 11 passed.\n- `cargo test -p irserve-core dispatch::tests::etag`: 4 passed.\n- `cargo test -p irserve-core dispatch::tests`: 21 passed\n  (8 of which are 304-related, the rest are encode_* /\n  extension_* siblings).\n\nNo runtime / code change; no behavior change.\n\nVerification: `cargo fmt --check` exit 0;\n`cargo clippy -p irserve-core --all-targets -- -D warnings`\nclean; `npx -y @fission-ai/openspec@latest validate --all\n--strict` 20 of 20.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a65b89a7c80102a8fda7d22a99cfb64cdb4a372b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/a65b89a7c80102a8fda7d22a99cfb64cdb4a372b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/75f9619fd3d8a15141d0e275ef69b708196dda61","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/75f9619fd3d8a15141d0e275ef69b708196dda61","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDc1Zjk2MTlmZDNkOGExNTE0MWQwZTI3NWVmNjliNzA4MTk2ZGRhNjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/be46e60997581e2c3dc11de16f01c0c9df5621f7","sha":"be46e60997581e2c3dc11de16f01c0c9df5621f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/be46e60997581e2c3dc11de16f01c0c9df5621f7"}],"sha":"75f9619fd3d8a15141d0e275ef69b708196dda61","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/75f9619fd3d8a15141d0e275ef69b708196dda61"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/be46e60997581e2c3dc11de16f01c0c9df5621f7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T08:40:44Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T08:40:44Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-7a): address Codex review round 3 (P3 doc polish)\n\nP3.1: the source comment at build_file_or_304 still listed\n\"ETag emission is enabled by config\" as condition (a) for 304.\nAfter round 2''s `etag: false`-plus-user-rule clarification, this\nis wrong — 304 fires whenever the merged response carries an\nETag header, whatever its provenance (default sha1 OR\nuser-supplied via `headers` rule, even when `etag: false`\ndisabled the default). Reworded to \"the merged response carries\nan `ETag` header — either the default sha1 (when\n`serve_config.etag != Some(false)`) OR one supplied by a user\n`headers` rule.\" Runtime behavior unchanged; the comment now\nmatches what the code does (and what the round-2 unit test\n`etag_false_still_honors_custom_rule_and_304` pins).\n\nP3.2: design.md / proposal.md / tasks.md still claimed seven\ndispatch tests (round 2 added an eighth:\n`etag_false_still_honors_custom_rule_and_304`) and quoted a\ncargo filter `dispatch::tests::etag` that only matches the four\n`etag_*`-prefixed tests, not the full 304-decision surface.\nBumped to \"eight\" and replaced the filter claim with:\n- `cargo test -p irserve-core etag` (catches the etag.rs module\n  tests + the four `dispatch::tests::etag_*` cases — 11 total)\n- `cargo test -p irserve-core dispatch::tests` (catches all\n  eight 304-related dispatch tests, including those whose names\n  don''t start with `etag_` — `range_*`, `no_if_*`,\n  `custom_etag_*` — for 21 total when counting the\n  pre-existing extension_* / encode_* siblings).\n\nVerification:\n- `cargo fmt --check`: exit 0.\n- `cargo clippy -p irserve-core --all-targets -- -D warnings`:\n  clean.\n- `cargo test --workspace`: 265 + 18 + 1 (oracle) green.\n- `cargo test -p irserve-core etag`: 11 tests (matches the\n  design.md claim).\n- `cargo test -p irserve-core dispatch::tests`: 21 tests\n  (eight 304-related, as claimed; plus the unchanged\n  encode_*/extension_* siblings).\n- `npx -y @fission-ai/openspec@latest validate --all --strict`:\n  20 of 20 passed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"48af3f9669e07b426ed20c60d13aeedca88566ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/48af3f9669e07b426ed20c60d13aeedca88566ba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/be46e60997581e2c3dc11de16f01c0c9df5621f7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/be46e60997581e2c3dc11de16f01c0c9df5621f7","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKGJlNDZlNjA5OTc1ODFlMmMzZGMxMWRlMTZmMDFjMGM5ZGY1NjIxZjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/2124896e8fd696a10291a7c15a102d23d54705bd","sha":"2124896e8fd696a10291a7c15a102d23d54705bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/2124896e8fd696a10291a7c15a102d23d54705bd"}],"sha":"be46e60997581e2c3dc11de16f01c0c9df5621f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/be46e60997581e2c3dc11de16f01c0c9df5621f7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/2124896e8fd696a10291a7c15a102d23d54705bd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T08:19:36Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T08:19:36Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-7a): address Codex review round 2 (P2 + P3 fixes)\n\nP2 (doc/code drift): the OpenSpec spec, delta, proposal, design,\nand tasks still described the round-1-prior header ordering (\"ETag\ninserted in file_response BEFORE the outer apply_custom_headers\npass\") and pointed at stale dispatch.rs line numbers (:837, :800,\n:818). After 4745014 the real flow is: file_response (default\nETag) → apply_custom_headers INSIDE build_file_or_304 → 304 check\non merged. Synced every doc to that ordering and refreshed line\nreferences (build_file_or_304:687, file_response:637,\netag_value:655). The design.md § 1 code snippet was rewritten to\nshow the round-1 signature + the merge-before-decide pattern;\n§ 4 (ETag vs user `headers` rules) now spells out the dispatcher\nreturning None for headers_path so the outer wrapper does not\nre-apply.\n\nP3 (under-specified `etag: false` semantics with custom rules):\nthe spec said `\"etag\": false` means \"no ETag header, 304 never\nfires.\" This contradicted the reference and irserve''s actual\nbehavior: `serve-handler/src/index.js:227-241` gates only the\n`defaultHeaders[''ETag'']` assignment, then unconditionally merges\n`customHeaders` via `Object.assign(defaultHeaders, related)`, so\na user `headers` rule lands on the response whether or not the\ndefault was suppressed. The 304 check at `:760` then operates on\nthe merged `headers.ETag`. IrServe already matches the reference\nhere — Codex''s manual repro returned 200 + custom ETag, then 304\non replay. Clarified the spec, added a Compatibility note pinning\nthe gate-then-merge ordering, added a new scenario showing the\nuser-override round-trip, and added a unit test\n`dispatch::tests::etag_false_still_honors_custom_rule_and_304`\nlocking the contract.\n\nUpdated the `etag_value` source comment to match.\n\nVerification:\n- `cargo test -p irserve-core`: 265 passed (was 264, +1 for the\n  new P3 unit test).\n- `cargo test --workspace`: green.\n- `cargo clippy -p irserve-core --all-targets -- -D warnings`:\n  clean.\n- `cargo fmt --check`: exit 0.\n- `npx -y @fission-ai/openspec@latest validate --all --strict`:\n  20 of 20 passed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3d57f75efe74fc3af0916a116499c38b6f285721","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/3d57f75efe74fc3af0916a116499c38b6f285721"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/2124896e8fd696a10291a7c15a102d23d54705bd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/2124896e8fd696a10291a7c15a102d23d54705bd","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDIxMjQ4OTZlOGZkNjk2YTEwMjkxYTdjMTVhMTAyZDIzZDU0NzA1YmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/4745014552d96be8fa638a2e8b62e3db3061edfd","sha":"4745014552d96be8fa638a2e8b62e3db3061edfd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/4745014552d96be8fa638a2e8b62e3db3061edfd"}],"sha":"2124896e8fd696a10291a7c15a102d23d54705bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/2124896e8fd696a10291a7c15a102d23d54705bd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/4745014552d96be8fa638a2e8b62e3db3061edfd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T07:50:19Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T07:50:19Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-7a): address Codex review round 1 (P1 + P2 + P3 fixes)\n\nP1 (correctness): user `serve.json#headers` rules can override or\ndelete ETag, but the 304 short-circuit was comparing `If-None-Match`\nagainst the DEFAULT sha1, not the merged value. Reference behavior is\ngetHeaders-then-304-check at `serve-handler/src/index.js:241, 760`.\nRestructured `build_file_or_304` to run `apply_custom_headers`\ninline before the 304 decision; both call sites in `dispatch_inner`\nnow signal `None` for `headers_path` so the outer wrapper does not\ndouble-apply. Two new unit tests pin: (a) `ETag: \"custom\"` rule →\nreplay of `\"custom\"` returns 304, replay of default sha1 returns\n200; (b) `value: null` ETag delete → no ETag emitted, 304 never\nfires (mirrors SRV-HDR-002 prune).\n\nP2 (lint): `clippy::items-after-test-module` was failing\n`cargo clippy -p irserve-core --all-targets -- -D warnings`. The\nnew `file_response` / `etag_value` / `build_file_or_304` helpers\nlanded below `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` in slices 2-3. Moved them\nabove the test module.\n\nP3 (doc staleness): `docs/stage7_l3_capabilities.md` claimed 7b\nwould wire the `etag: bool` config field, calling it\n\"parsed-and-ignored\". Stage 7a''s slice 2 already wired it; 7b only\nneeds to add the `--no-etag` CLI flag. Updated the 7b row and\nmarked the 7a row done with a brief summary of what landed.\n\nAlso: `cargo fmt --all` to clear the workspace fmt-check backlog.\nThe Stage 7a files (`dispatch.rs`, `etag.rs`) plus three\npre-existing fmt issues (`cors.rs`, `server.rs`, `listen_spec.rs`)\nare now formatted. Folded into this commit because the Codex review\nflagged `cargo fmt --check` as failing alongside Stage 7a-specific\nissues.\n\nVerification:\n- `cargo test --workspace`: 264 + 18 + 1 (oracle) tests, all pass.\n- `cargo clippy -p irserve-core --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo test -p irserve --test oracle`: 75 passed / 6 skipped / 0\n  failed under `target=irserve` (unchanged from Stage 7a close).\n- `cargo fmt --check`: exit 0.\n- `npx -y @fission-ai/openspec@latest validate --all --strict`:\n  20 of 20 passed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2508f413698bacef92f8088cb881522cbf4eac0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/2508f413698bacef92f8088cb881522cbf4eac0f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/4745014552d96be8fa638a2e8b62e3db3061edfd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/4745014552d96be8fa638a2e8b62e3db3061edfd","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDQ3NDUwMTQ1NTJkOTZiZThmYTYzOGEyZThiNjJlM2RiMzA2MWVkZmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/2276cc2c24157cb6c9962f13e7b424576c8c4733","sha":"2276cc2c24157cb6c9962f13e7b424576c8c4733","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/2276cc2c24157cb6c9962f13e7b424576c8c4733"}],"sha":"4745014552d96be8fa638a2e8b62e3db3061edfd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/4745014552d96be8fa638a2e8b62e3db3061edfd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/2276cc2c24157cb6c9962f13e7b424576c8c4733/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T07:27:25Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T07:27:25Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-7a): slice 5 — spec deltas + D-017 + ORC flips + README\n\nCloses Stage 7a. The implementation slices 1-4 land the etag module,\n200 emission, 304 short-circuit, and probe-runner capture-replay; this\nslice ships the spec / decisions / docs surface so the change is\ncontractually anchored.\n\n- `openspec/changes/011-etag-conditional/` — proposal + design +\n  tasks + ADDED delta against the new `http-cache` capability.\n- `openspec/specs/http-cache/spec.md` — first L3 capability spec.\n  One requirement keyed to SRV-CACHE-001, two scenarios, four\n  Compatibility notes (hash-function divergence allowance, ETag on\n  custom error pages deferred, Range guard rationale, no-etag CLI\n  flag deferred to 7b, in-memory cache as future-not-contractual).\n- `docs/reference/serve/decisions.md` — D-017 records the hash\n  formula choice (sha1 of `extname + ''-'' + contents`) and what is\n  / is NOT contractual (round-trip yes, hex value no).\n- `docs/reference/serve/oracle-matrix.md` — ORC-042 / ORC-043\n  promoted to dual-target via the `etag-roundtrip` `runner.l0.clean`\n  partition + the probe runner''s `$fromResponse` capture-replay.\n- `README.md` — Stage 7a row → done; \"Try IrServe\" gains an\n  ETag/304 demo; \"What is NOT yet observable\" no longer lists\n  `ETag`/conditional GETs.\n\nOpenSpec validation: `npx -y @fission-ai/openspec@latest validate\n--all --strict` → 20 of 20 passed, 0 failed.\n\nDelegated to a subagent per the kickoff-template subagent-delegation\npattern; main agent reviewed the output before committing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"770e96c9eff5a7039836efb45055d8a33e8fbb8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/770e96c9eff5a7039836efb45055d8a33e8fbb8a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/2276cc2c24157cb6c9962f13e7b424576c8c4733","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/2276cc2c24157cb6c9962f13e7b424576c8c4733","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDIyNzZjYzJjMjQxNTdjYjZjOTk2MmYxM2U3YjQyNDU3NmM4YzQ3MzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/1b7758c467deb4ce4af2f59f648226d14f553f52","sha":"1b7758c467deb4ce4af2f59f648226d14f553f52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/1b7758c467deb4ce4af2f59f648226d14f553f52"}],"sha":"2276cc2c24157cb6c9962f13e7b424576c8c4733","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/2276cc2c24157cb6c9962f13e7b424576c8c4733"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/1b7758c467deb4ce4af2f59f648226d14f553f52/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T07:19:40Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T07:19:40Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"feat(stage-7a): slice 4 — probe runner capture-replay for round-trip cases\n\nExtends the case-file request-header value type: a value may be either\na literal string OR a `$fromResponse` object that the runner resolves\nat request time by reading a named header from a prior request''s\nresponse. The wire sees the resolved string; the snapshot records the\nsymbolic form so the recording stays hash-/timestamp-agnostic across\nreference and irserve targets.\n\nThe new mechanism is reusable for Stage 7b (Last-Modified →\nIf-Modified-Since) and Stage 7c (If-Range). One investment,\nmulti-stage payback.\n\n`etag-roundtrip.json`:\n- second_with_inm.if-none-match now uses\n  `$fromResponse(first_get, etag)`.\n- Adds `runner.l0.clean = [first_get, second_with_inm]` flipping\n  ORC-042 and ORC-043 to dual-target.\n- Reference snapshot re-recorded; the captured ETag bytes match\n  irserve''s (we mirror the sha1 formula).\n\n`etag-conditional.json`:\n- Adds `runner.l0` partition with\n  `contentLengthMayDiffer = [first_get, if_none_match_bogus]` —\n  irserve emits `content-length: 0` on the cleanUrls 301 while the\n  reference omits the header. Pre-existing transport detail, not\n  Stage 7a contract.\n\nOracle harness: target=irserve goes from 73 passed / 8 skipped to\n75 passed / 6 skipped; target=reference still 81/81.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b8b8388838608b9d1c2c06a276fc1c2d78118833","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/b8b8388838608b9d1c2c06a276fc1c2d78118833"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/1b7758c467deb4ce4af2f59f648226d14f553f52","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/1b7758c467deb4ce4af2f59f648226d14f553f52","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDFiNzc1OGM0NjdkZWI0Y2U0YWYyZjU5ZjY0ODIyNmQxNGY1NTNmNTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/7d32663d3786309cfa59a03830488293b6f97da6","sha":"7d32663d3786309cfa59a03830488293b6f97da6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/7d32663d3786309cfa59a03830488293b6f97da6"}],"sha":"1b7758c467deb4ce4af2f59f648226d14f553f52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/1b7758c467deb4ce4af2f59f648226d14f553f52"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/7d32663d3786309cfa59a03830488293b6f97da6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T07:13:21Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T07:13:21Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"feat(stage-7a): slice 3 — 304 short-circuit on If-None-Match match\n\nAdds `build_file_or_304` helper between the dispatcher''s file-response\ncall sites and `file_response`. When ETag emission is enabled, the\nrequest carries no `Range` header, and `If-None-Match` matches the\ncomputed ETag verbatim, the helper returns a fresh 304 response with\nno body, no Content-Type, and no ETag echo — mirroring\n`serve-handler/src/index.js:760-765`.\n\nMatch is exact string equality on the strong-quoted form. No\nweak/strong distinction, no comma-list, no `*` — reference uses `===`\non `headers.ETag` vs `request.headers[''if-none-match'']`.\n\nThe `Range`-absent guard is a Stage 7c precursor; Range parsing\n(206/416) lands there, but the guard goes in now so 7c doesn''t have\nto revisit this code.\n\nFive unit tests in `dispatch::tests`: (a) match → 304, (b) mismatch\n→ 200, (c) Range present + match → 200, (d) etag=false config → no\nETag emission ever, (e) absent If-None-Match → 200. Oracle harness\nstill 73/73 L0 pass; the two etag-* probes remain skipped (no L0\npartition declared — flip lands in slice 4).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b111b6c2131969f277f843d4e499ec495a522fe0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/b111b6c2131969f277f843d4e499ec495a522fe0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/7d32663d3786309cfa59a03830488293b6f97da6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/7d32663d3786309cfa59a03830488293b6f97da6","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDdkMzI2NjNkMzc4NjMwOWNmYTU5YTAzODMwNDg4MjkzYjZmOTdkYTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/63330cd806adfba44d26bc5c6c3c28f6d174d1ac","sha":"63330cd806adfba44d26bc5c6c3c28f6d174d1ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/63330cd806adfba44d26bc5c6c3c28f6d174d1ac"}],"sha":"7d32663d3786309cfa59a03830488293b6f97da6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/7d32663d3786309cfa59a03830488293b6f97da6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/63330cd806adfba44d26bc5c6c3c28f6d174d1ac/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T07:10:29Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T07:10:29Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"feat(stage-7a): slice 2 — emit ETag header on 200 file responses\n\nWires `compute_etag` into both file-response call sites in\n`dispatch.rs`: the File/Index arm (line ~320) and the renderSingle\nshort-circuit (line ~430). New `etag_value` helper centralizes the\non/off decision — irserve''s CLI default is `etag=true` (mirrors\n`vercel/serve/source/main.ts`); only an explicit `\"etag\": false` in\n`serve.json` disables emission.\n\n`file_response` signature gains `etag: Option<HeaderValue>` and\ninserts it after `Content-Type` when `Some`. Directory listings, 3xx\nredirects, and error responses are unaffected — they go through\ndifferent code paths.\n\nNo 304 logic yet (slice 3). Oracle harness 73/73 L0 pass; the new\nETag header is automatically masked by `L0_EXTRA_VOLATILE_HEADERS`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"987bcc2135335e2c7419448d0e730432ac050795","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/987bcc2135335e2c7419448d0e730432ac050795"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/63330cd806adfba44d26bc5c6c3c28f6d174d1ac","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/63330cd806adfba44d26bc5c6c3c28f6d174d1ac","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDYzMzMwY2Q4MDZhZGZiYTQ0ZDI2YmM1YzZjM2MyOGY2ZDE3NGQxYWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/9521ec4f4150c6427eb38e3ea2959de7832a3c02","sha":"9521ec4f4150c6427eb38e3ea2959de7832a3c02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/9521ec4f4150c6427eb38e3ea2959de7832a3c02"}],"sha":"63330cd806adfba44d26bc5c6c3c28f6d174d1ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/63330cd806adfba44d26bc5c6c3c28f6d174d1ac"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/9521ec4f4150c6427eb38e3ea2959de7832a3c02/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T07:08:30Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T07:08:30Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"feat(stage-7a): slice 1 — etag module mirroring reference formula\n\nAdds `crates/irserve-core/src/etag.rs` with `compute_etag(path, bytes)`\ncomputing `sha1(extname + ''-'' + contents)` per\n`third_party/serve-handler/src/index.js:24-36`. Returned as the\nquoted strong-ETag string `\"<40 hex chars>\"`.\n\nUnit test pins byte-equality with the reference snapshot: the fixture\n`body{color:red}\\n` named `asset.css` hashes to\n`3638b78821a961fcf35969f0bc67cc5944d64a0b`, matching\n`tools/probe/snapshots/etag-roundtrip.json`.\n\nNot wired into responses yet (slice 2). `#[cfg_attr(not(test),\nallow(dead_code))]` silences the temporary unused-function warning.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"24bb6c4c4b5be05ef23d8cb7a6794d2747f35d15","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/24bb6c4c4b5be05ef23d8cb7a6794d2747f35d15"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/9521ec4f4150c6427eb38e3ea2959de7832a3c02","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/9521ec4f4150c6427eb38e3ea2959de7832a3c02","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDk1MjFlYzRmNDE1MGM2NDI3ZWIzOGUzZWEyOTU5ZGU3ODMyYTNjMDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/ebcb9740a998f50d359aa9337a0931a36783f3a2","sha":"ebcb9740a998f50d359aa9337a0931a36783f3a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/ebcb9740a998f50d359aa9337a0931a36783f3a2"}],"sha":"9521ec4f4150c6427eb38e3ea2959de7832a3c02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/9521ec4f4150c6427eb38e3ea2959de7832a3c02"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/ebcb9740a998f50d359aa9337a0931a36783f3a2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T07:05:55Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T07:05:55Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-7a): plan for ETag + 304 conditional GET\n\nCaptures decisions D1-D3 (sha1 mirror of reference, capture-replay in\nprobe runner, default etag=true), the 8 small technical decisions taken\nwithout asking, the 5-slice implementation plan, and the mandatory\npre-stage out-of-scope list per anti-hallucination rule #10.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9477f6f1b694c25d90b97a54f8e4b0e9c48a3b4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/9477f6f1b694c25d90b97a54f8e4b0e9c48a3b4b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/ebcb9740a998f50d359aa9337a0931a36783f3a2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/ebcb9740a998f50d359aa9337a0931a36783f3a2","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKGViY2I5NzQwYTk5OGY1MGQzNTlhYTkzMzdhMDkzMWEzNjc4M2YzYTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/795f10b7fd0a056b6d10049e575efff238869c3a","sha":"795f10b7fd0a056b6d10049e575efff238869c3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/795f10b7fd0a056b6d10049e575efff238869c3a"}],"sha":"ebcb9740a998f50d359aa9337a0931a36783f3a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/ebcb9740a998f50d359aa9337a0931a36783f3a2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/795f10b7fd0a056b6d10049e575efff238869c3a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T06:45:25Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T06:45:25Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-7): decomposition + README roadmap rows\n\nPre-stage scaffolding for Stage 7 (L3 polish). Author the canonical\nsub-stage breakdown so 7a-7e can be planned and delivered one-by-one\nthe same way 6a-6h were.\n\n`docs/stage7_l3_capabilities.md` (NEW, mirrors the structure of\n`docs/stage6_l1_l2_capabilities.md`):\n- 7a — ETag + 304 If-None-Match (SRV-CACHE-001, P0).\n- 7b — `Last-Modified` + `--no-etag` + `If-Modified-Since`\n  (SRV-CACHE-002/003 + SRV-CLI-013, P1; closes Q-009). Depends on 7a.\n- 7c — Range requests 206/416 (SRV-CACHE-004, P2).\n- 7d — `Cache-Control` default + `OPTIONS` (CORS preflight)\n  (SRV-CACHE-005 + SRV-CORS-001 preflight policy).\n- 7e — HTTP compression (`-u`/`--no-compression`; SRV-CLI-012,\n  P2; closes Q-002).\n\nMethodological signals flagged up front:\n- 7a hash function divergence (D-NNN candidate; reference uses\n  `sha1(extname + ''-'' + fileContents)` but only the round-trip is\n  contractual).\n- 7b If-Modified-Since semantics unknown in source — anti-hallucination\n  rule #8 mandates probe-first.\n- 7d preflight pass-through vs 204 short-circuit decision.\n- 7e compression library emulation is the biggest risk in Stage 7\n  (anti-hallucination #8 zone); pre-stage out-of-scope list is\n  mandatory before slice 1.\n\nOut of scope (deferred to L4 or beyond): `-S`/`--symlinks` and\nSRV-SYM-001, `--ssl-*`, SRV-WIN-001, cleanUrls extglob (Q-012),\nterminal-output polish (D-002).\n\n`README.md`:\n- Replace the single `| 7 | Polish ... | todo |` row with five rows\n  7a-7e, each pointing at its prospective change package\n  (`011-etag-conditional` ... `015-compression`).\n- Update the cross-reference paragraph: Stage 7 now has its own\n  canonical detail document; L4 stays out of scope until prioritized.\n\n`docs/commands/stage_kickoff_template.md`:\n- Generalize from \"Stage 6 only\" to \"Stage 6/7 onward\": header\n  mentions 6a-6h done + 7a-7e next; roadmap pointer accepts either\n  file; placeholders flipped from `{6X}` to `{NX}`; review-commit\n  title example covers both stages; plan-file convention bumped\n  to `0001..0014`.\n\nNo code or oracle changes; commit is pure scaffolding for the next\ngroup of stages.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8f577dbe5c765cad79749759dc0a90567d83ac42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/8f577dbe5c765cad79749759dc0a90567d83ac42"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/795f10b7fd0a056b6d10049e575efff238869c3a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_ur