pi.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/db5918b7e41b69b1903b873319ba8bca6590d9d3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T21:37:20Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T21:37:20Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-6h): address Codex review round 3 (P2 + P3 fixes)\n\nP2 (proposal.md leftover pre-round-1 surface).\nThe \"Runner gate fully drained\" bullet still listed five new probes,\nomitting the round-1 follow-on `cors-user-override`. The\n`cors-on-redirect` line still said `→ 301`, contradicting the\nprobe (which sets `type: 302` and records `status=302` in\nORC-165). The \"Final oracle\" line still pinned the pre-round-1\ncounts (`total=80 passed=72`, reference 80/80).\n\nUpdated to \"Six new probe cases\" with the round-1 `cors-user-override`\nlisted as the sixth, the cors-on-redirect line corrected to `→ 302`\nwith the explicit `type: 302` redirect rule, and the final oracle\ncounts flipped to `total=81 passed=73 skipped=8 failed=0` /\nreference 81/81.\n\nP3 (tcp:// still classified as malformed; stale expected-delta).\n- 0014_PLAN slice-1 unit-test list still listed `tcp://` under\n  \"malformed (`tcp://`, `tcp://host:notnum`)\". The parser actually\n  accepts `tcp://` as the both-defaults case (Q-001 closure:\n  host=`localhost`, port=`3000`), so the test fixture sits in\n  `parses_tcp_both_defaults_q001`, not in the malformed bucket.\n  Reclassified to match the round-1 fix already applied to\n  tasks.md.\n- design.md §1 had the same listing; reclassified the same way.\n- 0014_PLAN''s \"Expected delta\" block at the end of the verification\n  section still said `+5 new probes / 0 reference snapshot changes`\n  and omitted both the round-1 follow-on probe and the final\n  oracle counts. Rewritten to describe the post-round-1 state:\n  six new probes, no existing-snapshot churn, six new reference\n  snapshots, final 81/73 + 81/81 counts.\n\nTasks.md and design.md \"Validation\" / \"Verification\" subsections\nalso still showed the pre-round-1 oracle counts (`total=80\npassed=72`, reference 80/80). Updated to 81/73 + 81/81 with a\nnote that the +1 is the round-1 `cors-user-override` probe and\nthe four CORS unit tests now include the round-1\n`preserves_user_set_header` flip of the prior\n`overwrites_existing_header` test.\n\nVerification: openspec validate --all --strict 18 passed, 0 failed.\nOracle harness unchanged (round 3 is doc-only): target=irserve\ntotal=81 passed=73 skipped=8 failed=0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1c29cc6edd36627e05ad238514031c85fb4f9191","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/1c29cc6edd36627e05ad238514031c85fb4f9191"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/db5918b7e41b69b1903b873319ba8bca6590d9d3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/db5918b7e41b69b1903b873319ba8bca6590d9d3","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKGRiNTkxOGI3ZTQxYjY5YjE5MDNiODczMzE5YmE4YmNhNjU5MGQ5ZDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/6e89cd84cdfd2c5efcfe308f4ade9b1b8c35b480","sha":"6e89cd84cdfd2c5efcfe308f4ade9b1b8c35b480","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/6e89cd84cdfd2c5efcfe308f4ade9b1b8c35b480"}],"sha":"db5918b7e41b69b1903b873319ba8bca6590d9d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/db5918b7e41b69b1903b873319ba8bca6590d9d3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/6e89cd84cdfd2c5efcfe308f4ade9b1b8c35b480/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T21:30:02Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T21:30:02Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-6h): address Codex review round 2 (P2 fixes)\n\nP2-1 (change-package + plan still describe pre-round-1 CORS contract).\nCodex round 1 corrected the `apply_cors` semantics from\noverwrite-everything to set-only-if-missing, but the prose in\nproposal.md, design.md, tasks.md (slice 3), and the kickoff plan\n0014_PLAN_stage6h_cli_fill_in.md still asserted the old shape:\n\"inserts all four headers unconditionally\", \"user CORS headers are\noverwritten by `*`\", \"the reference does the overwrite\". The mismatch\nrisked the next agent re-introducing the round-1 bug.\n\nUpdated all four documents to describe set-only-if-missing semantics\n+ the per-key user-rule-wins behavior, citing the\nserve.ts:65-70 / index.js:245-251 / index.js:767 ordering. Tasks.md\nslice 3 now references the round-1 follow-on probe\n(`cors-user-override`) and the renamed unit test\n(`preserves_user_set_header`).\n\nP2-2 (cors-on-redirect Scenario pinned 301; probe and ORC are 302).\nThe probe `cors-on-redirect.json` explicitly sets `type: 302` in the\nserve.json redirect, and the recorded snapshot / ORC-165 both record\n`status=302`. The spec delta''s \"All four CORS headers on a 3xx\nredirect\" Scenario contradicted that with `THEN status is 301`.\nUpdated the Scenario''s GIVEN to include the explicit `type: 302`\nredirect rule and flipped the THEN to `302`. Same flip in the\n0014_PLAN walkthrough''s slice-3 manual smoke (the Set-Content +\ncurl pair).\n\nVerification: openspec validate --all --strict 18 passed, 0 failed.\nOracle harness target=irserve total=81 passed=73 skipped=8 failed=0\n(unchanged — round 2 is doc-only).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"aa07991ec165ed386967b3910bfb54baf363cea9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/aa07991ec165ed386967b3910bfb54baf363cea9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/6e89cd84cdfd2c5efcfe308f4ade9b1b8c35b480","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/6e89cd84cdfd2c5efcfe308f4ade9b1b8c35b480","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDZlODljZDg0Y2RmZDJjNWVmY2ZlMzA4ZjRhZGU5YjFiOGMzNWI0ODA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/6d53924fcea6be9d49284bb4718b9af2235df1c7","sha":"6d53924fcea6be9d49284bb4718b9af2235df1c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/6d53924fcea6be9d49284bb4718b9af2235df1c7"}],"sha":"6e89cd84cdfd2c5efcfe308f4ade9b1b8c35b480","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/6e89cd84cdfd2c5efcfe308f4ade9b1b8c35b480"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/6d53924fcea6be9d49284bb4718b9af2235df1c7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T21:19:53Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T21:19:53Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-6h): address Codex review round 1 (P1 + P2 + P3 fixes)\n\nP1 (--cors overwriting user serve.json#headers values).\nSlice 3 mis-modeled reference''s setHeader order. The reference''s\n`server.ts:65-70` setHeader(''ACAO'',''*'') runs BEFORE serve-handler;\nserve-handler then merges user `headers` rules via\n`Object.assign(defaultHeaders, related)` (`serve-handler/src/index.js:245`)\nand writes via `response.setHeader` (`:767`), so a user rule for any\nof the four CORS keys WINS. Empirically confirmed: reference returned\n`access-control-allow-origin: https://example.test` while irserve\nreturned `*`.\n\nFix: `apply_cors` switches to set-only-if-missing semantics — each\nCORS default fills in only when the response does not already carry\nthat header from `apply_custom_headers`. The other three defaults\nstill fill in when only one is overridden. Unit test\n`overwrites_existing_header` flipped to `preserves_user_set_header`.\nNew regression probe `cors-user-override.json` (`**/*.css` rule sets\n`access-control-allow-origin: https://example.test`; the value\nsurvives, the other three fill in). Spec delta wording flipped:\n\"header overwrite\" Note → \"user-rule precedence\" Note; added\nexplicit Scenario for the override case.\n\nP2 (oracle-matrix.md missing ORC-163/164 + new CORS rows).\nSpec delta cited ORC-163 / ORC-164 but `oracle-matrix.md` had no\nmatching rows. Added:\n- ORC-163 (cli-tcp-uri, L1) — verifies SRV-CLI-003.\n- ORC-164 (cli-p-alias, L1) — verifies SRV-CLI-006.\n- ORC-165 (cors-on-redirect, L3-disputed) — verifies SRV-CLI-010\n  CORS-on-3xx.\n- ORC-166 (cors-user-override, L3-disputed) — verifies SRV-CLI-010\n  user-rule precedence + SRV-HDR-001.\n\nCoverage gaps section updated: SRV-CLI-003 and SRV-CLI-006 entries\nstruck-through with closure pointers; SRV-CLI-016 entry rewritten to\nreflect the D-016 promotion to `adapted` and unit-test verification.\n\nP3 (tasks.md mis-classified `tcp://` as malformed).\nSlice 1''s task list listed `tcp://` under \"malformed (`tcp://`,\n`tcp://host:notnum`)\", but the parser accepts it as the\nboth-defaults case (Q-001 closure: host=`localhost`, port=`3000`).\nReclassified the test list to separate the both-defaults case from\nthe malformed/rejected ones.\n\nVerification: cargo test --workspace passes; oracle harness\ntotal=81 passed=73 skipped=8 failed=0; openspec validate --all\n--strict 18 passed, 0 failed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"14d25eda8d17466b45a00ffcab801bab6d9a60fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/14d25eda8d17466b45a00ffcab801bab6d9a60fa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/6d53924fcea6be9d49284bb4718b9af2235df1c7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/6d53924fcea6be9d49284bb4718b9af2235df1c7","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDZkNTM5MjRmY2VhNmJlOWQ0OTI4NGJiNDcxOGI5YWYyMjM1ZGYxYzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/d943ce396b142469472e6a5e78325a8a1f7c447b","sha":"d943ce396b142469472e6a5e78325a8a1f7c447b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/d943ce396b142469472e6a5e78325a8a1f7c447b"}],"sha":"6d53924fcea6be9d49284bb4718b9af2235df1c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/6d53924fcea6be9d49284bb4718b9af2235df1c7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/d943ce396b142469472e6a5e78325a8a1f7c447b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T21:01:05Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T21:01:05Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-6h): spec deltas + D-016 + Q-001 closure + meta\n\nAuthor the openspec change package `010-cli-fill-in` (proposal /\ndesign / tasks / cli MOD spec delta) capturing the six SRVs delivered\nby slices 1-5 (SRV-CLI-003 / -006 / -010 / -014 / -015 / -016).\n\nStatus flips and Notes:\n- SRV-CLI-003 (tcp:// URI): accepted → verified. Q-001 closure folded\n  into a Note: defaults host=`localhost`, port=`3000`, citing\n  `cli.ts:128-130`.\n- SRV-CLI-006 (-p alias): accepted → verified.\n- SRV-CLI-010 (--cors): wording tightened to enumerate all four\n  reference headers explicitly. New \"CORS on redirects\" Scenario.\n- SRV-CLI-014 (--debug): adapted (no flip). Note documents the\n  elapsed-ms suffix as implementation-defined.\n- SRV-CLI-015 (--no-request-logging): adapted. Silencing effect made\n  contractual; format implementation-defined per D-002.\n- SRV-CLI-016 (--no-port-switching): accepted → adapted per D-016.\n  Default-retry Scenario added; refuse-fallback Scenario kept.\n  Compatibility Note records the upstream divergence\n  (vercel/serve#751).\n\nD-016 records the contract divergence: reference declares\n`--no-port-switching` at `cli.ts:158` but `server.ts:166-181` never\nreads it (regression introduced in v14.0.0; v13.0.4 worked). irserve\nhonors the documented contract under D-004''s no-bug-for-bug-parity\nauthorization. D-002 lightly amended to clarify that SRV-CLI-016''s\nbind/exit behavior IS contractual; only the warning/error wording is\nimplementation-defined.\n\nQ-001 marked closed in open-questions.md, pointing at the SRV-CLI-003\nNote.\n\nRoadmap and README:\n- `docs/stage6_l1_l2_capabilities.md` 6h row: name flipped to\n  `CLI fill-in (done — 010-cli-fill-in)`; closing-notes column\n  references the new D-016.\n- `README.md` stage map row 6h → `done`; status bullet appended;\n  \"Try IrServe\" header bumped to `(post-6h)`; long-prose paragraph\n  extended with the Stage-6h SRV surface; five new flag example\n  blocks (`tcp://`, `-p`, `--cors`, `--no-port-switching`,\n  `--debug`/`--no-request-logging`); \"What is NOT yet observable\"\n  trimmed to L3-only, obsolete `--no-port-switching` deferred-flag\n  example removed.\n\nValidation: `npx -y @fission-ai/openspec@latest validate --all\n--strict` → 18 passed, 0 failed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c516600530ae61adc3bddb40b6daf96bed839290","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/c516600530ae61adc3bddb40b6daf96bed839290"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/d943ce396b142469472e6a5e78325a8a1f7c447b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/d943ce396b142469472e6a5e78325a8a1f7c447b","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKGQ5NDNjZTM5NmIxNDI0Njk0NzJlNmE1ZTc4MzI1YThhMWY3YzQ0N2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/866521aed3a8341a59e7a825f74494febc990cbd","sha":"866521aed3a8341a59e7a825f74494febc990cbd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/866521aed3a8341a59e7a825f74494febc990cbd"}],"sha":"d943ce396b142469472e6a5e78325a8a1f7c447b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/d943ce396b142469472e6a5e78325a8a1f7c447b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/866521aed3a8341a59e7a825f74494febc990cbd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T20:43:33Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T20:43:33Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"feat(stage-6h): slice 5 — --debug + --no-request-logging + per-request log\n\nImplement SRV-CLI-014 / SRV-CLI-015 as a minimal stdout per-request log\ngated by both flags. Both default to off, so existing scripts that don''t\nopt in to either flag see the new log line — but per D-002 (terminal\noutput not contractual), the snapshot envelope already strips stdout/stderr\nfrom probe diffs, so no probe is sensitive to the change.\n\nFormat (implementation-defined):\n  default:               GET /path -> 200\n  --debug:               GET /path -> 200 (Xms)\n  --no-request-logging:  (silent)\n\nWiring:\n- `Cli::debug` (`-d`/`--debug`) and `Cli::no_request_logging`\n  (`-L`/`--no-request-logging`); `ServerConfig::{debug, no_request_logging}`;\n  `AppState::{debug, no_request_logging}`.\n- `handler` captures method/path before `dispatch` consumes the request\n  (Body cannot be cloned), times the dispatch only when `debug` is set,\n  and emits the line after `apply_cors`. Silenced when `no_request_logging`.\n- Drop `-d`, `--debug`, `-L`, `--no-request-logging` from\n  `L0_DEFERRED_FLAGS`. The set is now empty; all stage-6h flags accepted.\n\nProbes:\n- `cli-debug-flag` (acceptance): `--debug` accepted; HTTP 200 unchanged.\n- `cli-no-request-logging` (acceptance): same shape with `--no-request-logging`.\n\nVerified manually that the three modes emit the expected log lines.\nOracle harness: total=80 passed=72 skipped=8.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d0e06a0874c0f07803ee65e1015373012c322d51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/d0e06a0874c0f07803ee65e1015373012c322d51"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/866521aed3a8341a59e7a825f74494febc990cbd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/866521aed3a8341a59e7a825f74494febc990cbd","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDg2NjUyMWFlZDNhODM0MWE1OWU3YTgyNWY3NDQ5NGZlYmM5OTBjYmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/296142c392379285d5ed30ca71a8bffbf02c79a2","sha":"296142c392379285d5ed30ca71a8bffbf02c79a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/296142c392379285d5ed30ca71a8bffbf02c79a2"}],"sha":"866521aed3a8341a59e7a825f74494febc990cbd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/866521aed3a8341a59e7a825f74494febc990cbd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/296142c392379285d5ed30ca71a8bffbf02c79a2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T20:39:38Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T20:39:38Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"feat(stage-6h): slice 4 — port-switching default + --no-port-switching contract (D-016)\n\nImplement SRV-CLI-016 per the documented contract: by default a busy\nlisten address falls back to an ephemeral port; with `--no-port-switching`\nthe bind failure is fatal. The reference declares the flag at\n`third_party/serve/source/utilities/cli.ts:158` but never reads it\n(vercel/serve#751, regression in v14.0.0). irserve corrects the bug per\nD-016, authorized by D-004 (no bug-for-bug parity).\n\nWiring:\n- New `Error::PortInUse { addr }` variant; existing `Io` arm unchanged.\n- `bind_with_fallback(addr, allow_switching)` catches `ErrorKind::AddrInUse`\n  and either retries on `(addr.ip(), 0)` or surfaces `PortInUse`. All\n  other I/O errors propagate. Stderr emits a one-liner on retry / refusal\n  (format implementation-defined per D-002).\n- `ServerConfig::no_port_switching: bool`; `Cli::no_port_switching`\n  (long-only, no short alias — matches reference).\n- Drop `--no-port-switching` from `L0_DEFERRED_FLAGS`. irserve does NOT\n  receive the runner''s auto-injected `--no-port-switching` (the runner\n  always picks a free port; default retry is unobservable). The reference\n  still gets it injected on every spawn, where it''s a no-op (per the bug)\n  but harmless.\n\nVerification:\n- Three integration tests in `crates/irserve-core/src/server.rs::tests`:\n  retry-on-busy when switching allowed (different port returned), fatal\n  PortInUse when switching disabled, success on a free port.\n- Probe coverage of the busy-port failure mode is intentionally omitted —\n  pre-binding a port from the runner is harder than the case is worth.\n  Document this in SRV-CLI-016''s spec Note in slice 6.\n\nOracle harness: total=78 passed=70 skipped=8 (unchanged).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"82ba144e0b8b4dce1e00a2b02104908730e21065","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/82ba144e0b8b4dce1e00a2b02104908730e21065"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/296142c392379285d5ed30ca71a8bffbf02c79a2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/296142c392379285d5ed30ca71a8bffbf02c79a2","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDI5NjE0MmMzOTIzNzkyODVkNWVkMzBjYTcxYThiZmZiZjAyYzc5YTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/ec865ffa81dc6c9793997582da70b8df9b019728","sha":"ec865ffa81dc6c9793997582da70b8df9b019728","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/ec865ffa81dc6c9793997582da70b8df9b019728"}],"sha":"296142c392379285d5ed30ca71a8bffbf02c79a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/296142c392379285d5ed30ca71a8bffbf02c79a2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/ec865ffa81dc6c9793997582da70b8df9b019728/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T20:36:51Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T20:36:51Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"feat(stage-6h): slice 3 — --cors flag + 4-header CORS pass\n\nImplement SRV-CLI-010 end-to-end. The reference''s `--cors` branch sets\nfour headers UNCONDITIONALLY before serve-handler runs\n(third_party/serve/source/utilities/server.ts:65-70):\n- access-control-allow-origin: *\n- access-control-allow-headers: *\n- access-control-allow-credentials: true\n- access-control-allow-private-network: true\n\nPer anti-hallucination rule #4 (oracle > docs), mirror what the snapshot\ncaptures, not the help-text shorthand \"sets ACAO to *\". The roadmap''s\n\"L1 ACAO only\" wording for stage 6h refers to the differentiated CORS\nsurface (preflight, max-age, expose-headers — Stage 7+), not to the\nheader count.\n\nWiring:\n- New `irserve_core::cors::apply_cors` helper inserts the four headers\n  unconditionally on every status. Bypasses the redirect-skip logic in\n  `apply_custom_headers` because reference CORS rides on 3xx too —\n  verified by the new `cors-on-redirect` probe.\n- `ServerConfig::cors: bool`, `AppState::cors`, post-dispatch invocation\n  in `server::handler` (after `dispatch`''s own `apply_custom_headers`,\n  so a user-`headers` rule cannot suppress the flag-driven headers).\n- `Cli::cors` (`-C`/`--cors`) threads through.\n- Drop `-C`/`--cors` from `L0_DEFERRED_FLAGS` and add `runner.l0`\n  partitions to `cors-flag`, `cors-applied`, `cors-response-surface`\n  so they verify against irserve. `cors-flag` and `cors-on-redirect`\n  use `contentLengthMayDiffer` for the redirect anchor — same shape\n  as `_smoke#index_html_redirect` (reference uses chunked transfer\n  encoding on cleanUrls/configured 3xx; irserve sets `content-length: 0`).\n\nOracle harness: total=78 passed=70 skipped=8 (was 11). 4 unit tests\non apply_cors (200, 3xx, 4xx, overwrite-existing).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fef8242df006ccc50597a9cebcfa407d5faf7478","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/fef8242df006ccc50597a9cebcfa407d5faf7478"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/ec865ffa81dc6c9793997582da70b8df9b019728","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/ec865ffa81dc6c9793997582da70b8df9b019728","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKGVjODY1ZmZhODFkYzZjOTc5Mzk5NzU4MmRhNzBiOGRmOWIwMTk3Mjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/04dba9df298c22f307ee343e486a0f55bc273285","sha":"04dba9df298c22f307ee343e486a0f55bc273285","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/04dba9df298c22f307ee343e486a0f55bc273285"}],"sha":"ec865ffa81dc6c9793997582da70b8df9b019728","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/ec865ffa81dc6c9793997582da70b8df9b019728"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/04dba9df298c22f307ee343e486a0f55bc273285/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T20:31:15Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T20:31:15Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"feat(stage-6h): slice 2 — un-defer tcp:// + -p, probe coverage\n\nLift the runner gate for SRV-CLI-003 (`tcp://host:port` URI) and\nSRV-CLI-006 (`-p` deprecated alias):\n- Drop `-p` from `L0_DEFERRED_FLAGS`; remove the `tcp://` listen-value\n  check from `findDeferredL0Flag`.\n- Declare `-p` on `Cli` as a hidden short-only flag with the same\n  `value_parser`/`Append` shape as `--listen`. Clap can''t deposit two\n  distinct flags into the same `Vec`, so we collect into a separate\n  field and merge post-parse — mirrors the reference''s `''-p'': ''--listen''`\n  rewrite at `third_party/serve/source/utilities/cli.ts:176-178`.\n\nProbe wiring needed two small additions:\n- New `runner.defaultPortScenario=\"free-port\"` for cases that own their\n  own `--listen` value (the existing scenarios target SRV-CLI-001''s\n  default-port surface, not value-bearing flags).\n- `{port}` substitution in `serveArgs` so cases like\n  `--listen tcp://127.0.0.1:{port}` and `-p {port}` can reference the\n  runner-allocated port.\n\nTwo new probes (`cli-tcp-uri`, `cli-p-alias`) record the reference\nsnapshot and pass against irserve. Q-001 default-host/port behavior is\nunit-tested in slice 1 rather than probed (probing the defaults would\nrace with the runner''s own port allocation).\n\nOracle harness now reports total=77 passed=66 skipped=11 failed=0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2cd822d4f5aec918492ca15d31922a496fcb0e8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/2cd822d4f5aec918492ca15d31922a496fcb0e8c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/04dba9df298c22f307ee343e486a0f55bc273285","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/04dba9df298c22f307ee343e486a0f55bc273285","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDA0ZGJhOWRmMjk4YzIyZjMwN2VlMzQzZTQ4NmEwZjU1YmMyNzMyODU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/70369fa73571bef0c311636d97b2657a2f309400","sha":"70369fa73571bef0c311636d97b2657a2f309400","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/70369fa73571bef0c311636d97b2657a2f309400"}],"sha":"04dba9df298c22f307ee343e486a0f55bc273285","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/04dba9df298c22f307ee343e486a0f55bc273285"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/70369fa73571bef0c311636d97b2657a2f309400/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T20:26:16Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T20:26:16Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"feat(stage-6h): slice 1 — ListenSpec type + tcp:// parser\n\nWiden `Cli::listen` from `Vec<u16>` to `Vec<ListenSpec>` to unblock\nSRV-CLI-003 (`tcp://host:port` URI). Hand-rolled parser mirrors the\nreference''s `parseEndpoint` (third_party/serve/source/utilities/cli.ts:104-143)\nwithout pulling in the `url` crate: bare-port fast-path, `tcp://` scheme\nwith Q-001 defaults (host=`localhost`, port=`3000`), IPv6 brackets, and\nfocused rejections for `pipe:` / `unix:` schemes (out of scope this stage).\n\n`resolve()` short-circuits the literal `localhost` to IPv4 loopback so\nbinding stays consistent with the bare-port default on dual-stack Windows\nhosts (where `ToSocketAddrs` may return `::1` first and bind v6-only).\n\nNo probe coverage yet — slice 2 lifts the runner gate and adds\n`cli-tcp-uri` + `cli-p-alias` cases. All existing 64 irserve probes still\npass; 18 new unit tests cover the parser surface.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c09ac3299a9feb2ad41fab2f88e9503d5f35ab51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/c09ac3299a9feb2ad41fab2f88e9503d5f35ab51"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/70369fa73571bef0c311636d97b2657a2f309400","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/co