:48Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-6f): address Codex review round 4 (P2 + P3 fixes)\n\nP2 — headers spec normative text aligned with the implemented\ncontract. The opening SHALL paragraph said \"compiled with the same\nLiteral/Glob/Pattern matcher kernel as redirects/rewrites\" and\n\"custom headers SHALL apply to ... 4xx responses\" — both stale\nafter rounds 1-3. Replaced with:\n- Source compilation is minimatch-only (mirrors sourceMatches\n  without allowSegments at index.js:207); :name is literal `:`,\n  case-sensitive.\n- Apply per branch of sendError''s contract: skip JSON errors,\n  apply on custom <status>.html matched against /<status>.html,\n  apply on fallback HTML matched against request path EXCEPT for\n  traversal/decode 400, force Content-Type after fallback apply,\n  skip 3xx.\n\nP3 — decisions.md D-015 finding 7 still credited the round-1\nMatcher::compile_no_segments helper that round 2 superseded with\nHeaderMatcher. Re-narrated finding 7 to record both rounds: round 1\nadded compile_no_segments, round 2 surfaced its case-insensitive\nLiteral::try_match leak and replaced it with the slim HeaderMatcher\nenum in custom_headers.rs.\n\nNo code changes; openspec validate --all --strict passes 16/16.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b93c307061abb81fec162321c6961a3e5b6dc71b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/b93c307061abb81fec162321c6961a3e5b6dc71b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/f9fa964d1bcc469eaa3a25b9f1c84caf40da9def","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/f9fa964d1bcc469eaa3a25b9f1c84caf40da9def","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKGY5ZmE5NjRkMWJjYzQ2OWVhYTNhMjViOWYxYzg0Y2FmNDBkYTlkZWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/4199d2e71387a1038f4db2f01571ad0919eeb36b","sha":"4199d2e71387a1038f4db2f01571ad0919eeb36b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/4199d2e71387a1038f4db2f01571ad0919eeb36b"}],"sha":"f9fa964d1bcc469eaa3a25b9f1c84caf40da9def","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/f9fa964d1bcc469eaa3a25b9f1c84caf40da9def"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/4199d2e71387a1038f4db2f01571ad0919eeb36b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T15:49:46Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T15:49:46Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-6f): address Codex review round 3 (P1 + P2 fixes)\n\nP1 — custom <status>.html branch always applies user headers:\n- error_response now takes (header_rules, request_path,\n  skip_fallback_headers). The custom-page branch unconditionally\n  applies headers matched against /<status>.html (mirrors\n  reference''s getHeaders(.., errorPage, stats) at index.js:508).\n- The fallback HTML branch honors skip_fallback_headers — round 2\n  passed &[] for traversal/decode 400 sites which suppressed both\n  branches. Round 3 splits the controls so a custom 400.html + `**`\n  rule yields x-error-page: yes even when 400 was triggered by\n  /../package.json.\n\nP1 — fallback HTML force-overrides Content-Type:\n- After apply_custom_headers runs in the fallback branch,\n  error_response forces Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8\n  via response.headers_mut().insert(). Mirrors reference''s order at\n  index.js:519-520 — a user rule with `value: application/x-custom`\n  cannot override a 4xx fallback''s content type. The custom-page\n  branch keeps the merge-with-override semantics matching\n  reference''s Object.assign(defaultHeaders, related).\n\nP2 — success-path header matching uses the lexical resolved URL:\n- dispatch_inner now tracks a lexical_url: String alongside\n  ResolveOutcome rather than deriving the matching path from the\n  canonicalized PathBuf. cleanUrls candidate URLs (/page/index.html,\n  /page.html), rewrite destination strings, and the original url_path\n  flow through the success arm verbatim.\n- The canonical PathBuf is now used only for tokio::fs::read, never\n  for header matching. Fixes the Windows regression where canonicalize\n  folds /ASSET.CSS to /asset.css and admitted matches that reference''s\n  case-sensitive minimatch on the lexical path.relative rejects.\n\nProbe: cases/error-page-400-headers.json (ORC-162) pins that a custom\n400.html carries x-error-page: yes when GET /../package.json triggers\nthe traversal 400. Companion to D-015 which separately pins that the\nfallback HTML branch does NOT carry the same rule''s headers in this\nscenario.\n\nVerification: cargo test -p irserve-core (212 passed); cargo test\n--test oracle (56 passed / 14 skipped / 0 failed); openspec validate\n--all --strict (16/16).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e7870af07c6d693b37167dfb881f175f8ed12e24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/e7870af07c6d693b37167dfb881f175f8ed12e24"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/4199d2e71387a1038f4db2f01571ad0919eeb36b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/4199d2e71387a1038f4db2f01571ad0919eeb36b","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDQxOTlkMmU3MTM4N2ExMDM4ZjRkYjJmMDE1NzFhZDA5MTllZWIzNmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/585b3cad32426db8095d1251b84e696a1d1ccc9c","sha":"585b3cad32426db8095d1251b84e696a1d1ccc9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/585b3cad32426db8095d1251b84e696a1d1ccc9c"}],"sha":"4199d2e71387a1038f4db2f01571ad0919eeb36b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/4199d2e71387a1038f4db2f01571ad0919eeb36b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/585b3cad32426db8095d1251b84e696a1d1ccc9c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T15:14:08Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T15:14:08Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-6f): address Codex review round 2 (P1 + P2 fixes)\n\nP1 — success path matches against resolved file:\n- dispatch_inner now passes the FINAL resolved file path (post-cleanUrls,\n  post-rewrite) to apply_custom_headers via a new\n  url_path_for_resolved_file helper that strips the canonicalized root\n  prefix from the ResolveOutcome::File/Index PathBuf and presents it as\n  a `/foo.html`-form URL. Mirrors getHeaders(.., absolutePath, stats)\n  at index.js:746 where absolutePath reflects findRelated''s update at\n  :622-625. The prior implementation matched against the pre-resolution\n  url_path, missing rules like `**/*.html` for `GET /page` resolving to\n  `/page.html`.\n\nP1 — traversal 400 carries no custom headers:\n- The lexical-escape and URIError-malformed-decode error_response sites\n  now pass `&[]` for header_rules, mirroring reference''s empirical\n  behavior captured in D-015 finding 3 (slasher-normalized\n  outside-root relativePath does not match `**` in practice). The\n  defense-in-depth ResolveOutcome::EscapedRoot arm passes `&[]` too.\n\nP1 — header source match is case-sensitive minimatch only:\n- Replace path_pattern::Matcher reuse with a slim HeaderMatcher enum\n  (Literal / Glob) compiled directly in custom_headers.rs.\n- HeaderMatcher::Literal is case-SENSITIVE (mirrors minimatch''s default\n  `nocase: false`). `:name` and other no-glob sources land here as\n  pure literal strings, matched only via exact equality after\n  path_posix_resolve normalization. Source `/Case` no longer matches\n  `/case`; source `/api/:id` no longer matches `/api/42`.\n- HeaderMatcher::Glob reuses the per-segment match_segments kernel\n  shared with redirects/rewrites for `*`/`?`/`[`/`{`/`!` patterns.\n- Drop Matcher::compile_no_segments from path_pattern.rs (no remaining\n  callers).\n- New regression test: literal_source_is_case_sensitive.\n\nP2 — specs/headers/spec.md aligned with the new implementation:\n- Document the case-sensitive minimatch-only matching contract.\n- Document the resolved-path-not-url-path matching contract for\n  successes.\n- Replace the stale \"two-pass null-prune; early null deletes later\n  value\" prose with the corrected \"single-pass last-write-wins;\n  later non-null wins over earlier null\" semantics.\n- Reference the new HeaderMatcher and the dispatch_inner\n  (Response, Option<String>) contract.\n- Add a new Scenario pinning that an early null does NOT delete a\n  later set value.\n\nProbe coverage:\n- New cases/headers-after-cleanurls.json (ORC-161) pins the\n  resolved-path matching: GET /page resolves to /page.html via\n  cleanUrls and the `**/*.html` rule applies, mirroring reference.\n\nVerification: cargo test -p irserve-core (212 passed); cargo test\n--test oracle (55 passed / 14 skipped / 0 failed); openspec validate\n--all --strict (16/16).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"263086c7b6b0c71bac93c7036eb6f6187eee75b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/263086c7b6b0c71bac93c7036eb6f6187eee75b5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/585b3cad32426db8095d1251b84e696a1d1ccc9c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/585b3cad32426db8095d1251b84e696a1d1ccc9c","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDU4NWIzY2FkMzI0MjZkYjgwOTVkMTI1MWI4NGU2OTZhMWQxY2NjOWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/3f8110bd94b9ccb74e8370d3d927a57b4e708b2b","sha":"3f8110bd94b9ccb74e8370d3d927a57b4e708b2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/3f8110bd94b9ccb74e8370d3d927a57b4e708b2b"}],"sha":"585b3cad32426db8095d1251b84e696a1d1ccc9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/585b3cad32426db8095d1251b84e696a1d1ccc9c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/3f8110bd94b9ccb74e8370d3d927a57b4e708b2b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T14:54:26Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T14:54:26Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-6f): address Codex review round 1 (P1 + P2 fixes)\n\nP1 — headers source is minimatch-only:\n- Add Matcher::compile_no_segments to path_pattern.rs (skips\n  path-to-regexp routing, treats `:name` as literal `:`).\n- custom_headers::compile_rules uses it. Source `/api/:id` now\n  matches only the literal request path, not `/api/42`.\n- Mirrors getHeaders'' sourceMatches call without `allowSegments`\n  at serve-handler/src/index.js:207.\n\nP1 — error_response applies headers per branch:\n- error_response now takes header_rules + request_path. JSON branch\n  returns BEFORE getHeaders (mirrors index.js:477-487). Custom-page\n  branch matches against `/<status>.html` (mirrors index.js:508).\n  Fallback HTML branch matches against the request path\n  (mirrors index.js:519).\n- dispatch_inner returns (Response, Option<String>); the outer\n  dispatch wrapper applies apply_custom_headers only when\n  Some(path) — for success / 405 paths whose reference equivalent\n  flows through the success-site getHeaders.\n\nP1 — null-prune is single-pass last-write-wins:\n- Replace two-pass implementation (insert non-null, then walk again\n  deleting any matched-rule''s null) with a single-pass insert/remove\n  walk. An early null does NOT delete a value set later by a\n  separate matching rule.\n- Mirrors the reference''s two-stage Object.assign + prune-final-null\n  semantics at index.js:245-251.\n- New regression test: later_set_value_wins_over_earlier_null_prune.\n\nP2 — strict UTF-8 in try_percent_decode:\n- Switch from decode_utf8_lossy() to decode_utf8(). `/%FF` (valid\n  %xx syntax but invalid UTF-8 byte sequence) now returns 400,\n  mirroring decodeURIComponent''s URIError. Closes D-010''s deferred\n  promotion.\n\nP2 — change package completeness:\n- Add MOD spec deltas for static-files (SRV-FILE-003) and security\n  (SRV-SEC-001 + SRV-SEC-002), each carrying a Compatibility note\n  documenting D-015 wiring.\n- Tick all slice-6 task checkboxes.\n- D-015 expanded with the four corrective methodological signals\n  surfaced by this review round.\n\nVerification: cargo test -p irserve-core (211 passed); cargo test\n--test oracle (54 passed / 14 skipped / 0 failed); openspec\nvalidate --all --strict (16/16 pass).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2747ce7bc1bb81b241859c674b02e598995073fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/2747ce7bc1bb81b241859c674b02e598995073fd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/3f8110bd94b9ccb74e8370d3d927a57b4e708b2b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/3f8110bd94b9ccb74e8370d3d927a57b4e708b2b","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDNmODExMGJkOTRiOWNjYjc0ZTgzNzBkM2Q5MjdhNTdiNGU3MDhiMmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/35ca24031b53d324f0052b61eccee62e32e24d78","sha":"35ca24031b53d324f0052b61eccee62e32e24d78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/35ca24031b53d324f0052b61eccee62e32e24d78"}],"sha":"3f8110bd94b9ccb74e8370d3d927a57b4e708b2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/3f8110bd94b9ccb74e8370d3d927a57b4e708b2b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/35ca24031b53d324f0052b61eccee62e32e24d78/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T14:27:04Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T14:27:04Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-6f): spec deltas + decisions log + meta\n\nOpenSpec change package:\n- proposal.md, design.md, tasks.md\n- specs/headers/spec.md (ADDED): SRV-HDR-001 + SRV-HDR-002\n\nSpec deltas for static-files (SRV-FILE-003) and security (SRV-SEC-001,\nSRV-SEC-002) are intentionally absent: their requirement text is\nunchanged — 6f delivers the contract that was already specified but\ndeferred. Coverage growth lives in the probe `runner.l0` partitions\nand in D-015''s evidence trail.\n\nD-015 records the four methodological signals surfaced during the\nslice work:\n1. traversal-raw-encoded snapshot resync (5b L0-hygiene 404 → 400);\n2. 3xx redirects skip header application (matches reference''s\n   writeHead-only path);\n3. 400 path-traversal does not carry custom headers under reference\n   (minimatch + slasher quirk on outside-root absolutePath);\n4. value: null is unreachable through the reference CLI (@zeit\n   schema rejects); SRV-HDR-002 ships verified by unit tests.\n\nOracle matrix gains ORC-159 (headers-on-error) and ORC-160\n(headers-accumulate). README \"Try IrServe\" reflows to post-6f with\ncustom-error-page, path-traversal-400, and custom-headers smoke\nexamples. Stage-map row flips to done.\n\nValidated via `openspec validate --all --strict`: 16/16 pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"468eef29358b803c0bea47f97556807a77bba967","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/468eef29358b803c0bea47f97556807a77bba967"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/35ca24031b53d324f0052b61eccee62e32e24d78","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/35ca24031b53d324f0052b61eccee62e32e24d78","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDM1Y2EyNDAzMWI1M2QzMjRmMDA1MmI2MWVjY2VlNjJlMzJlMjRkNzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/dbba30ed698b134fdda66a650cc68b45390f84f8","sha":"dbba30ed698b134fdda66a650cc68b45390f84f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/dbba30ed698b134fdda66a650cc68b45390f84f8"}],"sha":"35ca24031b53d324f0052b61eccee62e32e24d78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/35ca24031b53d324f0052b61eccee62e32e24d78"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/dbba30ed698b134fdda66a650cc68b45390f84f8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T14:17:29Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T14:17:29Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"feat(stage-6f): SRV-HDR-002 — `value: null` deletes a prior header\n\nWiden HeaderItem.value to Option<String> in config.rs. After the\naccumulate pass, apply_custom_headers walks matched rules a second\ntime and removes any header whose value is None (case-insensitive,\nmirroring index.js:247-251''s two-phase merge: Object.assign first,\nprune null entries last).\n\nMethodological finding: serve''s @zeit/schemas/deployment/config-static\ndeclares `value: { type: ''string'', minLength: 1 }`, rejecting `null`\nat config-load time. The reference CLI cannot validate this feature\nend-to-end, so SRV-HDR-002 ships as an irserve-extension verified by\nunit tests in custom_headers::tests rather than an oracle probe.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"909ce6689d0a603356fedc319d9b25a5a73f7a29","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/909ce6689d0a603356fedc319d9b25a5a73f7a29"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/dbba30ed698b134fdda66a650cc68b45390f84f8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/dbba30ed698b134fdda66a650cc68b45390f84f8","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKGRiYmEzMGVkNjk4YjEzNGZkZGE2NmE2NTBjYzY4YjQ1MzkwZjg0Zjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/fa188d7839274b2ed0a1661bc96259e9a13b3555","sha":"fa188d7839274b2ed0a1661bc96259e9a13b3555","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/fa188d7839274b2ed0a1661bc96259e9a13b3555"}],"sha":"dbba30ed698b134fdda66a650cc68b45390f84f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/dbba30ed698b134fdda66a650cc68b45390f84f8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/fa188d7839274b2ed0a1661bc96259e9a13b3555/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T14:13:44Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T14:13:44Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"feat(stage-6f): custom response headers — accumulate + override (SRV-HDR-001)\n\nCompile serve.json `headers: [{source, headers: [{key, value}]}]` rules\nat startup via path_pattern.rs (Literal/Glob/Pattern matchers shared\nwith redirects/rewrites). The new custom_headers module exposes\napply_custom_headers, run as a post-dispatch pass on every response —\niterating rules in order, layering matching headers via case-insensitive\nlast-write-wins (axum''s HeaderMap normalizes).\n\nTwo methodological surprises surfaced empirically against the reference:\n\n1. 3xx redirect responses are skipped — reference''s\n   `response.writeHead(301, { Location: ... })` at index.js:586-588\n   bypasses getHeaders entirely, so custom headers never layer onto\n   redirects. Mirroring this preserves snapshot parity on\n   headers-custom (cleanUrls 301 path).\n\n2. 400 path-traversal responses do NOT carry the user''s `**` rule\n   either: reference''s getHeaders is invoked with absolutePath outside\n   the served root, so path.relative yields a `../`-prefixed string\n   that minimatch''s slasher-normalized form does not match `**`\n   against. Out of scope for this probe; the headers-on-error case\n   focuses on the 404 anchor where parity holds.\n\nNew probes: headers-on-error (404 + X-Test), headers-accumulate (two\nrules layer X-One + X-Two on the same path). headers-applied,\nheaders-custom opt into the irserve target via runner.l0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"078f61aa9029256a02aeae86e2da25cb191c2d46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/078f61aa9029256a02aeae86e2da25cb191c2d46"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/fa188d7839274b2ed0a1661bc96259e9a13b3555","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/fa188d7839274b2ed0a1661bc96259e9a13b3555","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKGZhMTg4ZDc4MzkyNzRiMmVkMGExNjYxYmM5NjI1OWU5YTEzYjM1NTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/c5e3a5338b1cece72ce9595362dab7967fda7195","sha":"c5e3a5338b1cece72ce9595362dab7967fda7195","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/c5e3a5338b1cece72ce9595362dab7967fda7195"}],"sha":"fa188d7839274b2ed0a1661bc96259e9a13b3555","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/fa188d7839274b2ed0a1661bc96259e9a13b3555"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/c5e3a5338b1cece72ce9595362dab7967fda7195/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T14:04:39Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T14:04:39Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"feat(stage-6f): full SRV-SEC-001 surface (lexical containment → 400)\n\nAdd a phase-1 lexical containment check (lexical_path_escapes_root) that\nwalks decoded path segments and short-circuits to 400 when `..` segments\nwould pop above the served root. Mirrors the reference''s `isPathInside`\ngate at serve-handler/src/index.js:570-580 — purely lexical, before any\nfilesystem I/O, so missing-file `..` traversal still yields 400 (not the\n404 a fs-only check would emit when the escaped target happens not to\nexist).\n\nEscapedRoot''s dispatch arm now also routes to 400 as defense-in-depth\nfor symlink/canonicalize-based escapes. NotFound stays 404.\n\nThe traversal-raw-encoded case opts in all four wire-level anchors\n(bodyMayDiffer for each, since irserve emits its own error HTML rather\nthan serve-handler''s full errorTemplate). traversal-encoded (fetch mode)\nalso opts in: client-side normalization makes the four scenarios reduce\nto in-root resolves under irserve.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a5ea95c4e7291cb0acb5bd1859b3a6015e11b17b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/a5ea95c4e7291cb0acb5bd1859b3a6015e11b17b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/c5e3a5338b1cece72ce9595362dab7967fda7195","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/c5e3a5338b1cece72ce9595362dab7967fda7195","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKGM1ZTNhNTMzOGIxY2VjZTcyY2U5NTk1MzYyZGFiNzk2N2ZkYTcxOTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/e8585fec7d62ee9d760bff20fc7531ae10073134","sha":"e8585fec7d62ee9d760bff20fc7531ae10073134","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/e8585fec7d62ee9d760bff20fc7531ae10073134"}],"sha":"c5e3a5338b1cece72ce9595362dab7967fda7195","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/c5e3a5338b1cece72ce9595362dab7967fda7195"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/e8585fec7d62ee9d760bff20fc7531ae10073134/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T14:01:00Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T14:01:00Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"feat(stage-6f): strict %xx decode (SRV-SEC-002 partial; malformed → 400)\n\nPhase-1 syntactic gate for percent-encoded paths: try_percent_decode\nwalks the URI path and rejects any ''%'' not followed by exactly two\nASCII-hex chars. Mirrors decodeURIComponent''s URIError branch at\nserve-handler/src/index.js:561-567. On Err, dispatch short-circuits to\nerror_response(400, ..) before any phase 2+ runs.\n\nThe traversal-raw-encoded probe gains a runner.l0 partition opting in\nthe raw_malformed_percent anchor; the other three traversal anchors\nremain informational until slice 3 wires the EscapedRoot → 400 flip.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dba802bb863cea9a79571d7d8e042dc48432415f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/dba802bb863cea9a79571d7d8e042dc48432415f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/e8585fec7d62ee9d760bff20fc7531ae10073134","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/e8585fec7d62ee9d760bff20fc7531ae10073134","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKGU4NTg1ZmVjN2Q2MmVlOWQ3NjBiZmYyMGZjNzUzMWFlMTAwNzMxMzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/c724843b47df4f3b42dfec2615d3115baea49444","sha":"c724843b47df4f3b42dfec2615d3115baea49444","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/c724843b47df4f3b42dfec2615d3115baea49444"}],"sha":"e8585fec7d62ee9d760bff20fc7531ae10073134","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/e8585fec7d62ee9d760bff20fc7531ae10073134"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/c724843b47df4f3b42dfec2615d3115baea49444/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T13:58:25Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T13:58:25Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"feat(stage-6f): custom <status>.html error pages (SRV-FILE-003)\n\nGeneralize notfound.rs into error.rs with error_response(status, headers,\nroot). For HTML-accepting clients, look up <statusCode>.html at the served\nroot and serve it with the matching status; fall back to a generic\n<h1>STATUS REASON</h1> body otherwise. JSON-accepting clients receive a\nstatus-keyed envelope (not_found wired today; bad_request stub ready for\nslice 2).\n\nBoth 404 emission sites in dispatch.rs now flow through error_response,\nand error-page-custom + notfound-custom probes opt into the irserve target\nvia runner.l0 (with contentLengthMayDiffer on the JSON branch, mirroring\nnotfound-shape''s precedent for chunked-vs-content-length divergence).\n\nReference: serve-handler/src/index.js:467-524 (sendError).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6a1e737c5e776898633d803ee3c35b1c55d1c113","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/6a1e737c5e776898633d803ee3c35b1c55d1c113"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/c724843b47df4f3b42dfec2615d3115baea49444","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/c724843b47df4f3b42dfec2615d3115baea49444","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKGM3MjQ4NDNiNDdkZjRmM2I0MmRmZWMyNjE1ZDMxMTViYWVhNDk0NDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/a937ff16eebc820e5eb22c9337f38da49ab14c4e","sha":"a937ff16eebc820e5eb22c9337f38da49ab14c4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/a937ff16eebc820e5eb22c9337f38da49ab14c4e"}],"sha":"c724843b47df4f3b42dfec2615d3115baea49444","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/c724843b47df4f3b42dfec2615d3115baea49444"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/a937ff16eebc820e5eb22c9337f38da49ab14c4e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T13:53:26Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T13:53:26Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-6f): plan for error pages, full L2 security, custom headers\n\nSub-stage 6f scope: SRV-FILE-003 (custom <status>.html), full SRV-SEC-001\n+ SRV-SEC-002 (single-pass decode, traversal/malformed -> 400), SRV-HDR-001\n+ SRV-HDR-002 (glob+accumulate+null-prune). Six-slice plan with order\nErrors -> Security -> Headers per plan-mode interview.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e60f6854bdcff29f3f4cecf20a7a8f1843575db7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/e60f6854bdcff29f3f4cecf20a7a8f1843575db7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/a937ff16eebc820e5eb22c9337f38da49ab14c4e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","ev