":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/b269af17c952baf53a7fcb0fd067c9bcda6c6f83/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T13:31:13Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T13:31:13Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-6e): address Codex review round 2 (P3 — citation fix)\n\nThe round-1 commit added a dispatch.rs comment citing\n`serve-handler/src/lib/paths.js` for `getPossiblePaths`, but no\n`lib/` subdirectory exists in the pinned reference. The function\nlives at `serve-handler/src/index.js:276` (called from `findRelated`\nat `index.js:282`). Pure citation hallucination on my part —\nbehavior was unaffected. Citation corrected.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4e01430c5f2bd54f05ba4906ace326228b7e021e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/4e01430c5f2bd54f05ba4906ace326228b7e021e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/b269af17c952baf53a7fcb0fd067c9bcda6c6f83","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/b269af17c952baf53a7fcb0fd067c9bcda6c6f83","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKGIyNjlhZjE3Yzk1MmJhZjUzYTdmY2IwZmQwNjdjOWJjZGE2YzZmODM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/20920639146e9eafd37a8d9dda390802a627aebe","sha":"20920639146e9eafd37a8d9dda390802a627aebe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/20920639146e9eafd37a8d9dda390802a627aebe"}],"sha":"b269af17c952baf53a7fcb0fd067c9bcda6c6f83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/b269af17c952baf53a7fcb0fd067c9bcda6c6f83"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/20920639146e9eafd37a8d9dda390802a627aebe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T13:14:14Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T13:14:14Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-6e): address Codex review round 1 (P1 + P2 fixes)\n\nP1: extensionless rewrite-target-miss now falls back to ORIGINAL\npath''s resolve, mirroring the reference''s final lstat(absolutePath)\nat serve-handler/src/index.js:634-642 after findRelated returns\nnull. Pre-fix, /about (existing extensionless file) with rewrite\n/about → /missing.html returned 404; the reference returns 200\nserving /about. Fixed in dispatch.rs''s extensionless branch:\non resolve(target) NotFound|EscapedRoot, fall to resolve(url_path)\nWITHOUT cleanUrls candidates (mirrors findRelated''s\nrewrittenPath ? [rewrittenPath] : getPossiblePaths(...) gating).\n\nP2: url_path_has_extension now mirrors Node path.posix.extname for\ntrailing-slash paths. Node''s extname(''/foo.txt/'') === ''.txt''; the\nprior implementation used rsplit(''/'').next() which captured the\nempty trailing segment and let rewrites fire on directory-like\nrequests. Fix: rsplit(''/'').find(|b| !b.is_empty()) to skip empty\ntrailing segments before the dot-rule check. Six unit tests cover\nroot, dotfile, nested-dotfile-with-ext, trailing-slash-with-ext,\nand trailing-slash-extensionless cases.\n\nP2: routing spec wording corrected. The first cut claimed ORC-152\ncloses the \"rewrite-wins side\" of redirects↔rewrites compose, but\nORC-152 demonstrates redirect-wins (an explicit redirect overrides\n--single''s catch-all). New probe\nprec-redirects-rewrites-rewrite-wins.json#rewrite_fires_when_redirect_doesnt_match\n(ORC-158) explicitly pins the rewrite-wins side; spec attribution\ncorrected.\n\nNew probes (each recorded against the pinned reference first):\n  * rewrites-prestat.json — extensioned_skipped (ORC-154),\n    extensionless_wins (ORC-155), extensionless_miss_falls_back\n    (ORC-156, the P1 corner).\n  * rewrites-extensioned-miss.json — extensioned_falls_to_rewrite\n    (ORC-157).\n  * prec-redirects-rewrites-rewrite-wins.json —\n    rewrite_fires_when_redirect_doesnt_match (ORC-158).\n\nPushed back on two of Codex''s planned-but-undelivered probes:\nrewrites-cycle.json (snapshot would be unstable; reference has no\ncap so cycle behavior is implementation-defined; D-014''s\nirserve-only cap is exercised by depth_cap_clamps_to_last_path\nunit test) and rewrites-chain#chain_order_independent\n(algorithmically identical to chain_a_to_b_to_c; covered by the\nchain_order_independent Rust unit test).\n\nVerified: 201/201 irserve-core unit tests (was 195 — added six\nurl_path_has_extension cases), 46/46 oracle anchors (was 43 —\nadded five new ORCs from the three new probes), 15/15 openspec\nvalidate --all --strict.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9bec8b0bf72b3a440e67d0d4eb6929783cc28e8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/9bec8b0bf72b3a440e67d0d4eb6929783cc28e8d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/20920639146e9eafd37a8d9dda390802a627aebe","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/20920639146e9eafd37a8d9dda390802a627aebe","node_id":"C_kwDOSWNt69oAKDIwOTIwNjM5MTQ2ZTllYWZkMzdhOGQ5ZGRhMzkwODAyYTYyN2FlYmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commit/c5d8d50cbda5e5098e3f71980860690e53b0c2b4","sha":"c5d8d50cbda5e5098e3f71980860690e53b0c2b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/c5d8d50cbda5e5098e3f71980860690e53b0c2b4"}],"sha":"20920639146e9eafd37a8d9dda390802a627aebe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/20920639146e9eafd37a8d9dda390802a627aebe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sotnyk","id":890642,"login":"sotnyk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDY0Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sotnyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/commits/c5d8d50cbda5e5098e3f71980860690e53b0c2b4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T12:47:34Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T12:47:34Z","email":"serge.sotnyk@gmail.com","name":"serge-sotnyk"},"message":"docs(stage-6e): spec deltas + decisions log + meta\n\nSlice 6 of Stage 6e. Authors openspec/changes/007-configured-rewrites/\n(proposal + design + tasks + spec deltas for rewrites/routing/cli)\nand refreshes the reference docs:\n\n* decisions.md: D-013 (un-defer SRV-RWRT-001 + SRV-CLI-008 + close\n  redirects↔rewrites compose corner of SRV-ROUT-006); D-014\n  (recursion-depth cap = 64 on rewrite chaining, irserve-only\n  graceful clamp).\n* inventory.md: extend SRV-RWRT-001 + SRV-CLI-008 oracle test lists\n  with the new probe IDs and the rewrites-chain probe.\n* oracle-matrix.md: ORC-148 (chain), ORC-149/150/151 (single-flag),\n  ORC-152 (single-with-redirect), ORC-153 (single-with-rewrites).\n* README.md: flip Stage 6e to done; refresh \"Try IrServe\" with\n  rewrites + --single examples; trim \"What is NOT yet observable\".\n* stage6_l1_l2_capabilities.md: 6e row → done with summary.\n\nValidates: openspec validate --all --strict → 15/15 passed.\nTests: 195/195 irserve-core unit + 43/43 oracle anchors green\n(target=irserve, snapshot=verified). Stage 6e closes\nSRV-RWRT-001, SRV-CLI-008, and the rewrite-wins side of\nSRV-ROUT-006.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"77e33ebdbab56bfea32e8607fb7756a67d175c45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/trees/77e33ebdbab56bfea32e8607fb7756a67d175c45"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/serge-sotnyk/irServe/git/commits/c5d8d50cbda5e5098e3f71980860690e53b0c2b4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/890642?v=4","events_url":"https://ap