":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/555d08025adeb0695b55068fc2d2ba7a209bf855","node_id":"C_kwDOSWT-J9oAKDU1NWQwODAyNWFkZWIwNjk1YjU1MDY4ZmMyZDJiYTdhMjA5YmY4NTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/ba851d8e0a176533e492f4026221f6bcaa61f3c7","sha":"ba851d8e0a176533e492f4026221f6bcaa61f3c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/ba851d8e0a176533e492f4026221f6bcaa61f3c7"}],"sha":"555d08025adeb0695b55068fc2d2ba7a209bf855","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/555d08025adeb0695b55068fc2d2ba7a209bf855"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44301196?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers","id":44301196,"login":"NoelHuibers","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzAxMTk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/ba851d8e0a176533e492f4026221f6bcaa61f3c7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T22:48:40Z","email":"noel@huibers.io","name":"Noel Huibers"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T22:48:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf: CellList editor virtualization + canvas viewport culling (#24) (#167)\n\n* perf(web-app): virtualize CellList editors to near-viewport window\n\nEvery cell eagerly mounted a live CodeMirror EditorView, so a large\nnotebook paid the full editor cost for cells the user can''t see. Window\nthe editors to the near viewport: cells far off-screen render the\nexisting lightweight read-only fallback instead of CodeMirror.\n\n- shouldRenderFullEditor (lib/cellVirtualization.ts, unit-tested): a\n  cell is full when it''s near the viewport, is the focused cell, or is\n  the streaming cell — so the caret and live output never land on a\n  demoted cell.\n- useNearCellIndices (IntersectionObserver, ~200% rootMargin over each\n  cell wrapper) produces the near set. When IntersectionObserver is\n  unavailable (SSR/jsdom) or before it first reports, it returns null =\n  \"all near\", preserving today''s behavior on first paint and in tests.\n- Anti-jank: CellList captures each full cell''s rendered wrapper height\n  after paint and applies it as the fallback''s min-height the instant\n  the cell demotes, so collapsing a tall editor can''t shift scroll.\n- CellOutputs still renders for every cell; only the editor is\n  virtualized. Debounced ingest, add/delete/copy/paste, keyboard nav and\n  the canvas->cell scroll handoff (which focuses its target, keeping it\n  full) are untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* perf(graph-canvas): cull offscreen nodes with onlyRenderVisibleElements\n\nEnable ReactFlow viewport culling so nodes and edges outside the visible\narea aren''t rendered. On a large canvas this drops the render/measure\ncost for everything the user can''t currently see.\n\nSafe because ReactFlow treats nodes without measured dimensions as\nvisible: the first mount still renders and measures every node, so\nfitView and the initial MeasuredGroupLayout group stacking are\nunchanged. The only residual is that an offscreen node whose content\ngrows after a run keeps a briefly-stale height in nodeInternals (no\nResizeObserver fires while it''s unmounted); scrolling it back into view\nremounts it, re-measures, and MeasuredGroupLayout re-stacks with the\ncorrected height. Documented inline for browser verification.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cdabdc3246dc64fd4ec227d5d3b0a3570861802c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/trees/cdabdc3246dc64fd4ec227d5d3b0a3570861802c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/commits/ba851d8e0a176533e492f4026221f6bcaa61f3c7","verification":{"payload":"tree cdabdc3246dc64fd4ec227d5d3b0a3570861802c\nparent cd8e5874d6f312befdd2338553cc513bee116290\nauthor Noel Huibers <noel@huibers.io> 1785192520 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785192520 +0200\n\nperf: CellList editor virtualization + canvas viewport culling (#24) (#167)\n\n* perf(web-app): virtualize CellList editors to near-viewport window\n\nEvery cell eagerly mounted a live CodeMirror EditorView, so a large\nnotebook paid the full editor cost for cells the user can''t see. Window\nthe editors to the near viewport: cells far off-screen render the\nexisting lightweight read-only fallback instead of CodeMirror.\n\n- shouldRenderFullEditor (lib/cellVirtualization.ts, unit-tested): a\n  cell is full when it''s near the viewport, is the focused cell, or is\n  the streaming cell — so the caret and live output never land on a\n  demoted cell.\n- useNearCellIndices (IntersectionObserver, ~200% rootMargin over each\n  cell wrapper) produces the near set. When IntersectionObserver is\n  unavailable (SSR/jsdom) or before it first reports, it returns null =\n  \"all near\", preserving today''s behavior on first paint and in tests.\n- Anti-jank: CellList captures each full cell''s rendered wrapper height\n  after paint and applies it as the fallback''s min-height the instant\n  the cell demotes, so collapsing a tall editor can''t shift scroll.\n- CellOutputs still renders for every cell; only the editor is\n  virtualized. Debounced ingest, add/delete/copy/paste, keyboard nav and\n  the canvas->cell scroll handoff (which focuses its target, keeping it\n  full) are untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* perf(graph-canvas): cull offscreen nodes with onlyRenderVisibleElements\n\nEnable ReactFlow viewport culling so nodes and edges outside the visible\narea aren''t rendered. On a large canvas this drops the render/measure\ncost for everything the user can''t currently see.\n\nSafe because ReactFlow treats nodes without measured dimensions as\nvisible: the first mount still renders and measures every node, so\nfitView and the initial MeasuredGroupLayout group stacking are\nunchanged. The only residual is that an offscreen node whose content\ngrows after a run keeps a briefly-stale height in nodeInternals (no\nResizeObserver fires while it''s unmounted); scrolling it back into view\nremounts it, re-measures, and MeasuredGroupLayout re-stacks with the\ncorrected height. Documented inline for browser verification.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ+BICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALr8QAJBNv26NGNFd5/ogd3VpF+jj\nDkZFyhyHqin0vk6gg/HyEbfOOsNtg1QQd4IHVwLS2T/S9oKIzhWiP24HJg0czjGp\n3PExvCVVX15GD9a7f3zH+1kLlxKqQm4Mb5ESndOP6YRMeRRj8nmzlE6qZ+b83qXX\neHjKiPP2b+hSpMIcrcTor0VWr+dStAmLckl70XR0YEK8oQOupJmkd7NspXEqYJjo\n+oIIZ63wRTiusxHj45CHJto+kk/d4dSGtfGmD5pJjXHMVVF1nis2qy2OUZ1GBmlD\nXzUhJcih7FhTgtK1YkF2+HkohOkRXaY23TGppykDBmsQJmTL0QqBx2xNP72V8XA4\nT7qeUoEFqomVrNN8UCK9XLxoN8JW7PIGH0P92y8XFP3q1RmJX5okc/50UGOSb2iU\nKKSxQi19afkSQw2XzQoj7Cpfk4p0LHGgVymXlrLiaKTS3/io5OeYpbLwjPoRE4no\nuPOul+taIlYnsmYBtuNgEI2FKIxmEIlKxnMvuqF/mkdw4BX2vFZ5C9SFK9evJg+3\nVD6wFL/ves2K/lz2+q9CTBLxZLQ2ODYpCApjkG7NcBH8YHQIVyO8Kl15rm24dH2w\nVXrDCys58o0lDn2HCe+afUGT7F5L8WzPAxlJ/DcUb4wtsA/HFDCPaNhYj/R3IAta\nCag/Yhfd6Sq3eM8MKnhc\n=pP/p\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-27T22:48:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/ba851d8e0a176533e492f4026221f6bcaa61f3c7","node_id":"C_kwDOSWT-J9oAKGJhODUxZDhlMGExNzY1MzNlNDkyZjQwMjYyMjFmNmJjYWE2MWYzYzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/cd8e5874d6f312befdd2338553cc513bee116290","sha":"cd8e5874d6f312befdd2338553cc513bee116290","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/cd8e5874d6f312befdd2338553cc513bee116290"}],"sha":"ba851d8e0a176533e492f4026221f6bcaa61f3c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/ba851d8e0a176533e492f4026221f6bcaa61f3c7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44301196?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers","id":44301196,"login":"NoelHuibers","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzAxMTk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/cd8e5874d6f312befdd2338553cc513bee116290/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T22:42:48Z","email":"noel@huibers.io","name":"Noel Huibers"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T22:42:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"bench: reproducible performance suite for the paper (SyncEngine ingest + DataBus) (#166)\n\n* test(bench): add reproducible perf benchmark suite (SyncEngine ingest + DataBus)\n\nAdds a committed, re-runnable benchmark suite under bench/ producing\npaper-grade numbers for two already-merged optimizations:\n\n- Benchmark 1: SyncEngine.ingestNotebook scaling (graph-canvas, TS via\n  Vitest) over 10..3200 synthetic cells, fresh + re-ingest paths, median\n  of 15 after 5 warmups; characterizes ~linear scaling.\n- Benchmark 2: DataBus intermediate-DataFrame handling (engine, Python)\n  comparing forced-spill baseline (threshold=0) vs the default 8 MB\n  in-memory optimization; single put+get latency (1k/50k/500k rows) and\n  a sequential N-intermediate pipeline (wall time, tracemalloc peak,\n  disk), median of N/trials with a fixed numpy seed.\n\nIncludes a methodology README (what/workload/protocol/how-to-run/caveats),\nrun_all.mjs orchestrator, and a captured representative result\n(results/2026-07-28-noel.{md,json}) prefixed with full machine context and\nthe git SHA. The suite is isolated from CI: the graph-canvas vitest config\nonly includes src/**, pytest testpaths=[\"tests\"], and tsc rootDir=src, so\n`pnpm test` never runs it. No product code is modified.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: exclude bench/ from biome (benchmarks use console output)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: restore biome.json formatting after bench exclusion\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a55679b07397e074c06710aa59f8887f823f9521","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/trees/a55679b07397e074c06710aa59f8887f823f9521"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/commits/cd8e5874d6f312befdd2338553cc513bee116290","verification":{"payload":"tree a55679b07397e074c06710aa59f8887f823f9521\nparent 753e97adc1f22f923ef2717d1cb7b9b6b125c73c\nauthor Noel Huibers <noel@huibers.io> 1785192168 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785192168 +0200\n\nbench: reproducible performance suite for the paper (SyncEngine ingest + DataBus) (#166)\n\n* test(bench): add reproducible perf benchmark suite (SyncEngine ingest + DataBus)\n\nAdds a committed, re-runnable benchmark suite under bench/ producing\npaper-grade numbers for two already-merged optimizations:\n\n- Benchmark 1: SyncEngine.ingestNotebook scaling (graph-canvas, TS via\n  Vitest) over 10..3200 synthetic cells, fresh + re-ingest paths, median\n  of 15 after 5 warmups; characterizes ~linear scaling.\n- Benchmark 2: DataBus intermediate-DataFrame handling (engine, Python)\n  comparing forced-spill baseline (threshold=0) vs the default 8 MB\n  in-memory optimization; single put+get latency (1k/50k/500k rows) and\n  a sequential N-intermediate pipeline (wall time, tracemalloc peak,\n  disk), median of N/trials with a fixed numpy seed.\n\nIncludes a methodology README (what/workload/protocol/how-to-run/caveats),\nrun_all.mjs orchestrator, and a captured representative result\n(results/2026-07-28-noel.{md,json}) prefixed with full machine context and\nthe git SHA. The suite is isolated from CI: the graph-canvas vitest config\nonly includes src/**, pytest testpaths=[\"tests\"], and tsc rootDir=src, so\n`pnpm test` never runs it. No product code is modified.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: exclude bench/ from biome (benchmarks use console output)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: restore biome.json formatting after bench exclusion\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ97oCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcwoQAFbkLtjx//DWrSowp3bIWhJd\n2iR6qPOVZ+AjIIH4efInTq6UB6IpmYS/1+eqZKrTyBSa3JWWKboInj5/SFsHo2b1\nTvOzbalS3xZxWaNeV4x9NWnewuMdyeDsfbKSIPT1rdb+zOnt7NWjVI8sGtOJJU3s\nPHRXaGRRGZHUSNS9CYDN4OgVTSlPRdWpfB0/7cpA1w+ctaq3yIIsWAjxoCHm4RTE\nH1XSiN+Irq7asvJ/qJ+QZhwiGUIS31kCDJ2+EVQVs+lts5JXUcdMsH0apLQSkmzx\nKo5vmBG/8jv9v+Kn8w00ftgO/WDbBiv7/CmUzIcctU5zxdO2rM6zQRUxSj1JdJMk\nv8KcsTZYXovHILAsSDC76YdOmYtbZbrwBZAs9zPJ+4MV14g3OrAIdDnDYyfWE1nk\nrRS3yxDV7ROUMT9dHa8Tb2JoWdS++rxRlqWJiCNZ05W+q+bNYNfC/Jt1bP8AWvfg\njp+4RAbo1I85fBPMs5Yk/GXzqU6unVkGFcypwRjj9XLK0g7cktatoyFvtdrRMTSI\nbtqlOzV+YBbd6JaU0fSsmejclgrgZU/yTo5qN0TTbLzx6u0HLNx2ya7ZdgcKa0rO\n9b7tJ+UJ+Ca8BEDD+XT+cTCvix8lM0tneVyjOJM4BSHHW2Lc4l0d8yjJA66lZgxd\nBwB/QidwiR+PSSWGsjia\n=vdNd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-27T22:42:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/cd8e5874d6f312befdd2338553cc513bee116290","node_id":"C_kwDOSWT-J9oAKGNkOGU1ODc0ZDZmMzEyYmVmZGQyMzM4NTUzY2M1MTNiZWUxMTYyOTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/753e97adc1f22f923ef2717d1cb7b9b6b125c73c","sha":"753e97adc1f22f923ef2717d1cb7b9b6b125c73c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/753e97adc1f22f923ef2717d1cb7b9b6b125c73c"}],"sha":"cd8e5874d6f312befdd2338553cc513bee116290","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/cd8e5874d6f312befdd2338553cc513bee116290"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44301196?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers","id":44301196,"login":"NoelHuibers","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzAxMTk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/753e97adc1f22f923ef2717d1cb7b9b6b125c73c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T21:39:29Z","email":"noel@huibers.io","name":"Noel Huibers"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T21:39:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf(graph-canvas): reconcile node identity so a run event re-renders one node, not all (#165)\n\n`buildNodes` rebuilds EVERY React Flow node object (fresh `data`) whenever any\noverlay map changes (runtimeByNode/timingByNode/metaByNode/unresolvedByNode).\nA single runtime-status event therefore handed React Flow N brand-new node\nobjects, defeating its per-node memo and re-rendering the whole canvas.\n\nAdd `reconcileNodes(prev, next)`: it diffs the freshly-built array against the\nprevious build and reuses the prior object reference for any node whose content\nis deeply unchanged. The returned array stays value-identical to the fresh build\n(same length, order, ids, per-node content) — only object identities are\npreserved for untouched nodes, so React Flow skips re-rendering them. `deepEqualValue`\ncompares primitives/arrays/objects recursively and functions by reference; its\nonly failure mode is a false \"not equal\" (rebuild anyway, exactly as before),\nnever a false \"equal\" (which would risk staleness).\n\nBehaviour-preserving: node contents/positions are unchanged; the sole observable\neffect is fewer re-renders. Existing 137 graph-canvas tests pass unchanged; 11\nnew tests cover the reconcile + equality logic.\n\nBEFORE/AFTER (synthetic graph, N=60 nodes, single runtime event flipping one\nnode to \"running\"):\n  rebuilt node objects  BEFORE=60  AFTER=1\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0ed8ae7acc8b64e2def61f6d1fd1c1cce5646bfe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/trees/0ed8ae7acc8b64e2def61f6d1fd1c1cce5646bfe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/commits/753e97adc1f22f923ef2717d1cb7b9b6b125c73c","verification":{"payload":"tree 0ed8ae7acc8b64e2def61f6d1fd1c1cce5646bfe\nparent d799e056ed89ed0f36d129170c2f0a8353a1244e\nauthor Noel Huibers <noel@huibers.io> 1785188369 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785188369 +0200\n\nperf(graph-canvas): reconcile node identity so a run event re-renders one node, not all (#165)\n\n`buildNodes` rebuilds EVERY React Flow node object (fresh `data`) whenever any\noverlay map changes (runtimeByNode/timingByNode/metaByNode/unresolvedByNode).\nA single runtime-status event therefore handed React Flow N brand-new node\nobjects, defeating its per-node memo and re-rendering the whole canvas.\n\nAdd `reconcileNodes(prev, next)`: it diffs the freshly-built array against the\nprevious build and reuses the prior object reference for any node whose content\nis deeply unchanged. The returned array stays value-identical to the fresh build\n(same length, order, ids, per-node content) — only object identities are\npreserved for untouched nodes, so React Flow skips re-rendering them. `deepEqualValue`\ncompares primitives/arrays/objects recursively and functions by reference; its\nonly failure mode is a false \"not equal\" (rebuild anyway, exactly as before),\nnever a false \"equal\" (which would risk staleness).\n\nBehaviour-preserving: node contents/positions are unchanged; the sole observable\neffect is fewer re-renders. Existing 137 graph-canvas tests pass unchanged; 11\nnew tests cover the reconcile + equality logic.\n\nBEFORE/AFTER (synthetic graph, N=60 nodes, single runtime event flipping one\nnode to \"running\"):\n  rebuilt node objects  BEFORE=60  AFTER=1\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ9ARCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkf8QAKK967/hNknkJRtDeGUPJkw8\n7jIptGqjuJNFefxu0Z5v1jEPFfk3D9QoKaecPzphR6dvvWCJSzG5NrCgF7B5q5/n\nvYdn8Y2TA9Q2UNtVY7H/eDtr24pcwfcD2tYCCN5TLp0aLSkQ+9dScqDY0KYtTywm\n+S4/38NFcZQnq0p8FZSA9VN3kOOAXr3aAH08BN4hmggrgoyTp5QHgN2tKEJFuSIf\nXtI7RphgTbsODjgFXG3do9jOLYb/JnlhH+YwaQuTm+MH/NQl1yctqvL6UsCQQT/F\n/pDLRfo+Hq7zYMXIViIHa6I15BroVS4jWl630+XZd7NAW7LRIWspF1szoAG9yXqF\nB+zfv//DA7UHTnuwcdjJLSSYGZLBk09BvrT+4nchl4h99dT3H903m5F5TSMVN+8M\n54w94QhHTAlEqUbttTstrcnnXvyk9W6iCYT1BaOVbiOUpi3AHwHRKuK/4LOhassF\nTR1Rvwe2BDhOnwWx2A0CCuPT+VFpMCc+39AR7Xet3Gb+r09rRtOdP4DatO5Fytzs\nLIjTlWrVgrtfUFPzy48ftK8B6K07IlBv0rxEe1St1Lize38JwBLQBWmPfwJVocKo\ncuosnnufI+/IBG+I62no8guih1OXzbn4mzgr+IniIj/ZrMlJaGij/Dgz9jLhIADb\nug2Tp7mN/U5N5dy7yaQo\n=gPJW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-27T21:39:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_