ll}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44301196?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers","id":44301196,"login":"NoelHuibers","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzAxMTk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/41a8802f577344523915e65ad7f0677b08e3115a","node_id":"C_kwDOSWT-J9oAKDQxYTg4MDJmNTc3MzQ0NTIzOTE1ZTY1YWQ3ZjA2NzdiMDhlMzExNWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/1b8c8bc4141f1c569bed9e28adaf7d80f00f6a00","sha":"1b8c8bc4141f1c569bed9e28adaf7d80f00f6a00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/1b8c8bc4141f1c569bed9e28adaf7d80f00f6a00"}],"sha":"41a8802f577344523915e65ad7f0677b08e3115a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/41a8802f577344523915e65ad7f0677b08e3115a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44301196?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers","id":44301196,"login":"NoelHuibers","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzAxMTk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/71f0064d14778535596ff8ced2300133bb1aa384/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-25T20:52:27Z","email":"noel@huibers.io","name":"Noel Huibers"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-25T20:52:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"AI consolidation: one ⌘K command palette, decluttered header, keyboard fix (Part A) (#149)\n\n* feat(app-core): add CommandPalette router for the AI command surface\n\nConsolidate the fragmented AI dialogs behind one ⌘K command palette. The\npalette opens on a filterable list of AI commands (Ask, Create node [Part A\nplaceholder, disabled], Compose, Explain) and routes:\n\n- Ask / Compose reveal that command''s textarea + result inline, delegating to\n  the host''s existing handlers via a clean controlled prop shape.\n- Explain fires the host handler immediately and closes (its banner renders\n  the result).\n\nKeyboard: ArrowUp/Down navigate (skipping the disabled row), Enter picks,\nEscape closes and stopPropagation()s so the app-global Escape handler stays\nout of it, Enter/⌘Enter submit a revealed textarea (Shift+Enter = newline).\n\nPure command-routing helpers (buildCommands/filterCommands/nextSelectableIndex/\nfirstSelectableIndex) are extracted and unit-tested. Exports added to the\napp-core index.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(web-app): consolidate AI header buttons into the ⌘K command palette\n\nReplace the three separate AI header buttons (Explain / Compose / Ask AI) and\nthe duplicate standalone keyboard-shortcuts button with a single \"Ask AI ⌘K\"\nbutton that opens the unified CommandPalette. The \"?\" HelpMenu remains the one\nvisible path to the shortcuts dialog.\n\n- App.tsx: single isCommandPaletteOpen state replaces isAskOpen/isComposeOpen;\n  CommandPalette is wired with the existing ask/compose/explain handlers and\n  their state. commandLabels are built from the new command.* namespace via the\n  Object.keys(defaults) → t() loop; ExplanationPanel banner stays as-is.\n- AppHeader.tsx: drop onExplain/onOpenCompose/onOpenAsk/onToggleShortcuts-as-\n  button; add onOpenCommandPalette and an onOpenShortcuts prop for the HelpMenu.\n- i18n: add the command.* namespace (EN+DE, registered in messages.ts) and\n  remove the now-unused explain/compose/shortcuts app.toolbar keys.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(web-app): repair the ⌘K / Escape keyboard model\n\nMove the global Escape branch below the isTypingTarget guard so a focused\neditor or an open modal owns Escape; on the bare canvas it still collapses the\nsidebar / closes the shortcuts dialog. The command palette''s Escape already\nstopPropagation()s, so it never falls through to this handler.\n\nMake ⌘K open-only (idempotent) instead of a blind toggle: it opens the palette\nfrom anywhere — including from within a cell editor — without the keystroke\nfighting typing, and the palette closes itself.\n\nAdd a focused jsdom test pinning isTypingTarget, the pure guard the routing\ndepends on.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d7fa7400ea32ca80486b2040e456bd1d52520e4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/trees/d7fa7400ea32ca80486b2040e456bd1d52520e4b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/commits/71f0064d14778535596ff8ced2300133bb1aa384","verification":{"payload":"tree d7fa7400ea32ca80486b2040e456bd1d52520e4b\nparent fc21234cfbc6acd30f4d442c3408b3d25d4c78fa\nauthor Noel Huibers <noel@huibers.io> 1785012747 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785012747 +0200\n\nAI consolidation: one ⌘K command palette, decluttered header, keyboard fix (Part A) (#149)\n\n* feat(app-core): add CommandPalette router for the AI command surface\n\nConsolidate the fragmented AI dialogs behind one ⌘K command palette. The\npalette opens on a filterable list of AI commands (Ask, Create node [Part A\nplaceholder, disabled], Compose, Explain) and routes:\n\n- Ask / Compose reveal that command''s textarea + result inline, delegating to\n  the host''s existing handlers via a clean controlled prop shape.\n- Explain fires the host handler immediately and closes (its banner renders\n  the result).\n\nKeyboard: ArrowUp/Down navigate (skipping the disabled row), Enter picks,\nEscape closes and stopPropagation()s so the app-global Escape handler stays\nout of it, Enter/⌘Enter submit a revealed textarea (Shift+Enter = newline).\n\nPure command-routing helpers (buildCommands/filterCommands/nextSelectableIndex/\nfirstSelectableIndex) are extracted and unit-tested. Exports added to the\napp-core index.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(web-app): consolidate AI header buttons into the ⌘K command palette\n\nReplace the three separate AI header buttons (Explain / Compose / Ask AI) and\nthe duplicate standalone keyboard-shortcuts button with a single \"Ask AI ⌘K\"\nbutton that opens the unified CommandPalette. The \"?\" HelpMenu remains the one\nvisible path to the shortcuts dialog.\n\n- App.tsx: single isCommandPaletteOpen state replaces isAskOpen/isComposeOpen;\n  CommandPalette is wired with the existing ask/compose/explain handlers and\n  their state. commandLabels are built from the new command.* namespace via the\n  Object.keys(defaults) → t() loop; ExplanationPanel banner stays as-is.\n- AppHeader.tsx: drop onExplain/onOpenCompose/onOpenAsk/onToggleShortcuts-as-\n  button; add onOpenCommandPalette and an onOpenShortcuts prop for the HelpMenu.\n- i18n: add the command.* namespace (EN+DE, registered in messages.ts) and\n  remove the now-unused explain/compose/shortcuts app.toolbar keys.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(web-app): repair the ⌘K / Escape keyboard model\n\nMove the global Escape branch below the isTypingTarget guard so a focused\neditor or an open modal owns Escape; on the bare canvas it still collapses the\nsidebar / closes the shortcuts dialog. The command palette''s Escape already\nstopPropagation()s, so it never falls through to this handler.\n\nMake ⌘K open-only (idempotent) instead of a blind toggle: it opens the palette\nfrom anywhere — including from within a cell editor — without the keystroke\nfighting typing, and the palette closes itself.\n\nAdd a focused jsdom test pinning isTypingTarget, the pure guard the routing\ndepends on.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZSILCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjpcQAChozxDlLHtB3UmDOVLrpTUw\nCgHHSyFW5NwsYvyxzNjPmqgqe07WansOMCxsQRzsJ6chswaU6iMykhYTytp7Qjxu\nreaPWlYqp5eO90o9G1sXudGg2S94nuA3MtL6Ns8UFOwEtsv19fqObSO6UnNksw2H\nBHB8HPH/GxfOL9Xm6/MN+8nOQGK/jJEPZFmD8+98RLXdhRUWcuar0eJyv2jgyTal\nrvfldMQLNgpxIOC+7mi1q8vUErAdjATYdw0w0FjNkqb4anSlsgXsFH+HG3zoUHW0\n+0ZS3QsooAGif7wl98r3fbd7TLlEfb0BbK6fNON4S1xbLJjq7sMYNBVAL8bFLsdk\n3xO711TfEE5BN+LmkN6qaLpJmrOeKExnYHYgmy+R9Mo850Fm4W6EBuE78SlT35pe\n1HBQDIwIzZuYa/LQIcAaOK08j9f1AVZ4KYi6OR0v5YtfFoHBrfRDphHCIalUqR4x\nL8YxYVnLA9kRpauxw8hdbNYzbTmnubpJu/lWcu73HpKiK9tRj2KQ9nEr9WZkdc6g\nSBHp8kfKsv0iySit6ZgTEVIBwv3ygS0al4FSjApDCsdDqTNyQoVSEiVemb9zDTHw\nFViocMRc574/r9vfWVs/djfsAtw0KD4NEyRAd3J6NGrT2QHh2bCMw2hKB5rKB52z\nX6PFQouFE7sL8ZA4kjmk\n=y3Lj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-25T20:52:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/71f0064d14778535596ff8ced2300133bb1aa384","node_id":"C_kwDOSWT-J9oAKDcxZjAwNjRkMTQ3Nzg1MzU1OTZmZjhjZWQyMzAwMTMzYmIxYWEzODQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/fc21234cfbc6acd30f4d442c3408b3d25d4c78fa","sha":"fc21234cfbc6acd30f4d442c3408b3d25d4c78fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/fc21234cfbc6acd30f4d442c3408b3d25d4c78fa"}],"sha":"71f0064d14778535596ff8ced2300133bb1aa384","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/71f0064d14778535596ff8ced2300133bb1aa384"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44301196?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers","id":44301196,"login":"NoelHuibers","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzAxMTk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/1b8c8bc4141f1c569bed9e28adaf7d80f00f6a00/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-25T20:20:09Z","email":"noel@huibers.io","name":"NoelHuibers"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-25T20:28:33Z","email":"noel@huibers.io","name":"NoelHuibers"},"message":"fix(web-app): keep engine JWT fresh and gate triggers on sign-in\n\nThe engine JWT was minted once at page load and never refreshed, so\nevery require_auth call (Run, triggers, cloud sync) started answering\n401 \"invalid token: Signature has expired\" ~15 min in, once BetterAuth''s\nshort-lived token went stale. Re-mint proactively before each token''s\nexp (new engineToken helper decodes exp; clamped to [10s, 15m]) and\nretry on transient failure.\n\nAlso gate the Triggers dialog on canRun like Run already is: signed-out\nvisitors hit require_auth trigger endpoints and got a raw 401\n\"missing bearer token\". Skip the listTriggers call and show a sign-in\nhint instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"06da070e09040c9788876cccb5db9315bba67d77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/trees/06da070e09040c9788876cccb5db9315bba67d77"},"url":"https