Huibers","id":44301196,"login":"NoelHuibers","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzAxMTk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/fc21234cfbc6acd30f4d442c3408b3d25d4c78fa","node_id":"C_kwDOSWT-J9oAKGZjMjEyMzRjZmJjNmFjZDMwZjRkNDQyYzM0MDhiM2QyNWQ0Yzc4ZmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/d721d478db202c01443556b354f471cdede1a1a5","sha":"d721d478db202c01443556b354f471cdede1a1a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/d721d478db202c01443556b354f471cdede1a1a5"}],"sha":"fc21234cfbc6acd30f4d442c3408b3d25d4c78fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/fc21234cfbc6acd30f4d442c3408b3d25d4c78fa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44301196?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers","id":44301196,"login":"NoelHuibers","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzAxMTk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/d721d478db202c01443556b354f471cdede1a1a5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-25T19:34:27Z","email":"noel@huibers.io","name":"Noel Huibers"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-25T19:34:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Typography: IBM Plex Mono app surface + Plex Sans prose, self-hosted (#50) (#147)\n\n* feat(web-app): self-host IBM Plex fonts and set Plex font tokens\n\nEstablish the typographic identity for the web app (issue #50) with a\ncohesive IBM Plex family, self-hosted so the strict `font-src ''self'' data:`\nCSP is satisfied — no Google Fonts / CDN.\n\n- Add @fontsource/ibm-plex-mono + @fontsource/ibm-plex-sans; import only the\n  latin-subset weights the UI renders (mono 400/500/600, sans 400/500/600/700)\n  in __root.tsx alongside the other global CSS so Vite bundles the woff2\n  same-origin and the client bundle loads them under SSR.\n- Define Tailwind v4 `--font-mono` / `--font-sans` theme tokens as Plex so the\n  font-mono / font-sans utilities (cells, code, badges) resolve to Plex.\n- The app editor shell opts into font-mono for its tool identity and points\n  the shared graph-canvas `--notebookflow-font-family` var at the mono token\n  so canvas nodes match, without touching the graph-canvas package.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(web-app): render onboarding prose in Plex Sans\n\nThe landing and legal surfaces already opt into font-sans and read as Plex\nSans via the new token; the document default is Plex Sans too. Extend the\nlong-form treatment to the onboarding overlays, which render inside the mono\napp shell and would otherwise inherit IBM Plex Mono (issue #50).\n\n- WelcomeCard: the whole welcome card uses font-sans — a prose moment, and its\n  bold title now lands on the bundled Plex Sans 700 instead of faux-bold mono.\n- TourOverlay: the reading body opts into font-sans while the progress label\n  and step title stay mono, tying the tour to the tool it spotlights.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cd01c018afcc4c5b8314308bc693dbcdef264496","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/trees/cd01c018afcc4c5b8314308bc693dbcdef264496"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/commits/d721d478db202c01443556b354f471cdede1a1a5","verification":{"payload":"tree cd01c018afcc4c5b8314308bc693dbcdef264496\nparent cd4d5aca57d5cdb6b012e210209076e9c91fd959\nauthor Noel Huibers <noel@huibers.io> 1785008067 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785008067 +0200\n\nTypography: IBM Plex Mono app surface + Plex Sans prose, self-hosted (#50) (#147)\n\n* feat(web-app): self-host IBM Plex fonts and set Plex font tokens\n\nEstablish the typographic identity for the web app (issue #50) with a\ncohesive IBM Plex family, self-hosted so the strict `font-src ''self'' data:`\nCSP is satisfied — no Google Fonts / CDN.\n\n- Add @fontsource/ibm-plex-mono + @fontsource/ibm-plex-sans; import only the\n  latin-subset weights the UI renders (mono 400/500/600, sans 400/500/600/700)\n  in __root.tsx alongside the other global CSS so Vite bundles the woff2\n  same-origin and the client bundle loads them under SSR.\n- Define Tailwind v4 `--font-mono` / `--font-sans` theme tokens as Plex so the\n  font-mono / font-sans utilities (cells, code, badges) resolve to Plex.\n- The app editor shell opts into font-mono for its tool identity and points\n  the shared graph-canvas `--notebookflow-font-family` var at the mono token\n  so canvas nodes match, without touching the graph-canvas package.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(web-app): render onboarding prose in Plex Sans\n\nThe landing and legal surfaces already opt into font-sans and read as Plex\nSans via the new token; the document default is Plex Sans too. Extend the\nlong-form treatment to the onboarding overlays, which render inside the mono\napp shell and would otherwise inherit IBM Plex Mono (issue #50).\n\n- WelcomeCard: the whole welcome card uses font-sans — a prose moment, and its\n  bold title now lands on the bundled Plex Sans 700 instead of faux-bold mono.\n- TourOverlay: the reading body opts into font-sans while the progress label\n  and step title stay mono, tying the tour to the tool it spotlights.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZQ/DCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXj8QAB1fTCo7uhJHOAR/eptEV039\nDUOuWdA0jSmR8tBlQJuPp9njGJ8c+VBpj5UN4lW6mG970MdyUkC2gEQ780VmcflV\n0jz0jdHWrEmaqNXak4C2wbAMuj3xCuXelXEJCOZPsM49vMsJdo2eV556OgVeTcwL\n56Q8onuiyPoUdbqJzWYM5iZPm6PwVkj8+IEzmnCn25R9QvMXzdRcpqv9mP+zd/qt\n+D+AijVaV9TLOPt6BdZW4KFnQqM3T8ph+6/9e5slFngkOuoMKnMM2qM8KNLMxcfu\nAAHTLJ5M/9r1WX7uxONNMUIbLs/Sx2OY+x4qaG20At4BSFlBkoP8mcyP6zMXMmNs\n8ee9b7vvnHtpwV1OlCiK3TfCWpqLbyLDxriUnzvoSB9XKtTVqTbNHArjzPOvPnVI\nCsU731G83EAbvKWhRIzhCG5rF7vKY2CqBZaYkQKMwdvNC002ljVb45AVOoYcbjO6\nsUU2bPvtUep5a0o/eLCKBiB5if0bFTGj9epUYRsw+HQi2Kw4r64TCK9et/gsu05l\n2LHtsgTbyFss/fvDsw7pt1UX4evHKwQITpbZEICXX7mZP8DB8T4x/2HOfTZLq9fr\ns6uH5B6y/8PMl+GRZqIQ9gho4Eqk84qR0Sx8/Uh0APqp3Tg0RUx1mbfoyWhAwJj0\nK22Kr8rptLoM/6nbFZxI\n=cH8M\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-25T19:34:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.git