following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers","id":44301196,"login":"NoelHuibers","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzAxMTk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/bad1b12ee299dacce743a30c2651047f82755e30","node_id":"C_kwDOSWT-J9oAKGJhZDFiMTJlZTI5OWRhY2NlNzQzYTMwYzI2NTEwNDdmODI3NTVlMzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/b0086b013a08fc6fa7ae66f665c1db2c6424a5fa","sha":"b0086b013a08fc6fa7ae66f665c1db2c6424a5fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/b0086b013a08fc6fa7ae66f665c1db2c6424a5fa"}],"sha":"bad1b12ee299dacce743a30c2651047f82755e30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/bad1b12ee299dacce743a30c2651047f82755e30"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44301196?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers","id":44301196,"login":"NoelHuibers","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzAxMTk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/b0086b013a08fc6fa7ae66f665c1db2c6424a5fa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-25T13:33:39Z","email":"noel@huibers.io","name":"Noel Huibers"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-25T13:33:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Signed-out surface: public palette + autocomplete, BYOK-only anonymous AI, execution stays gated (#142)\n\n* feat(engine): open palette/analyze and BYOK-only LLM surface to signed-out callers\n\nHosted signed-out visitors get the node palette, port autocomplete, and\nthe AI features with their own key; pipeline execution stays sign-in\ngated (it is exec() on a shared box -- the JWT is the only RCE barrier).\n\n- New `optional_auth` dependency: like `require_auth`, but a missing or\n  invalid credential yields an anonymous OptionalPrincipal instead of a\n  401 (self-host / open deploys stay fully trusted).\n- GET /nodes and POST /cells/analyze are now public (analyze is pure\n  ast.parse -- nothing executes).\n- /nodes/synthesize, /pipelines/explain, /pipelines/propose, /llm/ask:\n  anonymous callers on an auth-configured deploy must send a non-empty\n  api_key in the credentials block (401 \"credentials required when not\n  signed in\" otherwise), and credential resolution never falls back to\n  the host''s env keys (`resolve_credentials(allow_env_fallback=False)`)\n  so signed-out traffic can''t spend the hosted LLM budget.\n- /pipelines/{id}/run, /ws, /files*, /triggers* unchanged (require_auth).\n- Rate limiting unchanged: request_identity already keys anonymous\n  traffic by client IP (Fly-Client-IP).\n- Tests: full matrix -- anonymous vs token/JWT vs open self-host across\n  nodes/analyze/all four LLM endpoints/exec surface, env-fallback\n  blocking for anonymous, env fallback intact for signed-in and\n  self-host; existing /nodes 401 tests retargeted to /files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(web-app): signed-out surface UX — open palette/autocomplete, gated Run, BYOK AI hints\n\nMatch the engine''s new anonymous surface: the palette and port\nautocomplete load for signed-out visitors, AI features work with a key\nfrom Settings, and only hosted execution stays sign-in gated.\n\n- The engineAuthRequired latch from #141 is kept only as an old-engine\n  fallback (engines that still 401 /nodes); current engines never\n  trigger it, so palette + analyze just load signed-out. The\n  palette.signInToLoad hint stays, unchanged, for that fallback path.\n- Run gating: new lib/engineAccess with pure canRunPipeline(signedIn,\n  hasEngineOverride, hasStaticEngineToken). Signed out against the\n  hosted engine (no override, no static token) the header Run button is\n  disabled with a localized tooltip (app.toolbar.runSignedOut EN+DE);\n  keyboard/programmatic runs surface the same message in the run-error\n  slot. An engine URL override (BYO engine) or VITE static token keeps\n  signed-out Run enabled.\n- AI dialogs: the engine''s 401 (credentials required) in ask / compose /\n  explain / node-config synthesize is detected via\n  isEngineCredentialsError (EngineRequestError.status === 401) and shown\n  as a friendly app.errors.aiNeedsKey hint (EN+DE) in each dialog''s\n  error slot instead of raw error copy.\n- Tests: engineAccess.test.ts covers the canRunPipeline matrix and\n  credentials-error detection.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6a98a8ea2c66deb6a5834067f698a149d2207552","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/trees/6a98a8ea2c66deb6a5834067f698a149d2207552"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/commits/b0086b013a08fc6fa7ae66f665c1db2c6424a5fa","verification":{"payload":"tree 6a98a8ea2c66deb6a5834067f698a149d2207552\nparent 2feb6ab7ee496ad860779ed4aad592818f1abe5d\nauthor Noel Huibers <noel@huibers.io> 1784986419 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784986419 +0200\n\nSigned-out surface: public palette + autocomplete, BYOK-only anonymous AI, execution stays gated (#142)\n\n* feat(engine): open palette/analyze and BYOK-only LLM surface to signed-out callers\n\nHosted signed-out visitors get the node palette, port autocomplete, and\nthe AI features with their own key; pipeline execution stays sign-in\ngated (it is exec() on a shared box -- the JWT is the only RCE barrier).\n\n- New `optional_auth` dependency: like `require_auth`, but a missing or\n  invalid credential yields an anonymous OptionalPrincipal instead of a\n  401 (self-host / open deploys stay fully trusted).\n- GET /nodes and POST /cells/analyze are now public (analyze is pure\n  ast.parse -- nothing executes).\n- /nodes/synthesize, /pipelines/explain, /pipelines/propose, /llm/ask:\n  anonymous callers on an auth-configured deploy must send a non-empty\n  api_key in the credentials block (401 \"credentials required when not\n  signed in\" otherwise), and credential resolution never falls back to\n  the host''s env keys (`resolve_credentials(allow_env_fallback=False)`)\n  so signed-out traffic can''t spend the hosted LLM budget.\n- /pipelines/{id}/run, /ws, /files*, /triggers* unchanged (require_auth).\n- Rate limiting unchanged: request_identity already keys anonymous\n  traffic by client IP (Fly-Client-IP).\n- Tests: full matrix -- anonymous vs token/JWT vs open self-host across\n  nodes/analyze/all four LLM endpoints/exec surface, env-fallback\n  blocking for anonymous, env fallback intact for signed-in and\n  self-host; existing /nodes 401 tests retargeted to /files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(web-app): signed-out surface UX — open palette/autocomplete, gated Run, BYOK AI hints\n\nMatch the engine''s new anonymous surface: the palette and port\nautocomplete load for signed-out visitors, AI features work with a key\nfrom Settings, and only hosted execution stays sign-in gated.\n\n- The engineAuthRequired latch from #141 is kept only as an old-engine\n  fallback (engines that still 401 /nodes); current engines never\n  trigger it, so palette + analyze just load signed-out. The\n  palette.signInToLoad hint stays, unchanged, for that fallback path.\n- Run gating: new lib/engineAccess with pure canRunPipeline(signedIn,\n  hasEngineOverride, hasStaticEngineToken). Signed out against the\n  hosted engine (no override, no static token) the header Run button is\n  disabled with a localized tooltip (app.toolbar.runSignedOut EN+DE);\n  keyboard/programmatic runs surface the same message in the run-error\n  slot. An engine URL override (BYO engine) or VITE static token keeps\n  signed-out Run enabled.\n- AI dialogs: the engine''s 401 (credentials required) in ask / compose /\n  explain / node-config synthesize is detected via\n  isEngineCredentialsError (EngineRequestError.status === 401) and shown\n  as a friendly app.errors.aiNeedsKey hint (EN+DE) in each dialog''s\n  error slot instead of raw error copy.\n- Tests: engineAccess.test.ts covers the canRunPipeline matrix and\n  credentials-error detection.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZLszCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuYsQAGqlJoOXPs5vG1t2xtcYu2Le\nqgm9PKHjqU6k+QavFJj8qLK5eGxNawoF6guxiNp1X1BuV1NbaEcFjRdwLpjSm53j\nZNkSOmltzz9ubbkCx8aS/zoQi/TFfy1vGtgZvu4beISXANpiLddDVnT0B+gpdvBP\n58RquCEq9PSyHjhERuA8O3JcQA5JjM3Et7qcX3jmLc7LW0UNp+4jX7Y8y9nVKWlW\necGEKOHy2PDfVC6BUh5fBg3urk7Gk+85L1Gl6fv+BZjv6/7acP3aSwqnrLFdysXA\n8Mc5WAyuhPdaqQ9rOJrD4jLraxHSAH5zi9hSbsbaaMyY3qZGALIEVkJJvpCTRqZJ\nqWDvtGr037A5HcfNwZfi4MfcHsVJ6kK/4OJh8+V+m1XsifNb3jaFH2LtMuep+yEL\nYQs+RZkck/XSXqgSWnESr3+hQ2r10xATGhDIezUL0xl79WQZsR08GfKud7IqgqCz\nTHiln8qqC3wTscfywRWcFIyrNNvmBbawvmW7Hym0o8fXaoQhEdnwyH9jsJ4OyUdR\n3hCRWefU312uAeKclThL95UVzjz2sslcf4+aUJpE4u52Q30joCL3clE61HasY6ZH\nH4TH/BvxOMM/caMSquDeA2BRzfmML62JXJ6Edw0mxtmftREYsv9kjItr5cVs0ecw\nBA/vGGflMeiZEQbhg97A\n=AuAY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-25T13:33:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/b0086b013a08fc6fa7ae66f665c1db2c6424a5fa","node_id":"C_kwDOSWT-J9oAKGIwMDg2YjAxM2EwOGZjNmZhN2FlNjZmNjY1YzFkYjJjNjQyNGE1ZmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/2feb6ab7ee496ad860779ed4aad592818f1abe5d","sha":"2feb6ab7ee496ad860779ed4aad592818f1abe5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/2feb6ab7ee496ad860779ed4aad592818f1abe5d"}],"sha":"b0086b013a08fc6fa7ae66f665c1db2c6424a5fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/b0086b013a08fc6fa7ae66f665c1db2c6424a5fa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44301196?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers","id":44301196,"login":"NoelHuibers","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzAxMTk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/2feb6ab7ee496ad860779ed4aad592818f1abe5d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-25T12:36:18Z","email":"noel@huibers.io","name":"Noel Huibers"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-25T12:36:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Console polish: retarget stale GSAP hero selectors, graceful signed-out engine state (#141)\n\n* fix(landing): retarget GSAP hero timeline at the analyst-pipeline markup\n\nThe hero scene was rebuilt around the multi-notebook analyst pipeline, but\nthe GSAP timeline still targeted the old markup: .nf-node[data-node=\n\"forecast\"] (2 tweens) and .nf-container[data-c=\"a\"|\"b\"] no longer matched\nanything, so GSAP logged \"target not found\" 4x and the second-notebook /\ncontainer beats silently no-oped.\n\nSelectors are now derived from graph-data in hero-selectors.ts (source\nnotebook = \"pre\"; its nodes lift in act 2, the linked model/post notebooks,\ntheir ports and remaining wires arrive in act 3), so the choreography is\npreserved and the timeline can no longer drift from the data. A jsdom\nvitest renders GraphScene and asserts every timeline selector matches real\nmarkup, plus graph-data internal consistency (RUN_ORDER, edges, containers).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(web-app): graceful signed-out engine state instead of raw 401 errors\n\nSigned-out visitors on the hosted app saw \"Could not load node registry:\nEngineClient.listNodes: 401\" in the palette, and the cell-analysis effect\nkept firing a 401 per keystroke — the hosted engine requires a session JWT\nthat only signed-in users mint.\n\n- app-core: HTTP failures now throw EngineRequestError carrying the HTTP\n  status (message identical to the previous plain Error), so hosts can\n  detect a 401 without parsing strings.\n- web-app: a 401 without a session JWT latches engineAuthRequired — the\n  palette shows a localized sign-in hint (EN/DE, palette.signInToLoad)\n  instead of the raw error, and cell analysis pauses so the engine isn''t\n  hit on every keystroke. The registry load now re-runs when the JWT lands\n  or the engine URL changes, clearing the latch after sign-in.\n\nSelf-host engines with auth disabled never answer 401, so their behavior\nis unchanged; a 401 with a JWT attached (token rejected) still surfaces as\na real error.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"643a43b08d1b603922d274e01f9403a12e1ed654","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/trees/643a43b08d1b603922d274e01f9403a12e1ed654"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/commits/2feb6ab7ee496ad860779ed4aad592818f1abe5d","verification":{"payload":"tree 643a43b08d1b603922d274e01f9403a12e1ed654\nparent 78fbfb4982d201dd5201988bc32f40384c934c8c\nauthor Noel Huibers <noel@huibers.io> 1784982978 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784982978 +0200\n\nConsole polish: retarget stale GSAP hero selectors, graceful signed-out engine state (#141)\n\n* fix(landing): retarget GSAP hero timeline at the analyst-pipeline markup\n\nThe hero scene was rebuilt around the multi-notebook analyst pipeline, but\nthe GSAP timeline still targeted the old markup: .nf-node[data-node=\n\"forecast\"] (2 tweens) and .nf-container[data-c=\"a\"|\"b\"] no longer matched\nanything, so GSAP logged \"target not found\" 4x and the second-notebook /\ncontainer beats silently no-oped.\n\nSelectors are now derived from graph-data in hero-selectors.ts (source\nnotebook = \"pre\"; its nodes lift in act 2, the linked model/post notebooks,\ntheir ports and remaining wires arrive in act 3), so the choreography is\npreserved and the timeline can no longer drift from the data. A jsdom\nvitest renders GraphScene and asserts every timeline selector matches real\nmarkup, plus graph-data internal consistency (RUN_ORDER, edges, containers).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(web-app): graceful signed-out engine state instead of raw 401 errors\n\nSigned-out visitors on the hosted app saw \"Could not load node registry:\nEngineClient.listNodes: 401\" in the palette, and the cell-analysis effect\nkept firing a 401 per keystroke — the hosted engine requires a session JWT\nthat only signed-in users mint.\n\n- app-core: HTTP failures now throw EngineRequestError carrying the HTTP\n  status (message identical to the previous plain Error), so hosts can\n  detect a 401 without parsing strings.\n- web-app: a 401 without a session JWT latches engineAuthRequired — the\n  palette shows a localized sign-in hint (EN/DE, palette.signInToLoad)\n  instead of the raw error, and cell analysis pauses so the engine isn''t\n  hit on every keystroke. The registry load now re-runs when the JWT lands\n  or the engine URL changes, clearing the latch after sign-in.\n\nSelf-host engines with auth disabled never answer 401, so their behavior\nis unchanged; a 401 with a JWT attached (token rejected) still surfaces as\na real error.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZK3CCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjCEQAGI43wICn7smk47IP0cqbU8j\nQBHQHSspQKPwjswIQSMjb67TEIMoPMM9KvKjebMY3gbmIW/9m6ueDqzg5aY4hd3V\nKnOq4M11/L/uupBXRKNzdN4R+tmWCIa/fcQFNS9Z9IItlzpTgaWi6N+QcH/lSNoc\nrJz2gb4LRwvALIpyZxOKVgpjF1sNiD2GUvqjt3MhK8mlRAJcy2wmqftxXrHm93ni\n2vDrXqg22tL0GRj2sT3xyATDl08gWHP1WZDk2WWtaTpGb5K45DVIQRVzcr86WrQU\nMYwn7PwC0Twdb/c2EH+TitROBvEPqoaB3ha9meM9mZE2SCZhAYrVct5Y4u6arSpv\nzbuf9br2gp4HcD1ODoM9O57J0WBwA7RjUqxfMWsAr15Ku5wVmj+Jp+nkT8lGH4Uy\nDcprP3voSqB8fp9BI8i5MzRW7ZrX6N3xEjhoCoLHFOosELuP96/4VJKYnCwkOBvB\nNJeclcgTSa/n5V1suXPlSvxFF3qCa9hYuFe0SxAUj2MsLyZbK7FMwldsFChB9bmP\n6ygrQwxAVr/4viBsxrUlzljo6tFMMjhmxvdvdPg8a3r+BVvbYrfBfrKcEsAUcuHw\nC/up8xi8riqHWMffoy3dGNHLKgADhIuGLhw0HyQI8XbgReDIkWx1/eblQhXaF0rk\n5E5zJDma/zgtU2hRzUCk\n=5ttl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-25T12:36:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/2feb6ab7ee496ad860779ed4aad592818f1abe5d","node_id":"C_kwDOSWT-J9oAKDJmZWI2YWI3ZWU0OTZhZDg2MDc3OWVkNGFhZDU5MjgxOGYxYWJlNWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/78fbfb4982d201dd5201988bc32f40384c934c8c","sha":"78fbfb4982d201dd5201988bc32f40384c934c8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/78fbfb4982d201dd5201988bc32f40384c934c8c"}],"sha":"2feb6ab7ee496ad860779ed4aad592818f1abe5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/2feb6ab7ee496ad860779ed4aad592818f1abe5d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44301196?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers","id":44301196,"login":"NoelHuibers","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzAxMTk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/78fbfb4982d201dd5201988bc32f40384c934c8c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-25T00:13:55Z","email":"noel@huibers.io","name":"Noel Huibers"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-25T00:13:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(web-app): force single @codemirror/state instance (prod cell crash) (#140)\n\nThe #139 lockfile refresh left two @codemirror/state versions (6.6.0 +\n6.7.1) in the tree; CodeMirror rejects extensions created by a foreign\ninstance with ''Unrecognized extension value in extension set'', crashing\nthe cells pane in production. A pnpm override pins one version, and a\nnew node-level regression test creates an EditorState with the editor''s\nreal extension stack — the exact call that throws under duplication.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"478bbc94ee8acd4ce40976e0c48b28c3106dd20b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/trees/478bbc94ee8acd4ce40976e0c48b28c3106dd20b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/commits/78fbfb4982d201dd5201988bc32f40384c934c8c","verification":{"payload":"tree 478bbc94ee8acd4ce40976e0c48b28c3106dd20b\nparent 6af5eb158b6a6074fb19bb42190c0f799faff862\nauthor Noel Huibers <noel@huibers.io> 1784938435 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784938435 +0200\n\nfix(web-app): force single @codemirror/state instance (prod cell crash) (#140)\n\nThe #139 lockfile refresh left two @codemirror/state versions (6.6.0 +\n6.7.1) in the tree; CodeMirror rejects extensions created by a foreign\ninstance with ''Unrecognized extension value in extension set'', crashing\nthe cells pane in production. A pnpm override pins one version, and a\nnew node-level regression test creates an EditorState with the editor''s\nreal extension stack — the exact call that throws under duplication.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqY//DCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeOwQADWt8zyEe