6af5eb158b6a6074fb19bb42190c0f799faff862","sha":"6af5eb158b6a6074fb19bb42190c0f799faff862","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/6af5eb158b6a6074fb19bb42190c0f799faff862"}],"sha":"78fbfb4982d201dd5201988bc32f40384c934c8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/78fbfb4982d201dd5201988bc32f40384c934c8c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44301196?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers","id":44301196,"login":"NoelHuibers","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzAxMTk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/6af5eb158b6a6074fb19bb42190c0f799faff862/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-24T23:55:46Z","email":"noel@huibers.io","name":"Noel Huibers"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-24T23:55:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"First-run onboarding: cinematic welcome + spotlight tour + help menu (#78) (#138)\n\n* feat(web-app): onboarding tour engine\n\nSpotlight-tour foundation for first-run onboarding (#78):\n\n- lib/onboarding.ts: nf.onboarding.v1 seen-flag helpers (injectable\n  storage), the five-step tour config (files/cells/canvas/run/ask), and\n  pure spotlight/card-placement geometry with viewport flipping.\n- components/onboarding/useTour.ts: step state machine, data-tour target\n  measuring (double-rAF + settle pass + resize), and the keyboard\n  protocol (arrows/Enter advance, Esc skips, app shortcuts swallowed).\n- components/onboarding/TourOverlay.tsx: portal above dialogs with a\n  box-shadow spotlight cutout (teal ring + glow), GSAP position/size\n  tweens between steps, content crossfade, animated progress dots.\n- components/onboarding/WelcomeCard.tsx: first-visit glass card with\n  GSAP rise/scale entrance and staggered content cascade.\n- data-tour attributes on FilesRail, cells pane, canvas section, and\n  the Run / Ask AI header buttons.\n- New bilingual onboarding i18n namespace (EN + DE).\n- Pure-node vitest coverage for the flag, step-list integrity, and the\n  rect math (padding, flip, clamp, center fallback).\n\nAll animation paths honor prefers-reduced-motion with instant states.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(web-app): wire tour + welcome into App\n\n- App shows the welcome overlay on first visit (nf.onboarding.v1 unset);\n  the lazy state init runs only inside the route''s ClientOnly island, so\n  SSR/hydration never flashes it.\n- Take the tour / Skip both persist the seen-flag; the tour expands a\n  collapsed files or cells pane via the panelLayout setters before\n  spotlighting it (panes stay open afterwards, deliberately).\n- New ''?'' help popover in AppHeader (next to keyboard shortcuts):\n  Replay tour (clears the flag and restarts), Keyboard shortcuts (the\n  existing dialog), and Documentation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* polish(web-app): onboarding self-review fixes\n\nFixes from the polish pass (dev server boots, /app SSR serves only the\nClientOnly fallback — zero onboarding markup, so no welcome flash):\n\n- useTour: next() decided finish-vs-advance inside the setStepIndex\n  updater, calling onClose (a parent setState) from a function React may\n  replay; moved the decision out via a stepIndex ref mirror.\n- TourOverlay: position tweens now pass overwrite:''auto'' so rapid\n  stepping or resize storms kill in-flight tweens instead of letting\n  them fight over top/left/width/height.\n- Progress dots get motion-reduce:transition-none so reduced-motion\n  users see instant states everywhere.\n\nVerified: biome clean, both tsconfig typechecks, 71 vitest tests,\nproduction build, dev server 200 on / and /app.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"928b549f8eaef3d8d647614f361386d659d7271d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/trees/928b549f8eaef3d8d647614f361386d659d7271d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/commits/6af5eb158b6a6074fb19bb42190c0f799faff862","verification":{"payload":"tree 928b549f8eaef3d8d647614f361386d659d7271d\nparent 169724dccb929bf4c40b8389fbece5e1a04cc7b1\nauthor Noel Huibers <noel@huibers.io> 1784937346 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784937346 +0200\n\nFirst-run onboarding: cinematic welcome + spotlight tour + help menu (#78) (#138)\n\n* feat(web-app): onboarding tour engine\n\nSpotlight-tour foundation for first-run onboarding (#78):\n\n- lib/onboarding.ts: nf.onboarding.v1 seen-flag helpers (injectable\n  storage), the five-step tour config (files/cells/canvas/run/ask), and\n  pure spotlight/card-placement geometry with viewport flipping.\n- components/onboarding/useTour.ts: step state machine, data-tour target\n  measuring (double-rAF + settle pass + resize), and the keyboard\n  protocol (arrows/Enter advance, Esc skips, app shortcuts swallowed).\n- components/onboarding/TourOverlay.tsx: portal above dialogs with a\n  box-shadow spotlight cutout (teal ring + glow), GSAP position/size\n  tweens between steps, content crossfade, animated progress dots.\n- components/onboarding/WelcomeCard.tsx: first-visit glass card with\n  GSAP rise/scale entrance and staggered content cascade.\n- data-tour attributes on FilesRail, cells pane, canvas section, and\n  the Run / Ask AI header buttons.\n- New bilingual onboarding i18n namespace (EN + DE).\n- Pure-node vitest coverage for the flag, step-list integrity, and the\n  rect math (padding, flip, clamp, center fallback).\n\nAll animation paths honor prefers-reduced-motion with instant states.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(web-app): wire tour + welcome into App\n\n- App shows the welcome overlay on first visit (nf.onboarding.v1 unset);\n  the lazy state init runs only inside the route''s ClientOnly island, so\n  SSR/hydration never flashes it.\n- Take the tour / Skip both persist the seen-flag; the tour expands a\n  collapsed files or cells pane via the panelLayout setters before\n  spotlighting it (panes stay open afterwards, deliberately).\n- New ''?'' help popover in AppHeader (next to keyboard shortcuts):\n  Replay tour (clears the flag and restarts), Keyboard shortcuts (the\n  existing dialog), and Documentation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* polish(web-app): onboarding self-review fixes\n\nFixes from the polish pass (dev server boots, /app SSR serves only the\nClientOnly fallback — zero onboarding markup, so no welcome flash):\n\n- useTour: next() decided finish-vs-advance inside the setStepIndex\n  updater, calling onClose (a parent setState) from a function React may\n  replay; moved the decision out via a stepIndex ref mirror.\n- TourOverlay: position tweens now pass overwrite:''auto'' so rapid\n  stepping or resize storms kill in-flight tweens instead of letting\n  them fight over top/left/width/height.\n- Progress dots get motion-reduce:transition-none so reduced-motion\n  users see instant states everywhere.\n\nVerified: biome clean, both tsconfig typechecks, 71 vitest tests,\nproduction build, dev server 200 on / and /app.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqY/uCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAH98QAKEGADHRLUArxkcYd9n+JXk/\n9K+ab5n8TCdjNQwc80TEPMydVyvdLfuTyUfT+2CP0jS5U0CWOHSPBRCexL1U5/pm\npnMYr+3RlKBvCZWabaj5GQHnqlGA33huRIRiVZ009Z5eu98t5avW18uRdwf0r8sT\n3wlnKri+NVM+pE+x3qhfU4ws+6G//5jTB1r0Ca4PDJI5GFVY4VvpWqmsRPAyrWqA\nLEgjQYB6zl2MRxDBAoLyRkuPjCSa1VSQqnD8WKSDkqNlSM7VfkFutj+p7LJK0DgW\nCTP/4T/u08Prw9P54qUOrLEPYOwBx8yDa5UPQ0YuuPOujrR6O8iYVeaoy1J/LOrM\nKEpGG/In7O7dSJzE3eIvLkD1iSBRskkCyNinoiqowL2OmEgSqPnKkoy2xjZZJ5E7\n/2i+whL8z9HCxC5GYdtMndP9RxNasmp/NpctDkK2qBMUlrV26d/VcHUH5f9urJlS\nJgfFQUeORH7dMSg9yp80e/dnRx3go1Tp0/qR39uuUp+5CqOnuB3Ndd3kh+Rx++KX\nuNbek9tXfSbEocMy4lyF5W5Sz6IxzHN9OF8StTWa14SmxNUpPeaz1UCGUvkWfd+4\ngeJlgeDZAe67N2Den/1ZnmlgWa8AG3on6OeqhfBCwjBPt/JkKkSfBvYHhG8P7+uH\npWx2OSw3sU4T/DnBvZiP\n=e8dM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-24T23:55:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/6af5eb158b6a6074fb19bb42190c0f799faff862","node_id":"C_kwDOSWT-J9oAKDZhZjVlYjE1OGI2YTYwNzRmYjE5YmI0MjE5MGMwZjc5OWZhZmY4NjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/169724dccb929bf4c40b8389fbece5e1a04cc7b1","sha":"169724dccb929bf4c40b8389fbece5e1a04cc7b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/169724dccb929bf4c40b8389fbece5e1a04cc7b1"}],"sha":"6af5eb158b6a6074fb19bb42190c0f799faff862","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/6af5eb158b6a6074fb19bb42190c0f799faff862"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44301196?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers","id":44301196,"login":"NoelHuibers","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzAxMTk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/169724dccb929bf4c40b8389fbece5e1a04cc7b1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-24T23:51:50Z","email":"noel@huibers.io","name":"Noel Huibers"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-24T23:51:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Batched dependency sweep: 23 dependabot bumps, audit cleanup, pip-audit now blocking (#139)\n\n* chore(deps): batched dependency sweep across JS, engine, and CI actions\n\nReplaces the open dependabot PRs with one verified batch.\n\nJS workspaces:\n- lucide-react ^1.25.0 (app-core, graph-canvas, vscode-extension, web-app)\n- @jupyterlab/* to the 4.6 line: application/notebook/nbformat/settingregistry\n  ^4.6.1, apputils ^4.7.1, services ^7.6.1 (their release-train equivalents);\n  builder ^4.5.10 (no stable 4.6.x of builder exists on npm)\n- @lumino/widgets ^2.9.0\n- i18next ^26.3.6, react-i18next ^17.0.10, @uiw/react-codemirror ^4.25.11\n- @types/node ^26.1.1 (vscode-extension, web-app)\n- pnpm dedupe to collapse duplicate @lumino/coreutils (2.2.2/2.2.3) that broke\n  Token<T> assignability under exactOptionalPropertyTypes\n- rebuilt committed vscode dist-webview\n\nEngine (uv):\n- fastapi >=0.139.2, uvicorn >=0.51.0, watchfiles >=1.2.0, pandas >=3.0.3,\n  matplotlib >=3.11.1, jupyterlab >=4.6.1, pytest >=9.1.1, ruff >=0.15.22,\n  ty >=0.0.61\n- litellm held at >=1.91.4,<1.92 instead of the proposed >=1.92.0: 1.92+ ships\n  manylinux-only wheels (new Rust bridge) and the sdist needs Rust+MSVC, which\n  breaks Windows/macOS dev installs\n\nCI actions: checkout@v7, setup-node@v7, pnpm/action-setup@v6, setup-uv@v7,\ngitleaks-action@v3 (v3 not locally verified; CI validates).\n\nVerified: pnpm typecheck 7/7, biome check, vitest (app-core 54, graph-canvas\n137, web-app 54, jupyterlab 16), web-app production build, jupyterlab\nbuild:lab, engine pytest 255 passed, ruff 0.16.0 clean, ty 0.0.63 clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(ci): keep dependency audits advisory; document post-sweep findings\n\nBoth audits are still not clean after the deps sweep, so the two\ncontinue-on-error steps stay advisory rather than flipping to blocking:\n\n- pnpm audit: 1 critical (shell-quote via concurrently) + 13 high, all\n  transitive except better-auth <1.6.22 (patch available within the\n  existing ^1.6.20 range)\n- pip-audit: idna 3.13, pillow 12.2.0, starlette 1.0.0 — stale lock\n  entries upgradeable within current floors, left for a focused bump\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(security): clear pip-audit findings, patch better-auth, make pip-audit blocking\n\n- uv lock --upgrade-package idna (3.18) / pillow (12.3.0) / starlette\n  (1.3.1) — pip-audit now clean; validated against the full 255-test\n  engine suite.\n- better-auth pinned to ^1.6.22 (clears the one direct-dep npm advisory;\n  1.6.25 regresses jwtClient typing under exactOptionalPropertyTypes,\n  so the minimal patched version is used).\n- ci.yml: pip-audit step is now BLOCKING; pnpm audit stays advisory\n  (remaining findings are all transitive) with an updated inventory.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4a197238e291b2ed2755a5a98b6bd53b3d1c392d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/trees/4a197238e291b2ed2755a5a98b6bd53b3d1c392d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/commits/169724dccb929bf4c40b8389fbece5e1a04cc7b1","verification":{"payload":"tree 4a197238e291b2ed2755a5a98b6bd53b3d1c392d\nparent fca96f252f6f8c98a131bfbecc236eff8eed8e73\nauthor Noel Huibers <noel@huibers.io> 1784937110 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784937110 +0200\n\nBatched dependency sweep: 23 dependabot bumps, audit cleanup, pip-audit now blocking (#139)\n\n* chore(deps): batched dependency sweep across JS, engine, and CI actions\n\nReplaces the open dependabot PRs with one verified batch.\n\nJS workspaces:\n- lucide-react ^1.25.0 (app-core, graph-canvas, vscode-extension, web-app)\n- @jupyterlab/* to the 4.6 line: application/notebook/nbformat/settingregistry\n  ^4.6.1, apputils ^4.7.1, services ^7.6.1 (their release-train equivalents);\n  builder ^4.5.10 (no stable 4.6.x of builder exists on npm)\n- @lumino/widgets ^2.9.0\n- i18next ^26.3.6, react-i18next ^17.0.10, @uiw/react-codemirror ^4.25.11\n- @types/node ^26.1.1 (vscode-extension, web-app)\n- pnpm dedupe to collapse duplicate @lumino/coreutils (2.2.2/2.2.3) that broke\n  Token<T> assignability under exactOptionalPropertyTypes\n- rebuilt committed vscode dist-webview\n\nEngine (uv):\n- fastapi >=0.139.2, uvicorn >=0.51.0, watchfiles >=1.2.0, pandas >=3.0.3,\n  matplotlib >=3.11.1, jupyterlab >=4.6.1, pytest >=9.1.1, ruff >=0.15.22,\n  ty >=0.0.61\n- litellm held at >=1.91.4,<1.92 instead of the proposed >=1.92.0: 1.92+ ships\n  manylinux-only wheels (new Rust bridge) and the sdist needs Rust+MSVC, which\n  breaks Windows/macOS dev installs\n\nCI actions: checkout@v7, setup-node@v7, pnpm/action-setup@v6, setup-uv@v7,\ngitleaks-action@v3 (v3 not locally verified; CI validates).\n\nVerified: pnpm typecheck 7/7, biome check, vitest (app-core 54, graph-canvas\n137, web-app 54, jupyterlab 16), web-app production build, jupyterlab\nbuild:lab, engine pytest 255 passed, ruff 0.16.0 clean, ty 0.0.63 clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(ci): keep dependency audits advisory; document post-sweep findings\n\nBoth audits are still not clean after the deps sweep, so the two\ncontinue-on-error steps stay advisory rather than flipping to blocking:\n\n- pnpm audit: 1 critical (shell-quote via concurrently) + 13 high, all\n  transitive except better-auth <1.6.22 (patch available within the\n  existing ^1.6.20 range)\n- pip-audit: idna 3.13, pillow 12.2.0, starlette 1.0.0 — stale lock\n  entries upgradeable within current floors, left for a focused bump\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(security): clear pip-audit findings, patch better-auth, make pip-audit blocking\n\n- uv lock --upgrade-package idna (3.18) / pillow (12.3.0) / starlette\n  (1.3.1) — pip-audit now clean; validated against the full 255-test\n  engine suite.\n- better-auth pinned to ^1.6.22 (clears the one direct-dep npm advisory;\n  1.6.25 regresses jwtClient typing under exactOptionalPropertyTypes,\n  so the minimal patched version is used).\n- ci.yml: pip-audit step is now BLOCKING; pnpm audit stays advisory\n  (remaining findings are all transitive) with an updated inventory.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqY/qWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlkUQAARJjSHPDVNp7aHLQc3yidC/\nLrWRUMIt1cgrBctTTn5g2ZBD681/wVNh6PU2U5hYYhoWidsIJuH4pnG7Z7perRTw\nKIDSei1eiVFLfwV75LGKbz2sRtSkihdkuSFcWLt/4KpFdN0P7rCtb2ueXtX3BgQl\nzqyZ4xcgOyQ9o+JCewiq+DwU9gEPUwfR729Y7vL1Pm40F3/PzjgFiZgCySVbOPaJ\nt2lIhMGoN+dzYmAJA9CMMrfb59s0oS47SfPM0Cot26e5aJY1wImPUssb3JxEltCT\nUNkbWrk7/IhRFXbpUy/5aIerlA/a4kqKtxxw+VLLYkRZ1twn4ZG/au+sFPfAZp09\nFCAeCRy+vP3trfU2YSQNFZEtJUIQiZqigcHkyZq8J2yqws7BsegWlS9svO6E2/cW\niCu6upFsxZ4wxbEkcJu/JK7HdbqwJZvkall9dJcBfsxIRMvmRlBXs0CHYUWzPPCu\nVzu/uGb8Kbx+hlx7wSBsy8wjYxIaaFClAo5x8w42crp5qfCY3PpYxdCMf/0rVpQL\n6ie/RBLS6j2fYGBoGelLS48akKL/2Z6DYpOr8E0c1+jbXAIrTo4nQxuQaSyUUmJI\n7XWgd//nM9kE1pt+gl1OuRzh9nVysdsmY8pto1bbRsuD5/PjStNStQk9hhwwJtBb\nNPIQKkfYaHZjHS4803C5\n=ENgR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-24T23:51:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/169724dccb929bf4c40b8389fbece5e1a04cc7b1","node_id":"C_kwDOSWT-J9oAKDE2OTcyNGRjY2I5MjliZjRjNDBiODM4OWZiZWNlNWUxYTA0Y2M3YjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/fca96f252f6f8c98a131bfbecc236eff8eed8e73","sha":"fca96f252f6f8c98a131bfbecc236eff8eed8e73","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/fca96f252f6f8c98a131bfbecc236eff8eed8e73"}],"sha":"169724dccb929bf4c40b8389fbece5e1a04cc7b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/169724dccb929bf4c40b8389fbece5e1a04cc7b1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44301196?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers","id":44301196,"login":"NoelHuibers","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzAxMTk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/fca96f252f6f8c98a131bfbecc236eff8eed8e73/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-24T22:44:37Z","email":"noel@huibers.io","name":"Noel Huibers"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-24T22:44:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Perf: DataBus in-memory threshold (53×) and near-linear SyncEngine ingest (#24) (#137)\n\n* perf(engine): keep small DataFrames in memory instead of spilling to parquet\n\nEvery pd.DataFrame put() used to write a parquet file and every get()\nre-read it from disk, so even a 1.4 MB frame paid a full disk round-trip\nper hop. Frames whose memory_usage(deep=True).sum() is at or below\nNOTEBOOKFLOW_SPILL_THRESHOLD_BYTES (default 8_000_000) now stay resident;\nlarger frames spill exactly as before. Setting the env var to 0 is the\nescape hatch that forces every frame to spill (old behavior).\n\nIsolation semantics are preserved exactly: put() stores a deep copy\n(mirroring the write-time snapshot a parquet write takes, so producer\nmutation after put never leaks) and get() returns a fresh deep copy per\nconsumer (mirroring the fresh object a parquet re-read materializes).\nReplacement transitions reuse the existing orphan-unlink from PR #136:\nspill->memory and spill->spill unlink the old file; memory payloads hold\na DataFrame, not a Path, so there is nothing to unlink. clear_node /\nclear_run drop both forms unchanged.\n\nBenchmark (bench-tmp/bench_databus.py, single put/get excludes the\npyarrow warm-up call):\n\n  BEFORE  50k rows (1.4 MB):   100x(put+get) = 17.01 s   spilled=True\n  AFTER   50k rows (1.4 MB):   100x(put+get) =  0.32 s   spilled=False  (~53x)\n\n  BEFORE  500k rows (14.4 MB):  10x(put+get) =  7.17 s   spilled=True\n  AFTER   500k rows (14.4 MB):  10x(put+get) =  3.99-6.61 s spilled=True\n  (500k path unchanged in behavior; timings are disk-bound and vary\n  4.0-7.2 s run-to-run on this machine in both builds)\n\nVerified: uv run pytest (255 passed, incl. new threshold-boundary,\nisolation, threshold=0, and memory<->spill transition tests), ruff, ty.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* perf(graph-canvas): O(n) wire recompute + cheap graph snapshots in SyncEngine\n\nTwo ingest-path fixes from the #24 benchmarks, both behavior-preserving:\n\n1. recomputeAllWires resolved every binding through resolveRef /\n   groupIdForAlias, which linearly scan group.nodeIds / all groups per\n   call - O(n^2) per ingest. It now rebuilds a name-resolution index\n   (alias -> groupId, groupId -> name -> node) once at the start of each\n   recompute, O(n), then resolves all bindings via O(1) lookups. The\n   index is deliberately recompute-local rather than maintained across\n   mutation sites, so there is no invalidation to get wrong. First-wins\n   ordering on alias and name collisions matches the old scans exactly.\n   resolveRef/groupIdForAlias remain for the single-shot routeInputRef path.\n\n2. Every emission ran onGraphUpdate(structuredClone(graph)). Mutation-model\n   analysis: ingest rebuilds the ingested group''s NodeModels fresh, but\n   nodes in OTHER groups persist and ARE mutated in place afterwards\n   (renameNode writes node.name + sibling inputs; createWire/applyPorts/\n   ensureOutputPort/ensurePassthroughNode reassign inputs/outputs;\n   updateNodeContents swaps metadata; upsertGroup/ingest mutate\n   group.alias/nodeIds). Sharing internal references with emissions is\n   therefore NOT safe - a later in-place mutation would rewrite a snapshot\n   a React consumer already holds - so instead of the shallow-share or\n   changed-group-clone-cache variants, getGraph() keeps full deep-clone\n   semantics but swaps structuredClone for a shape-aware clone: the model\n   shapes (NodeModel/NodeGroupModel/WireModel, types.ts) are flat, so\n   spread + fresh arrays is a complete deep clone; node.metadata is the one\n   open-ended field and keeps structuredClone. Identical isolation at a\n   fraction of the cost; consumers still get all-new object identities per\n   emission. All getGraph call sites (internal emissions, addManifestNode,\n   tests; extensions consume only via onGraphUpdate) get the same snapshot\n   semantics as before.\n\nBenchmark (bench-tmp/bench_syncengine.ts - single synthetic notebook,\nchained markers, 80% marker / 20% plain cells, median of 9):\n\n  cells   fresh BEFORE   fresh AFTER   re-ingest BEFORE   re-ingest AFTER\n    50        1.2 ms        1.2 ms          0.9 ms             1.3 ms\n   100        1.2 ms        1.2 ms          1.5 ms             1.8 ms\n   200        3.0 ms        2.5 ms          2.6 ms             2.3 ms\n   400       12.4 ms        4.2 ms          8.9 ms             5.5 ms\n   800       73.9 ms       11.4 ms         55.1 ms            13.1 ms\n  1600      248.5 ms       27.5 ms        224.5 ms            28.1 ms\n\nGrowth is now near-linear (2x cells ~ 2.4x time at the top end vs ~3.4x\nquadratic before); 800 cells lands at ~11-19 ms across runs, well under\nthe ~35 ms target.\n\nVerified: graph-canvas vitest 137/137 unchanged, tsc -b, biome, repo\npnpm typecheck 7/7, web-app vitest 54/54.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e6f80d08d0ad73704047cd19f14ee562f5d3aa57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/trees/e6f80d08d0ad73704047cd19f14ee562f5d3aa57"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/commits/fca96f252f6f8c98a131bfbecc236eff8eed8e73","verification":{"payload":"tree e6f80d08d0ad73704047cd19f14ee562f5d3aa57\nparent bad72fc2dcf3e22211b0b03d40a298f3805f832e\nauthor Noel Huibers <noel@huibers.io> 1784933077 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784933077 +0200\n\nPerf: DataBus in-memory threshold (53×) and near-linear SyncEngine ingest (#24) (#137)\n\n* perf(engine): keep small DataFrames in memory instead of spilling to parquet\n\nEvery pd.DataFrame put() used to write a parquet file and every get()\nre-read it from disk, so even a 1.4 MB frame paid a full disk round-trip\nper hop. Frames whose memory_usage(deep=True).sum() is at or below\nNOTEBOOKFLOW_SPILL_THRESHOLD_BYTES (default 8_000_000) now stay resident;\nlarger frames spill exactly as before. Setting the env var to 0 is the\nescape hatch that forces every frame to spill (old behavior).\n\nIsolation semantics are preserved exactly: put() stores a deep copy\n(mirroring the write-time snapshot a parquet write takes, so producer\nmutation after put never leaks) and get() returns a fresh deep copy per\nconsumer (mirroring the fresh object a parquet re-read materializes).\nReplacement transitions reuse the existing orphan-unlink from PR #136:\nspill->memory and spill->spill unlink the old file; memory payloads hold\na DataFrame, not a Path, so there is nothing to unlink. clear_node /\nclear_run drop both forms unchanged.\n\nBenchmark (bench-tmp/bench_databus.py, single put/get excludes the\npyarrow warm-up call):\n\n  BEFORE  50k rows (1.4 MB):   100x(put+get) = 17.01 s   spilled=True\n  AFTER   50k rows (1.4 MB):   100x(put+get) =  0.32 s   spilled=False  (~53x)\n\n  BEFORE  500k rows (14.4 MB):  10x(put+get) =  7.17 s   spilled=True\n  AFTER   500k rows (14.4 MB):  10x(put+get) =  3.99-6.61 s spilled=True\n  (500k path unchanged in behavior; timings are disk-bound and vary\n  4.0-7.2 s run-to-run on this machine in both builds)\n\nVerified: uv run pytest (255 passed, incl. new threshold-boundary,\nisolation, threshold=0, and memory<->spill transition tests), ruff, ty.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* perf(graph-canvas): O(n) wire recompute + cheap graph snapshots in SyncEngine\n\nTwo ingest-path fixes from the #24 benchmarks, both behavior-preserving:\n\n1. recomputeAllWires resolved every binding through resolveRef /\n   groupIdForAlias, which linearly scan group.nodeIds / all groups per\n   call - O(n^2) per ingest. It now rebuilds a name-resolution index\n   (alias -> groupId, groupId -> name -> node) once at the start of each\n   recompute, O(n), then resolves all bindings via O(1) lookups. The\n   index is deliberately recompute-local rather than maintained across\n   mutation sites, so there is no invalidation to get wrong. First-wins\n   ordering on alias and name collisions matches the old scans exactly.\n   resolveRef/groupIdForAlias remain for the single-shot routeInputRef path.\n\n2. Every emission ran onGraphUpdate(structuredClone(graph)). Mutation-model\n   analysis: ingest rebuilds the ingested group''s NodeModels fresh, but\n   nodes in OTHER groups persist and ARE mutated in place afterwards\n   (renameNode writes node.name + sibling inputs; createWire/applyPorts/\n   ensureOutputPort/ensurePassthroughNode reassign inputs/outputs;\n   updateNodeContents swaps metadata; upsertGroup/ingest mutate\n   group.alias/nodeIds). Sharing internal references with emissions is\n   therefore NOT safe - a later in-place mutation would rewrite a snapshot\n   a React consumer already holds - so instead of the shallow-share or\n   changed-group-clone-cache variants, getGraph() keeps full deep-clone\n   semantics but swaps structuredClone for a shape-aware clone: the model\n   shapes (NodeModel/NodeGroupModel/WireModel, types.ts) are flat, so\n   spread + fresh arrays is a complete deep clone; node.metadata is the one\n   open-ended field and keeps structuredClone. Identical isolation at a\n   fraction of the cost; consumers still get all-new object identities per\n   emission. All getGraph call sites (internal emissions, addManifestNode,\n   tests; extensions consume only via onGraphUpdate) get the same snapshot\n   semantics as before.\n\nBenchmark (bench-tmp/bench_syncengine.ts - single synthetic notebook,\nchained markers, 80% marker / 20% plain cells, median of 9):\n\n  cells   fresh BEFORE   fresh AFTER   re-ingest BEFORE   re-ingest AFTER\n    50        1.2 ms        1.2 ms          0.9 ms             1.3 ms\n   100        1.2 ms        1.2 ms          1.5 ms             1.8 ms\n   200        3.0 ms        2.5 ms          2.6 ms             2.3 ms\n   400       12.4 ms        4.2 ms          8.9 ms             5.5 ms\n   800       73.9 ms       11.4 ms         55.1 ms            13.1 ms\n  1600      248.5 ms       27.5 ms        224.5 ms            28.1 ms\n\nGrowth is now near-linear (2x cells ~ 2.4x time at the top end vs ~3.4x\nquadratic before); 800 cells lands at ~11-19 ms across runs, well under\nthe ~35 ms target.\n\nVerified: graph-canvas vitest 137/137 unchanged, tsc -b, biome, repo\npnpm typecheck 7/7, web-app vitest 54/54.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqY+rVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAl6EQABc8TSNg2Lr3a4XV9cdBXOOb\nYt1ytwfuFkB3vwld9tRIsYhlARsr+CefNtd2laNzVirKw57WJV2LzburobBmprbI\nMuU3raeaFZaU0e3VyYJBDbusMQTICAmj1OcCEDI8VzQL2eH5i7cJUoewqsQMp3p6\n9arLrUqgwQ4ux/vynChLWx0xY9YjctdgZOdMMTuhv7PzQN9V58dSrA7mlttS28rm\nnXPBVh+H3pys51rU8JkqwBpQEP79HypqhyWJVnhiiCTJB7SB/jksDaWcg/wGLEZM\niHWxtCtYcrQMFWiYjDZCfriBjYLMpds4vbINTJ3UJxv28qADRLWqWpe/V0x508M7\n5FjpE125WA2bwF/KooUAjY+3l8BGqrPW1R4m8sARJAeX41ChBlqRVHa7dAZp+Kwf\n3iwvwLtxgLNT75OCTl4jpkXqsPPqSflA2O7EpiDr5POjFZW9n+PW3gcuZGxMHLtA\ni4ynWuFfhtqJY5b0562K+4PHH0yPTEY2w74so9i+3kzUv0CgRALrISsDqyHND9kj\necYUi7qLkM888g+Xw88dtXUbEb1bnv5i58jwJSAXlwaocQKiRV1Vk0c8eOL+2JpH\n9FywJO97KIXqzFlbPR0rwP2fRFiP3Z4IrXBB2n+4wUtMOT27gbXdKDYWynZ7oB/X\nemaXBYoXl7ufL60FnW2k\n=egFt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-24T22:44:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/fca96f252f6f8c98a131bfbecc236eff8eed8e73","node_id":"C_kwDOSWT-J9oAKGZjYTk2ZjI1MmY2ZjhjOThhMTMxYmZiZWNjMjM2ZWZmOGVlZDhlNzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/bad72fc2dcf3e22211b0b03d40a298f3805f832e","sha":"bad72fc2dcf3e22211b0b03d40a298f3805f832e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/bad72fc2dcf3e22211b0b03d40a298f3805f832e"}],"sha":"fca96f252f6f8c98a131bfbecc236eff8eed8e73","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/fca96f252f6f8c98a131bfbecc236eff8eed8e73"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44301196?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers","id":44301196,"login":"NoelHuibers","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzAxMTk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/bad72fc2dcf3e22211b0b03d40a298f3805f832e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-21T14:57:56Z","email":"noel@huibers.io","name":"Noel Huibers"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-21T14:57:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Perf quick wins from the #24 benchmarks: memoized cells, single-file ingest, decoupled suggestions, DataBus fixes (#136)\n\n* perf(web-app): memoize CellEditor and skip re-ingesting unchanged files\n\nTwo S-effort fixes from the issue-#24 benchmark report:\n\nCellList/CellEditor: typing in one cell re-rendered every cell because\nCellEditor was unmemoized and two props broke identity each render (the\ninline onChange closure and the `?? []` outputs fallback). CellEditor is\nnow wrapped in React.memo; the change callback becomes a stable\nindex-tagged onChangeAt (CellEditor already receives `index`), and a\nmodule-level frozen EMPTY_OUTPUTS constant replaces the per-render `[]`.\nCellEditor/CellOutputs outputs prop widened to `readonly NbOutput[]`\n(type-only; both components only read the array). Remaining props are\nalready identity-stable for untouched cells: `cell` (CellList''s\nhandleChange slices the draft but reuses unchanged cell objects), and\nthe primitives index/isStreaming.\n\nApp ingest loop: on every cellsByPath change the effect re-ingested all\nopen files, but each SyncEngine.ingestNotebook already runs\nrecomputeAllWires() workspace-wide, so re-ingesting unchanged files is\nredundant. The effect now tracks the last-ingested cells array per path\nand skips identity-unchanged entries; a new SyncEngine (open/close)\nresets the tracker so all files ingest into the fresh engine as before.\n\nZero-behavior-change reasoning for the ingest skip:\n- useWorkspaceFiles'' cellsByPath memo preserves per-path entry identity\n  for untouched files (active file maps to notebook.cells, inactive\n  files to their frozen snapshot.cells), so identity comparison is a\n  sound \"unchanged\" signal.\n- ingestNotebook ignores its timestamp param (_timestamp), is\n  idempotent per path, and cross-file wires come from\n  recomputeAllWires() which the changed file''s ingest still triggers.\n- The only skipped side effect is clearLastCellEditsFor(path) for\n  unchanged paths; the web-app never calls markCellEdited, so\n  lastCellEdit is always empty in this host and the skip is a no-op.\n\nVerified: app-core + web-app vitest green, repo-wide typecheck, web-app\nvite build, biome check clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* perf(graph-canvas): decouple input suggestions from runtime-event rebuilds\n\nThe baseNodes memo in Canvas depends on the runtime overlays\n(runtimeByNode/timingByNode/metaByNode/unresolvedByNode), so every\nruntime-status event rebuilds all node data — and each rebuild reran\ncollectInputRefs per node, an O(n^2) sweep over the whole graph\n(portSuggestions.ts).\n\nInput-ref autocomplete pools only depend on the graph shape and\nvariablesByNode, so they now live in their own useMemo keyed on exactly\nthose two inputs, producing a nodeId -> string[] record that buildNodes\nconsumes. Runtime events still rebuild the node-data objects themselves\n(that overlay split is the M-effort follow-up, out of scope here) but no\nlonger recompute suggestions.\n\nBehavior-preserving: the memo calls the same collectInputRefs(graph,\nvars, nodeId) for every node in graph.nodes, so contents and order per\nnode are byte-identical; buildNodes assigns the precomputed entry (the\n`?? []` fallback is unreachable for nodes sourced from graph.nodes).\nSuggestions are now also precomputed for nodes in collapsed groups\n(previously skipped) — extra unused work in a rarer path, no output\ndifference.\n\nVerified: graph-canvas vitest 137/137 green (portSuggestions.test.ts and\ncomponent tests unchanged), tsc build, biome check clean, repo-wide\ntypecheck (web-app + vscode + jupyterlab against rebuilt dist).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* perf(engine): DataBus spill-leak fix + scalar fast paths in put/get\n\nThree small DataBus fixes from the issue-#24 benchmark report:\n\n- Overwriting a key that held a spilled DataFrame left the previous\n  parquet file on disk until clear_run. put() now best-effort unlinks\n  (missing_ok) the replaced spill file — both when a DataFrame replaces\n  a DataFrame and when a JSON value replaces a DataFrame. The unlink\n  runs only after the new value is validated/spilled, so a failing put\n  still leaves the previous payload and its file intact.\n- put() ran json.dumps validation on every payload; None/bool/int/\n  float/str are JSON-serializable by construction, so scalars now skip\n  the round-trip. Containers (dict/list) keep the validation, so the\n  \"not JSON-serializable\" error for bad contents is unchanged.\n- get() deep-copied every in-memory value; scalars are immutable\n  (deepcopy returns the same object anyway) and are now returned\n  directly. Containers are still deep-copied, preserving fan-out\n  isolation between consumers.\n\nNew tests: overwrite unlinks the old parquet (and DataFrame→JSON\nreplacement empties the spill dir), failed put keeps the previous\npayload + file, scalar round-trip preserves value and exact type, and\ncontainer payloads remain isolated across gets after mutation.\n\nVerified: uv run pytest (247 passed, mirrors ci.yml), ruff check, ty\ncheck all clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8df93deecfa3821bc37d67f6ae510cca406ee4b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/trees/8df93deecfa3821bc37d67f6ae510cca406ee4b2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/commits/bad72fc2dcf3e22211b0b03d40a298f3805f832e","verification":{"payload":"tree 8df93deecfa3821bc37d67f6ae510cca406ee4b2\nparent 998b48d6f8ac5aa557d9ca54bc43d99e82194f7e\nauthor Noel Huibers <noel@huibers.io> 1784645876 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784645876 +0200\n\nPerf quick wins from the #24 benchmarks: memoized cells, single-file ingest, decoupled suggestions, DataBus fixes (#136)\n\n* perf(web-app): memoize CellEditor and skip re-ingesting unchanged files\n\nTwo S-effort fixes from the issue-#24 benchmark report:\n\nCellList/CellEditor: typing in one cell re-rendered every cell because\nCellEditor was unmemoized and two props broke identity each render (the\ninline onChange closure and the `?? []` outputs fallback). CellEditor is\nnow wrapped in React.memo; the change callback becomes a stable\nindex-tagged onChangeAt (CellEditor already receives `index`), and a\nmodule-level frozen EMPTY_OUTPUTS constant replaces the per-render `[]`.\nCellEditor/CellOutputs outputs prop widened to `readonly NbOutput[]`\n(type-only; both components only read the array). Remaining props are\nalready identity-stable for untouched cells: `cell` (CellList''s\nhandleChange slices the draft but reuses unchanged cell objects), and\nthe primitives index/isStreaming.\n\nApp ingest loop: on every cellsByPath change the effect re-ingested all\nopen files, but each SyncEngine.ingestNotebook already runs\nrecomputeAllWires() workspace-wide, so re-ingesting unchanged files is\nredundant. The effect now tracks the last-ingested cells array per path\nand skips identity-unchanged entries; a new SyncEngine (open/close)\nresets the tracker so all files ingest into the fresh engine as before.\n\nZero-behavior-change reasoning for the ingest skip:\n- useWorkspaceFiles'' cellsByPath memo preserves per-path entry identity\n  for untouched files (active file maps to notebook.cells, inactive\n  files to their frozen snapshot.cells), so identity comparison is a\n  sound \"unchanged\" signal.\n- ingestNotebook ignores its timestamp param (_timestamp), is\n  idempotent per path, and cross-file wires come from\n  recomputeAllWires() which the changed file''s ingest still triggers.\n- The only skipped side effect is clearLastCellEditsFor(path) for\n  unchanged paths; the web-app never calls markCellEdited, so\n  lastCellEdit is always empty in this host and the skip is a no-op.\n\nVerified: app-core + web-app vitest green, repo-wide typecheck, web-app\nvite build, biome check clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* perf(graph-canvas): decouple input suggestions from runtime-event rebuilds\n\nThe baseNodes memo in Canvas depends on the runtime overlays\n(runtimeByNode/timingByNode/metaByNode/unresolvedByNode), so every\nruntime-status event rebuilds all node data — and each rebuild reran\ncollectInputRefs per node, an O(n^2) sweep over the whole graph\n(portSuggestions.ts).\n\nInput-ref autocomplete pools only depend on the graph shape and\nvariablesByNode, so they now live in their own useMemo keyed on exactly\nthose two inputs, producing a nodeId -> string[] record that buildNodes\nconsumes. Runtime events still rebuild the node-data objects themselves\n(that overlay split is the M-effort follow-up, out of scope here) but no\nlonger recompute suggestions.\n\nBehavior-preserving: the memo calls the same collectInputRefs(graph,\nvars, nodeId) for every node in graph.nodes, so contents and order per\nnode are byte-identical; buildNodes assigns the precomputed entry (the\n`?? []` fallback is unreachable for nodes sourced from graph.nodes).\nSuggestions are now also precomputed for nodes in collapsed groups\n(previously skipped) — extra unused work in a rarer path, no output\ndifference.\n\nVerified: graph-canvas vitest 137/137 green (portSuggestions.test.ts and\ncomponent tests unchanged), tsc build, biome check clean, repo-wide\ntypecheck (web-app + vscode + jupyterlab against rebuilt dist).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* perf(engine): DataBus spill-leak fix + scalar fast paths in put/get\n\nThree small DataBus fixes from the issue-#24 benchmark report:\n\n- Overwriting a key that held a spilled DataFrame left the previous\n  parquet file on disk until clear_run. put() now best-effort unlinks\n  (missing_ok) the replaced spill file — both when a DataFrame replaces\n  a DataFrame and when a JSON value replaces a DataFrame. The unlink\n  runs only after the new value is validated/spilled, so a failing put\n  still leaves the previous payload and its file intact.\n- put() ran json.dumps validation on every payload; None/bool/int/\n  float/str are JSON-serializable by construction, so scalars now skip\n  the round-trip. Containers (dict/list) keep the validation, so the\n  \"not JSON-serializable\" error for bad contents is unchanged.\n- get() deep-copied every in-memory value; scalars are immutable\n  (deepcopy returns the same object anyway) and are now returned\n  directly. Containers are still deep-copied, preserving fan-out\n  isolation between consumers.\n\nNew tests: overwrite unlinks the old parquet (and DataFrame→JSON\nreplacement empties the spill dir), failed put keeps the previous\npayload + file, scalar round-trip preserves value and exact type, and\ncontainer payloads remain isolated across gets after mutation.\n\nVerified: uv run pytest (247 passed, mirrors ci.yml), ruff check, ty\ncheck all clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX4j1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVvYQAE55V3wEOHiagyOx0rtn/0Ms\nePjHjeCcecKS9qSnb5d2/tvYiTtZ7iIB9FeJku8ObpbUUvUVg1Oe9UXFN91SlehC\ntqwP+vT1fz2qtl80ll1BCMBkoGzu0PgrWJz0LqXFpYsGsn1ZOj6Qp4ccZ277o/Ig\ntu9zUBtGMLHPxUjF0p0pIn/OOeps96QAzQZpUH16hJlSUUNPNhT1prTsoIImhtdS\nE4eYG58xbdzXUWT0+W8OvLZ