298f3805f832e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/bad72fc2dcf3e22211b0b03d40a298f3805f832e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44301196?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers","id":44301196,"login":"NoelHuibers","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzAxMTk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/998b48d6f8ac5aa557d9ca54bc43d99e82194f7e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-19T19:52:35Z","email":"noel@huibers.io","name":"Noel Huibers"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-19T19:52:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Cross-surface accounts: device-flow sign-in + shared cloud notebooks and BYOK key in both extensions (#88) (#135)\n\n* docs: decide engine deployment approach\n\n* feat(web-app): enable device-authorization + bearer auth for extensions\n\nAdds the BetterAuth deviceAuthorization plugin (15m codes, 5s polling,\nabsolute /device verification URI, client allowlist for the VS Code and\nJupyterLab extensions) and the bearer plugin so device access tokens work\nagainst the existing /api handlers via getSession. New deviceCode table +\ngenerated migration; device-flow rate-limit rules; device client plugin on\nthe browser auth client.\n\nPart of #88 (Phase A).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(web-app): add /device approval page and CORS for extension API routes\n\n/device (DE+EN) reads ?user_code or accepts manual entry, prompts sign-in\nwhen signed out, claims the code via GET /api/auth/device (required before\napprove/deny), then approves or denies via the device-authorization client.\nGitHub/Google brand icons move to components/BrandIcons for reuse with\n/login.\n\nCORS (bearer-only, no Allow-Credentials) is handled for /api/notebooks,\n/api/provider-key and /api/auth/device in both the dev dispatcher\n(src/server/api.ts) and the self-contained Vercel handler (api/index.ts);\nVite''s built-in CORS middleware is disabled so dev matches prod.\n\nPart of #88.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(app-core): add CloudClient and workspaceDoc for cross-surface cloud access\n\nCloudClient mirrors EngineClient conventions (injected baseUrl + bearer\ntoken, setToken, Authorization only when a token is set) and covers the\nVercel /api surface only: notebooks CRUD and the BYOK provider key. A\n`credentials` option enables cookie mode so the web app can keep using the\nsession cookie; extensions use the device-flow bearer token instead (#88).\nFailures throw a typed CloudRequestError carrying the HTTP status.\n\nserializeWorkspace/parseWorkspace and the Workspace* document types move\nfrom the web app''s notebooksApi into app-core''s pure workspaceDoc module;\nparse failures now throw WorkspaceParseError with a machine-readable code.\nThe web app''s notebooksApi/providerKeyApi become thin adapters that keep\ntheir existing export signatures and map the typed errors onto the same\nLocalizableError keys as before, so web-app behavior and tests are\nunchanged.\n\nPart of #88.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vscode): optional NotebookFlow Cloud account — device sign-in, cloud notebooks, account BYOK\n\nAdds host-side cloud commands (#88 Phase B) on top of the device-\nauthorization flow the server enabled: cloudSignIn requests a device code\n(client_id notebookflow-vscode), copies the user code to the clipboard,\nopens the browser to the verification URL, and polls the token endpoint\n(slow_down backoff, expired/denied messages, cancellable progress) before\nstoring the bearer token in SecretStorage; cloudSignOut deletes it.\nopenCloudNotebook lists the account''s notebooks, writes the picked\nworkspace''s .ipynb files into the first workspace folder (asking before\noverwriting) and opens the first; saveNotebookToCloud serializes the\nactive notebook editor to nbformat JSON and creates a single-file cloud\nworkspace. A status bar item ($(cloud) NotebookFlow) reflects the sign-in\nstate and opens a small action picker.\n\nThe webview credentials push now falls back to the signed-in account''s\nsaved provider key when no local llmApiKey secret is set (local settings\nwin; silent skip on failure) — the key is still only used with the LOCAL\nengine. All cloud traffic targets the new notebookflow.cloud.baseUrl\nsetting (default https://notebookflow.app); the extension never talks to\nthe hosted engine, and signed-out behavior is unchanged.\n\nPart of #88.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(jupyterlab): optional NotebookFlow Cloud account — device sign-in, cloud notebooks, account BYOK\n\nAdds the cloud commands (#88 Phase C) over the same device-authorization\nflow as VS Code: notebookflow:cloud-sign-in requests a device code\n(client_id notebookflow-jupyterlab, browser fetch against the CORS-enabled\n/api/auth/device routes), shows the user code in a dialog with an Open\nBrowser button, polls with slow_down backoff and typed expired/denied\nerrors (pure deviceAuth module + tests), and writes the token to the new\ncloudToken setting (plain-text caveat documented, like llmApiKey);\ncloud-sign-out clears it. open-cloud-notebook lists the account''s\nnotebooks, writes the picked workspace''s .ipynb files next to the current\nnotebook via the Contents API and opens the first through docmanager:open;\nsave-notebook-to-cloud wraps the current panel''s on-disk nbformat JSON as\na single-file cloud workspace. All four are in the palette, plus a small\nlocalized (EN/DE) Cloud menu button in the SplitView header.\n\nSplitView''s credentials application now falls back to the signed-in\naccount''s saved provider key when llmApiKey is empty (local settings win;\nsilent skip on failure, stale-response guards) — the key is only ever sent\nto the LOCAL kernel/engine. Cloud traffic targets the new cloudBaseUrl\nsetting (default https://notebookflow.app); signed-out behavior is\nunchanged.\n\nPart of #88.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"77de9dd0dcc7ee9eff9ae27c561cf23d195b4c78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/trees/77de9dd0dcc7ee9eff9ae27c561cf23d195b4c78"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/commits/998b48d6f8ac5aa557d9ca54bc43d99e82194f7e","verification":{"payload":"tree 77de9dd0dcc7ee9eff9ae27c561cf23d195b4c78\nparent bd6fbf235ce89a81e6a9aff74fa0868f44c78c90\nauthor Noel Huibers <noel@huibers.io> 1784490755 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784490755 +0200\n\nCross-surface accounts: device-flow sign-in + shared cloud notebooks and BYOK key in both extensions (#88) (#135)\n\n* docs: decide engine deployment approach\n\n* feat(web-app): enable device-authorization + bearer auth for extensions\n\nAdds the BetterAuth deviceAuthorization plugin (15m codes, 5s polling,\nabsolute /device verification URI, client allowlist for the VS Code and\nJupyterLab extensions) and the bearer plugin so device access tokens work\nagainst the existing /api handlers via getSession. New deviceCode table +\ngenerated migration; device-flow rate-limit rules; device client plugin on\nthe browser auth client.\n\nPart of #88 (Phase A).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(web-app): add /device approval page and CORS for extension API routes\n\n/device (DE+EN) reads ?user_code or accepts manual entry, prompts sign-in\nwhen signed out, claims the code via GET /api/auth/device (required before\napprove/deny), then approves or denies via the device-authorization client.\nGitHub/Google brand icons move to components/BrandIcons for reuse with\n/login.\n\nCORS (bearer-only, no Allow-Credentials) is handled for /api/notebooks,\n/api/provider-key and /api/auth/device in both the dev dispatcher\n(src/server/api.ts) and the self-contained Vercel handler (api/index.ts);\nVite''s built-in CORS middleware is disabled so dev matches prod.\n\nPart of #88.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(app-core): add CloudClient and workspaceDoc for cross-surface cloud access\n\nCloudClient mirrors EngineClient conventions (injected baseUrl + bearer\ntoken, setToken, Authorization only when a token is set) and covers the\nVercel /api surface only: notebooks CRUD and the BYOK provider key. A\n`credentials` option enables cookie mode so the web app can keep using the\nsession cookie; extensions use the device-flow bearer token instead (#88).\nFailures throw a typed CloudRequestError carrying the HTTP status.\n\nserializeWorkspace/parseWorkspace and the Workspace* document types move\nfrom the web app''s notebooksApi into app-core''s pure workspaceDoc module;\nparse failures now throw WorkspaceParseError with a machine-readable code.\nThe web app''s notebooksApi/providerKeyApi become thin adapters that keep\ntheir existing export signatures and map the typed errors onto the same\nLocalizableError keys as before, so web-app behavior and tests are\nunchanged.\n\nPart of #88.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vscode): optional NotebookFlow Cloud account — device sign-in, cloud notebooks, account BYOK\n\nAdds host-side cloud commands (#88 Phase B) on top of the device-\nauthorization flow the server enabled: cloudSignIn requests a device code\n(client_id notebookflow-vscode), copies the user code to the clipboard,\nopens the browser to the verification URL, and polls the token endpoint\n(slow_down backoff, expired/denied messages, cancellable progress) before\nstoring the bearer token in SecretStorage; cloudSignOut deletes it.\nopenCloudNotebook lists the account''s notebooks, writes the picked\nworkspace''s .ipynb files into the first workspace folder (asking before\noverwriting) and opens the first; saveNotebookToCloud serializes the\nactive notebook editor to nbformat JSON and creates a single-file cloud\nworkspace. A status bar item ($(cloud) NotebookFlow) reflects the sign-in\nstate and opens a small action picker.\n\nThe webview credentials push now falls back to the signed-in account''s\nsaved provider key when no local llmApiKey secret is set (local settings\nwin; silent skip on failure) — the key is still only used with the LOCAL\nengine. All cloud traffic targets the new notebookflow.cloud.baseUrl\nsetting (default https://notebookflow.app); the extension never talks to\nthe hosted engine, and signed-out behavior is unchanged.\n\nPart of #88.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(jupyterlab): optional NotebookFlow Cloud account — device sign-in, cloud notebooks, account BYOK\n\nAdds the cloud commands (#88 Phase C) over the same device-authorization\nflow as VS Code: notebookflow:cloud-sign-in requests a device code\n(client_id notebookflow-jupyterlab, browser fetch against the CORS-enabled\n/api/auth/device routes), shows the user code in a dialog with an Open\nBrowser button, polls with slow_down backoff and typed expired/denied\nerrors (pure deviceAuth module + tests), and writes the token to the new\ncloudToken setting (plain-text caveat documented, like llmApiKey);\ncloud-sign-out clears it. open-cloud-notebook lists the account''s\nnotebooks, writes the picked workspace''s .ipynb files next to the current\nnotebook via the Contents API and opens the first through docmanager:open;\nsave-notebook-to-cloud wraps the current panel''s on-disk nbformat JSON as\na single-file cloud workspace. All four are in the palette, plus a small\nlocalized (EN/DE) Cloud menu button in the SplitView header.\n\nSplitView''s credentials application now falls back to the signed-in\naccount''s saved provider key when llmApiKey is empty (local settings win;\nsilent skip on failure, stale-response guards) — the key is only ever sent\nto the LOCAL kernel/engine. Cloud traffic targets the new cloudBaseUrl\nsetting (default https://notebookflow.app); signed-out behavior is\nunchanged.\n\nPart of #88.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXSsDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgjIQAE21X+Wio6uKfGvT4iA5rePi\nlm1nRMzr1XTO/zUbP3fzN70wMlaf/V8aYFt7OyKvtEprgmExm8F7/SQQkFHBgzMM\nX3I5guyW/JDfNtf1+gO58xql9xgO46k/AGzxAriuLRLxXZ+lJ10Qoi/LBTsM3ycY\nW3VT8kko3Npn3cCid3WddivoZ7+xig7PWRGd7NPEk9W5IZUhS+PYGPS3ZlTvRTYf\ngkJF2VAC5BotM7RBrFrKMUfIKfaL/kO1bBIlleTPLE+qA5kGbPu79syd95YN9yDa\njVZ5YSGxt6KHzSwXWBklP05j8bChb4WATYYBChkh1KJNWYYib5bHp9Mk2DHMYcFT\nKobRYA9t+H9gs6Gop5N8Foe8uBq1IUrAq3lJMIMwnXl/veH1iN+hLghPCEisHWpW\nsvogSMDyJKxovBBg9o3k22+E6XnQVxTYYBktkJ1bwrWfzg60oLaRyRiqpACUqK4z\njrd1lqsvVGpJZPqIkCDlycfX3M5kFOpvac3J1JcAXApLpI7qR3+V1ZKAEt0L+Yqi\n2BPAi9Cj8NOFBheFVCsyNt1DsAOqZ8uFw1oW26RxwmGwekdbm6ihnfx7sD4km0EC\nqIGqAXVv/eon2zxjQqe6OoRhSmadaNSs3jxeM/H6FvOIzoZj1i5VIyLqX0A1YuNW\n3O7oyXRkmYAuWqxeCikx\n=u42Z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-19T19:52:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1