e_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/bd6fbf235ce89a81e6a9aff74fa0868f44c78c90","node_id":"C_kwDOSWT-J9oAKGJkNmZiZjIzNWNlODlhODFlNmE5YWZmNzRmYTA4NjhmNDRjNzhjOTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/2a79326246f5be74bd76ef1b5f874fdc66621e4a","sha":"2a79326246f5be74bd76ef1b5f874fdc66621e4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/2a79326246f5be74bd76ef1b5f874fdc66621e4a"}],"sha":"bd6fbf235ce89a81e6a9aff74fa0868f44c78c90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/bd6fbf235ce89a81e6a9aff74fa0868f44c78c90"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44301196?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers","id":44301196,"login":"NoelHuibers","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzAxMTk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/2a79326246f5be74bd76ef1b5f874fdc66621e4a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-19T14:08:09Z","email":"noel@huibers.io","name":"Noel Huibers"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-19T14:08:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Extension webviews: full Canvas prop parity — overlays, autocomplete, minimap, drag-to-add, palette filters (#85) (#133)\n\n* refactor(app-core): move extractSourceFilename into shared sourceMeta module\n\nLift the reader-literal filename heuristic out of the web-app''s notebook\nlib into @notebookflow/app-core so the VS Code and JupyterLab surfaces\ncan derive the same canvas meta line. Web-app now imports it from\napp-core; covered by a small vitest in app-core.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vscode): full Canvas prop parity in the webview\n\nBring the VS Code webview''s canvas up to the web-app''s behaviour:\n\n- Run overlay state: seed every node \"queued\" at run start, nodeStarted\n  -> running, nodeCompleted -> status/durationMs/rows, pipelineCompleted\n  -> run summary; maps reset on each run.\n- Debounced (300ms) analyzeCells effect feeding definedByCell, plus the\n  variablesByNode / metaByNode (shared extractSourceFilename + rows) /\n  unresolvedByNode derivations.\n- Minimap toggle via canvas control and bare M key (suppressed while\n  typing), matching the web-app shortcut.\n- Palette search box and tag-filter pills with EN+DE strings, filtering\n  the grouped palette list.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(jupyterlab): full Canvas prop parity in the split view\n\nBring the JupyterLab surface''s canvas up to the web-app''s behaviour:\n\n- Run overlay state captured inside handleRun''s onEvent: seed every\n  node \"queued\" at run start, nodeStarted -> running, nodeCompleted ->\n  status/durationMs/rows, pipelineCompleted -> run summary; existing\n  outputsByNodeId capture kept intact.\n- New optional AppProps.onAnalyzeCells wired through SplitView to the\n  app-core client''s analyzeCells; a debounced (300ms) effect over the\n  bridge''s cells feeds definedByCell, with variablesByNode / metaByNode\n  (shared extractSourceFilename + rows) / unresolvedByNode derivations.\n- Drag-to-add: palette buttons are draggable via setPaletteDragData,\n  handleAddNode gains an insertAtCellIndex option, and handlePaneDrop /\n  onPaneDrop route gap drops between nodes.\n- Minimap toggle via canvas control and bare M key (suppressed while\n  typing / inside CodeMirror).\n- Palette search box and tag-filter pills in the existing inline-style\n  conventions on --jp-* vars, with EN+DE strings.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e2fa92c9b3500f4a22ba2a8f5ecfdcaf0f2f8957","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/trees/e2fa92c9b3500f4a22ba2a8f5ecfdcaf0f2f8957"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/commits/2a79326246f5be74bd76ef1b5f874fdc66621e4a","verification":{"payload":"tree e2fa92c9b3500f4a22ba2a8f5ecfdcaf0f2f8957\nparent 7f085134672b9b0497483419ce5a28434c8e6389\nauthor Noel Huibers <noel@huibers.io> 1784470089 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784470089 +0200\n\nExtension webviews: full Canvas prop parity — overlays, autocomplete, minimap, drag-to-add, palette filters (#85) (#133)\n\n* refactor(app-core): move extractSourceFilename into shared sourceMeta module\n\nLift the reader-literal filename heuristic out of the web-app''s notebook\nlib into @notebookflow/app-core so the VS Code and JupyterLab surfaces\ncan derive the same canvas meta line. Web-app now imports it from\napp-core; covered by a small vitest in app-core.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vscode): full Canvas prop parity in the webview\n\nBring the VS Code webview''s canvas up to the web-app''s behaviour:\n\n- Run overlay state: seed every node \"queued\" at run start, nodeStarted\n  -> running, nodeCompleted -> status/durationMs/rows, pipelineCompleted\n  -> run summary; maps reset on each run.\n- Debounced (300ms) analyzeCells effect feeding definedByCell, plus the\n  variablesByNode / metaByNode (shared extractSourceFilename + rows) /\n  unresolvedByNode derivations.\n- Minimap toggle via canvas control and bare M key (suppressed while\n  typing), matching the web-app shortcut.\n- Palette search box and tag-filter pills with EN+DE strings, filtering\n  the grouped palette list.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(jupyterlab): full Canvas prop parity in the split view\n\nBring the JupyterLab surface''s canvas up to the web-app''s behaviour:\n\n- Run overlay state captured inside handleRun''s onEvent: seed every\n  node \"queued\" at run start, nodeStarted -> running, nodeCompleted ->\n  status/durationMs/rows, pipelineCompleted -> run summary; existing\n  outputsByNodeId capture kept intact.\n- New optional AppProps.onAnalyzeCells wired through SplitView to the\n  app-core client''s analyzeCells; a debounced (300ms) effect over the\n  bridge''s cells feeds definedByCell, with variablesByNode / metaByNode\n  (shared extractSourceFilename + rows) / unresolvedByNode derivations.\n- Drag-to-add: palette buttons are draggable via setPaletteDragData,\n  handleAddNode gains an insertAtCellIndex option, and handlePaneDrop /\n  onPaneDrop route gap drops between nodes.\n- Minimap toggle via canvas control and bare M key (suppressed while\n  typing / inside CodeMirror).\n- Palette search box and tag-filter pills in the existing inline-style\n  conventions on --jp-* vars, with EN+DE strings.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXNpJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIrYQACK52rDWqrNoOwweI8AD/1OE\nuw+zPbZsgyTXPtQK52XwHagK7hD57Wj5zgdoKKP2yVgyQx5s12HU3XZ7wGAwn9iX\njZow7cHuM