url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/7f085134672b9b0497483419ce5a28434c8e6389"}],"sha":"2a79326246f5be74bd76ef1b5f874fdc66621e4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/2a79326246f5be74bd76ef1b5f874fdc66621e4a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44301196?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers","id":44301196,"login":"NoelHuibers","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzAxMTk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/7f085134672b9b0497483419ce5a28434c8e6389/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-19T09:50:04Z","email":"noel@huibers.io","name":"Noel Huibers"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-19T09:50:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"JupyterLab: BYOK settings, AI surfaces, data upload, and image outputs via app-core (#87) (#132)\n\n* feat(jupyterlab): add BYOK settings via ISettingRegistry\n\nRegister a settings schema (llmProvider/llmModel/llmApiKey/engineUrlOverride)\nunder schema/plugin.json, require ISettingRegistry in the plugin, and thread a\nsnapshot+subscribe SettingsAccessor into every SplitView. Adds the\n@notebookflow/app-core workspace dependency ahead of the EngineClient\nconsolidation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(jupyterlab): consolidate on app-core EngineClient and add AI surfaces\n\nDelete the local reduced EngineClient in favour of @notebookflow/app-core''s\n(BYOK credentials via setCredentials from the plugin settings, re-applied on\nevery settings change; jupyter-server-proxy URL logic moved to engineUrl.ts\nand honouring the new engineUrlOverride setting). Wire types in App/\nKernelBridge/NotebookBridge now come from app-core.\n\nAdds the Ask (Ctrl/Cmd+K) / Compose / Explain surfaces via the shared\nAskPalette, ComposeDialog and ExplanationPanel components, wired through\nprop callbacks (onAsk/onCompose/onExplain) in the existing prop-driven\nstyle. Compose Apply replaces the notebook cells through the\nNotebookBridge patch surface. EN+DE strings mirror the VS Code webview.\n\nThe kernel-preferred onRun execution path is unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(jupyterlab): theme app-core components via Tailwind on --jp-* tokens\n\nAdd a @tailwindcss/cli prebuild (build:css, wired before tsc in build and\nbuild:lab) compiling style/tailwind.css -> style/index.css, imported from\nsrc/index.ts and bundled by the labextension webpack build. The source maps\nthe shadcn design-token slots onto JupyterLab''s --jp-* theme variables and\nscans app-core + this package''s sources for utilities.\n\nPreflight is intentionally omitted (the stylesheet loads into the whole Lab\npage); a border/box-sizing reset scoped to .notebookflow-split-view replaces\nthe pieces the utilities rely on. The generated style/index.css is committed\nso CI/pip labextension builds work from a clean checkout without running\nTailwind.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(jupyterlab): sidebar outputs surface and data-file uploads\n\nCapture each node''s nbformat outputs from the shared EngineEvent stream\n(kernel and engine paths alike) into per-node state and render the shared\nCellOutputs component (incl. image/png figures) in the Selected sidebar\nsection. Add a Data sidebar section listing/uploading/deleting data files:\nwhen a kernel is attached, files go to the notebook''s directory via the\nJupyter Contents API (the kernel''s cwd — engine /files uploads are invisible\nto kernel runs); otherwise the engine''s /files REST surface is used.\nLocalized EN+DE; degrades to a muted note when neither target is reachable.\n\nThe kernel-preferred onRun execution path is unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"45708430c31e1fc687ca0327cc32289117b66e3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/trees/45708430c31e1fc687ca0327cc32289117b66e3b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/commits/7f085134672b9b0497483419ce5a28434c8e6389","verification":{"payload":"tree 45708430c31e1fc687ca0327cc32289117b66e3b\nparent a6cd40da534b7acaaafcf8fa5e06acc01e93ffdb\nauthor Noel Huibers <noel@huibers.io> 1784454604 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784454604 +0200\n\nJupyterLab: BYOK settings, AI surfaces, data upload, and image outputs via app-core (#87) (#132)\n\n* feat(jupyterlab): add BYOK settings via ISettingRegistry\n\nRegister a settings schema (llmProvider/llmModel/llmApiKey/engineUrlOverride)\nunder schema/plugin.json, require ISettingRegistry in the plugin, and thread a\nsnapshot+subscribe SettingsAccessor into every SplitView. Adds the\n@notebookflow/app-core workspace dependency ahead of the EngineClient\nconsolidation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(jupyterlab): consolidate on app-core EngineClient and add AI surfaces\n\nDelete the local reduced EngineClient in favour of @notebookflow/app-core''s\n(BYOK credentials via setCredentials from the plugin settings, re-applied on\nevery settings change; jupyter-server-proxy URL logic moved to engineUrl.ts\nand honouring the new engineUrlOverride setting). Wire types in App/\nKernelBridge/NotebookBridge now come from app-core.\n\nAdds the Ask (Ctrl/Cmd+K) / Compose / Explain surfaces via the shared\nAskPalette, ComposeDialog and ExplanationPanel components, wired through\nprop callbacks (onAsk/onCompose/onExplain) in the existing prop-driven\nstyle. Compose Apply replaces the notebook cells through the\nNotebookBridge patch surface. EN+DE strings mirror the VS Code webview.\n\nThe kernel-preferred onRun execution path is unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(jupyterlab): theme app-core components via Tailwind on --jp-* tokens\n\nAdd a @tailwindcss/cli prebuild (build:css, wired before tsc in build and\nbuild:lab) compiling style/tailwind.css -> style/index.css, imported from\nsrc/index.ts and bundled by the labextension webpack build. The source maps\nthe shadcn design-token slots onto JupyterLab''s --jp-* theme variables and\nscans app-core + this package''s sources for utilities.\n\nPreflight is intentionally omitted (the stylesheet loads into the whole Lab\npage); a border/box-sizing reset scoped to .notebookflow-split-view replaces\nthe pieces the utilities rely on. The generated style/index.css is committed\nso CI/pip labextension builds work from a clean checkout without running\nTailwind.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(jupyterlab): sidebar outputs surface and data-file uploads\n\nCapture each node''s nbformat outputs from the shared EngineEvent stream\n(kernel and engine paths alike) into per-node state and render the shared\nCellOutputs component (incl. image/png figures) in the Selected sidebar\nsection. Add a Data sidebar section listing/uploading/deleting data files:\nwhen a kernel is attached, files go to the notebook''s directory via the\nJupyter Contents API (the kernel''s cwd — engine /files uploads are invisible\nto kernel runs); otherwise the engine''s /files REST surface is used.\nLocalized EN+DE; degrades to a muted note when neither target is reachable.\n\nThe kernel-preferred onRun execution path is unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXJ3MCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVksQABZSdDIX6wM6nIDpz0SA+ATr\nZQ589+BWVc/oJyFnUWhFJ1wPgAMFvk3EN7ocPaBn7L2jspvYupKjd02nM08WctIy\nL+B3/Cy+Un23yF9SZZHmKwkNd6WYorQ8Je8lBEKKJMJmOKqrMq206GxaaXi37kD4\nU9u0zV7kRNQFwxKrqWnAFNG6TRo7yw4OkXNtpSbVmUvoFmtA4IadRG1D4ecYA9cb\n/P8Uc+9QqAAR3XOwOBRi8mWt2vGUUsa1rMa3ulS9yJCb5r1SYyQ5GFI9/zwagKbx\nMNGZeUlhnEecIWmyysnc3+pXesaVSy4KdlOISz9qZA4UQPDHjMBm3eGqM/HhiSdy\nP2mRfFiN20QnHsGfpwVCKt2Ti9G4mDmU9jzaEI+15DwSRaTBsxPAsj+qchOUdKGV\nSr14Ir2qWeFhsdrXloeAtNuoX1PUCJjcbm7HV8V9ELXfCkAu6N2KI8NJZvZK58I7\nYcOuljbI13EtLkamdaMQ/6+lR6ezKy9mW5YxDy/F8hk/1yLc9/4cMB+6vkQhVYRe\n9sl4A317XBgWb/7fJnKbWyHhegMp8icfsvt0zRi6RBYIKrOhAaXUVrgfcCSsXTT0\nGDddhXMB4rSKpB9AiiNUIETHNwYEBl564zNWG+T+Nduflg4KR4cMslXdc8yq5aGz\nkOhXu+DQ3SLpcizDlj7l\n=LmzZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-19T09:50:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/7f085134672b9b0497483419ce5a28434c8e6389","node_id":"C_kwDOSWT-J9oAKDdmMDg1MTM0NjcyYjliMDQ5NzQ4MzQxOWNlNWEyODQzNGM4ZTYzODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/a6cd40da534b7acaaafcf8fa5e06acc01e93ffdb","sha":"a6cd40da534b7acaaafcf8fa5e06acc01e93ffdb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/a6cd40da534b7acaaafcf8fa5e06acc01e93ffdb"}],"sha":"7f085134672b9b0497483419ce5a28434c8e6389","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/7f085134672b9b0497483419ce5a28434c8e6389"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44301196?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers","id":44301196,"login":"NoelHuibers","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzAxMTk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/a6cd40da534b7acaaafcf8fa5e06acc01e93ffdb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-19T09:29:41Z","email":"noel@huibers.io","name":"Noel Huibers"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-19T09:29:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"VS Code: BYOK settings, AI surfaces, and data-file upload via app-core (#86) (#131)\n\n* feat(vscode): add BYOK LLM settings, secret-stored API key, credentials push\n\n- contributes.configuration gains notebookflow.llm.provider (enum mirroring\n  the web-app provider list) and notebookflow.llm.model\n- new commands notebookflow.setLlmApiKey (password input box ->\n  SecretStorage) and notebookflow.clearLlmApiKey\n- CanvasWebviewPanel pushes a {type:\"credentials\"} message on webviewReady,\n  on notebookflow.llm config changes, and on secret changes; the key goes\n  over postMessage only, never into the rendered HTML\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vscode): wire Ask / Compose / Explain AI surfaces into the webview\n\n- webview consumes @notebookflow/app-core (vite source alias + tsconfig\n  reference + tailwind @source) with the missing shadcn token slots mapped\n  to --vscode-* theme variables\n- EngineClient constructed on engineUrl arrival; BYOK credentials message\n  applied via setCredentials (empty key clears); node synthesis and the\n  palette registry fetch now go through the client so credentials attach\n- Ask (Ctrl/Cmd+K) / Compose / Explain header buttons, app-core AskPalette /\n  ComposeDialog / ExplanationPanel with DE label tables in strings.ts\n- Compose apply replaces the notebook through the existing patch protocol\n  (delete all cells, insert drafted cells)\n- local pipeline/event helpers and wire-type duplicates replaced by\n  app-core buildPipelineDef / stripMarkerLine / renderEvent / types\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vscode): add data-file upload rail and rebuild webview bundle\n\n- Data section in the canvas sidebar below the palette: lists engine\n  /files via EngineClient.listDataFiles, hidden-input upload\n  (.csv/.tsv/.json/.parquet/.txt/.xlsx) through uploadDataFile, per-file\n  delete; refreshes on engineUrl arrival and after upload/delete\n- engine-down shows a localized hint instead of the list; failures land\n  in the execution-events log (EN+DE strings)\n- dist-webview rebuilt and staged (bundle is read at runtime)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ff7fc70dae4c1de6bdc539c5308ee3990b9238bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/trees/ff7fc70dae4c1de6bdc539c5308ee3990b9238bc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/commits/a6cd40da534b7acaaafcf8fa5e06acc01e93ffdb","verification":{"payload":"tree ff7fc70dae4c1de6bdc539c5308ee3990b9238bc\nparent c055cdb1d7ecfef6a63429d2c9f4f744feb13980\nauthor Noel Huibers <noel@huibers.io> 1784453381 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784453381 +0200\n\nVS Code: BYOK settings, AI surfaces, and data-file upload via app-core (#86) (#131)\n\n* feat(vscode): add BYOK LLM settings, secret-stored API key, credentials push\n\n- contributes.configuration gains notebookflow.llm.provider (enum mirroring\n  the web-app provider list) and notebookflow.llm.model\n- new commands notebookflow.setLlmApiKey (password input box ->\n  SecretStorage) and notebookflow.clearLlmApiKey\n- CanvasWebviewPanel pushes a {type:\"credentials\"} message on webviewReady,\n  on notebookflow.llm config changes, and on secret changes; the key goes\n  over postMessage only, never into the rendered HTML\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vscode): wire Ask / Compose / Explain AI surfaces into the webview\n\n- webview consumes @notebookflow/app-core (vite source alias + tsconfig\n  reference + tailwind @source) with the missing shadcn token slots mapped\n  to --vscode-* theme variables\n- EngineClient constructed on engineUrl arrival; BYOK credentials message\n  applied via setCredentials (empty key clears); node synthesis and the\n  palette registry fetch now go through the client so credentials attach\n- Ask (Ctrl/Cmd+K) / Compose / Explain header buttons, app-core AskPalette /\n  ComposeDialog / ExplanationPanel with DE label tables in strings.ts\n- Compose apply replaces the notebook through the existing patch protocol\n  (delete all cells, insert drafted cells)\n- local pipeline/event helpers and wire-type duplicates replaced by\n  app-core buildPipelineDef / stripMarkerLine / renderEvent / types\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vscode): add data-file upload rail and rebuild webview bundle\n\n- Data section in the canvas sidebar below the palette: lists engine\n  /files via EngineClient.listDataFiles, hidden-input upload\n  (.csv/.tsv/.json/.parquet/.txt/.xlsx) through uploadDataFile, per-file\n  delete; refreshes on engineUrl arrival and after upload/delete\n- engine-down shows a localized hint instead of the list; failures land\n  in the execution-events log (EN+DE strings)\n- dist-webview rebuilt and staged (bundle is read at runtime)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXJkFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuNoQADa1dp4i+kSD2sJEXA8eqQde\n290qSsknmGJm4xlnpO4Y01GRHPttWLmga5YzliQaAzBZKqzf/FzGuP+unOzTMQSP\ngKVqvVIBZUiXuHjxpM/iRzsch8rebPotqmGsjErk2WPA6fr7Hn/lqVcezyE/yDJv\ni1u7M/q7UMkjFjqblZnFQgULBJqEoXHYEGoIBITi6gnAqKV52kv04IWLT/Cj/kNH\nU8PgqG2hFR3eh0n7guRhoWGFuVl5CrHivob3+IvBquSvnet2CKcrSAg3m8ZfqALv\ngn57CdPplLdsMaHldkpP8HnfwfS3eCqWFq7bspVkZ4I1J/1uJNFsN7+BaQ0Mi+cS\nBtNBPN4Mzgcc3h5sAHCQSZBrhVDSpWHoBub0HC0JMTX4EzgEzh20zsj/yXzsAyT0\nD1Nllzo4mLZJgDfhobPivzGQl8OnLvenhiQFw761Vr2DclE1KmKSl6IAq0dApIV2\nut7BwEjkX1BACkV6WBAwwlatbrfihX0dqgpe4ljuLPJ++8Bg7EwBztDTsp5NuUgx\n4HAC549HVdy3IgG22SrbWPnWc5MFPbg7xLgBlRa5S+kjpbQ/Y1l7UgkzIXY520/U\n0ramvaP