5MTE1NDhjMmMwZmFiODc1NThhNGE2MDlhMWJkNzY3NDhjZGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/6bd6a2cfe3ab64f660d4df8f16b364ae6d4dcb95","sha":"6bd6a2cfe3ab64f660d4df8f16b364ae6d4dcb95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/6bd6a2cfe3ab64f660d4df8f16b364ae6d4dcb95"}],"sha":"e3c0911548c2c0fab87558a4a609a1bd76748cda","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/e3c0911548c2c0fab87558a4a609a1bd76748cda"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44301196?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers","id":44301196,"login":"NoelHuibers","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzAxMTk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/6bd6a2cfe3ab64f660d4df8f16b364ae6d4dcb95/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-18T23:34:10Z","email":"noel@huibers.io","name":"Noel Huibers"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-18T23:34:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Shared host-core package: extract EngineClient, output rendering, AI dialogs into @notebookflow/app-core (#84) (#130)\n\n* feat(app-core): add host-agnostic workspace core package\n\nNew @notebookflow/app-core package holding the engine client, the engine\nwire types, and the pure pipeline/event helpers, mirroring graph-canvas\nconventions (tsc -b composite build, isolatedDeclarations, vitest).\n\n- src/types.ts: all engine wire/data types moved out of the web-app\n  EngineClient module (NbOutput, EngineEvent, PipelineDef, triggers, ...)\n- src/EngineClient.ts: the client class with the URL/token injected by\n  the host; the import.meta.env defaults intentionally did NOT move\n- src/pipeline.ts: buildPipelineDef/stripMarkerLine verbatim\n- src/events.ts: renderEvent/buildGenerationStatus/statusGlyph with an\n  EventLabels seam (graph-canvas labels pattern); no-arg calls produce\n  the exact previous English strings\n- node-env vitest coverage for URL/auth-token/credentials handling,\n  event formatting defaults + overrides, and pipeline assembly\n- CI: run app-core vitest alongside graph-canvas\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(web-app): consume the engine core from @notebookflow/app-core\n\nZero behavior change: the web app now sources the engine client, wire\ntypes, and pipeline/event helpers from the new app-core package.\n\n- src/lib/EngineClient.ts becomes a thin shim: re-exports everything\n  from app-core and keeps the web-app-only Vite env defaults\n  (DEFAULT_ENGINE_URL/DEFAULT_ENGINE_TOKEN) plus an EngineClient\n  subclass applying them, so all existing importers stay unchanged\n- src/lib/pipeline.ts and src/lib/events.ts deleted; App.tsx imports\n  buildPipelineDef/stripMarkerLine/renderEvent/buildGenerationStatus\n  from @notebookflow/app-core directly\n- Vite resolve.alias points @notebookflow/app-core at its source (same\n  dual-consumption wiring as graph-canvas) + tsconfig project reference\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(app-core): move CellOutputs into the shared core with a labels seam\n\nExtract the cell-output renderer from the web-app into\n@notebookflow/app-core so every surface can render nbformat outputs:\n\n- components/CellOutputs.tsx with the CellOutputsLabels interface +\n  defaultCellOutputsLabels English defaults, following the\n  EventLabels/defaultEventLabels injection pattern; hosts override via\n  the optional labels prop.\n- The DOMPurify sanitization moves to a pure sanitizeOutputHtml helper\n  (outputHtml.ts) so the tag/attr allowlist is independently testable;\n  its vitest opts into jsdom via a per-file pragma while the package\n  default stays node.\n- dompurify and react (deps + peer, mirroring graph-canvas) move to\n  app-core; dompurify leaves the web-app (sole consumer moved).\n- web-app: CellEditor consumes the shared component and passes labels\n  built from the cells i18n namespace; index.css gains an @source\n  directive for app-core so Tailwind v4 keeps its classes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(app-core): move the AI dialogs into the shared core with labels seams\n\nMove AskPalette, ComposeDialog, and ExplanationPanel from the web-app\ninto @notebookflow/app-core so every surface can render the AI flows.\nAll three stay fully controlled — state lives in the host.\n\n- Each component gains a labels interface (AskPaletteLabels,\n  ComposeDialogLabels, ExplanationPanelLabels) with English defaults,\n  mirroring the CellOutputsLabels pattern; hosts override via the\n  optional labels prop. Types now import from ../types.\n- The badge/button/scroll-area shadcn primitives and the cn util are\n  copied into app-core (src/components/ui, src/lib/utils.ts) so the\n  package is self-contained; variant props become explicit unions to\n  satisfy isolatedDeclarations. The web-app keeps its own ui/* copies\n  for its remaining local consumers — consolidation deferred.\n- app-core gains the radix slot/scroll-area, cva, clsx, tailwind-merge,\n  and lucide-react deps.\n- web-app: App.tsx consumes the shared dialogs and builds their labels\n  from the ask/compose/explanation catalogs via the existing\n  canvasLabels iterate-the-defaults pattern (catalog keys match the\n  label keys 1:1); the DE/EN catalogs stay in the web-app as the\n  translation source.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bcdf0e31c2297ff58bb75c87a42ceb05995f643e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/trees/bcdf0e31c2297ff58bb75c87a42ceb05995f643e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/commits/6bd6a2cfe3ab64f660d4df8f16b364ae6d4dcb95","verification":{"payload":"tree bcdf0e31c2297ff58bb75c87a42ceb05995f643e\nparent 41bcd5ff8e4d71749d2fe6b50f7febd64f89a94c\nauthor Noel Huibers <noel@huibers.io> 1784417650 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784417650 +0200\n\nShared host-core package: extract EngineClient, output rendering, AI dialogs into @notebookflow/app-core (#84) (#130)\n\n* feat(app-core): add host-agnostic workspace core package\n\nNew @notebookflow/app-core package holding the engine client, the engine\nwire types, and the pure pipeline/event helpers, mirroring graph-canvas\nconventions (tsc -b composite build, isolatedDeclarations, vitest).\n\n- src/types.ts: all engine wire/data types moved out of the web-app\n  EngineClient module (NbOutput, EngineEvent, PipelineDef, triggers, ...)\n- src/EngineClient.ts: the client class with the URL/token injected by\n  the host; the import.meta.env defaults intentionally did NOT move\n- src/pipeline.ts: buildPipelineDef/stripMarkerLine verbatim\n- src/events.ts: renderEvent/buildGenerationStatus/statusGlyph with an\n  EventLabels seam (graph-canvas labels pattern); no-arg calls produce\n  the exact previous English strings\n- node-env vitest coverage for URL/auth-token/credentials handling,\n  event formatting defaults + overrides, and pipeline assembly\n- CI: run app-core vitest alongside graph-canvas\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(web-app): consume the engine core from @notebookflow/app-core\n\nZero behavior change: the web app now sources the engine client, wire\ntypes, and pipeline/event helpers from the new app-core package.\n\n- src/lib/EngineClient.ts becomes a thin shim: re-exports everything\n  from app-core and keeps the web-app-only Vite env defaults\n  (DEFAULT_ENGINE_URL/DEFAULT_ENGINE_TOKEN) plus an EngineClient\n  subclass applying them, so all existing importers stay unchanged\n- src/lib/pipeline.ts and src/lib/events.ts deleted; App.tsx imports\n  buildPipelineDef/stripMarkerLine/renderEvent/buildGenerationStatus\n  from @notebookflow/app-core directly\n- Vite resolve.alias points @notebookflow/app-core at its source (same\n  dual-consumption wiring as graph-canvas) + tsconfig project reference\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(app-core): move CellOutputs into the shared core with a labels seam\n\nExtract the cell-output renderer from the web-app into\n@notebookflow/app-core so every surface can render nbformat outputs:\n\n- components/CellOutputs.tsx with the CellOutputsLabels interface +\n  defaultCellOutputsLabels English defaults, following the\n  EventLabels/defaultEventLabels injection pattern; hosts override via\n  the optional labels prop.\n- The DOMPurify sanitization moves to a pure sanitizeOutputHtml helper\n  (outputHtml.ts) so the tag/attr allowlist is independently testable;\n  its vitest opts into jsdom via a per-file pragma while the package\n  default stays node.\n- dompurify and react (deps + peer, mirroring graph-canvas) move to\n  app-core; dompurify leaves the web-app (sole consumer moved).\n- web-app: CellEditor consumes the shared component and passes labels\n  built from the cells i18n namespace; index.css gains an @source\n  directive for app-core so Tailwind v4 keeps its classes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(app-core): move the AI dialogs into the shared core with labels seams\n\nMove AskPalette, ComposeDialog, and ExplanationPanel from the web-app\ninto @notebookflow/app-core so every surface can render the AI flows.\nAll three stay fully controlled — state lives in the host.\n\n- Each component gains a labels interface (AskPaletteLabels,\n  ComposeDialogLabels, ExplanationPanelLabels) with English defaults,\n  mirroring the CellOutputsLabels pattern; hosts override via the\n  optional labels prop. Types now import from ../types.\n- The badge/button/scroll-area shadcn primitives and the cn util are\n  copied into app-core (src/components/ui, src/lib/utils.ts) so the\n  package is self-contained; variant props become explicit unions to\n  satisfy isolatedDeclarations. The web-app keeps its own ui/* copies\n  for its remaining local consumers — consolidation deferred.\n- app-core gains the radix slot/scroll-area, cva, clsx, tailwind-merge,\n  and lucide-react deps.\n- web-app: App.tsx consumes the shared dialogs and builds their labels\n  from the ask/compose/explanation catalogs via the existing\n  canvasLabels iterate-the-defaults pattern (catalog keys match the\n  label keys 1:1); the DE/EN catalogs stay in the web-app as the\n  translation source.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXA1zCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIXsQAH9Gxdukn3g4GeyJCcnqU8tC\n/qn9sWdoMkddMhKekJHzhOl+O9P19glcwlnGXfLh7hHE5Shb9ltSzhX71nPFF2JI\nMLqskGO6oacOuRj2Ox4rnzR8qQexsBco6J/582mQ5wQZaUETNBqEt4sWFbwS6735\nitAdadUTKvqrEJKjXCFWBZvDnuIcd65x1+mWj8MEZVU0Mk+rNot4NkSq5xZYjQOV\nAXv+bzmJM76E13ODASvIc6IO/Xxd/4h3zgDuWon3XwiMszSq1D1apmYKMlDv5Jj1\njn4kbnnTyLPggPnwhrV2Ee2kcKG/TIec5GG/58wpUoxs5Ahl79Z4EsU6nvdC2NrY\n4S9v5eD4Yp8wkiLhx5etTkBcZRURMae9+O80whqedLd7qjdibDmlG5NW5fETwVCN\nn+kvGgiQp5heeGK9S3ARk+lJKFNmCd3xGmDKLZVfCqsnqL1uOpkvpUh0zwiRX1Dn\nskntKRwnZacKh+aHC9wCK0C9HKr+QOCLmiW8NQEWaEA9aAkyKXdqol