okflow/commit/0d3def4579340428d79f4ae4726a646c0b22e613","node_id":"C_kwDOSWT-J9oAKDBkM2RlZjQ1NzkzNDA0MjhkNzlmNGFlNDcyNmE2NDZjMGIyMmU2MTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/549505b6e8c86631046f070ca3c31b60ba6573a4","sha":"549505b6e8c86631046f070ca3c31b60ba6573a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/549505b6e8c86631046f070ca3c31b60ba6573a4"}],"sha":"0d3def4579340428d79f4ae4726a646c0b22e613","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/0d3def4579340428d79f4ae4726a646c0b22e613"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44301196?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers","id":44301196,"login":"NoelHuibers","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzAxMTk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/549505b6e8c86631046f070ca3c31b60ba6573a4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-18T20:34:20Z","email":"noel@huibers.io","name":"Noel Huibers"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-18T20:34:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Security hardening: headers/CSP, engine CORS + rate limits, auth rate limits, CI scanning (#82) (#104)\n\n* feat(web-app): add security headers and CSP to all responses\n\nvercel.json gains a headers block (HSTS, nosniff, X-Frame-Options DENY,\nReferrer-Policy, Permissions-Policy, CSP) applied to every response of the\nsingle Vercel function. script-src keeps ''unsafe-inline'' because TanStack\nStart injects an inline hydration script (nonce plumbing is a follow-up);\nconnect-src stays broad (https:/wss: + localhost) because the engine URL is\nuser-configurable (BYO-engine). Vite dev mirrors the same headers by reading\nvercel.json, so dev and prod cannot drift.\n\nPart of #82.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(web-app): harden BetterAuth with trusted origins, cookie pinning, rate limits\n\n- trustedOrigins from BETTER_AUTH_URL origin plus comma-separated\n  NOTEBOOKFLOW_TRUSTED_ORIGINS override (e.g. preview deploys).\n- Explicit cookie posture: useSecureCookies in production.\n- Rate limiting enabled in all environments (30 req/60s default,\n  /sign-in/* 10/60s, /token 30/60s) with database-backed counters —\n  the default in-memory store resets on every Vercel cold start.\n- New rate_limit table in the drizzle schema plus the initial generated\n  migration (drizzle/ did not exist before; the repo used db:push only).\n\nPart of #82.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(engine): CORS origin lock, per-identity rate limits, upload size pre-check\n\n- NOTEBOOKFLOW_ALLOWED_ORIGINS (comma-separated) restricts CORS when set;\n  unset keeps the open self-host default. fly.toml pins the hosted engine\n  to the web-app origin.\n- New notebookflow/ratelimit.py: dependency-free sliding-window limiter\n  keyed by (auth subject or client IP honoring Fly-Client-IP, bucket) with\n  an injectable clock; 429 + Retry-After on limit. Applied to the LLM\n  endpoints (/llm/ask, /pipelines/propose, /pipelines/explain,\n  /nodes/synthesize) at 10/min, POST /files at 20/min and\n  POST /pipelines/{id}/run at 30/min.\n- POST /files rejects with 413 from the request Content-Length before\n  buffering the body; the exact post-read quota check stays authoritative.\n- Tests: limiter window/identity/bucket semantics, 429 + Retry-After via\n  TestClient, and the Content-Length 413 path (proven to fire pre-read).\n\nPart of #82.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: add dependabot plus dependency-audit and secret-scanning jobs\n\n- .github/dependabot.yml: weekly npm (workspace root), pip (engine/) and\n  github-actions update PRs.\n- New `security` CI job: pnpm audit (high+) and pip-audit over the engine''s\n  exported uv lockfile — both non-blocking for now because known transitive\n  advisories exist (npm: shell-quote critical via concurrently, vite/ws/\n  form-data highs via vitest and the vscode-extension build; pip: idna,\n  pillow, starlette) that aren''t fixable from our own manifests — plus a\n  gitleaks full-history secret scan (blocking).\n\nPart of #82.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b2f6fd3c7602de9f9028e31efee5821fc3a02dbf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/trees/b2f6fd3c7602de9f9028e31efee5821fc3a02dbf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/commits/549505b6e8c86631046f070ca3c31b60ba6573a4","verification":{"payload":"tree b2f6fd3c7602de9f9028e31efee5821fc3a02dbf\nparent 5af01bdfc6c48ab73de73236dc9336ad3b57b119\nauthor Noel Huibers <noel@huibers.io> 1784406860 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784406860 +0200\n\nSecurity hardening: headers/CSP, engine CORS + rate limits, auth rate limits, CI scanning (#82) (#104)\n\n* feat(web-app): add security headers and CSP to all responses\n\nvercel.json gains a headers block (HSTS, nosniff, X-Frame-Options DENY,\nReferrer-Policy, Permissions-Policy, CSP) applied to every response of the\nsingle Vercel function. script-src keeps ''unsafe-inline'' because TanStack\nStart injects an inline hydration script (nonce plumbing is a follow-up);\nconnect-src stays broad (https:/wss: + localhost) because the engine URL is\nuser-configurable (BYO-engine). Vite dev mirrors the same headers by reading\nvercel.json, so dev and prod cannot drift.\n\nPart of #82.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(web-app): harden BetterAuth with trusted origins, cookie pinning, rate limits\n\n- trustedOrigins from BETTER_AUTH_URL origin plus comma-separated\n  NOTEBOOKFLOW_TRUSTED_ORIGINS override (e.g. preview deploys).\n- Explicit cookie posture: useSecureCookies in production.\n- Rate limiting enabled in all environments (30 req/60s default,\n  /sign-in/* 10/60s, /token 30/60s) with database-backed counters —\n  the default in-memory store resets on every Vercel cold start.\n- New rate_limit table in the drizzle schema plus the initial generated\n  migration (drizzle/ did not exist before; the repo used db:push only).\n\nPart of #82.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(engine): CORS origin lock, per-identity rate limits, upload size pre-check\n\n- NOTEBOOKFLOW_ALLOWED_ORIGINS (comma-separated) restricts CORS when set;\n  unset keeps the open self-host default. fly.toml pins the hosted engine\n  to the web-app origin.\n- New notebookflow/ratelimit.py: dependency-free sliding-window limiter\n  keyed by (auth subject or client IP honoring Fly-Client-IP, bucket) with\n  an injectable clock; 429 + Retry-After on limit. Applied to the LLM\n  endpoints (/llm/ask, /pipelines/propose, /pipelines/explain,\n  /nodes/synthesize) at 10/min, POST /files at 20/min and\n  POST /pipelines/{id}/run at 30/min.\n- POST /files rejects with 413 from the request Content-Length before\n  buffering the body; the exact post-read quota check stays authoritative.\n- Tests: limiter window/identity/bucket semantics, 429 + Retry-After via\n  TestClient, and the Content-Length 413 path (proven to fire pre-read).\n\nPart of #82.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: add dependabot plus dependency-audit and secret-scanning jobs\n\n- .github/dependabot.yml: weekly npm (workspace root), pip (engine/) and\n  github-actions update PRs.\n- New `security` CI job: pnpm audit (high+) and pip-audit over the engine''s\n  exported uv lockfile — both non-blocking for now because known transitive\n  advisories exist (npm: shell-quote critical via concurrently, vite/ws/\n  form-data highs via vitest and the vscode-extension build; pip: idna,\n  pillow, starlette) that aren''t fixable from our own manifests — plus a\n  gitleaks full-history secret scan (blocking).\n\nPart of #82.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqW+NMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8AcQAF8hLzvWfd7I3tkkkPR3hU0M\nZdkoRd1FX1uZwT/3mSUcw6joZgtWUNzu/IFiCJ5mr4Hp5wgTh2sqeLzheqkUPYbK\ngkQrC9tBsUA+Gs9jxDRir/iHVD0ck3LuPE792r/q476R9VRUOYdTaaP8QtANMK0e\n+Vd4yXlS7KEhcNZP7LDwo10MeChTWz7HuNSOm5cwPmi9sulbF+KKTu9Mei8KQKBH\n0wHB4EBrQtJqvTtLeYUmEqk5tEwgzlRGoJrQ/EcKVikWu8zJo862MPabl297agys\nF/RIDaKs3YmGh5K0iZPTtE/QRQlQtWXknbrLhD9UgI9SmAI6sWElNVTYmtcnUkmD\n79POWWDbmifDB1HoeTBYMYV7f2b1n4ddBFVCgJ2HBWxRXZEdLez1xTlcbkyXSIjt\nDIUJcqHhvl4EcEG23H76f+TrCbcwoferEsOaXGcWuDdUfwpWzzVrWHiDDzveyTNh\nNVa/OjOVzPf9bK3fuaoM/Uf49J9QgqKfxh3bC+3xF6MMCZwXWQGKVkjilPNZgVUF\n3/Iejj/95ZI0p8Q0Yt7VMhtRVMPFuy/u4YzVXUWQPX7AsCYRLxgD+cJrj3XfPZ65\nVbR58trCM8ER6koTaDOS2dGzC4jZ0ypjYYZvY1mnQ2V5FKaLjNSZnr6OBtM+WVXE\n9Zt2lO2ZpEtyrFKMbuu1\n=8VNB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-18T20:34:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api