//api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/5af01bdfc6c48ab73de73236dc9336ad3b57b119/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-18T20:01:37Z","email":"noel@huibers.io","name":"Noel Huibers"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-18T20:01:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Extension canvas i18n (DE+EN): wire the labels API into VS Code + JupyterLab (#103)\n\n* feat(graph-canvas): ship German canvas labels and canvasLocale helper\n\ngraph-canvas now exports deCanvasLabels/deNodeConfigLabels (verbatim from\nthe web app''s canvas namespace) plus canvasLocale() for mapping BCP-47\ntags to the shipped locales. The web app''s canvas message module derives\nits en/de catalogs from graph-canvas instead of duplicating the strings.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vscode-extension): localize the canvas webview (DE+EN)\n\nThe extension host injects vscode.env.language into the webview HTML as\nwindow.__NBF_LOCALE__ (nonce''d script, CSP-compatible). The webview\nresolves it through graph-canvas''s canvasLocale, swaps its UI strings via\na new webview/strings.ts table, and passes the German label sets to\n<Canvas> and <NodeConfigEditor> when the display language is German.\nIncludes the rebuilt dist-webview bundle.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(jupyterlab-extension): localize the canvas surface (DE+EN)\n\nResolves the UI locale from <html lang> (JupyterLab language packs) with\na navigator.language fallback via graph-canvas''s canvasLocale, swaps the\nApp strings through a new src/strings.ts table, and passes the German\nlabel sets to <Canvas> and <NodeConfigEditor> when the locale is German.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"13e99b90eeb5f00299463d1e1f19257e20956bd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/trees/13e99b90eeb5f00299463d1e1f19257e20956bd6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/commits/5af01bdfc6c48ab73de73236dc9336ad3b57b119","verification":{"payload":"tree 13e99b90eeb5f00299463d1e1f19257e20956bd6\nparent fdcddb873894020ccb5603d77a0f4fb00b12e93b\nauthor Noel Huibers <noel@huibers.io> 1784404897 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784404897 +0200\n\nExtension canvas i18n (DE+EN): wire the labels API into VS Code + JupyterLab (#103)\n\n* feat(graph-canvas): ship German canvas labels and canvasLocale helper\n\ngraph-canvas now exports deCanvasLabels/deNodeConfigLabels (verbatim from\nthe web app''s canvas namespace) plus canvasLocale() for mapping BCP-47\ntags to the shipped locales. The web app''s canvas message module derives\nits en/de catalogs from graph-canvas instead of duplicating the strings.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(vscode-extension): localize the canvas webview (DE+EN)\n\nThe extension host injects vscode.env.language into the webview HTML as\nwindow.__NBF_LOCALE__ (nonce''d script, CSP-compatible). The webview\nresolves it through graph-canvas''s canvasLocale, swaps its UI strings via\na new webview/strings.ts table, and passes the German label sets to\n<Canvas> and <NodeConfigEditor> when the display language is German.\nIncludes the rebuilt dist-webview bundle.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(jupyterlab-extension): localize the canvas surface (DE+EN)\n\nResolves the UI locale from <html lang> (JupyterLab language packs) with\na navigator.language fallback via graph-canvas''s canvasLocale, swaps the\nApp strings through a new src/strings.ts table, and passes the German\nlabel sets to <Canvas> and <NodeConfigEditor> when the locale is German.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqW9uhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAozwQAKGAFlfw1wTizEGxSp7a3gMF\nvfBVQwrMUEDmnlHZceKTDQewaEa3I1BYdBlTOHKEAzavYHKJ4KHxfTKpxJC60uQB\nBzrd2e/PecNb6McF8P0qZTrAlUZaIGPN5bVjL10o04WuVBKEWfzsalknaNS9zkKE\nTN8h6NwT4v1KsrEbo8TDtgQ6fROxD970x/02KPUdVY3Zf3sIkaIaRseH/+Oi6nTM\n9W6HthM3Mwm1q+gWpqFu4tsjBErufgR09Wywvzdl24LbJGVTXpbIHBWebxGKA7bS\nEoso7vTjKK4HHpQWFW5wn2pcquIU41Dlq4hecNckOEIJs/daFdl2QC8SgQDNEjZ8\naKkQp7X/LdvprOcOcYbbxsLDsx0HRLwxjqcBxtTKWJFLx9Xv5kAShu0azmqz7RyK\nKvCNvzRo20xfcurjbAsQFpY61lbyVWbEKoCqWRAkyXcJ/KbhPMesnPsXdzzjeqHb\ny4X4+hjRNWMpe4uprR0JB6IPDyiNrLl6fI99qpEs3SPtFU/laRQwkXng93A5ssFP\nNFj2IgvmDMAShdkpoihQeXOm/aTqNbPISivIrrigIsY3pNGGQZyUB041KEguH3Kg\nr4FzGcoR7GTXIF7h+Wac2k4IITuklP0qRfUSMedtWltqFnn/eZLQc9AMaGPoquWm\nA64le0nMuyf5XoBAhcFl\n=UMB+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-18T20:01:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/5af01bdfc6c48ab73de73236dc9336ad3b57b119","node_id":"C_kwDOSWT-J9oAKDVhZjAxYmRmYzZjNDhhYjczZGU3MzIzNmRjOTMzNmFkM2I1N2IxMTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/fdcddb873894020ccb5603d77a0f4fb00b12e93b","sha":"fdcddb873894020ccb5603d77a0f4fb00b12e93b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/fdcddb873894020ccb5603d77a0f4fb00b12e93b"}],"sha":"5af01bdfc6c48ab73de73236dc9336ad3b57b119","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/5af01bdfc6c48ab73de73236dc9336ad3b57b119"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44301196?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers","id":44301196,"login":"NoelHuibers","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzAxMTk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/fdcddb873894020ccb5603d77a0f4fb00b12e93b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-18T19:59:36Z","email":"noel@huibers.io","name":"Noel Huibers"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-18T19:59:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Workspace smoothness: fix rough edges, decompose App.tsx, finish canvas i18n (#101)\n\n* refactor(web-app): dedupe blob downloads into a shared triggerDownload helper\n\nThree near-identical anchor-click download snippets (downloadNotebook,\ndownloadWorkspaceZip, downloadWorkspaceDocument) collapse into one\nlib/download.ts helper; zip entry naming becomes a pure, tested function.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(web-app): localize lib error messages via LocalizableError\n\nParse/API errors from lib/notebook.ts and lib/notebooksApi.ts were\nhardcoded English and leaked into translated toasts (mixed-language\nerrors for DE users). Libs now throw LocalizableError(key, params) and\nthe UI resolves it with formatError(t, err, fallbackKey), which also\nreplaces the dozen hand-rolled ''err instanceof Error ?'' snippets.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(web-app): surface zip-export failures and detach cloudId on new notebook\n\n- handleDownloadAll swallowed JSZip failures as an unhandled rejection\n  and cleared the dirty flag even when nothing was exported; the reset\n  now happens only after a successful export, and failures show a\n  translated error.\n- Creating a notebook now resets cloudId so the next ''Save to cloud''\n  creates a new record instead of silently overwriting (and renaming)\n  the previously opened one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(web-app): extract AppHeader and ToolbarOverflowMenu from App\n\nMove the toolbar <header> JSX out of App.tsx into a presentational\nAppHeader component (state stays in App, flows in as props) and give the\n\"...\" overflow menu its own component that owns the open/close state and\nthe JUPYTER_URL env resolution. Zero behavior change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(web-app): extract usePanelLayout hook and pure panel clamps\n\nMove the pane split ratios, collapse flags, sidebar width, divider\ndrag/keyboard handlers, grid style memos, and the layout persistence\neffect from App.tsx into hooks/usePanelLayout. The pure clamp helpers\nand layout constants move to lib/panels (with vitest coverage), and the\nhook exposes applyWorkspaceUi/collectUiState as the workspace\nimport/export seams. Zero behavior change: same initial values,\npersistence key/shape, and clamping.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(web-app): extract useWorkspaceFiles hook and pure workspace-file helpers\n\nZero-behavior-change extraction of the multi-file workspace core out of\nApp.tsx (~2365 -> ~1939 lines):\n\n- src/lib/workspaceFiles.ts: pure helpers (makeFileId,\n  uniqueUntitledNotebookName, createBlankNotebook,\n  createInitialWorkspaceFiles, firstInitialWorkspaceFile,\n  shiftOutputsAfterDelete/Insert, isLikelyWorkspaceFilename) with a\n  pure-node vitest suite. App keeps importing the shiftOutputsAfter*\n  index math for its cell operations.\n- src/hooks/useWorkspaceFiles.ts: workspace state (notebook, openFiles,\n  activeFileId, workspaceRevision, baselineSources, snapshots,\n  fileHandle, outputsByCell, canvas group positions, patch-lookup ref),\n  outputs helpers, cellsByPath/openFilesKey memos, rename-sync effect,\n  isDirty, and the open/create/switch/close file operations.\n  Cross-cutting App writes flow in as callbacks (onDocumentChange,\n  onNotebookCreated, applyUi, onError, onWorkspaceReplaced, t).\n- SyncEngine construction/ingest effects, resetTransient, cell ops, and\n  the run pipeline stay in App, reaching the workspace through the\n  hook''s returned setters and refs. Dep arrays gained hook-returned\n  stable identities to satisfy useExhaustiveDependencies (runtime\n  no-ops).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(web-app): extract workspace export into useWorkspaceExport hook\n\nMove collectWorkspaceFiles into a pure lib function (with tests) and the\nworkspace-document collector + download handlers into a thin hook. No\nbehavior change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(web-app): extract cloud notebooks into useCloudNotebooks hook\n\nMove the cloud dialog state and save/open/delete handlers verbatim into a\nhook; App bridges the onWorkspaceReplaced -> detach cycle with a stable\nref. No behavior change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(web-app): extract canvas selection sync into useCanvasSelectionSync\n\nMove selected/focusedCellIndex/cellNavigationTarget state, the graph\nreconcile and focus-follow effects, and the focus/select handlers into a\nhook; findNodeForCellIndex becomes a pure lib function with tests. App\nreaches the hook''s reset/setters via a stable ref for pre-hook callbacks.\nNo behavior change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(graph-canvas): translate the canvas strings missed by #100\n\nStatus/Last-run tooltips, the unresolved-refs warning, port-remove\naria-labels, and the port combobox aria-labels move into the labels\nAPI with DE catalog entries; drop the dead PortEditor component\n(nothing imported it — the live editor is InletOutletGrid''s own\ncreatePortEditorActions).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"371a0764407c729d5233ecb81d79d933e0e132a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/trees/371a0764407c729d5233ecb81d79d933e0e132a0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/commits/fdcddb873894020ccb5603d77a0f4fb00b12e93b","verification":{"payload":"tree 371a0764407c729d5233ecb81d79d933e0e132a0\nparent ec2fcb2aa05da57a6426111bd4d8cba52c9992c6\nauthor Noel Huibers <noel@huibers.io> 1784404776 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784404776 +0200\n\nWorkspace smoothness: fix rough edges, decompose App.tsx, finish canvas i18n (#101)\n\n* refactor(web-app): dedupe blob downloads into a shared triggerDownload helper\n\nThree near-identical anchor-click download snippets (downloadNotebook,\ndownloadWorkspaceZip, downloadWorkspaceDocument) collapse into one\nlib/download.ts helper; zip entry naming becomes a pure, tested function.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(web-app): localize lib error messages via LocalizableError\n\nParse/API errors from lib/notebook.ts and lib/notebooksApi.ts were\nhardcoded English and leaked into translated toasts (mixed-language\nerrors for DE users). Libs now throw LocalizableError(key, params) and\nthe UI resolves it with formatError(t, err, fallbackKey), which also\nreplaces the dozen hand-rolled ''err instanceof Error ?'' snippets.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(web-app): surface zip-export failures and detach cloudId on new notebook\n\n- handleDownloadAll swallowed JSZip failures as an unhandled rejection\n  and cleared the dirty flag even when nothing was exported; the reset\n  now happens only after a successful export, and failures show a\n  translated error.\n- Creating a notebook now resets cloudId so the next ''Save to cloud''\n  creates a new record instead of silently overwriting (and renaming)\n  the previously opened one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(web-app): extract AppHeader and ToolbarOverflowMenu from App\n\nMove the toolbar <header> JSX out of App.tsx into a presentational\nAppHeader component (state stays in App, flows in as props) and give the\n\"...\" overflow menu its own component that owns the open/close state and\nthe JUPYTER_URL env resolution. Zero behavior change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(web-app): extract usePanelLayout hook and pure panel clamps\n\nMove the pane split ratios, collapse flags, sidebar width, divider\ndrag/keyboard handlers, grid style memos, and the layout persistence\neffect from App.tsx into hooks/usePanelLayout. The pure clamp helpers\nand layout constants move to lib/panels (with vitest coverage), and the\nhook exposes applyWorkspaceUi/collectUiState as the workspace\nimport/export seams. Zero behavior change: same initial values,\npersistence key/shape, and clamping.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(web-app): extract useWorkspaceFiles hook and pure workspace-file helpers\n\nZero-behavior-change extraction of the multi-file workspace core out of\nApp.tsx (~2365 -> ~1939 lines):\n\n- src/lib/workspaceFiles.ts: pure helpers (makeFileId,\n  uniqueUntitledNotebookName, createBlankNotebook,\n  createInitialWorkspaceFiles, firstInitialWorkspaceFile,\n  shiftOutputsAfterDelete/Insert, isLikelyWorkspaceFilename) with a\n  pure-node vitest suite. App keeps importing the shiftOutputsAfter*\n  index math for its cell operations.\n- src/hooks/useWorkspaceFiles.ts: workspace state (notebook, openFiles,\n  activeFileId, workspaceRevision, baselineSources, snapshots,\n  fileHandle, outputsByCell, canvas group positions, patch-lookup ref),\n  outputs helpers, cellsByPath/openFilesKey memos, rename-sync effect,\n  isDirty, and the open/create/switch/close file operations.\n  Cross-cutting App writes flow in as callbacks (onDocumentChange,\n  onNotebookCreated, applyUi, onError, onWorkspaceReplaced, t).\n- SyncEngine construction/ingest effects, resetTransient, cell ops, and\n  the run pipeline stay in App, reaching the workspace through the\n  hook''s returned setters and refs. Dep arrays gained hook-returned\n  stable identities to satisfy useExhaustiveDependencies (runtime\n  no-ops).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(web-app): extract workspace export into useWorkspaceExport hook\n\nMove collectWorkspaceFiles into a pure lib function (with tests) and the\nworkspace-document collector + download handlers into a thin hook. No\nbehavior change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(web-app): extract cloud notebooks into useCloudNotebooks hook\n\nMove the cloud dialog state and save/open/delete handlers verbatim into a\nhook; App bridges the onWorkspaceReplaced -> detach cycle with a stable\nref. No behavior change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(web-app): extract canvas selection sync into useCanvasSelectionSync\n\nMove selected/focusedCellIndex/cellNavigationTarget state, the graph\nreconcile and focus-follow effects, and the focus/select handlers into a\nhook; findNodeForCellIndex becomes a pure lib function with tests. App\nreaches the hook''s reset/setters via a stable ref for pre-hook callbacks.\nNo behavior change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(graph-canvas): translate the canvas strings missed by #100\n\nStatus/Last-run tooltips, the unresolved-refs warning, port-remove\naria-labels, and the port combobox aria-labels move into the labels\nAPI with DE catalog entries; drop the dead PortEditor component\n(nothing imported it — the live editor is InletOutletGrid''s own\ncreatePortEditorActions).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqW9soCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdU8QAKG7UXrqalnDv2CkDlvkif6h\n/dXxXgSHwmt+s1JLmRAUqZuaqynB69Q8IJxnNPn5uXqR2LPMg3kLvvk4OjCDDOKn\no+iJk89kijcAd4wBRfic+vZSVIX+LmkRiSeAjbUX5bjAx0RVY1K0pTSWJbYyhshe\nRWFV7g4NtA0b7jRhb4Go/bo/GW68/srAkBQ0Ij1wuCk8c7xiXDtz5EvrZfQyHKRA\n/ZxIYi+q5JvoD0xZXTSFd1aX09PzgO9t4w+3Hv0De2F5yZl7M1X4Dz100b0eDzw8\ntMDjZNXFIvW47zfH4UCqaE1HsGdJ8JCMIC674XJeFlrvRwwRJZQVYFwB10lyR59p\ndlbceC0oZqisdlDY8WLudoT9gg00qzQfaq7M/eMEfDlWLQwmksNF3Z/ZZZTNykWO\n31X+jEX0ZK+rl4KzXFDWIlfy7hnUuDK2AHwbdhpzFGTXO0/vZKUNQDmcY3S4tpfA\n6URrPtGVAeeut18pMKFgAOw6mkq035kHRG065cuGx6D120fxTQjt8sf7/HCQtVXp\n