om/users/NoelHuibers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers","id":44301196,"login":"NoelHuibers","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzAxMTk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/34793a5c1454ad23483c6fa237640e15c5f6372a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-26T02:01:19Z","email":"noel@huibers.io","name":"Noel Huibers"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-26T02:01:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(web-app): translate the whole app to DE + EN (#99)\n\nCloses #75. Extends the i18n foundation (#73) across the entire app — landing,\neditor, and every dialog — not just the public chrome.\n\n- Bilingual landing (#75): hero (<Trans> for the accent word + inline code),\n  the three scroll captions, features, steps, CTA, nav, footer. The hero graph''s\n  node names stay English on purpose — they mirror the `# @node: Load Data`\n  markers in the illustrated .ipynb, so translating them would desync the diagram.\n- Editor fully internationalized: App.tsx top bar + toasts/errors, EngineStatus,\n  SettingsDialog, ShortcutsDialog, ComposeDialog, CloudNotebooksDialog, AskPalette,\n  PaletteDrawer, ExplanationPanel, TriggersDialog, and the cell/file panes.\n- Catalog split into per-namespace modules under lib/i18n/messages/ (common,\n  login, legal, notFound stay inline). Each module exports `en` + `de: typeof en`,\n  so the compiler enforces DE/EN key parity per namespace.\n- Pluralization via react-i18next _one/_other (cell count, events, firings);\n  interpolation via {name}/{message}.\n\n~250 strings across 12 namespaces. German is informal \"du\", glossary-consistent\n(Pipeline/Knoten/Zelle/Engine/Trigger); brand, code, and identifiers kept verbatim.\n\nVerified: typecheck (enforces DE/EN parity), biome, build all green; SSR renders\nboth locales with the correct <html lang>; every literal t()/Trans key resolves\nto the catalog (237/237).","tree":{"sha":"252d0891337877cdd85a7cca8c447c18a0fdbd76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/trees/252d0891337877cdd85a7cca8c447c18a0fdbd76"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/commits/34793a5c1454ad23483c6fa237640e15c5f6372a","verification":{"payload":"tree 252d0891337877cdd85a7cca8c447c18a0fdbd76\nparent 3a5f7b76d2907e1f7253615a8a36d2f04625f9dc\nauthor Noel Huibers <noel@huibers.io> 1782439279 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782439279 +0200\n\nfeat(web-app): translate the whole app to DE + EN (#99)\n\nCloses #75. Extends the i18n foundation (#73) across the entire app — landing,\neditor, and every dialog — not just the public chrome.\n\n- Bilingual landing (#75): hero (<Trans> for the accent word + inline code),\n  the three scroll captions, features, steps, CTA, nav, footer. The hero graph''s\n  node names stay English on purpose — they mirror the `# @node: Load Data`\n  markers in the illustrated .ipynb, so translating them would desync the diagram.\n- Editor fully internationalized: App.tsx top bar + toasts/errors, EngineStatus,\n  SettingsDialog, ShortcutsDialog, ComposeDialog, CloudNotebooksDialog, AskPalette,\n  PaletteDrawer, ExplanationPanel, TriggersDialog, and the cell/file panes.\n- Catalog split into per-namespace modules under lib/i18n/messages/ (common,\n  login, legal, notFound stay inline). Each module exports `en` + `de: typeof en`,\n  so the compiler enforces DE/EN key parity per namespace.\n- Pluralization via react-i18next _one/_other (cell count, events, firings);\n  interpolation via {name}/{message}.\n\n~250 strings across 12 namespaces. German is informal \"du\", glossary-consistent\n(Pipeline/Knoten/Zelle/Engine/Trigger); brand, code, and identifiers kept verbatim.\n\nVerified: typecheck (enforces DE/EN parity), biome, build all green; SSR renders\nboth locales with the correct <html lang>; every literal t()/Trans key resolves\nto the catalog (237/237).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPd1vCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1sAQADcoTojS5W8UVkpO+J4H3Xkg\njT29RuAEhc5K7oNB6niovN0bissmr213U4bMjU2XjVLfnnqHK5zNm8urFABa35IG\nRSAIod6J70rRyQ7jLWLrK/MLpxw12y+kjgOUa2egxfnFzP5fnhbv2TriORqskkI5\no/VBIww+Iy5B7lUVaHYNT5NTrlJTnU/5birPiezmPZj/TQiT44sDV6gH5ZiIGt82\nxsNf7bnWvEGENmHrUmndOredJ9TwZgAsZpf7mmZhJPiWbWA+4dewIprNPZFzGZMR\nroGdrOJ4bolHJPduMNzsSUa9zpWJ/Bef8xbAot8r4g12+e093d0wib1G235zqgjf\nxL4vgzQIqqbI8yTmIwPhCXSEo24cZIKIg+1UdNXDQbId/rC1NvDykAJDf+wUbru6\nQzGs/e3vAlp3oIZl1iw4jS4OG2bYEVXE/1KImp2jKsRssPpEN2Ya/J9W73mGViN7\neui+x1dRSm0Ytsm1GiVopkmmds+d5tGdFcUwuSiQ6/RIEy6XshALR8soJM74SaoK\ntNQwzHkJz9a5X59JKURI9jR73OPszwpSti+AqCy0PcgbmMKuok0YgyJawjxtqkI5\nVGD2ChkTX8YJzeWyedt5OTRW3ZyPBw01bgunKPvY0PBVQII8SAxZf+hPNZEPYQed\nVymZegQbrbaC8EbmPIIx\n=MOYR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-26T02:01:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/34793a5c1454ad23483c6fa237640e15c5f6372a","node_id":"C_kwDOSWT-J9oAKDM0NzkzYTVjMTQ1NGFkMjM0ODNjNmZhMjM3NjQwZTE1YzVmNjM3MmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/3a5f7b76d2907e1f7253615a8a36d2f04625f9dc","sha":"3a5f7b76d2907e1f7253615a8a36d2f04625f9dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/3a5f7b76d2907e1f7253615a8a36d2f04625f9dc"}],"sha":"34793a5c1454ad23483c6fa237640e15c5f6372a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/34793a5c1454ad23483c6fa237640e15c5f6372a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44301196?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers","id":44301196,"login":"NoelHuibers","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzAxMTk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/3a5f7b76d2907e1f7253615a8a36d2f04625f9dc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-26T01:34:14Z","email":"noel@huibers.io","name":"Noel Huibers"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-26T01:34:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(web-app): i18n foundation (DE + EN) with react-i18next (#98)\n\nBilingual (DE/EN) foundation for the public surfaces, SSR-correct and persisted.\nResolves #73.\n\n- react-i18next + i18next, with a fresh instance created per request/locale\n  (createI18n) so i18next''s singleton is never mutated across concurrent SSR\n  renders; initAsync:false makes t() ready during the server render.\n- Locale resolved in the root beforeLoad: cookie (nf_locale) then Accept-Language,\n  via @tanstack/react-start/server getCookie/getRequestHeader on the server and\n  document.cookie/navigator.language on the client — same precedence both sides,\n  so SSR and hydration agree. Drives <html lang> and the I18nProvider.\n- Typed message catalogs (messages.ts), namespaced (common/login/legal/notFound/\n  settings) so marketing/app/legal can share keys; en is the source of truth, de\n  is type-checked against it.\n- LanguageSwitcher (EN/DE) persists the cookie and router.invalidate()s to\n  re-resolve — no full reload. Visible on login, legal, 404, and in Settings.\n- Public chrome fully translated: login, legal shell (localized headings), 404.\n  Editor app (~150+ strings) intentionally deferred — add namespaces + swap\n  literals incrementally without touching the foundation.\n\nURL strategy is cookie-based (no /de /en prefix) to avoid restructuring routes\nmid-flight; path-prefixed locales can come later if SEO needs them.","tree":{"sha":"6141e632e534e849f289995ae953cc18cd9ce987","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/trees/6141e632e534e849f289995ae953cc18cd9ce987"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/commits/3a5f7b76d2907e1f7253615a8a36d2f04625f9dc","verification":{"payload":"tree 6141e632e534e849f289995ae953cc18cd9ce987\nparent 1014a5fcaf73f8bd44217ae6d6de315e0b1fa91d\nauthor Noel Huibers <noel@huibers.io> 1782437654 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782437654 +0200\n\nfeat(web-app): i18n foundation (DE + EN) with react-i18next (#98)\n\nBilingual (DE/EN) foundation for the public surfaces, SSR-correct and persisted.\nResolves #73.\n\n- react-i18next + i18next, with a fresh instance created per request/locale\n  (createI18n) so i18next''s singleton is never mutated across concurrent SSR\n  renders; initAsync:false makes t() ready during the server render.\n- Locale resolved in the root beforeLoad: cookie (nf_locale) then Accept-Language,\n  via @tanstack/react-start/server getCookie/getRequestHeader on the server and\n  document.cookie/navigator.language on the client — same precedence both sides,\n  so SSR and hydration agree. Drives <html lang> and the I18nProvider.\n- Typed message catalogs (messages.ts), namespaced (common/login/legal/notFound/\n  settings) so marketing/app/legal can share keys; en is the source of truth, de\n  is type-checked against it.\n- LanguageSwitcher (EN/DE) persists the cookie and router.invalidate()s to\n  re-resolve — no full reload. Visible on login, legal, 404, and in Settings.\n- Public chrome fully translated: login, legal shell (localized headings), 404.\n  Editor app (~150+ strings) intentionally deferred — add namespaces + swap\n  literals incrementally without touching the foundation.\n\nURL strategy is cookie-based (no /de /en prefix) to avoid restructuring routes\nmid-flight; path-prefixed locales can come later if SEO needs them.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPdcWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnNIQAIUpRTuHr/wUyP/mwQtUHPri\nB5S/6lXWeVCVr5xniKrwtUxDVJyxLtaTUF/p7Mf8su8ldM6RlIA5jgzl60aG+qoJ\nSkbdGCzcMLm7hPcGDIQig/5EDZmEa