:"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/c44715df823ce4109f828d210a25d77fed38033e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-25T23:41:29Z","email":"noel@huibers.io","name":"NoelHuibers"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-25T23:41:29Z","email":"noel@huibers.io","name":"NoelHuibers"},"message":"docs: ADR 0001 — execution isolation (closed beta on shared Fly engine)\n\nDecision for #55. For now: keep the single shared Fly engine + exec(), gated to\na closed group of trusted beta testers (access control removes the untrusted-\nmulti-tenant threat — no sandbox to build/operate/pay for). Public launch later\nadopts a tiered model: bring-your-own-engine + a safe hosted default (Pyodide or\ntrust-gate) + a managed sandbox (Option B) as the escape hatch.\n\nFlags the two gates that must be set for the beta to actually be closed: engine\nJWT auth on Fly, and a sign-in allowlist (both currently open).","tree":{"sha":"00a4db0d8f5a6117184df5d0cf95749fb4748f68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/trees/00a4db0d8f5a6117184df5d0cf95749fb4748f68"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/commits/c44715df823ce4109f828d210a25d77fed38033e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44301196?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers","id":44301196,"login":"NoelHuibers","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzAxMTk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/c44715df823ce4109f828d210a25d77fed38033e","node_id":"C_kwDOSWT-J9oAKGM0NDcxNWRmODIzY2U0MTA5ZjgyOGQyMTBhMjVkNzdmZWQzODAzM2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commit/47b2a4d3f6d5bf9135cf266bfc1ee76f879a5bcc","sha":"47b2a4d3f6d5bf9135cf266bfc1ee76f879a5bcc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/47b2a4d3f6d5bf9135cf266bfc1ee76f879a5bcc"}],"sha":"c44715df823ce4109f828d210a25d77fed38033e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/c44715df823ce4109f828d210a25d77fed38033e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44301196?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NoelHuibers","id":44301196,"login":"NoelHuibers","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzAxMTk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoelHuibers","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/commits/47b2a4d3f6d5bf9135cf266bfc1ee76f879a5bcc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-25T23:13:06Z","email":"noel@huibers.io","name":"Noel Huibers"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-25T23:13:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: clear the 3 non-fatal Vercel function type errors at source (#93)\n\nThe function deploys + runs fine, but Vercel''s per-function tsc (NodeNext, no\nskipLibCheck) logged 3 type errors. Fixed each at the source:\n\n- TS2459 (@libsql/client `Config` not exported under NodeNext): drop the type\n  annotation in db/index.ts; the object is inferred.\n- TS2578 (unused @ts-expect-error on the dist import): replace with an ambient\n  declaration (api/dist-server.d.ts) referenced via triple-slash — no directive\n  that flips between \"needed\"/\"unused\" depending on whether the build artifact\n  exists at compile time.\n- TS2305 (better-auth''s drizzle adapter `.d.mts` omits the `drizzleAdapter`\n  export — a packaging bug; the runtime .mjs has it): isolate the one needed\n  `@ts-ignore` in src/lib/db/drizzle-adapter.ts (must be @ts-ignore, since\n  @ts-expect-error would flip to \"unused\" under `bundler`); disable noTsIgnore\n  for that one file in biome.json.\n\nNo runtime change. Verified: app + strict-server typecheck green, biome clean,\nbuild green, dev /api/auth/jwks 200.","tree":{"sha":"44f07d60c8ce0af1c575741a325c8870ed474543","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/git/trees/44f07d60c8ce0af1c575741a325c8870ed474543"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NoelHuibers/notebookflow/