hub.com/users/addisokw/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/addisokw/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/addisokw","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/addisokw/WetCourt/commits/f2175011b8250afa0477ad7a4f1e541268941501/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-19T04:55:26Z","email":"ken@kenaddison.com","name":"Ken Addison"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-19T04:55:26Z","email":"ken@kenaddison.com","name":"Ken Addison"},"message":"display: operator console defers TTS playback to the ?audio=1 kiosk (no echo)\n\nThe console always rendered TTS with no equivalent of the mic''s owner-deferral,\nso opening the operator tab alongside the /case?audio=1 speaker kiosk played\nthe audio twice (echo). Mirror the mic_owner mechanism: track audio_present,\nbroadcast AudioOwner{present}, carry it in the snapshot, and gate the console''s\nPCM enqueue on audioEnabled() (readOnly ? audioView : !audioOwnerPresent).\nSilence in-flight TTS the moment a kiosk claims audio; resume if it drops.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"524435133f3789f0c9c3ca6866cb8cd7ad31bd43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/addisokw/WetCourt/git/trees/524435133f3789f0c9c3ca6866cb8cd7ad31bd43"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/addisokw/WetCourt/git/commits/f2175011b8250afa0477ad7a4f1e541268941501","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/209685?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/addisokw/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/addisokw/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/addisokw/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/addisokw/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/addisokw","id":209685,"login":"addisokw","node_