subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/addisokw/WetCourt/commits/32248fc451bfc05fe7f8c20019e180858561ee4d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T17:22:55Z","email":"55170422+lbozz4@users.noreply.github.com","name":"lbozz4"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T17:22:55Z","email":"55170422+lbozz4@users.noreply.github.com","name":"lbozz4"},"message":"scripts: deploy_spark.sh — rsync the checkout onto the Spark''s live copy\n\nLAN-first host probe with Tailscale fallback (SPARK_HOST to override);\n--restart for bind-mounted persona/config/crimes changes, --build to\nrebuild orchestrator/vision/counsel images.\n\nProtects Spark-local runtime state with two-sided excludes: .env (sole\ncopy of LITELLM_MASTER_KEY), console-tuned orchestrator/calibration/,\ncaptures/, print_templates.json, transcripts.jsonl, counsel recordings/,\nand the pre-downloaded vision/models/. The gitignore filter alone is\nsender-side only — under --delete it would have removed these on the\nSpark (verified via a local sync simulation, hence the explicit list).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EQksTYzZa8a3WpQ5Re7rqz","tree":{"sha":"d980b465523293e49c6dcb5ff09c55fcf0d89de6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/addisokw/WetCourt/git/trees/d980b465523293e49c6dcb5ff09c55fcf0d89de6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/addisokw/WetCourt/git/commits/32248fc451bfc05fe7f8c20019e180858561ee4d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55170422?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lbozz4","id":55170422,"login":"lbozz4","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MTcwNDIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/addisokw/WetCourt/commit/32248fc451bfc05fe7f8c20019e180858561ee4d","node_id":"C_kwDOSWXeyNoAKDMyMjQ4ZmM0NTFiZmMwNWZlN2Y4YzIwMDE5ZTE4MDg1ODU2MWVlNGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/addisokw/WetCourt/commit/7bccfcf8cc0e9f476714aa886a2d35debbed9e86","sha":"7bccfcf8cc0e9f476714aa886a2d35debbed9e86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/addisokw/WetCourt/commits/7bccfcf8cc0e9f476714aa886a2d35debbed9e86"}],"sha":"32248fc451bfc05fe7f8c20019e180858561ee4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/addisokw/WetCourt/commits/32248fc451bfc05fe7f8c20019e180858561ee4d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55170422?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lbozz4","id":55170422,"login":"lbozz4","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MTcwNDIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/addisokw/WetCourt/commits/7bccfcf8cc0e9f476714aa886a2d35debbed9e86/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T16:51:31Z","email":"55170422+lbozz4@users.noreply.github.com","name":"lbozz4"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T16:51:31Z","email":"55170422+lbozz4@users.noreply.github.com","name":"lbozz4"},"message":"Personas: brief Wettington, drop leniency tilt, ban TTS stage directions\n\n- wettington: example-anchored BREVITY rule cuts verdicts 107 -> ~46 words\n  (~43s -> ~18s of TTS) with rubric quality intact (word-count caps alone\n  were ignored; in-voice example verdicts are what landed)\n- all personas: remove the LENIENCY TILT coin-flip clauses — they\n  double-specified the disposition that the guilty_bias slider already\n  injects via bias_directive() and would fight console slider changes;\n  character texture from those paragraphs is kept. A/B eval showed the\n  removal is behavior-neutral.\n- core.md VOICE: everything before the marker lines is spoken verbatim —\n  never emit *stage directions*; evals showed judges opening with\n  *adjusts spectacles* that Kokoro would read aloud\n- scripts/persona_eval.py: offline persona eval harness that rebuilds the\n  exact production verdict prompt (core + persona + bias directive,\n  CHARGE/PLEA message) and runs a probe-plea battery against the\n  Anthropic API — for when the Spark is down. Reports are gitignored.\n\nTuned against claude-haiku-4-5; re-verify on Qwen via the persona /test\nendpoint once vLLM is back before doors open.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EQksTYzZa8a3WpQ5Re7rqz","tree":{"sha":"9f53904be08ea4abc68f893966a145c6947efccc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/addisokw/WetCour