/api.github.com/repos/addisokw/WetCourt/commits/fd2aea7e9cc4d1ae6e6d34db58b3839375d79f8b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T02:58:10Z","email":"55170422+lbozz4@users.noreply.github.com","name":"lbozz4"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T02:58:10Z","email":"55170422+lbozz4@users.noreply.github.com","name":"lbozz4"},"message":"Counsel: tighten lawyer calls — cap at 2 exchanges, snappier Dewey\n\nShorter calls land better: max_exchanges 5 -> 2 (config + dev config),\ngreeting loses the BLT detour, signoff swaps \"Stubb out\" for \"Godspeed\",\nand replies are held to one or two sentences.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EQksTYzZa8a3WpQ5Re7rqz","tree":{"sha":"e8e68cf8598c5ac649d329e3927f397649b8295a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/addisokw/WetCourt/git/trees/e8e68cf8598c5ac649d329e3927f397649b8295a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/addisokw/WetCourt/git/commits/fd2aea7e9cc4d1ae6e6d34db58b3839375d79f8b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55170422?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lbozz4","id":55170422,"login":"lbozz4","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MTcwNDIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/addisokw/WetCourt/commit/fd2aea7e9cc4d1ae6e6d34db58b3839375d79f8b","node_id":"C_kwDOSWXeyNoAKGZkMmFlYTdlOWNjNGQxYWU2ZTZkMzRkYjU4YjM4MzkzNzVkNzlmOGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/addisokw/WetCourt/commit/a951de2aead7c6a56c8fed13d997d508f456dcae","sha":"a951de2aead7c6a56c8fed13d997d508f456dcae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/addisokw/WetCourt/commits/a951de2aead7c6a56c8fed13d997d508f456dcae"}],"sha":"fd2aea7e9cc4d1ae6e6d34db58b3839375d79f8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/addisokw/WetCourt/commits/fd2aea7e9cc4d1ae6e6d34db58b3839375d79f8b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55170422?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lbozz4","id":55170422,"login":"lbozz4","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MTcwNDIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/addisokw/WetCourt/commits/a951de2aead7c6a56c8fed13d997d508f456dcae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T02:48:07Z","email":"55170422+lbozz4@users.noreply.github.com","name":"lbozz4"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T02:48:07Z","email":"55170422+lbozz4@users.noreply.github.com","name":"lbozz4"},"message":"Judge-neck 0.5: slew-limited motion safety after the tilt-mount break\n\nCold boot used to command center while gravity had the head at droop; the\nfull-speed lift snapped the tilt mount (2026-07-14). The commanded pulse can\nno longer jump:\n\n- AIM sets targets; the wetline tick slews toward them (600 us/s — 1500\n  read as jerky on the real head; homing/protective moves at 250 us/s).\n- Cold boot soft-homes from the measured droop (TILT_DROOP 2167; the\n  counter-spring puts droop ABOVE the working range, 1500 is the spring\n  crash limit, so wrong guesses fail downward into the spring).\n- Warm resets resume from the STM32''s held pulses (hardware-verified),\n  trusted only while the mode reg still reads 3 — a power-cycled board\n  can''t spoof a held pulse.\n- Droop-zone pan lock: pan is frozen (on boot not even powered) while tilt\n  is beyond TILT_SAFE — the drooped head only clears the booth with pan\n  centered.\n- Overcurrent stall guard (0xA0): sustained draw eases tilt to TILT_SAFE\n  and emits unsolicited OVERCURRENT (spec''d in protocol/README.md; host\n  logs + skips it). Polled only while moving — 0.4''s always-on 4 Hz poll\n  jittered the STM32''s software PWM and made the parked head twitch.\n\nDesktop suite (test_motion_desktop.py) runs the real main.py under CPython\nfakes: ramp shape, slew/dt caps, readback trust, pan lock, OC trip/re-arm,\nparked-bus silence. Flashed + exercised on the rig 2026-07-14.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EQksTYzZa8a3WpQ5Re7rqz","tree":{"sha":"7746a8936c810bc8ec3492ae63b33608366bee25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/addisokw/WetCourt/git/trees/7746a8936c810bc8ec3492ae63b33608366bee25"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/addisokw/WetCourt/git/commits/a951de2aead7c6a56c8fed13d997d508f456dcae","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55170422?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lbozz4","id":55170422,"login":"lbozz4","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MTcwNDIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/addisokw/WetCourt/commit/a951de2aead7c6a56c8fed13d997d508f456dcae","node_id":"C_kwDOSWXeyNoAKGE5NTFkZTJhZWFkN2M2YTU2YzhmZWQxM2Q5OTdkNTA4ZjQ1NmRjYWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/addisokw/WetCourt/commit/0bf2bfdb0fb831b2392b72094e97e075df8331ed","sha":"0bf2bfdb0fb831b2392b72094e97e075df8331ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/addisokw/WetCourt/commits/0bf2bfdb0fb831b2392b72094e97e075df8331ed"}],"sha":"a951de2aead7c6a56c8fed13d997d508f456dcae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/addisokw/WetCourt/commits/a951de2aead7c6a56c8fed13d997d508f456dcae"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55170422?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lbozz4","id":55170422,"login":"lbozz4","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MTcwNDIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/addisokw/WetCourt/commits/0bf2bfdb0fb831b2392b72094e97e075df8331ed/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-14T15:42:21Z","email":"55170422+lbozz4@users.noreply.github.com","name":"lbozz4"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-14T22:20:19Z","email":"55170422+lbozz4@users.noreply.github.com","name":"lbozz4"},"message":"Print panel: pad inverse text inside the black bar\n\nFlush glyphs read as cut off at the bar''s edge (and wrap() strips any\npadding the user types), so inverse text blocks now reserve one space per\nside — scales with magnification. Preview mirrors the padding.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EQksTYzZa8a3WpQ5Re7rqz","tree":{"sha":"6c38a0e1323c960ba1e1d68ffa02af413ea6f718","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/addisokw/WetCourt/git/trees/6c38a0e1323c960ba1e1d68ffa02af413ea6f718"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/addisokw/WetCourt/git/commits/0bf2bfdb0fb831b2392b72094e97e075df8331ed","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55170422?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lbozz4/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lbozz4","id":55170422,"login":"lbozz4","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1MTcwNDIy","organizations_url